E["item:broken-and-battered-samophlange"] = {t="item",n="Broken and Battered Samophlange",z="orgrimmar",s="In the northern Barrens, Venture Company machinery lies battered after a failed inspection. The damaged samophlange must reach goblin experts in Orgrimmar, where someone may understand how it works.",h="In the northern Barrens, Venture Company machinery lies battered after a failed inspection.",sec={{t="Tinkered Beyond Recognition",b="The Venture Company made samophlanges for its resource work in the northern Barrens. Wenikee Boltbucket tried to inspect and modify one, adding gauges, levers, and dials to measure its stability. Her tinkering weakened the mechanism instead, leaving it battered and close to ruin. Knowing more additions might make it fail completely, she sent the fragile device to someone with factory experience.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Orgrimmar",b="Repairing the device calls for someone who has worked on Venture Company production lines. Rilli Greasygob, a former Venture employee, works at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. The battered apparatus catches the engineer's eye. Anyone who scavenges from goblin operations may seem daring, or simply foolhardy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a samophlange?",a="A samophlange is machinery made by the Venture Company for its industrial work in the Barrens. Few outsiders understand the secrets of its goblin engineering.",al={"what is this item","what does a samophlange do","samophlange purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the samophlange broken and battered?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket tried to modify the samophlange with extra gauges to measure its stability. The additions weakened it and damaged its sensitive inner parts.",al={"who broke the samophlange","why is it damaged","wenikee broke it"}},{q="Who can fix this damaged apparatus?",a="Rilli Greasygob can examine the damaged device. The former Venture Company employee works at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",al={"who do i bring this to","where does the samophlange go","who repairs it"}},{q="Where did this machinery originally come from?",a="The machinery came from Venture Company's drilling and extraction operations in the northern Barrens. Goblin engineers use it to power heavy extraction machinery.",al={"samophlange origin","where was it found","venture company origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Rilli Greasygob want the Broken and Battered Samophlange?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket tried to tinker with the delicate apparatus by adding extra gauges, only to reduce its structural integrity to an all-time low. Admitting further tinkering might ruin it entirely, Wenikee sends you to deliver the damaged contraption to Rilli Greasygob at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar. As a former Venture Company employee, Rilli has the technical expertise to repair their specialized machinery.",al={"why bring samophlange to rilli","who wants the broken samophlange","why does rilli want samophlange"},it="why_wanted",add="35e2c2bf"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the danger in adding dials and levers to an unstable Venture Company mechanism without a schematic.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you bring salvaged Venture Company machinery from the Barrens to Orgrimmar's goblin machine shops, where it may reveal valuable technical secrets."},kw={"barrens","machine shop","nogg","orgrimmar","rilli greasygob","samophlange","venture company","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"quest:3923","quest:3921","quest:894","topic:venture-company","npc:nogg","subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:orgrimmar","zone:barrens"},src={"Broken and Battered Samophlange","Rilli Greasygob (quest)"}}
E["item:cache-of-zanzil-s-altered-mixture"] = {t="item",n="Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture",z="orgrimmar",s="At the Venture Company tower near the Sludge Fen, a stockpile of potent poison lies locked away. The mixture bears the name of Zanzil, a jungle troll witch doctor, and draws the Shattered Hand's attention.",h="At the Venture Company tower near the Sludge Fen, a stockpile of potent poison lies locked away.",sec={{t="A Toxic Enterprise",b="North of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens, the Venture Company holds a tower outpost. At its summit, Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix keeps a cache of altered mixture bearing the name of the troll witch doctor Zanzil in his private strongbox. A poison has weakened everyone in the tower, leaving its goblin inhabitants vulnerable to a bold intruder.",sp=0},{t="Recovery for the Shattered Hand",b="The Shattered Hand, a secretive rogue guild beneath Orgrimmar, has taken notice of dangerous alchemical materials so close to Durotar. Master trainer Shenthul sends operatives to storm the tower, kill Gallywix, and break open his lockbox. The guild seeks both to neutralize the threat and to study the mixture for its own intelligence work. Recovering the volatile cache demands strong infiltration skills. The contaminated container's toxins can leave whoever handles it exposed and debilitated.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Zanzil's Altered Mixture?",a="Zanzil's Altered Mixture is a potent poison named for the troll witch doctor Zanzil. A cache of it lies locked in the Venture Company tower near the Sludge Fen, where a poison has weakened everyone inside.",al={"what is zanzil mixture","what is the cache","zanzil potion"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the cache found?",a="The cache is in Gallywix's Lockbox at the top of the Venture Company tower, north of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens.",al={"where is the mixture","where is zanzil cache","mixture location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Shattered Hand want the mixture?",a="Shenthul and the Shattered Hand seek to neutralize the Venture Company operation right on the Horde's doorstep and recover the compound for their own intelligence studies.",al={"who wants the mixture","why does shenthul want it","shattered hand mission"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How do you open the chest containing the cache?",a="The chest has delicate tumbler locks that call for advanced lockpicking skill, and the contaminated container can expose its handler to debilitating toxins.",al={"how to open gallywix lockbox","open zanzil chest","lockpicking zanzil cache"},gp=true},{q="Where does Zanzil's Altered Mixture come from, and who made it?",a="The concoction originates from the witch doctor Zanzil, though it fell into the hands of the Venture Company operating out of the Barrens. Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix kept the remaining altered supply locked away in his personal lockbox at the top of their drilling tower near the Sludge Fen.",al={"who made zanzil altered mixture","origin of altered mixture","where did zanzil mixture come from"},it="origin",add="83dd2f73"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Horde rogues, retrieving the mixture is an essential rite of passage, proving mastery of lockpicking, pickpocketing, and poison handling in service to the Shattered Hand.",["faction:Horde"]="The Venture Company's poison-laden tower north of the Sludge Fen threatens the surroundings and security of both Durotar and the Barrens."},kw={"altered mixture","gallywix","lockbox","poison","shattered hand","shenthul","sludge fen","venture co","zanzil"},rel={"quest:2478","npc:shenthul","item:gallywix-s-head","item:silixiz-s-tower-key","subzone:sludge-fen","zone:barrens","quest:1858","topic:rogue"},src={"Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture","Mission: Possible But Not Probable"}}
E["item:dirt-caked-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Dirt-Caked Pendant",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Barrens, a captive orc gives up the Dirt-Caked Pendant he carried. The keepsake reaches Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar, where it is used to draw a succubus.",h="In the Barrens, a captive orc gives up the Dirt-Caked Pendant he carried.",sec={{t="A Tragic Token",b="Dogran gives up the Dirt-Caked Pendant while held captive in the Barrens. Poisoned and crippled beyond recovery, he will not return to his mate, Zankaja, as a burden. He chooses to die fighting his captors instead. The pendant carries his unspoken love for her. A warlock takes the keepsake to Orgrimmar, where the warlocks of the Cleft of Shadow put its heartbreak and devotion to use.",sp=1},{t="Bait for a Demon",b="In the Cleft of Shadow, Gan'rul Bloodeye sees how the pendant can draw a succubus. These demons are drawn to mortal yearning, romance, and tragedy. The warlock cleans and polishes Dogran's pendant until it shines, turning a token of devoted love into a lure. The warlock then calls a succubus forth to face ritual combat and be dominated.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Dirt-Caked Pendant come from?",a="Dogran, a captive orc warrior in the Barrens, hands you the pendant after you give him Ken'zigla's draught and revive his senses.",al={"pendant origin","where do i get the pendant","who gives the pendant"},it="origin"},{q="What is the pendant's connection to Zankaja?",a="Zankaja is Dogran's mate in Orgrimmar. He gives up the pendant and hides that he survived so she will not have to care for him as an invalid warrior.",al={"who is zankaja","dogran and zankaja","pendant meaning"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye need this specific pendant?",a="Succubi are drawn to powerful mortal feelings, especially romance, heartbreak, and devotion. Once cleaned, Dogran's pendant can focus the call that draws a succubus into the summoning circle.",al={"why need pendant","succubus bait pendant","ganrul bloodeye pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after the pendant is delivered to Orgrimmar?",a="After you deliver the pendant to Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye cleans it and uses its allure to begin The Binding. A succubus is drawn into the circle beneath the Cleft of Shadow for you to defeat and subjugate.",al={"what next pendant","what to do with pendant"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Dirt-Caked Pendant?",a="The Dirt-Caked Pendant is a tarnished personal keepsake carried by the captured orc Dogran. Given as a token tied to his mate, Zankaja, it carries the strong emotional resonance of love and longing—the precise qualities a warlock requires when preparing to lure and subjugate a succubus.",al={"what is dirt caked pendant","dirt caked pendant lore","what kind of item is dirt caked pendant"},it="identity",add="cbd86f91"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock in training, you see how mortal grief and devotion can help command demons from the Twisting Nether.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see Dogran's bittersweet choice: he refuses to burden his clan and mate as a cripple, giving up his keepsake to make a warrior's final stand."},kw={"devourer of souls","dirt-caked pendant","dogran","gan'rul bloodeye","love's gift","succubus","zankaja"},rel={"quest:1512","quest:1471","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1515","npc:zankaja","quest:1472","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Dirt-Caked Pendant","Love's Gift"}}
E["item:dogran-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Dogran's Pendant",z="orgrimmar",s="Dogran's Pendant draws a succubus toward the warlocks of Orgrimmar. Dogran, a wounded orc, carries it while separated from his mate, Zankaja. In the Cleft of Shadow, warlocks turn the sorrow bound to it into a lure.",h="Dogran's Pendant draws a succubus toward the warlocks of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Conduit of Heartbreak",b="Dogran's Pendant carries the sorrow of an orc separated from Zankaja. Captivity and crippling wounds have overshadowed their love. The warlocks of the Cleft of Shadow know that demons such as succubi prey on love, yearning, and vulnerability. They use the pendant's grief to draw a succubus across the Twisting Nether and into Neeru Fireblade's summoning circle.",sp=0},{t="Subjugation and Remembrance",b="Under Gan'rul Bloodeye's direction, an aspiring warlock uses the pendant to summon a succubus and subdue it in combat. The trial proves mastery over the demon's seductive manipulations. When the ritual ends, the pendant goes back to Gan'rul, who is to deliver it to Zankaja.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dogran's Pendant used for?",a="Warlocks use Dogran's Pendant to summon a succubus inside Neeru Fireblade's tent in the Cleft of Shadow. After the demon is summoned and defeated, the pendant goes back to Gan'rul Bloodeye.",al={"use of pendant","what do i do with dograns pendant","dogran pendant quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a succubus respond to the pendant?",a="A succubus feeds on desire, love, and passion, and knows how to manipulate them. Bound to Dogran and Zankaja's tragic love, the pendant draws the demon across the Nether.",al={"why succubus wants pendant","why pendant summons demon","pendant lore"},it="power"},{q="Who was Dogran?",a="Dogran is an orc whose captivity and injuries are investigated by Horde warlocks through contacts such as Blind Cazul and Ken'zigla. He loves Zankaja but refuses to burden her with caring for an invalid.",al={"who is dogran","dogran story"},it="ties"},{q="What happens to the pendant after the summoning ritual?",a="After the warlock defeats the summoned succubus, the pendant goes back to Gan'rul Bloodeye, who can deliver it to Zankaja.",al={"who gets the pendant","return dograns pendant"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Dogran's Pendant?",a="Dogran's Pendant is a personal keepsake tied to the tragic fate of the orc Dogran and his lover, Zankaja. Imbued with raw longing and sorrow, this small medallion serves as a powerful focus for dark magic, capable of luring a succubus across the void during warlock binding rituals.",al={"what is dograns pendant","dograns pendant info","dogran pendant lore"},it="identity",add="f4378ded"},{q="Why is Dogran's Pendant wanted?",a="Warlocks seek the pendant because its emotional resonance makes it an ideal lure for a succubus, drawing the demon directly into a summoning circle to be broken and bound. Once the ritual concludes, Gan'rul Bloodeye requires its return so he can deliver the news to Dogran's mate, Zankaja.",al={"why do they want dograns pendant","who wants dogran's pendant","purpose of dogran's pendant"},it="why_wanted",add="bd6e6859"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you use Dogran's Pendant to prove mastery over the Nether and learn to summon a succubus.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see the pendant's ties to personal tragedies in the Barrens and Durotar, and to the warlock coven in Orgrimmar."},kw={"cleft of shadow","dogran","dogran's pendant","gan'rul bloodeye","orgrimmar","succubus","the binding","zankaja"},rel={"quest:1471","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","npc:zankaja","quest:1512","quest:1515","quest:1472","zone:orgrimmar","topic:warlock"},src={"Dogran's Pendant","The Binding (Succubus, Orgrimmar)"}}
E["item:gallywix-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Gallywix's Head",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Gallywix's Head proves that a Venture Company overseer was executed. The Shattered Hand demands the trophy as proof of the killing.",h="In Orgrimmar, Gallywix's Head proves that a Venture Company overseer was executed.",sec={{t="A Grim Proof of Elimination",b="Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix directed the Venture Company's work from its tower north of the Sludge Fen. When word arrived that the Venture Co. planned something on a grand scale, the Shattered Hand sent operatives to dismantle the facility. Bringing Gallywix's head to Shenthul in Orgrimmar proves the overseer was executed and secures the rogue's standing within the guild.",sp=0},{t="The Sludge Fen Incursion",b="The order to take Gallywix's head also calls for a stolen cache of Zanzil's altered mixture and the slaughter of the tower's poisoned personnel. Operatives assassinate Gallywix atop his perch and return his head to the Cleft of Shadow. The deed confirms that the Venture Company's grand scheme in the Barrens has been broken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Whose head is this?",a="The head belongs to Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, a goblin supervisor overseeing Venture Company operations at the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens.",al={"who is gallywix","puzik gallywix","gallywix head origin"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Gallywix's Head?",a="Shenthul wants Gallywix's Head. He is a rogue trainer and Shattered Hand operative in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",al={"who do i give the head to","turn in gallywix head","shenthul head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the Shattered Hand want him dead?",a="Puzik Gallywix ran the Venture Company tower north of the Sludge Fen, where the Venture Co. planned something on a grand scale. He also kept the last cache of Zanzil's altered mixture in his lockbox. The Shattered Hand marked him for death to break the operation and seize the mixture.",al={"why kill gallywix","gallywix assassination reason"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Puzik Gallywix located?",a="Puzik Gallywix is at the very top of the Venture Company tower, just north of the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens.",al={"where is gallywix","gallywix location","sludge fen tower boss"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Gallywix's Head come from?",a="The head is severed from Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, a goblin supervisor overseeing operations at the Venture Company's tower north of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens. Tasked by the Shattered Hand to infiltrate the stronghold and eliminate its inhabitants, an assassin claims the foreman's head directly from his corpse atop the tower as proof that the operation has been decisively broken.",al={"where do you get gallywix head","gallywix head origin","how to get gallywix head"},it="origin",add="862bd188"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, retrieving Gallywix's Head proves your lethal skill in covert infiltration, stealth, and targeted assassination for the Shattered Hand.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help curb the Venture Company's exploitative industrial incursions threatening the borders of the Barrens and Durotar."},kw={"barrens","gallywix","orgrimmar","puzik","shattered hand","shenthul","sludge fen","venture co"},rel={"quest:2478","npc:shenthul","subzone:sludge-fen","quest:1858","item:cache-of-zanzil-s-altered-mixture","item:silixiz-s-tower-key","quest:764","zone:barrens"},src={"Gallywix's Head","Mission: Possible But Not Probable"}}
E["item:glyphs-of-summoning"] = {t="item",n="Glyphs of Summoning",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, apprentice warlocks use the Glyphs of Summoning to call a voidwalker. Transcribed from the ancient Tablet of Verga, the inscriptions draw one from the Nether into a summoning circle and bind it to the warlock’s service.",h="In Orgrimmar, apprentice warlocks use the Glyphs of Summoning to call a voidwalker.",sec={{t="A Pact Forged in Shadow",b="In the Cleft of Shadow, warlocks study the dark arts far from the prying eyes of the Warchief’s guards. For an aspiring warlock learning from Gan'rul Bloodeye, commanding a voidwalker marks an important step. The Glyphs of Summoning come from knowledge inscribed on the Tablet of Verga, and bridge Azeroth and the Nether. In Neeru Fireblade's tent, the warlock lays them within a summoning circle. They open a threshold and draw a creature of the Void into the mortal realm. Before Gan'rul teaches the final methods of binding, the warlock must defeat the summoned creature in combat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Glyphs of Summoning used for?",a="The glyphs are ritual writings used in the summoning circle inside Neeru Fireblade's tent in Orgrimmar. They call a hostile voidwalker from the Nether, which the warlock must subdue to master its summoning.",al={"what do glyphs of summoning do","glyphs of summoning purpose","how to use glyphs of summoning"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do the Glyphs of Summoning come from?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye, the warlock trainer in the Cleft of Shadow, provides them. They draw on knowledge preserved on the Tablet of Verga.",al={"where to get glyphs of summoning","who gives glyphs of summoning"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the summoning ritual performed?",a="The ritual takes place inside Neeru Fireblade's tent, across the cavern floor in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow.",al={"where do i summon voidwalker","summoning circle location orgrimmar","neeru fireblade circle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do warlocks have to defeat the summoned creature?",a="A warlock must establish dominance to control a demon or creature of the Void safely. Defeating the summoned creature proves the warlock's resolve, allowing Gan'rul Bloodeye to teach how to bind its kind to their will.",al={"why fight the voidwalker","subdue voidwalker"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Glyphs of Summoning?",a="The Glyphs of Summoning are arcane and demonic inscriptions transcribed directly from the Tablet of Verga. Entrusted to developing warlocks by Gan'rul Bloodeye beneath Orgrimmar, they carry the precise invocations needed to tear open the veil and call forth a hostile voidwalker from the Nether for binding.",al={"what are glyphs of summoning","glyphs of summoning lore","what is glyphs of summoning"},it="identity",add="094a8ca5"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want the Glyphs of Summoning back?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye requires you to bring the glyphs back alongside proof of your victory so he can complete your training. Once you demonstrate you have the strength to summon and subdue a raging voidwalker, Gan'rul uses the glyphs and your demonstrated mastery to teach you how to permanently bind such entities to your service.",al={"why return glyphs of summoning","why does gan'rul want glyphs of summoning","why are glyphs of summoning wanted"},it="why_wanted",add="fd669514"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you face an essential rite of passage. The glyphs let you prove your mastery over the Void and claim a voidwalker servant."},kw={"cleft of shadow","gan'rul bloodeye","glyphs of summoning","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","tablet of verga","the binding","voidwalker"},rel={"quest:1504","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","item:tablet-of-verga","quest:1501","quest:1506","zone:orgrimmar","quest:829"},src={"Glyphs of Summoning","The Binding (Voidwalker, Orgrimmar)"}}
E["item:gryshka-s-letter"] = {t="item",n="Gryshka's Letter",z="orgrimmar",s="Innkeeper Gryshka sends a note of thanks to Zargh at the Crossroads after receiving fresh meat. The letter also introduces young Horde couriers to the wind rider flight network.",h="Innkeeper Gryshka sends a note of thanks to Zargh at the Crossroads after receiving fresh meat.",sec={{t="A Grateful Innkeeper",b="Innkeeper Gryshka thanks Zargh for the steaks he sends from the Barrens to Orgrimmar's central tavern. She recalls the time he lost a finger while preparing meat, then teases that he looks handsome even when bloodied by his trade.",sp=0},{t="Courier Along the Flight Paths",b="To return Gryshka's Letter to the Crossroads, you report to Doras, the wind rider master atop Orgrimmar's plateau. Show him that you have already checked in with Devrak at the Crossroads, and Doras introduces young couriers to the wyvern flight paths linking settlements in Durotar and the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote Gryshka's Letter?",a="Innkeeper Gryshka, who manages a tavern in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, wrote the letter after receiving fresh meat.",al={"who wrote this","gryshka letter author","sender"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the letter intended for?",a="The letter is addressed to Zargh, a butcher at the Crossroads in the Barrens who supplied Gryshka with meat.",al={"recipient","who gets gryshka letter","where does the letter go"},it="item"},{q="What is written inside the letter?",a="Gryshka thanks Zargh for his cuts, recalls the accident when he lost a finger while preparing meat, and teases that he looks handsome even when bloodied.",al={"letter text","what does gryshka say","letter contents"}},{q="Why does Doras need to see the letter?",a="Doras is Orgrimmar's wind rider master. Gryshka sends you to show that you have checked in with Devrak at the Crossroads, so Doras can introduce you to the wyvern flight paths.",al={"why show doras","doras the wind rider master","orgrimmar flight master"}},{q="What is Gryshka's Letter?",a="It is a handwritten message of gratitude penned by Innkeeper Gryshka of Orgrimmar. She drafted it in response to a special shipment of meat sent to her inn, intending it as both a note of thanks and a flirtatious gesture of affection to be carried back to the Barrens.",al={"what is gryshka's letter","gryshka letter item","about gryshkas letter"},it="identity",add="950e527c"},{q="Why does anyone want Gryshka's Letter?",a="The butcher Zargh at the Crossroads eagerly awaits word on how his prime meat was received. Gryshka desires to have it delivered to show her heartfelt thanks and return his affection, while Doras the wind rider master simply needs to confirm your destination to arrange flight back across the Barrens.",al={"why deliver gryshkas letter","who wants gryshka's letter","why does zargh want gryshkas letter"},it="why_wanted",add="0c09fbc7"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Delivering Gryshka's Letter introduces young Horde adventurers to the wyvern flight master network linking Durotar and the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","doras","gryshka","gryshka's letter","meat","orgrimmar","wind rider","zargh"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-gryshka","npc:zargh","npc:doras","quest:6385","quest:6386","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar","npc:devrak"},src={"Gryshka's Letter","Doras the Wind Rider Master (Classic)","Return to the Crossroads."}}
E["item:lieutenant-s-insignia"] = {t="item",n="Lieutenant's Insignia",z="orgrimmar",s="Near Orgrimmar, cultists bear Lieutenant's Insignia and the Burning Blade's mark. Horde adventurers recover it from them.",h="Near Orgrimmar, cultists bear Lieutenant's Insignia and the Burning Blade's mark.",sec={{t="A Mark of the Cult",b="Cultists at Skull Rock on Durotar's eastern shore carry Lieutenant's Insignia. The mark names its bearer an officer of the Burning Blade. Warchief Thrall will not suffer traitors in his new nation. Yet a purge might scatter the cult before its masters are exposed. So he entrusts the badge to a champion, to test those suspected of infiltrating beneath Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="The Cleft of Shadow",b="Warchief Thrall sends his agent to the Cleft of Shadow with Lieutenant's Insignia, to show it to Neeru Fireblade. Neeru mistakes the agent for a newly promoted subordinate. Sure of his standing, the warlock boasts that the Burning Blade serves the Shadow Council and the Burning Legion. Those words give Thrall a way to expose the corruption beneath the city.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.2","q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="Where does the Lieutenant's Insignia come from?",a="Burning Blade fanatics and apprentices in Skull Rock carry Lieutenant's Insignia. The cavern lies on Durotar's coast east of Orgrimmar.",al={"how do i get lieutenants insignia","who drops lieutenants insignia","lieutenant insignia source"},it="origin"},{q="What is the insignia used for?",a="Warchief Thrall gives Lieutenant's Insignia to his agent as a disguise. A young adventurer bearing it can pass as a Burning Blade officer and reach places Thrall's agents cannot, to learn who leads the cult.",al={"why do i need lieutenants insignia","lieutenants insignia quest use","what to do with insignia"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Neeru Fireblade?",a="Neeru Fireblade is an orc warlock in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He claims to serve Thrall by showing how warlocks can aid the Horde, but secretly leads the local Burning Blade cult.",al={"who is neeru","neeru fireblade lore"},sp=2,it="identity",bt={"q5726.2"}},{q="Why doesn't Thrall just kill Neeru Fireblade immediately?",a="Thrall knows Neeru is a traitor, but an early strike could warn the cult's true masters and scatter its network. He uses Neeru as an unwitting informant to uncover the Shadow Council's wider presence in Durotar.",al={"why thrall doesnt kill neeru","why keep neeru alive","why infiltrate neeru"},sp=1,it="motive",bt={"q5726.2"}},{q="What is the Lieutenant's Insignia?",a="It is an emblem carried by officers within the Burning Blade cult, marking the bearer as an acknowledged ranking lieutenant among their ranks. To demonic cultists operating in secret throughout Durotar, presenting this token signifies loyalty, standing, and authority within the Shadow Council's network.",al={"what is lieutenants insignia","lieutenant insignia what is it","burning blade insignia"},it="identity",add="2e1cfb76"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the young Horde, Lieutenant's Insignia marks the danger of demonic corruption trying to undermine Thrall's new nation from within.",["class:Warlock"]="For a warlock, Lieutenant's Insignia shows the Burning Blade turning fel magic to the Burning Legion's service. That strains Thrall's tolerance of lawful Horde warlocks."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","durotar","hidden enemies","lieutenant's insignia","neeru fireblade","shadow council","skull rock","thrall"},rel={"quest:5726","npc:thrall","quest:829","topic:burning-blade-clan","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:827","topic:shadow-council","zone:durotar"},src={"Lieutenant's Insignia","Hidden Enemies","Hidden Enemies (2)"}}
E["item:samophlange-manual"] = {t="item",n="Samophlange Manual",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob seeks the scattered pages of the Samophlange Manual. The handbook holds instructions for repairing and operating the Venture Company's samophlange.",h="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob seeks the scattered pages of the Samophlange Manual.",sec={{t="Secrets of the Contraption",b="Boss Copperplug guarded the Venture Company's knowledge of the samophlange. The ambitious overseer kept the manual's pages from most workers, giving scattered leaves only to his most loyal subordinates. When the device slipped from company hands, no one could repair it without gathering the torn documentation from Copperplug and his crew at the Boulder Lode Mine.",sp=0},{t="A Rival's Ambition",b="Rilli Greasygob left the Venture Company and settled in Orgrimmar to learn how the samophlange was built. Copperplug had never favored him, so Rilli depends on enterprising travelers to retrieve the manual's cover and loose leaves. Reassembled, the handbook gives goblin tinkerers working alongside the Horde a rare look at Venture Company engineering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Samophlange Manual?",a="The Samophlange Manual explains how to operate and repair the Venture Company's complex, eccentric mechanical device.",al={"what is samophlange manual","samophlange book","samophlange guide"},it="identity"},{q="Who owned the manual originally?",a="Boss Copperplug, a Venture Company overseer at the Boulder Lode Mine in the northeastern Barrens, kept the manual. He guarded its secrets and gave individual pages only to his most trusted workers.",al={"who has the manual","boss copperplug manual","who wrote the manual"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the manual torn into pages?",a="Boss Copperplug separated the manual to keep rivals and untrusted subordinates from understanding the whole device. He kept the cover and distributed five specific pages among his miners and operators.",al={"why find manual pages","scattered manual pages","why are pages missing"},it="history"},{q="Who wants to read the completed manual?",a="Rilli Greasygob, an engineer in Orgrimmar, wants the reassembled manual to understand and repair the broken samophlange recovered from the Barrens.",al={"who needs the manual","rilli greasygob","who wants samophlange manual"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a samophlange used for?",a="No one outside the Venture Company seems to know what a samophlange is used for. The company experimented with one at a small research site southwest of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens, but even the engineers who studied it could make little sense of it.",al={"what does samophlange do","purpose of samophlange","samophlange purpose"},it="purpose"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The manual reveals proprietary Venture Company technology and shows how goblin tinkerers guard trade secrets and working schematics from their peers.",["faction:Horde"]="The manual lets Horde-aligned goblins in Orgrimmar study and repurpose corporate drilling machinery under the Venture Company's nose."},kw={"barrens","boss copperplug","boulder lode mine","engineering","manual","rilli greasygob","samophlange","sputtervalve","venture company"},rel={"quest:3924","quest:894","quest:3923","subzone:boulder-lode-mine","topic:venture-company","npc:sputtervalve","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Samophlange Manual","Samophlange Manual (quest)"}}
E["item:sample-of-zanzil-s-altered-mixture"] = {t="item",n="Sample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture",z="orgrimmar",s="A courier carries Sample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture across the sea to Tarren Mill. The brew came from the witch doctor Zanzil and leaves its carrier weakened. Serge Hinott may find a cure and uncover the poison's workings.",h="A courier carries Sample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture across the sea to Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Toxic Token",b="An operative carries the mixture after infiltrating the Venture Company's tower near the Sludge Fen in the Barrens. The sample came from a cache in Gallywix's lockbox, and Zanzil's brew has left the agent afflicted. Shenthul sends the stricken operative across the Great Sea with the sample. At Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, apothecary Serge Hinott has the rare skill to isolate the toxin and learn its components.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of Poisoncraft",b="Serge Hinott studies the altered mixture to help the afflicted courier and reveal how to brew and handle potent poisons in the field. Horde rogues seek this knowledge to master the darker arts of their trade.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is this mixture?",a="It is an alchemical brew tied to the witch doctor Zanzil, recovered from the Venture Company's tower near the Sludge Fen in the Barrens. Its potent toxin causes lingering, debilitating effects on anyone who touches it directly.",al={"what is zanzils mixture","sample of zanzils altered mixture","zanzil poison sample"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need to take it to Serge Hinott?",a="Serge Hinott is an apothecary at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. His knowledge can neutralize the brew's effects and produce a reliable cure before the toxin causes permanent harm.",al={"who is serge hinott","why take to tarren mill","cure for zanzil mixture"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Zanzil?",a="Zanzil the Outcast is a jungle troll witch doctor known for creating madness-inducing elixirs, poisons, and mutagens. His toxic recipes have spread beyond his native jungles into mercenary and industrial operations such as the Venture Company.",al={"who is zanzil","zanzil the outcast","zanzil lore"},it="origin"},{q="How do you reach Tarren Mill to deliver it?",a="Take the zeppelin from Durotar to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades. Then follow the main road south through Silverpine Forest and the signs east into the Hillsbrad Foothills to Tarren Mill.",al={"how to get to tarren mill","travel to hillsbrad","tarren mill directions"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you carry this dangerous sample to Serge Hinott, whose lessons cover brewing, handling, and applying lethal poisons.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you carry the brew across a continent by zeppelin and road, following routes from Kalimdor to the Forsaken territories in Lordaeron."},kw={"altered mixture","hillsbrad","poisons","rogue","serge hinott","sludge fen","tarren mill","zanzil"},rel={"quest:2479","npc:serge-hinott","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity"},src={"Sample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture","Hinott's Assistance"}}
E["item:silixiz-s-tower-key"] = {t="item",n="Silixiz's Tower Key",z="orgrimmar",s="Foreman Silixiz carries the key to the Venture Company tower near the Sludge Fen. Shattered Hand operatives must take it from his pocket as part of an undercover sabotage assignment.",h="Foreman Silixiz carries the key to the Venture Company tower near the Sludge Fen.",sec={{t="A Test of Subtlety",b="North of the Sludge Fen, the Venture Company keeps its tower under tight security. Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix oversees the isolated lookout, while goblin mercenaries patrol the compound. Outside, Foreman Silixiz carries the tower key. A Shattered Hand operative from Orgrimmar must steal it and keep it. Force will not do: the operative must enter unseen and pick Silixiz's pocket, proving their stealth before climbing into the tower's toxic upper levels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Foreman Silixiz?",a="Foreman Silixiz is outside the Venture Company tower, directly north of the Sludge Fen in the northeastern Barrens.",al={"silixiz location","where is foreman silixiz","find silixiz"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Can I obtain the key by killing Foreman Silixiz?",a="No. The key cannot be taken from Silixiz's corpse. An operative must pick his pocket while he is alive.",al={"silixiz key drop","can i kill silixiz","loot silixiz key"},gp=true},{q="Who requires this key?",a="Shattered Hand contacts assign the key to be delivered to Shenthul, the rogue trainer in Orgrimmar.",al={"who wants the key","turn in silixiz key","silixiz tower key quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the key used for?",a="The key proves an operative infiltrated the Venture Company's tower near the Sludge Fen. It is delivered to the Shattered Hand with Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix's head and the cache of Zanzil's altered mixture.",al={"what does silixiz key unlock","silixiz key purpose","use tower key"},sp=1,it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Silixiz's Tower Key?",a="It is a key held by Foreman Silixiz outside the Venture Company tower north of the Sludge Fen. The operative is told to steal it and hold on to it in case the Shattered Hand contact needs it later.",al={"what is silixiz tower key","silixiz key","venture co tower key"},it="identity",add="163c94d7"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, taking Silixiz's Tower Key is a trial for entering the ranks of the Shattered Hand. It demands skill in sneaking and pickpocketing.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry a trophy tied to efforts against Venture Company exploitation and chemical experiments in the northern Barrens."},kw={"barrens","foreman silixiz","shattered hand","shenthul","silixiz","sludge fen","tower key","venture co"},rel={"npc:shenthul","quest:1858","subzone:sludge-fen","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar","item:gallywix-s-head","item:cache-of-zanzil-s-altered-mixture","topic:rogue"},src={"Silixiz's Tower Key","Mission: Possible But Not Probable"}}
E["item:tablet-of-verga"] = {t="item",n="Tablet of Verga",z="orgrimmar",s="In Skull Rock, the Tablet of Verga lies in Burning Blade hands, its demonic runes sought by warlocks in Orgrimmar.",h="In Skull Rock, the Tablet of Verga lies in Burning Blade hands, its demonic runes sought by warlocks in...",sec={{t="A Stolen Relic",b="The Tablet of Verga bears ritual runes for summoning creatures of the Nether and bending them to a master's will. The Burning Blade cult stole the stone and hid it in a chest inside Skull Rock, just east of Orgrimmar. Warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow seek it to study the markings and learn to summon a voidwalker. Recovering it also keeps the cult from gaining that same advantage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Tablet of Verga located?",a="The Tablet of Verga is hidden in a Burning Blade Stash inside Skull Rock, a cavern complex crawling with cultists just east of Orgrimmar in Durotar.",al={"tablet of verga location","where to find tablet of verga","where is verga tablet"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Tablet of Verga recovered?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye, a master warlock in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar, sends initiates to retrieve the tablet so he can teach them to summon greater minions.",al={"who needs tablet of verga","who do i bring tablet of verga to","gan'rul tablet"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What power does the tablet contain?",a="The stone bears ancient runes needed to summon and bind a voidwalker, a creature drawn from the Twisting Nether.",al={"what does the tablet do","tablet of verga lore","tablet of verga runes"},it="power"},{q="Why did the Burning Blade steal it?",a="The Burning Blade cult seeks to disrupt the Horde and increase its demonic power. Stealing the tablet denies Orgrimmar's practitioners key ritual knowledge while the cult keeps it for itself.",al={"why do burning blade have tablet","burning blade verga"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Tablet of Verga?",a="The Tablet of Verga is a relic inscribed with arcane warlock knowledge, specifically the runes and rituals necessary to summon and bind a voidwalker. Stolen away by cultists of the Burning Blade, it holds dark secrets prized by warlocks seeking to advance their mastery over the Twisting Nether and summon demonic servants to their bidding.",al={"what is tablet of verga","tablet of verga","verga tablet"},it="identity",add="5fa1e5b5"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock training in Orgrimmar, recovering the tablet marks a step toward proving your worth to the Horde and learning to bind a defensive voidwalker servant.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the Burning Blade close to Orgrimmar's gates. Taking stolen relics from the cult strikes at its influence over Thrall's fledgling nation."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","durotar","gan'rul bloodeye","skull rock","tablet of verga","voidwalker"},rel={"quest:1473","quest:1471","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:827","zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar","topic:warlock","topic:horde"},src={"Tablet of Verga","Creature of the Void (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["item:tazan-s-satchel"] = {t="item",n="Tazan's Satchel",z="orgrimmar",s="Near Ratchet, Tazan carries a locked satchel as he deals with pirates along the coast. The Shattered Hand wants the secret information inside.",h="Near Ratchet, Tazan carries a locked satchel as he deals with pirates along the coast.",sec={{t="Secrets of the Barrens",b="Tazan deals with pirates camped along the Barrens coast near Ratchet. Therzok, a guild master of the Shattered Hand beneath Orgrimmar in the Cleft of Shadow, takes notice. The guild seeks covert power beyond Warchief Thrall's cautious diplomacy, and marks Tazan for elimination to seize the intelligence in his satchel.",sp=0},{t="A Complex Lock",b="The satchel's lock makes it hard to open in the field. Tazan gave the key to Gamon, his associate, who is a drunken fixture in an Orgrimmar tavern. Rogues seeking the satchel must lift the key from Gamon's pocket without raising an alarm, then they can read Tazan's logbook.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who does this satchel belong to?",a="The satchel belongs to Tazan, a troll who deals with pirates near Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"who is tazan","tazan owner","satchel owner"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Shattered Hand want Tazan's Satchel?",a="Therzok and the Shattered Hand want the intelligence from Tazan's dealings with coastal pirates to expand their network and reclaim martial pride from the shadows.",al={"why does therzok want this","shattered hand satchel","why steal the satchel"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the key to open the satchel?",a="Tazan left the key with his associate Gamon, a drunken patron in an Orgrimmar tavern.",al={"how to open satchel","tazan key","where is the key"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What is inside Tazan's Satchel?",a="Tazan's logbook rests inside the locked satchel and details his secret trades and ties to coastal buccaneers.",al={"satchel contents","what is in the bag","tazan logbook"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you must recover the satchel and lift its key from Gamon to earn your place in the Shattered Hand.",["faction:Horde"]="In Orgrimmar, the Shattered Hand seeks covert advantage while Warchief Thrall pursues a more measured course."},kw={"barrens","cleft of shadow","gamon","ratchet","shattered hand","tazan","tazan's satchel","therzok"},rel={"quest:1858","quest:1859","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar","topic:rogue","subzone:ratchet","topic:pirate"},src={"Tazan's Satchel","The Shattered Hand (Classic)","The Shattered Hand (2)"}}
E["npc:aelthalyste"] = {t="npc",n="Aelthalyste",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Undercity's War Quarter, Aelthalyste trains Forsaken priests in the power of Shadow. She guides their spiritual discipline and sends troll acolytes to their own elders in Orgrimmar.",h="In the Undercity's War Quarter, Aelthalyste trains Forsaken priests in the power of Shadow.",sec={{t="Voice of the Forgotten Shadow",b="Aelthalyste trains Forsaken priests in the power of Shadow. While many priests across Azeroth revere the Holy Light, her students have turned from it. She rose as an incorporeal banshee and shares the spectral agony and relentless resolve of Sylvanas Windrunner's followers. From her chamber in the Undercity's War Quarter, she calls aspiring priests from distant outposts to master their darker arts. She teaches them to harness suffering as a weapon.",sp=0},{t="Ties with the Horde",b="Aelthalyste respects the spiritual traditions of other Horde practitioners. She sends troll initiates away from her shadow teachings, directing them across the sea to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar, where they can learn Darkspear spiritualism. Her deference lets Horde spellcasters develop within their own traditions and strengthens ties between Kalimdor and Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aelthalyste?",a="Aelthalyste is a banshee and a leading teacher of the Forsaken priesthood. In the War Quarter of the Undercity, she trains Forsaken practitioners in Shadow magic.",al={"aelthalyste lore","who is the banshee priest","aelthalyste npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Aelthalyste?",a="Aelthalyste can be found in the War Quarter beneath the ruins of Capital City, in the Undercity. Fellow Forsaken instructors are nearby.",al={"aelthalyste location","where is aelthalyste","find aelthalyste"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do Forsaken priests believe?",a="Many Forsaken priests believe the Holy Light abandoned them in undeath. They have turned from the Light they revered in life toward shadow, embracing darkness, willpower, and personal discipline.",al={"forgotten shadows","forsaken priest religion","cult of forgotten shadows"}},{q="Why does Aelthalyste send troll priests to Orgrimmar?",a="Aelthalyste sends troll priests to Orgrimmar because troll ties to spirits and shadow differ from Forsaken doctrine. She respects that difference and sends troll acolytes to train with Ur'kyo, the Darkspear priest trainer in the Valley of Spirits.",al={"ur'kyo aelthalyste","why send trolls away","aelthalyste troll quest"},it="purpose"},{q="What does Aelthalyste teach?",a="Aelthalyste gives Forsaken characters core priest instruction and guides advanced acolytes in undead rites. Her teachings include spells such as Touch of Weakness and Dark Sacrifice.",al={"priest training aelthalyste","what spells does aelthalyste give","aelthalyste abilities"},gp=true},{q="Is Aelthalyste loyal to Sylvanas?",a="Yes. Aelthalyste is a banshee in the Undercity who serves Sylvanas Windrunner. She works to strengthen the Forsaken through mastery of dark magic.",al={"aelthalyste faction","is she loyal to undercity","banshee loyalty"},it="side"},{q="Why is Aelthalyste in the Undercity?",a="Aelthalyste resides in the War Quarter of the Undercity to instruct and guide practitioners of shadow magic. As a head priestess of the Forsaken priesthood, she oversees the training of Forsaken priests and summons promising disciples from afar so they may master the darker rites of their faith.",al={"why is aelthalyste here","aelthalyste undercity purpose","why is aelthalyste in war quarter"},it="why_here",add="71b5fa08"},{q="What does Aelthalyste want?",a="Aelthalyste seeks to expand the strength and discipline of the Forsaken priesthood. She focuses on cultivating shadow magic among the Forsaken, calling initiated priests back to the Undercity to refine their darker powers while ensuring that allied practitioners, such as troll priests, receive proper training from their own elders.",al={"aelthalyste goals","what is aelthalyste's goal","aelthalyste motive"},it="wants",add="84a14853"},{q="Who is Aelthalyste allied with?",a="Aelthalyste serves the Forsaken as a prominent leader of the Forsaken priesthood. She maintains close instructional ties with priest trainers across Horde lands and shares mutual respect with Darkspear elders like Ur'kyo, ensuring that troll students are guided back to their own spiritual masters in Orgrimmar.",al={"aelthalyste connections","who does aelthalyste work with","aelthalyste allies"},it="ties",add="61183540"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you find in Aelthalyste a teacher of your doctrine, dark spells, and the ways of shadow.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you share the Forsaken turn from the Holy Light of former lives toward the practical power of Shadow.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you are directed by Aelthalyste to learn Darkspear rites from Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see Aelthalyste's respect for Ur'kyo's teachings helping bridge the coalition's cultural divides."},kw={"aelthalyste","banshee","devouring plague","priest","shadow","undercity","ur'kyo","war quarter"},rel={"zone:undercity","subzone:war-quarter","npc:ur-kyo","quest:5644","quest:5643","quest:5654","topic:forsaken","topic:darkspear-tribe"},src={"Aelthalyste"}}
E["npc:cazul"] = {t="npc",n="Cazul",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Cleft of Shadow, Cazul guides young warlocks toward greater command of demons. Blind and ancient, he remains a keeper of old orc warlock traditions.",h="In the Cleft of Shadow, Cazul guides young warlocks toward greater command of demons.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Dark",b="Cazul waits in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar, where rising warlocks seek his counsel. Blind though he is, he senses the currents of the Twisting Nether and hears the whispers of demons. Those who want to master their craft and bind more dangerous servitors are often sent to him. His sight is gone, but his arcane power remains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cazul?",a="Cazul is an elderly, blind orc warlock who lives in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He advises aspiring warlocks in dark sorcery and demonology.",al={"who is cazul","cazul lore","blind cazul npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Cazul blind?",a="No record tells why Cazul is blind.",al={"why is cazul blind","how did cazul lose his sight"}},{q="What role does Cazul play for warlocks?",a="Cazul guides warlocks seeking to advance their craft, especially those learning to summon and bind a succubus.",al={"cazul quests","what does cazul teach","warlock quest cazul"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Cazul on?",a="Cazul aligns with the Horde, making his home in the shadowed subterranean enclave of Orgrimmar. While practitioners of the dark arts operate under wary supervision beneath the Warchief's city, he peacefully shares his ancient knowledge with Horde practitioners who seek him out.",al={"cazul faction","is cazul horde","cazul loyalty"},it="side",add="9bd6f5fc"},{q="Why is Cazul in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="The Cleft of Shadow is the designated quarter where Orgrimmar's practitioners of darker magic conduct their studies away from the open public. Cazul stays there to teach and counsel warlocks who require ancient lore and mastery over summoned fiends.",al={"why is cazul here","cazul orgrimmar cleft","why is cazul in cleft of shadow"},it="why_here",add="f5d7dff7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock of the Horde, you can seek Cazul's guidance in the Cleft of Shadow when you want to bind deeper powers from the Nether.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see in Cazul the enduring presence of dark magic among your people. He practices away from the watchful eyes of Thrall's honor guard."},kw={"blind cazul","cazul","cleft of shadow","demonology","orgrimmar","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:1508","quest:1472","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft"},src={"Cazul"}}
E["npc:craven-drok"] = {t="npc",n="Craven Drok",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Craven Drok keeps to the Cleft of Shadow and seeks travelers for a delicate matter. He wants them to consider how the Alliance sees the Horde.",h="In Orgrimmar, Craven Drok keeps to the Cleft of Shadow and seeks travelers for a delicate matter.",sec={{t="A Skulker in the Shadows",b="Craven Drok avoids Orgrimmar's sunlit avenues and wanders the winding paths beneath the city. The Cleft of Shadow draws warlocks, rogues, and practitioners of less honorable trades. Drok keeps out of sight and hires passersby to handle discreet errands, including one about the Horde's standing with the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Craven Drok?",a="Craven Drok wanders the underground paths of the Cleft of Shadow, beneath Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares.",al={"craven drok location","where is craven drok","drok orgrimmar loc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he called 'Craven'?",a="Craven Drok earns his name by skulking in dark caverns and keeping his head down. He hires others to handle tasks he would rather avoid, against orcish ideals of bravery and martial glory.",al={"why is he craven","craven drok name","is craven drok a coward"},it="name"},{q="What is his involvement with the Alliance?",a="Craven Drok begins Alliance Relations by praising Thrall's wisdom and knowledge of human ways. He sends travelers to Keldran, who works to keep the Alliance from wrongly believing the Horde has made pacts with the Burning Legion.",al={"craven drok alliance","alliance relations drok"},it="side"},{q="Who does Craven Drok send travelers to?",a="Craven Drok sends travelers to Keldran, a student of magic whose hovel lies near Orgrimmar's western exit. With the Warchief's blessing, Keldran works to keep the Horde from being mistaken for an ally of the Burning Legion.",al={"who is keldran","drok contacts"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Craven Drok?",a="Craven Drok is an orc who wanders the subterranean cavern known as the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. Lurking among the warlocks, rogues, and shadowcasters of the city, he offers clandestine tasks to adventurers willing to delve into matters concerning the Alliance.",al={"who is drok","craven drok lore","who craven drok"},it="identity",add="bb25e48e"},{q="Why is Craven Drok in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="The Cleft of Shadow offers privacy and discretion away from the watchful eyes of Thrall's honor guard above. Craven Drok makes his rounds down here where shadowy dealings and sensitive matters regarding Horde intelligence and Alliance relations can be handled quietly.",al={"why is craven drok here","why cleft of shadow craven drok","craven drok location reason"},it="why_here",add="ff4e4871"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may see Craven Drok's habit of lurking in the Cleft of Shadow as a mark against the honor and courage your people prize.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may find the Cleft of Shadow familiar ground, where those who work out of sight gather and make contacts like Drok."},kw={"alliance relations","cleft of shadow","craven drok","orgrimmar"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:1431","topic:alliance"},src={"Craven Drok"}}
E["npc:deino"] = {t="npc",n="Deino",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, Deino trains Horde mages in the arcane arts. She teaches spellcasters to master arcane and elemental forces, and sends seasoned mages across Kalimdor to study ancient magic and seek remote tutors.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, Deino trains Horde mages in the arcane arts.",sec={{t="The Valley's Arcanist",b="Deino trains Horde mages in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. Totems, huts, and quiet waters surround the raised platforms where she teaches. Troll spellcasters balance spiritual reverence with arcane mastery, a path Deino shares with fellow instructors Enyo and Pephredo.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling Arcane Mysteries",b="Deino sends promising mages beyond Durotar to study arcane mysteries. In Ashenvale's corrupted wilds, they gather tainted Waters of Xavian and enchanted hair from the Laughing Sisters. When a student's power outgrows Orgrimmar's instruction, Deino directs them to remote masters, including Tabetha, a hermit sorceress in Dustwallow's swamplands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Deino?",a="Deino stands on raised platforms in the Valley of Spirits, in southwestern Orgrimmar. Fellow troll mage trainers Enyo and Pephredo stand with her.",al={"deino location","where is deino","deino orgrimmar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Deino teach?",a="Deino teaches arcane, fire, and frost spells, portal creation, and essential spell ranks as mages gain experience.",al={"deino trainer","what spells does deino teach"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does Deino send mages to Xavian?",a="Xavian is an ancient city in eastern Ashenvale, now held by satyrs. Its waters are said to hold great magical power, and Deino wants a sample from the bottom of its highest waterfall for study.",al={"waters of xavian quest","why xavian"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the trainers standing with Deino?",a="Enyo and Pephredo stand with Deino. The three share the names of the Graeae sisters of ancient myth and form Orgrimmar's central circle of troll mage mentors.",al={"who is enyo","pephredo","troll mages in valley of spirits"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Deino send mages to Dustwallow Marsh?",a="When a mage grows more skilled, Deino sends them to Tabetha, a powerful, reclusive human hermit deep in Dustwallow Marsh. Tabetha holds specialized arcane secrets.",al={"deino tabetha","journey to the marsh"},it="motive"},{q="Can non-trolls train with Deino?",a="Yes. Horde mages of any race, including trolls, orcs, and Forsaken, can learn class spells and receive guidance from Deino in the Valley of Spirits.",al={"can orcs train with deino","horde mage training"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Who is Deino?",a="Deino is a Darkspear troll mage trainer dwelling within the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar. While arcane study is uncommon among her kin, she has mastered the craft and works alongside her fellow trainers to guide emerging Horde mages in channeling their power responsibly.",al={"who is deino","deino lore","deino troll mage"},it="identity",add="6ebd5023"},{q="Whose side is Deino on?",a="Deino is steadfastly loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed within Orgrimmar, she dedicates her magical expertise to strengthening the Horde's spellcasters so they can better defend their new home.",al={"deino allegiance","deino faction","is deino horde"},it="side",add="c489d76d"},{q="What does Deino want?",a="Deino wants to ensure the Horde's mages are properly disciplined and fully prepared for the perils of Kalimdor. She sends promising practitioners across the world—seeking pure reagents and esoteric wisdom from distant scholars—to refine their craft and temper their arcane abilities.",al={"what does deino want","deino goal","deino purpose"},it="wants",add="d9121d13"},{q="Why is Deino in Orgrimmar?",a="Deino resides in the Valley of Spirits to offer guidance to young troll and Horde spellcasters. Settled in the heart of the Darkspear enclave within Orgrimmar, she provides a reliable source of arcane instruction in an otherwise shamanistic and martial society.",al={"why is deino in orgrimmar","deino valley of spirits","why is deino here"},it="why_here",add="c3103580"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can learn spells and portal magic from Deino in Orgrimmar, then study in Ashenvale and Dustwallow Marsh.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see how the Darkspear combine scholarly arcane magic with the traditions of the Valley of Spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find Deino in Orgrimmar's spiritual district, where she trains the faction's spellcasters alongside its shamans and warlocks."},kw={"deino","laughing sisters","mage trainer","orgrimmar","tabetha","troll mage","valley of spirits","waters of xavian","xavian"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar","quest:1944","quest:1945","npc:tabetha","subzone:xavian","topic:troll","topic:horde"},src={"Deino"}}
E["npc:dirge-quikcleave"] = {t="npc",n="Dirge Quikcleave",z="orgrimmar",s="Inside Gadgetzan's inn, Dirge Quikcleave holds court as a goblin culinary master and vendor. His inventive dishes are renowned across Azeroth, and seasoned chefs come to him to master artisan cooking.",h="Inside Gadgetzan's inn, Dirge Quikcleave holds court as a goblin culinary master and vendor.",sec={{t="Master of the Cleaver",b="In dusty Gadgetzan, Dirge Quikcleave serves drinks and meat to travelers parched by the Tanaris sands. Though his kitchen is in a frontier tavern, he claims to be Azeroth's greatest living culinary artist. Cooking trainers in cities send their most promising students to him when ordinary lessons are spent. Dirge's demanding recipes call for unusual ingredients, from giant clam meat and eggs for his Clamlette creations to exotic beasts from distant shores.",sp=0},{t="Exotic Flavors and Shady Favors",b="Dirge Quikcleave pairs a gourmand's bravado with a goblin's eye for business. Across Kalimdor, he keeps contacts with eccentric figures and seeks out dangerous culinary ventures. Those who bring him fierce beast cuts, such as meat from the monstrous chimaeroks of Feralas's Isle of Dread, can receive hearty recipes fit to sustain champions on perilous journeys. They must not ask too many questions about Dirge's private dealings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dirge Quikcleave?",a="Dirge Quikcleave is a goblin chef and provisioner inside the inn at Gadgetzan, Tanaris. Renowned as one of Azeroth's finest culinary practitioners, he teaches aspiring cooks to hone their craft toward artisan mastery.",al={"dirge quikcleave lore","who is dirge","gadgetzan chef"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Dirge Quikcleave be found?",a="Dirge Quikcleave can be found inside the tavern in Gadgetzan, a Steamwheedle cartel boomtown in the northern dunes of Tanaris.",al={"dirge location","where is dirge quikcleave","dirge inn"},it="place"},{q="Why do cooking trainers send adventurers to him?",a="Cooking trainers in the capital cities can take an apprentice only so far. When a cook reaches an expert threshold, they send them to Dirge in Gadgetzan through 'To Gadgetzan You Go!' to prove their worth and unlock artisan cooking.",al={"why visit dirge","artisan cooking quest","to gadgetzan you go"},it="purpose"},{q="What dishes is Dirge famous for?",a="Dirge Quikcleave is known for Clamlette Surprise, a savory omelet made from giant clam meat and eggs, hearty wolf steaks, and his potent Dirge's Kickin' Chimaerok Chops.",al={"dirge recipes","clamlette surprise","what does dirge cook"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Dirge Quikcleave on?",a="Dirge Quikcleave remains completely neutral, working out of the Steamwheedle Cartel's desert outpost of Gadgetzan. Like most goblins of the trade cartels, he serves anyone whose coin is good, willingly sharing his culinary mastery and peddling food to Alliance and Horde patrons alike.",al={"dirge quikcleave faction","is dirge horde or alliance","who does dirge quikcleave serve"},it="side",add="882c7cf6"},{q="What does Dirge Quikcleave want?",a="Dirge is driven by a passion for extreme and exotic cooking. He seeks rare, unusual meats and fresh ingredients from dangerous corners of the world to craft masterpieces like his famed clamlettes and chimaerok chops, always ready to turn daring harvests into culinary brilliance.",al={"dirge quikcleave goals","what does dirge quikcleave need","why does dirge want ingredients"},it="wants",add="6a938a01"},{q="Why is Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan?",a="Operating out of the bustling inn at Gadgetzan places Dirge right at a major crossroads of daring explorers, monster hunters, and desert travelers. It offers the goblin chef a steady stream of patrons eager for hearty provisions and daring cooks seeking his artisan instruction.",al={"why is dirge in gadgetzan","dirge quikcleave tanaris why","why is dirge here"},it="why_here",add="97163837"},{q="Who is Dirge Quikcleave tied to?",a="Dirge makes his home among the Steamwheedle Cartel goblins of Gadgetzan, serving travelers and desert wayfarers from all walks of life. He also maintains connections with eccentric figures like Narain Soothfancy, who knows where to turn when exotic, high-end dishes are required.",al={"dirge quikcleave associates","who does dirge know","dirge connections"},it="ties",add="60da7b2e"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As an ambitious chef, you can seek Dirge Quikcleave's artisan instruction. He tests your skill with his signature clamlette recipes before granting master status.",["race:Orc"]="As an aspiring Horde gourmand, you are sent straight from Orgrimmar by its trainers to seek Dirge's culinary tutelage in the Tanaris desert."},kw={"artisan cooking","clamlette surprise","cooking trainer","dirge quikcleave","gadgetzan","goblin chef","tanaris"},rel={"quest:6611","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","subzone:isle-of-dread","topic:goblin"},src={"Dirge Quikcleave"}}
E["npc:doras"] = {t="npc",n="Doras",z="orgrimmar",s="Above Orgrimmar, Doras directs the Horde's wind riders across Kalimdor. He oversees the capital's wyverns, sending couriers, scouts, and travelers on their way.",h="Above Orgrimmar, Doras directs the Horde's wind riders across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Master of the Skyway",b="Doras tends the wind riders on a wooden platform above the Valley of Strength. The Horde settled in Durotar, and these clever, leathery-winged beasts became its chief means of communication and travel across Kalimdor. Doras pairs resting mounts with riders and sees that important messages and reinforcements reach distant outposts. Their routes reach the Crossroads, Thunder Bluff, and settlements deep in Ashenvale or Dustwallow Marsh.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Doras?",a="Doras waits atop the flight tower overlooking Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Take the winding ramps up the central timber structures near the city entrance to reach his roost.",al={"doras location","where is orgrimmar flight master","orgrimmar wyvern master"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures does Doras train?",a="Doras manages wind riders, also called wyverns. Native to Kalimdor's arid crags and savannas, these intelligent, venomous winged predators befriended the Horde and carry riders over long distances.",al={"orgrimmar mounts","what does doras fly","what are wind riders"},gp=true},{q="Where can Doras send travelers?",a="Doras sends travelers from Orgrimmar to Horde outposts across central and northern Kalimdor. These include the Crossroads in the Barrens, Thunder Bluff in Mulgore, and military camps in Ashenvale and beyond.",al={"doras flight paths","where can i fly from orgrimmar","orgrimmar flight routes"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Doras?",a="Doras is the primary wind rider master for the Horde in Orgrimmar. Stationed high above the city, he tends to the capital's wyverns and coordinates aerial transit for couriers, soldiers, and adventurers journeying across Kalimdor.",al={"who is doras","doras identity","doras orgrimmar"},it="identity",add="65cae112"},{q="Whose side is Doras on?",a="Doras is loyal to the Horde and serves directly under Warchief Thrall's command in Orgrimmar. He ensures that only trusted allies of the Horde utilize the city's aerial transport network.",al={"doras faction","is doras horde","doras loyalty"},it="side",add="fb843279"},{q="Why is Doras here?",a="As the flight master of the Horde's capital, Doras oversees the central hub of their wind rider network. He remains stationed in Orgrimmar to provide vital transit links between the seat of the Warchief and outposts throughout Durotar, the Barrens, and beyond.",al={"why is doras in orgrimmar","doras role","doras purpose here"},it="why_here",add="54873cb0"},{q="What does Doras want?",a="Doras focuses on the care of his wind riders and maintaining reliable courier and travel lines throughout Kalimdor. He seeks to keep communications and reinforcements moving swiftly wherever the Horde's interests are contested.",al={"what does doras want","doras motives","doras goal"},it="wants",add="f6504325"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you can rely on Doras for swift flights from the capital to allied settlements across Kalimdor."},kw={"doras","flight master","orgrimmar","valley of strength","wind rider master","wyvern"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","quest:6385","quest:6386","topic:horde","subzone:crossroads","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Doras"}}
E["npc:eitrigg"] = {t="npc",n="Eitrigg",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Eitrigg stands beside Warchief Thrall as a trusted advisor. A veteran of the First and Second Wars, he left the Blackrock clan’s Horde after its defeat and lived in exile. Now he helps Thrall guide the New Horde toward honor and shamanism.",h="In Orgrimmar, Eitrigg stands beside Warchief Thrall as a trusted advisor.",sec={{t="A Veteran of the Old Horde",b="Born on Draenor among the Blackrock clan, Eitrigg fought for the Horde in the First and Second Wars. The battles and the Horde’s defeat in the second war forced him to face how far his people had fallen into bloodlust and demonic corruption. Sickened by what the Horde had become, he left its scattered remnants and sought solitude in the wilds of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Blood and Honor",b="During his exile, Eitrigg sheltered in an abandoned tower near Hearthglen. The human paladin Tirion Fordring found him, and their clash brought the tower’s ruins down around them. Eitrigg pulled the unconscious human to safety instead of finishing him. Moved by this act of martial honor, Tirion swore friendship and kept the hermit’s location secret. The local Alliance authorities eventually captured Eitrigg and sentenced him to hang in Stratholme. Tirion cast aside his knighthood, lands, and freedom to attack the city and rescue him. Their bond showed both warriors that honor could cross the hatred between their peoples.",sp=0},{t="Counselor to the Warchief",b="In Stratholme, Thrall’s newly united Horde raided the city during Tirion’s attempt to free Eitrigg and carried the aging warrior away. Meeting Thrall convinced Eitrigg that the orcs were casting off demonic corruption and returning to their ancestral shamanic heritage. He crossed the Great Sea with Thrall to Kalimdor and took a revered place in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Wisdom. Now Eitrigg advises the young Warchief inside Grommash Hold. He helps evaluate new recruits and shares the wisdom he earned, so the New Horde does not repeat the tragedies of the past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eitrigg?",a="Eitrigg is an elderly Blackrock orc warrior and veteran of the First and Second Wars. He now resides in Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, advising Warchief Thrall.",al={"who is eitrigg","eitrigg lore","orc standing by thrall"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Eitrigg consider a human his brother?",a="In exile in Lordaeron, Eitrigg saved the paladin Tirion Fordring when their duel brought down a stone tower. Tirion kept Eitrigg’s location secret and later fought his own people in Stratholme to prevent his execution, giving up his title and lands. Their shared honor made them brothers.",al={"eitrigg and tirion","eitrigg human friend","blood and honor"},it="ties"},{q="What clan does Eitrigg belong to?",a="Eitrigg belongs to the Blackrock clan. He fought in the old wars, then abandoned the Horde’s corrupt remnants after seeing their demonic corruption.",al={"eitrigg clan","is eitrigg blackrock"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Eitrigg leave the old Horde?",a="After the Horde’s defeat in the Second War, Eitrigg saw that bloodlust and demonic corruption had stripped his people of honor. He left in disgust, seeking a quiet place to die rather than serve a corrupt war machine.",al={"why did eitrigg leave","eitrigg exile"},it="history"},{q="How did Eitrigg end up in Orgrimmar?",a="When Alliance forces captured Eitrigg and prepared to execute him in Stratholme, Thrall’s forces raided the city and freed him. Eitrigg saw Thrall’s commitment to honor and the return to shamanism, then chose to follow him to Kalimdor.",al={"how did eitrigg meet thrall","eitrigg rescued"},it="why_here"},{q="What role does Eitrigg play in Orgrimmar right now?",a="In Grommash Hold, Eitrigg advises Thrall and helps test and evaluate recruits who swear loyalty to the New Horde.",al={"eitrigg quest","what does eitrigg do"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Eitrigg on?",a="Eitrigg is fully dedicated to Thrall's new Horde. Though he once fought for the old bloodthirsty Horde, he abandoned it after seeing the corruption behind its demonic crusade. Today, he stands beside Thrall in Grommash Hold as a loyal advisor and guardian, believing in this new shamanistic vision of honor and redemption for the orcish people.",al={"eitrigg faction","who does eitrigg serve","is eitrigg loyal to thrall"},it="side",add="53b3cb4d"},{q="What does Eitrigg want?",a="Eitrigg wants to see the orcish race guide itself with honor rather than repeating the dark mistakes of their past. After witnessing the deceit of the Shadow Council and living in exile, he now dedicates his remaining years to advising Warchief Thrall and preparing a disciplined, principled new generation of Horde warriors to safeguard their home.",al={"what are eitrigg goals","eitrigg motive","what does eitrigg hope for"},it="wants",add="f3c80f4d"},{q="Why is Eitrigg famous?",a="Eitrigg is renowned among veterans as a Blackrock warrior who fought through both the First and Second Wars. His survival, his dramatic rescue from execution in Stratholme, and his profound bond of honor with the human paladin Tirion Fordring have cemented his place in legend.",al={"why is eitrigg well known","what made eitrigg famous","eitrigg history war"},it="fame",add="46467f44"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Eitrigg as its living memory. He stands beside Thrall to help keep the mistakes of the demon-tainted past from being repeated.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can see in Eitrigg martial honor preserved through decades of tragedy. He survived two wars through strength and unbroken discipline.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you know the story of Eitrigg and Tirion Fordring as a renowned test of duty and righteous honor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc of Durotar, you can look to Eitrigg as a revered elder. His Blackrock heritage shows that any orc can embrace honor and redeem their people’s legacy."},kw={"blackrock clan","blood and honor","eitrigg","grommash hold","hearthglen","orgrim doomhammer","orgrimmar","stratholme","thrall","tirion fordring"},rel={"npc:thrall","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:new-horde","zone:orgrimmar","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:stratholme"},src={"Eitrigg"}}
E["npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"] = {t="npc",n="Gan'rul Bloodeye",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye trains warlocks beneath the city. In the Cleft of Shadow, Horde initiates learn darker demonic rites and how to bend voidwalkers and succubi to their will.",h="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye trains warlocks beneath the city.",sec={{t="A Master in the Shadows",b="Warlocks study out of sight in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. Warchief Thrall tolerates them in the new Horde, though Durotar's open sunlight is no place for their dark arts. The cavern gives shadow weavers, rogues, and fel casters room to study unmolested. From there, Gan'rul teaches rising practitioners of fel magic.",sp=0},{t="Binding the Nether",b="Ambitious warlocks come to Gan'rul to learn dangerous summoning rites. Those seeking to bind a greater demon, such as a resilient voidwalker or a seductive succubus, must secure ritual components and learn the precise incantations. The summoned creature must be dominated before it consumes its master.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye trains orc warlocks in Orgrimmar. He mentors novice and intermediate Horde warlocks in summoning and binding demons from the Twisting Nether.",al={"gan'rul bloodeye","who is ganrul","ganrul bloodeye role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Find Gan'rul in the Cleft of Shadow, a cavern network beneath Orgrimmar. He is among fellow dark practitioners, away from the city's main thoroughfares.",al={"ganrul location","where is gan'rul bloodeye","where is cleft of shadow trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are warlocks hidden in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Warlocks practice in the Cleft of Shadow because Warchief Thrall and the new Horde's shamanistic society distrust fel magic and demonic corruption after the orcs' past enslavement. The Horde permits warlocks for their utility, but keeps their practice in the shadows to prevent civic unrest.",al={"why in caves","why hide warlocks","cleft of shadow lore"},it="why_here"},{q="What demons does Gan'rul help summon?",a="Gan'rul guides warlocks in rituals to summon and subjugate voidwalkers and succubi. Completing his tasks proves a summoner has the will to control these fiends.",al={"demons ganrul teaches","ganrul demon quests","voidwalker succubus trainer"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Gan'rul have any known family?",a="Gan'rul shares a surname with Halga Bloodeye, but their precise relationship is not openly documented.",al={"gan'rul relatives","halga bloodeye relative"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Strahad, whom Gan'rul mentions?",a="Strahad Farsan is an accomplished warlock living in the Barrens near the Ratchet hills. Gan'rul sends promising students to him for more advanced instruction and greater challenges.",al={"seeking strahad","who is strahad","strahad quest"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Gan'rul Bloodeye on?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye serves the Horde, training practitioners of dark magic beneath Thrall's capital. Though warlocks are regarded with deep suspicion by the shamanistic leadership, Gan'rul aligns his arcane craft with the survival and strength of the Horde, mentoring those willing to harness fel powers in its defense.",al={"gan'rul bloodeye faction","ganrul allegiance","who does gan'rul serve"},it="side",add="11e29292"},{q="What does Gan'rul Bloodeye want?",a="Gan'rul seeks to expand the ranks of capable Horde warlocks by testing initiates and teaching them mastery over the Nether. He demands discipline and occult focus, guiding apprentices to bind dangerous demonic entities such as voidwalkers and succubi so that dark magic serves as an obedient weapon rather than a consuming threat.",al={"gan'rul goals","what does ganrul want","gan'rul purpose"},it="wants",add="67b7b1ae"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock seeking forbidden knowledge, you can learn from Gan'rul in Kalimdor and face the trials needed to bind voidwalkers and succubi.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how fel magic is used for military strength while its practitioners remain confined to the capital's underground recesses."},kw={"bloodeye","cleft of shadow","gan'rul","orgrimmar","succubus","trainer","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:1506","quest:1473","quest:1471","quest:1472","quest:1798","npc:carendin-halgar"},src={"Gan'rul Bloodeye"}}
E["npc:great-father-winter"] = {t="npc",n="Great-father Winter",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Great-father Winter hears children's wishes during the Feast of Winter Veil. Hired by Smokywood Pastures, he brings holiday cheer near Grommash Hold in the Valley of Strength, though the work wears on him.",h="In Orgrimmar, Great-father Winter hears children's wishes during the Feast of Winter Veil.",sec={{t="A Hired Myth",b="Greatfather Winter in the Valley of Strength is an orc performer hired by the Smokywood Pastures merchant company. Ancient lore tells of a majestic elemental spirit who wanders the land, bringing snow and seasonal renewal, but the figure in Orgrimmar promotes company wares and entertains Horde children. Some critics say the commercial mascot cheapens genuine seasonal traditions. Still, few deny the festive excitement he brings to the city streets.",sp=0},{t="Shift Work in the Valley of Strength",b="Greatfather Winter works outside Grommash Hold, beneath decorated evergreens. Children climb onto his lap to tell him what gifts they want, while he promotes Smokywood Pastures discounts and offers holiday greetings. The long shift wears him down. He admits he keeps festive spirits in his pack to quiet the noise when work ends, and visiting adventurers bring him snacks to help him endure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is this the real Greatfather Winter?",a="No. An ordinary orc hired by Smokywood Pastures dresses as the legendary Winter Veil figure and hands out holiday promotions in Orgrimmar.",al={"is he real","who is great-father winter","is he an actor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Great-father Winter in Orgrimmar?",a="Find Great-father Winter in the Valley of Strength, just outside Grommash Hold, by the Feast of Winter Veil tree and holiday stalls.",al={"great-father winter location","where is great father winter","where to find winter orc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does he do during the Feast of Winter Veil?",a="He entertains holiday-goers, listens to children's gift requests, gives out Smokywood Pastures promotional tasks, and hands out festive presents under the tree when the holiday peaks.",al={"what does he do","great-father winter purpose","winter veil quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does he want gingerbread cookies and milk?",a="Loud crowds and children taking turns on his lap leave him drained. He asks for gingerbread cookies and milk to keep his energy up through the shift.",al={"treats for great father winter","why milk and cookies","gingerbread quest"},it="wants"},{q="What does he think of his job?",a="The performance feels tedious and draining to him. He grumbles about eager children, rushes through company slogans, and counts the minutes until he can drink from a bottle of cheer in his bag.",al={"does he like his job","great-father winter quotes","is he drunk"},it="motive"},{q="Does the Alliance have an equivalent figure?",a="Yes. The Alliance's Greatfather Winter is an elderly dwarf employed by Smokywood Pastures, near the holiday tree in the Commons of Ironforge.",al={"alliance greatfather","ironforge santa","alliance counterpart"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Great-father Winter on?",a="This Great-father Winter is an orc working strictly within Orgrimmar for the Horde, though his ultimate employer is Smokywood Pastures. The goblin enterprise hired him to bring holiday cheer—and drive festive consumer spending—to the Valley of Strength. While he wears the festive red suit of legend, his true allegiance lies with his paycheck and surviving his grueling shift.",al={"is great-father winter horde","greatfather winter faction","who does great-father winter work for"},it="side",add="1d43ce2e"},{q="Why is Great-father Winter here?",a="He is stationed outside Grommash Hold because Smokywood Pastures hired him to anchor their Feast of Winter Veil celebrations in the Horde capital. The mercantile goblins set him up to entertain the city's youngsters, listen to their gift wishes, and steer eager families toward holiday merchandise and festive treats.",al={"why is great-father winter in orgrimmar","what brought greatfather winter here","reason great-father winter is here"},it="why_here",add="796ea74c"},{q="Who is Great-father Winter tied to?",a="He is directly employed by Smokywood Pastures, the enterprising goblin venture responsible for marketing the Feast of Winter Veil across the realm. They supply his festive costume, set his promotional scripts, and organize the gifts and treats he hands out around Grommash Hold.",al={"who hired great-father winter","greatfather winter connections","smokywood pastures great father winter"},it="ties",add="f14772a5"},{q="Why is Great-father Winter famous?",a="He claims the name and guise of Greatfather Winter, an ancient supernatural figure celebrated across Azeroth for heralding the turning of the seasons. While scholars argue this costumed orc is merely a commercial mascot, children and festive revelers still flock to him as the living face of Winter Veil cheer.",al={"why do people know great father winter","is greatfather winter legendary","great father winter reputation"},it="fame",add="826ac72e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, he is the seasonal figurehead in Orgrimmar, offering festival gifts and tasks for Smokywood Pastures.",["profession:Cooking"]="Chefs can bake gingerbread cookies with festive holiday recipes and bring them with milk to Great-father Winter to restore his spirits.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, seeing one of your own reduced to a costumed mascot selling vendor discounts can test a traditionalist's patience, even though orcs revere seasonal shifts and the elements."},kw={"gingerbread cookies","great-father winter","greatfather winter","orgrimmar","smokywood pastures","valley of strength","winter veil"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","subzone:grommash-hold","quest:6962","quest:6984","quest:8827","npc:greatfather-winter","topic:horde"},src={"Great-father Winter"}}
E["npc:grunt-dogran"] = {t="npc",n="Grunt Dogran",z="orgrimmar",s="Grunt Dogran waits in captivity deep in the southern Barrens. Once assigned to the Crossroads and then Camp Taurajo, he was taken during a patrol into Agama'gor.",h="Grunt Dogran waits in captivity deep in the southern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Grunt's Duty",b="Grunt Dogran was sent from the Crossroads to reinforce Camp Taurajo after rising in the Horde military. He led a detachment of grunts into Agama'gor, where they met the Bristleback quilboar in a fierce clash. Dogran was badly wounded and crippled. His comrades retreated without him, and the quilboar dragged him into captivity.",sp=0},{t="An Honorable Fate",b="Grunt Dogran remains trapped behind enemy lines, crippled by his wounds. He refuses to return home broken and make his mate care for an invalid. Instead, he asks for a final stand against the quilboar and for a token of his devotion to reach the one he loves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Grunt Dogran located?",a="Dogran is held captive at Agama'gor, a dense quilboar encampment in the southern Barrens, just north of Camp Taurajo.",al={"dogran location","where is dogran","find dogran barrens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was Dogran captured by the quilboar?",a="Dogran was captured after he led a patrol from Camp Taurajo to strike at the quilboar and suffered crippling injuries in the clash. His comrades could not carry him away in time, leaving him in their hands.",al={"why was dogran captured","how did dogran get caught"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Dogran refuse to be rescued?",a="Dogran was permanently crippled in battle and refuses to return home as a burden to his mate. He would rather die fighting the quilboar than live as an invalid.",al={"why wont dogran leave","dogran rescue"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="Who is looking for Dogran?",a="His mate Zankaja in Orgrimmar is looking for him after hearing nothing since he left for duty. Her worry leads travelers to Gazrog at the Crossroads, then to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo, where soldiers piece together what happened to the missing patrol.",al={"who sent me for dogran","dogran quest giver"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Grunt Dogran?",a="Grunt Dogran is an orc soldier of the Horde. After earning a promotion, he was stationed at the Crossroads before transferring to Camp Taurajo. While leading a detachment of grunts into the southern Barrens to confront the quilboar, he was severely crippled in combat and captured by the bristled beasts, who now hold him bound in their encampment at Agama'gor.",al={"who is dogran","grunt dogran identity","dogran lore"},it="identity",add="3efd280a"},{q="Whose side is Grunt Dogran on?",a="Dogran is a loyal soldier of the Horde. He proudly serves as a grunt under the command of the Warchief, stationed in the Barrens to defend Horde outposts and settlements from hostile forces like the Razormane and Bristleback quilboar.",al={"is dogran horde","dogran allegiance","dogran faction"},it="side",add="30754355"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Dogran reflects the belief that dying in battle brings more honor than surviving as a helpless invalid.",["faction:Horde"]="Dogran's capture shows the cost the Horde garrisons pay to secure trade roads and borders across the Barrens against aggressive quilboar tribes."},kw={"agama'gor","barrens","camp taurajo","crossroads","dogran","dorgran","grunt dogran","quilboar"},rel={"quest:1509","quest:1515","quest:1512","subzone:agama-gor","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Grunt Dogran"}}
E["npc:grunth"] = {t="npc",n="Grunth",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Grunth eagerly seeks the company of Horde champions. The young orc lives in the Drag orphanage and, during Children's Week, journeys across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms to learn what it means to be a hero.",h="In Orgrimmar, Grunth eagerly seeks the company of Horde champions.",sec={{t="A Curious Child of the Horde",b="Grunth is a young orc orphan in the Drag of Orgrimmar, where Orphan Matron Battlewail cares for him. Raised in Durotar's harsh red wastes, he watches armored adventurers with awe and asks them questions without end. Are armored warriors truly terrifying? Why does lightning on water not kill every fish? Will he ever see someone fight an actual dragon?",sp=0},{t="Children's Week Journeys",b="During Children's Week, an Orcish Orphan Whistle summons Grunth to travel with adventurers on a tour across the world. He wants to meet High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Mulgore, see the ruined throne room of Lordaeron, and visit the rugged frontiers where his people fight for their future.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grunth?",a="Grunth is an orc child at the Orgrimmar orphanage in the Drag. Orphan Matron Battlewail cares for him, and he dreams of becoming a legendary hero of the Horde.",al={"grunth npc","orc orphan","orgrimmar orphan"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Grunth be found?",a="Grunth lives with the other orphans in the Drag of Orgrimmar. During Children's Week, an Orcish Orphan Whistle from Orphan Matron Battlewail can summon him anywhere.",al={"grunth location","where is grunth","find grunth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What places does Grunth want to visit?",a="Grunth wants to see the great places and figures of the Horde. He asks to visit High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff, see the Ratchet docks, and travel to the ruined throne room of Lordaeron.",al={"grunth quests","what does the orphan want","grunth tour"},it="wants"},{q="What kind of personality does Grunth have?",a="Grunth is loud, curious, and full of imagination. He asks adventurers strange questions, like what “zug zug” means and whether a wingless fly is called a walk, and even mentions shoving a rock up his nose.",al={"grunth quotes","grunth dialogue","what does grunth say"}},{q="Whose side is Grunth on?",a="Grunth belongs wholly to the Horde. Raised in Orgrimmar under the care of Orphan Matron Battlewail, he looks up to the champions of the Horde and dreams of witnessing mighty deeds, like watching a hero battle a ferocious dragon.",al={"grunth horde or alliance","is grunth horde","grunth faction"},it="side",add="ec5570c7"},{q="Why is Grunth in Orgrimmar?",a="Grunth is an orcish orphan living under the care of the Orgrimmar orphanage in the Drag. During Children's Week, he is allowed out to explore the world alongside a seasoned Horde adventurer who answers his eager questions and shows him the wider realm.",al={"why is grunth here","why is grunth in orgrimmar","grunth location why"},it="why_here",add="06889c57"},{q="Who is Grunth tied to?",a="Grunth is cared for by Orphan Matron Battlewail at the orphanage in Orgrimmar. She looks after the young orc and entrusts him to Horde adventurers willing to mentor him and take him on travels across Kalimdor and beyond.",al={"who takes care of grunth","grunth ties","grunth orphan matron"},it="ties",add="0a265be0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, guiding Grunth during Children's Week shows you a generation born into freedom rather than demonic servitude, and what your faction strives to protect.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Grunth reflects Durotar's youth, raised with tribal honor and the demands of survival rather than the dark lethargy of the internment camps."},kw={"children's week","grunth","orc orphan","orgrimmar","orphan matron battlewail","orphan whistle","the drag"},rel={"npc:orphan-matron-battlewail","subzone:drag","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Grunth"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-gryshka"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Gryshka",z="orgrimmar",s="At the Broken Tusk in Orgrimmar, Innkeeper Gryshka welcomes travelers with food, drink, and a hearthstone binding. She keeps the inn supplied with meat from hunters across Durotar and the Barrens.",h="At the Broken Tusk in Orgrimmar, Innkeeper Gryshka welcomes travelers with food, drink, and a hearthstone...",sec={{t="Hearth of the Valley of Strength",b="Innkeeper Gryshka welcomes travelers at the Broken Tusk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. The inn stands just beyond the city's main gates, where warriors, messengers, and newcomers to Thrall's Horde can find shelter.",sp=0},{t="A Taste for Fresh Meat",b="Gryshka keeps the Broken Tusk's kitchen supplied with fresh meat. Trusted hunters across Horde lands send her game, including Zargh at the Crossroads and Grimtak in Durotar, who ship their finest cuts to the inn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Innkeeper Gryshka?",a="Innkeeper Gryshka welcomes Horde travelers at the Broken Tusk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. She binds hearthstones and sells food and drink.",al={"who is gryshka","gryshka orgrimmar","innkeeper broken tusk"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Innkeeper Gryshka be found?",a="You can find Innkeeper Gryshka inside the Broken Tusk in the Valley of Strength, the first major district beyond Orgrimmar's main southern gates.",al={"where is gryshka","broken tusk inn location","valley of strength innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Gryshka get her meat supplies?",a="Gryshka gets meat from hunters across Horde lands, including Zargh at the Crossroads in the Barrens and Grimtak in Durotar, who send her game cuts.",al={"gryshka food sources","who supplies the broken tusk","zargh meat delivery"}},{q="What services does Gryshka provide?",a="Gryshka can bind your hearthstone to the Broken Tusk, letting you return directly to Orgrimmar. She also sells food, bread, and drink to restore health and mana.",al={"can i bind my hearthstone here","broken tusk hearthstone","gryshka vendor items"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Gryshka have any connection to the wind rider roost?",a="Travelers sent on flight errands from the Barrens often bring packages to Gryshka before heading up to Doras, the wind rider master on the mesa above the city.",al={"doras quest","wind rider master broken tusk","ride to orgrimmar inn"},it="ties"},{q="What kind of personality does Gryshka have?",a="Gryshka is a practical, hearty host who likes good meat, direct talk, and a well-stocked, orderly tavern for the Horde warriors passing through the capital.",al={"is gryshka friendly","what is gryshka like"}},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Gryshka on?",a="Gryshka is a loyal daughter of the Horde. Operating within the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar, she caters directly to the warriors, hunters, and travelers who serve Warchief Thrall, ensuring they find respite and hearty sustenance under the Horde's banner.",al={"gryshka faction","who does gryshka serve","is gryshka horde"},it="side",add="ad24947b"},{q="What does Innkeeper Gryshka want?",a="Above all else, Gryshka wants to keep the Broken Tusk well-provisioned and lively. She possesses a legendary appetite for quality meat, constantly relying on friends across Durotar and the Barrens to deliver fresh, choice cuts to satisfy herself and her hungry patrons.",al={"what does gryshka want","gryshka goals","what is gryshka looking for"},it="wants",add="f36e4eb0"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Gryshka here?",a="Gryshka manages the Broken Tusk, the bustling inn at the very heart of Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. She remains here to offer hospitality, food, strong drink, and shelter to travelers passing through the capital or returning from the harsh wilderness.",al={"why is gryshka in orgrimmar","why is gryshka at broken tusk","gryshka purpose"},it="why_here",add="edbe4e1f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler arriving in Durotar, you can bind your hearthstone and resupply at Gryshka's inn in the Valley of Strength before heading deeper into Kalimdor.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can value Gryshka's care in sourcing prime cuts from hunters as far away as the Barrens."},kw={"broken tusk","doras","gryshka","hearthstone","innkeeper","orgrimmar","valley of strength","zargh"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:orgrimmar","npc:zargh","npc:doras","quest:6384","quest:6385","topic:horde"},src={"Innkeeper Gryshka"}}
E["npc:kaplak"] = {t="npc",n="Kaplak",z="orgrimmar",s="In Razor Hill, Kaplak trains young orc and troll rogues for the Horde. He teaches stealth, subterfuge, and bladecraft before sending them to Orgrimmar.",h="In Razor Hill, Kaplak trains young orc and troll rogues for the Horde.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Shadows",b="Kaplak trains new Horde rogues in Razor Hill. Orcish custom favors open combat and roaring charges, but he teaches the quieter skills needed to survive: stalking unseen, picking locks, and striking from behind. When his students outgrow his training in Durotar's dusty red ravines, he sends them north to Orgrimmar, where senior guild operatives can deepen their craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaplak?",a="Kaplak is an orc rogue trainer in Razor Hill, Durotar. He trains young orc and troll rogues from the Valley of Trials in early rogue skills, then sends them to higher trainers in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is kaplak","kaplak lore","kaplak razor hill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kaplak be found?",a="Kaplak can be found in Razor Hill, the central settlement of Durotar. He is usually resting in or around the local barracks with other class trainers.",al={"where is kaplak","kaplak location","find kaplak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Kaplak offer?",a="Kaplak guides rogue adventurers toward advanced trainers and assignments. He may send them to find Therzok in Orgrimmar.",al={"kaplak quests","quests from kaplak"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kaplak on?",a="Kaplak is loyal to the Horde and serves the orcs of Durotar. Stationed in Razor Hill, he guides the fledgling stalkers and scouts of Thrall's realm, honing their abilities so they can defend orcish lands from centaur raids, Kul Tiras infiltrators, and any other threats to the growing nation.",al={"kaplak faction","kaplak alliance or horde","who does kaplak serve"},it="side",add="c5a92913"},{q="Why is Kaplak in Razor Hill?",a="Kaplak is stationed in Razor Hill to train young orcs and trolls who practice the subtle arts of stealth, poisoning, and ambush. As recruits venture out from the Valley of Trials, he sharpens their rogue crafts before sending capable scouts forward to the capital city of Orgrimmar.",al={"why is kaplak here","kaplak purpose durotar","what is kaplak doing in razor hill"},it="why_here",add="d6e62700"},{q="What does Kaplak want?",a="Kaplak seeks to strengthen the ranks of the Horde's rogues. He looks for cunning, discipline, and swift blades among the newly arrived recruits, directing promising scouts onward to senior mentors like Therzok in Orgrimmar once their preliminary training is complete.",al={"kaplak motives","kaplak goals","what does kaplak need"},it="wants",add="044206c1"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a young orc or troll rogue leaving the Valley of Trials, you can learn your first trade from Kaplak before he directs you to the covert networks in Orgrimmar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can count on Kaplak to train scouts, spies, and assassins who guard Durotar and work beyond ordinary battle lines."},kw={"durotar","kaplak","orc","orgrimmar","razor hill","rogue trainer","stealth","therzok"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:1859","quest:2380","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Kaplak"}}
E["npc:kaymard-copperpinch"] = {t="npc",n="Kaymard Copperpinch",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Kaymard Copperpinch sells Smokywood Pastures goods for Winter Veil. He trades in the Valley of Strength, where travelers can find festive wares and help with holiday troubles.",h="In Orgrimmar, Kaymard Copperpinch sells Smokywood Pastures goods for Winter Veil.",sec={{t="A Goblin's Winter Veil",b="Kaymard Copperpinch brings Smokywood Pastures to the Valley of Strength each Feast of Winter Veil. Great-father Winter receives visitors nearby as Kaymard sells fine treats, festive wrapping paper, and other holiday goods. To a goblin, no grand festival is complete without a lively exchange of coin.",sp=0},{t="Holiday Complications",b="Kaymard also handles troubles that threaten Smokywood Pastures during the festival. Holiday confections go missing, and Metzen the Reindeer disappears. Kaymard calls on Horde adventurers to solve these problems and keep Winter Veil running smoothly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaymard Copperpinch?",a="Kaymard Copperpinch is a goblin merchant with Smokywood Pastures. During the Feast of Winter Veil, he trades in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, selling fine seasonal goods and asking passersby to help with holiday troubles.",al={"who is kaymard","kaymard copperpinch lore","what does kaymard do"},it="identity"},{q="What is Smokywood Pastures?",a="Smokywood Pastures is a vendor consortium that supplies food, treats, and seasonal goods for the Feast of Winter Veil across Azeroth. It supplies both the Horde and the Alliance, and turns a tidy profit.",al={"what is smokywood pastures","who does he work for","smokywood pastures lore"},it="ties"},{q="Where can I find Kaymard Copperpinch?",a="Kaymard Copperpinch stands in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, near the central festival display where Great-father Winter sits during the Feast of Winter Veil.",al={"kaymard location","where is kaymard copperpinch","where is he in orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="Why does he ask adventurers for help during the holidays?",a="Smokywood Pastures faces troubles during Winter Veil, including stolen holiday sweets and the kidnapping of its prized reindeer, Metzen. Kaymard hires willing adventurers to recover the stolen goods and Metzen, and protect the season's profits.",al={"kaymard quests","winter veil treats quest","metzen quest horde"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Kaymard Copperpinch on?",a="Kaymard works exclusively for Smokywood Pastures, a goblin commercial enterprise. While he sets up his holiday shop in the heart of Orgrimmar to serve Horde patrons and cater to the Feast of Winter Veil, his true loyalty lies with the company and the pursuit of honest profit rather than the politics of the Horde.",al={"kaymard copperpinch faction","is kaymard horde","who does kaymard work for"},it="side",add="10a0163d"},{q="Why is Kaymard Copperpinch here?",a="Kaymard has set up shop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength to celebrate the Feast of Winter Veil. Smokywood Pastures deploys merchants to major capitals every holiday season to sell treats, wrapping paper, recipes, and seasonal specialty wares to festive citizens.",al={"why is kaymard in orgrimmar","what is kaymard doing here","kaymard orgrimmar purpose"},it="why_here",add="699a38fb"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Kaymard brings Winter Veil's trade to Orgrimmar, where goblin enterprise joins the traditional winter celebrations.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can find seasonal recipes and specialty ingredients for traditional holiday treats through Kaymard and his Smokywood Pastures associates."},kw={"copperpinch","goblin","kaymard","metzen","orgrimmar","smokywood pastures","valley of strength","winter veil"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:orgrimmar","npc:great-father-winter","quest:6984","topic:horde"},src={"Kaymard Copperpinch"}}
E["npc:keldran"] = {t="npc",n="Keldran",z="orgrimmar",s="North of the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar, Keldran works to clear a path toward peace with the Alliance. He directs covert strikes against demonic remnants, hoping to show that the modern Horde has forsaken the Burning Legion.",h="North of the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar, Keldran works to clear a path toward peace with the Alliance.",sec={{t="A Diplomatic Crusade",b="Keldran works from Orgrimmar’s red rock terraces while Thrall governs from the Valley of Wisdom. The Alliance still sees all orcs as bloodthirsty puppets of demonic masters, a reputation forged during the first wars. Keldran believes Thrall is weary of endless conflict, but peace talks cannot begin while demon-worshiping cults endure in Kalimdor. Without the Warchief’s formal sanction, he takes the initiative himself. He directs trusted agents toward distant threats, hoping to erase the demonic stain and clear the way for diplomacy.",sp=0},{t="The War in Desolace",b="In Desolace, Keldran has sent Takata Steelblade and Maurin Bonesplitter to lead operations against demonic infestations. Their chief target is the Burning Blade cult. Keldran hopes to eradicate these practitioners and bring proof back to Orgrimmar, showing the Alliance that the new Horde stands against the Legion alongside humans and night elves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Keldran?",a="Keldran works north of the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar, organizing efforts against demonic influence to open a path toward diplomacy with the Alliance.",al={"who is keldran","keldran lore","keldran npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Keldran care about relations with the Alliance?",a="Keldran believes Thrall is growing weary of constant war with the Alliance. Peace talks cannot begin while the Alliance thinks the Horde remains allied with the Burning Legion.",al={"why alliance relations","keldran motives","why does he want peace"},it="wants"},{q="Is Keldran acting under Thrall's official orders?",a="No. Keldran acts without formal authorization from Warchief Thrall, seeking to clear the Horde’s name and prepare the way for peace.",al={"did thrall send keldran","thrall orders keldran","is keldran sanctioned"},it="side"},{q="What is Keldran doing in Desolace?",a="Keldran sent Takata Steelblade and Maurin Bonesplitter to Desolace to fight demonic forces, with special emphasis on wiping out the Burning Blade cultists.",al={"desolace operation","why desolace","keldran burning blade"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Keldran tied to?",a="Keldran works alongside loyal Horde operatives who share his vision of peace. To execute his strategy against demon worshippers in Desolace, he relies on Takata Steelblade and Maurin Bonesplitter, directing them to strike at the demonic menace and scour the Burning Blade from the region.",al={"keldran allies","who does keldran work with","keldran associates"},it="ties",add="b49902f3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Keldran represents a forward-thinking part of the Horde that sees the need to shed its demonic reputation to secure lasting peace on Kalimdor.",["class:Warlock"]="Keldran’s covert war against the Burning Blade shows how strongly the Horde’s leadership wants to distance itself from uncontrolled demonic corruption."},kw={"alliance relations","burning blade","desolace","keldran","maurin bonesplitter","orgrimmar","takata steelblade","valley of spirits"},rel={"quest:1431","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar","npc:takata-steelblade","npc:maurin-bonesplitter","zone:desolace","npc:thrall","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Keldran"}}
E["npc:ogunaro-wolfrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Ogunaro Wolfrunner",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar’s Valley of Honor, Ogunaro Wolfrunner tends the Horde’s foremost wolf kennel beside the Hunter’s Hall. He breeds and trains fierce wolves for orc champions and their trusted allies.",h="In Orgrimmar’s Valley of Honor, Ogunaro Wolfrunner tends the Horde’s foremost wolf kennel beside the Hunter’s...",sec={{t="Master of the Pack",b="Ogunaro Wolfrunner tends Orgrimmar’s battle wolves beside the Hunter’s Hall in the Valley of Honor. Orcs and wolves have shared a bond for generations, across Draenor’s plains and Durotar’s wilderness. It rests on mutual respect, not simple domestication. Ogunaro entrusts only the hardiest beasts, from dire wolves to agile timber prowlers, to warriors who have proven their strength and worth to the warchief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ogunaro Wolfrunner?",a="Ogunaro Wolfrunner is the Horde’s foremost wolf breeder and mount vendor, found outside the Hunter’s Hall in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Honor.",al={"ogunaro","wolf vendor orgrimmar","orc mount vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Can anyone purchase a wolf from him?",a="Orcs can acquire wolves through their heritage once properly trained. Other Horde members must earn exalted standing and Orgrimmar’s utmost trust before Ogunaro parts with a wolf.",al={"can non orcs buy wolves","wolf mount rep requirements"},gp=true},{q="What kinds of wolves does he provide?",a="Ogunaro provides black, brown, dire, and timber wolves, along with swift, armored breeds suited to veterans of war.",al={"types of wolf mounts","which wolves does ogunaro sell"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Ogunaro Wolfrunner on?",a="Ogunaro Wolfrunner is entirely loyal to the Horde and the city of Orgrimmar. He tends to the Horde's prized riding wolves in the Valley of Honor, providing mounts directly to his fellow orcs and those who have earned the deep trust and exalted respect of Orgrimmar.",al={"ogunaro wolfrunner faction","who does ogunaro serve","ogunaro horde alliance"},it="side",add="37d9a7a8"},{q="Why is Ogunaro Wolfrunner here in the Valley of Honor?",a="Ogunaro makes his home in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, right outside the Hunter's Hall. This quarter serves as the training and gathering grounds for the Horde's fiercest warriors and hunters, making it the natural place to stable, breed, and offer hardy war wolves to proven champions.",al={"why is ogunaro in orgrimmar","ogunaro wolfrunner location","why is ogunaro here"},it="why_here",add="c9c48f43"},{q="What does Ogunaro Wolfrunner want?",a="Ogunaro dedicates his craft to breeding and providing strong, dependable wolves for Horde champions. He seeks only to ensure that the iconic riding beasts of the orcish people find capable riders who know how to treat and command them in battle.",al={"what does ogunaro want","ogunaro goals","ogunaro wolfrunner motive"},it="wants",add="c3908665"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs, riding a wolf is an ancestral tradition that reaches back to the clans of Draenor. Ogunaro keeps that martial bond alive.",["faction:Horde"]="Trolls, tauren, and Forsaken must prove their dedication and honor to Orgrimmar before Ogunaro entrusts them with a wolf."},kw={"dire wolf","ogunaro wolfrunner","orgrimmar mounts","timber wolf","valley of honor","wolf mount"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Ogunaro Wolfrunner"}}
E["npc:orokk-omosh"] = {t="npc",n="Orokk Omosh",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orokk Omosh keeps his family's smithing craft alive. The aging orc has no children to inherit it, so he seeks worthy Horde apprentices to learn the Omosh armorcraft secrets.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orokk Omosh keeps his family's smithing craft alive.",sec={{t="A Lineage at Its End",b="In the Valley of Honor, Orokk Omosh is the last smith of the Omosh line. He has no children to inherit his craft, and he will not let his family's techniques die with him. Capable Horde blacksmiths can undertake his demanding trials of metalwork. Those who prove their dedication earn the revered secrets of Omosh armorcraft.",sp=0},{t="The Spirit of the Forge",b="Among fellow artisans, Orokk is known for his boisterous delight in true mastery. Those who complete his craftsmanship trials often see him perform the Omosh Dance of Joy, a jubilant celebration of traditional smithing that echoes through Orgrimmar's halls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orokk Omosh?",a="Orokk Omosh is an aging orc blacksmith in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He is the last smith of the Omosh lineage and seeks worthy Horde apprentices to preserve his family's craft.",al={"who is orokk","orokk omosh lore","orc smith orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Orokk Omosh be found?",a="You can find Orokk Omosh beside the smithing forges and anvils in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, in the city's northeastern section.",al={"orokk omosh location","where is orokk","find orokk omosh"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Orokk Omosh teaching outsiders his family secrets?",a="Orokk has no children to inherit his family's craft. He teaches skilled Horde blacksmiths who prove capable in his trials so the Omosh techniques do not die with him.",al={"why does orokk give quests","omosh legacy","why teach blacksmiths"},it="motive"},{q="What is the 'Omosh Dance of Joy'?",a="The Omosh Dance of Joy is a jubilant jig Orokk performs when an artisan proves their worth and masters his line's smithing techniques. It is his spirited tribute to the craft.",al={"dance of joy","omosh dance","joys of omosh"}},{q="Whose side is Orokk Omosh on?",a="Orokk Omosh is loyal to Thrall's Horde. Working from within the bustling heart of Orgrimmar, he willingly shares the hard-earned crafts and ancient metallurgical traditions of his bloodline strictly with promising Horde blacksmiths.",al={"orokk omosh faction","who does orokk omosh serve","is orokk omosh horde"},it="side",add="df415c30"},{q="What does Orokk Omosh want?",a="As the last living member of a venerable line of orc smiths and lacking children of his own, Orokk desires above all to preserve his family's legacy. He seeks capable smiths worthy of mastering and carrying forward the Omosh family's armory techniques before they are lost forever.",al={"what does orokk omosh want","orokk omosh goal","why is orokk looking for smiths"},it="wants",add="1085ff21"},{q="Why is Orokk Omosh here in Orgrimmar?",a="Orokk has settled in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, where the Horde's finest warriors, brawlers, and craftsmen congregate. It is the natural gathering ground for the mighty artisans and dedicated armorers he hopes will carry on his ancestral trade.",al={"why is orokk omosh in orgrimmar","orokk omosh location why"},it="why_here",add="5e3af98e"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Horde blacksmith, you can learn from Orokk Omosh and help preserve his family's ancestral craft.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help keep traditional orcish plate and mail techniques available to the warriors defending the fledgling Horde."},kw={"barbaric battlements","blacksmithing","dance of joy","omosh","orc smith","orgrimmar","orokk omosh","valley of honor"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2751","quest:2753","quest:2755","topic:horde"},src={"Orokk Omosh"}}
E["npc:orphan-matron-battlewail"] = {t="npc",n="Orphan Matron Battlewail",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orphan Matron Battlewail cares for children left without families by war. With Tosamina, she gives them shelter and raises young orcs.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orphan Matron Battlewail cares for children left without families by war.",sec={{t="Caretaker of the Horde's Youth",b="Orphan Matron Battlewail cares for children who have lost their kin to violence. In Orgrimmar, where war's toll reaches even the young capital, she and Tosamina shelter and nurture the next generation of the Horde. The orphanage in the Valley of Honor opens its doors to passing adventurers. During Children's Week, travelers are called upon to mentor the children.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orphan Matron Battlewail?",a="Orphan Matron Battlewail is an orc woman who oversees Orgrimmar's orphanage. She shelters and raises children whose parents died in battle.",al={"battlewail role","who is battlewail","matron battlewail"},it="identity"},{q="Where can she be found in Orgrimmar?",a="Battlewail and Tosamina care for the children in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, in the city's eastern reaches.",al={"battlewail location","where is the orphanage","find battlewail"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is her role during Children's Week?",a="During Children's Week, Battlewail sends willing champions out with an orphan to show them the wonders and heritage of the Horde.",al={"childrens week battlewail","warden of the horde","orphan quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who assists Battlewail at the orphanage?",a="Tosamina lives and works alongside Battlewail, helping watch over and protect the children in their care.",al={"tosamina","orphan matron helper"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Orphan Matron Battlewail on?",a="Matron Battlewail stands devotedly with the Horde. Based in Orgrimmar, she dedicates her life to raising the children of fallen Horde warriors, ensuring they grow up strong, protected, and proud of their people's legacy.",al={"battlewail faction","is battlewail horde"},it="side",add="5bd84e8a"},{q="What does Orphan Matron Battlewail want?",a="Her primary goal is the safety, welfare, and upbringing of the orphans under her care. During Children's Week in particular, she seeks dependable adventurers to take the children out into the world to show them life beyond Orgrimmar's walls.",al={"battlewail goal","what does the orphan matron want"},it="wants",add="c46a64f6"},{q="Why is Orphan Matron Battlewail here?",a="Battlewail runs the Orgrimmar orphanage in the Valley of Honor alongside her companion Tosamina. Constant conflicts across Kalimdor leave many orc youths without parents, making her compassionate yet stalwart guardianship essential to the city.",al={"why is battlewail in orgrimmar","why is battlewail here"},it="why_here",add="8b214374"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Battlewail gives guidance and shelter to children left behind by war, helping preserve the people's future.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc seeking a lasting homeland in Durotar, you can see in Battlewail's orphanage the sacrifices your people endure."},kw={"battlewail","children's week","orgrimmar","orphan matron battlewail","orphanage","tosamina","valley of honor","warden of the horde"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","quest:5502","topic:horde"},src={"Orphan Matron Battlewail"}}
E["npc:searn-firewarder"] = {t="npc",n="Searn Firewarder",z="orgrimmar",s="In Grommash Hold, Searn Firewarder guides Horde shamans toward the elements.",h="In Grommash Hold, Searn Firewarder guides Horde shamans toward the elements.",sec={{t="A Guide to the Elements",b="Inside Grommash Hold, Searn Firewarder guides shamans seeking the elements. Many Darkspear trolls commune with spirits through witch doctors and voodoo rituals. Searn guides initiates toward distant mentors and rites for the Call of Fire, Call of Water, and Call of Air, which teach them to commune with the elemental spirits of fire, water, and air. He stands among the Horde's high command in Orgrimmar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Searn Firewarder?",a="Searn Firewarder trains jungle troll shamans inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. He guides developing shamans across the Horde through their spiritual journeys.",al={"searn firewarder lore","who is searn","searn orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="What quests does Searn Firewarder offer?",a="Searn guides shamans through the Call of Fire, Call of Water, and Call of Air, pointing them toward distant shrines and spiritual teachers across the continents.",al={"searn quests","searn firewarder questline"},gp=true},{q="Why is a troll shaman stationed inside Grommash Hold?",a="Grommash Hold is the heart of Orgrimmar's leadership, where Warchief Thrall and prominent representatives of the allied races gather. Searn's presence reflects the close unity between the orcs and the Darkspear tribe, and shamanism's central place in the new Horde.",al={"why is searn in grommash hold","searn grommash hold"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Searn Firewarder on?",a="Searn Firewarder is loyal to the Horde and stands proudly with the Darkspear trolls. Stationed right inside Grommash Hold near Warchief Thrall, he serves the shamanistic traditions of the new Horde, guiding initiate shamans who walk the path of the elements in service of their people.",al={"searn firewarder faction","who does searn serve","searn firewarder allegiance"},it="side",add="9fd5962f"},{q="What does Searn Firewarder want?",a="Searn Firewarder seeks to test and instruct emerging shaman within the Horde. He directs practitioners through elemental trials—such as the Call of Fire, Water, and Air—ensuring that those who commune with the spirits prove their strength, dedication, and balance before wielding greater power.",al={"what does searn want","searn firewarder purpose","why talk to searn firewarder"},it="wants",add="7c90517e"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can look to Searn for guidance toward the masters and trials needed to bind the elements to your totem.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can see in Searn how your spiritual traditions stand alongside those of your orc and tauren allies."},kw={"call of air","call of fire","call of water","darkspear","grommash hold","orgrimmar","searn firewarder","shaman trainer"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold","zone:orgrimmar","quest:1524","quest:63","quest:1531","topic:troll","topic:horde"},src={"Searn Firewarder"}}
E["npc:seereth-stonebreak"] = {t="npc",n="Seereth Stonebreak",z="orgrimmar",s="Near Greatwood Vale, Seereth Stonebreak watches the land's disturbances. The orc shaman camps on the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens, guiding travelers against environmental ruin, rogue machines, and rising tensions in Kalimdor.",h="Near Greatwood Vale, Seereth Stonebreak watches the land's disturbances.",sec={{t="A Watchful Shaman",b="Seereth Stonebreak watches over Horde lands from her camp near Greatwood Vale. An orc shaman, she follows the harmony of the elements and protects the territories of the Horde. The land's spirits cried out against goblin plunder, and the Horde sent her to Stonetalon. There, she watches the landscape and guides travelers against dangers threatening the wild frontier.",sp=0},{t="Turmoil in Stonetalon",b="Seereth Stonebreak is troubled by turmoil across the Stonetalon range. Ruthless goblin ventures and mechanical shredders cutting through ancient woodlands have badly fractured the mountains' spiritual balance. She sends Horde envoys to confront the invaders and seek counsel from elder lorekeepers, in hopes of easing the land's distress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak is an orc shaman who serves the Horde. She guides travelers heading toward the Stonetalon Mountains against threats to the land and the Horde's presence.",al={"seereth","who is seereth","seereth stonebreak lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Seereth concerned about the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="The Stonetalon Mountains suffer from rampant deforestation, aggressive goblin logging machinery, and heightened conflict. Seereth senses the local spirits' agitation and works to halt the devastation.",al={"why stonetalon","seereth problems","stonetalon unrest"}},{q="What happened to her original post?",a="Seereth's original post remains near Greatwood Vale, on the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens. The Horde sent her to Stonetalon, and the camp lies along the road west of the Crossroads.",al={"seereth past","honors stand seereth","why did seereth move"}},{q="What tasks does Seereth offer to adventurers?",a="Seereth sends Horde adventurers into Stonetalon to confront Venture Company goblins, dismantle destructive shredding machines, commune with troubled spirits, and consult respected elders such as Magatha Grimtotem.",al={"seereth quests","what does seereth want","seereth stonebreak missions"},gp=true},{q="Who is the Elder Crone she mentions?",a="The Elder Crone is Magatha Grimtotem, a powerful and influential tauren elder who lives on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Seereth consults her for guidance on deep spiritual disturbances.",al={"the elder crone","who is elder crone","crone quest"}},{q="Why is she concerned with goblin operations?",a="Seereth is concerned because goblin logging operations use mechanical shredders to tear through sacred forests, pollute waterways, and enrage the nature spirits she is sworn to appease.",al={"seereth goblins","goblin invaders","why hate goblins"}},{q="Whose side is Seereth Stonebreak on?",a="Seereth Stonebreak stands firmly with the Horde. As an orc shaman, her loyalties lie with her people and their allies, seeking Horde champions to aid in defending the land and pushing back their enemies.",al={"seereth stonebreak faction","who does seereth serve","is seereth horde"},it="side",add="b2feb188"},{q="What does Seereth Stonebreak want?",a="Seereth seeks to safeguard the land and address the turmoil threatening the region. Camped on the border of the Stonetalon Mountains, she wants capable adventurers to heed the spirits and counter destructive forces pressing upon Horde interests.",al={"seereth stonebreak goals","what does seereth want","seereth stonebreak motive"},it="wants",add="8beca421"},{q="Why is Seereth Stonebreak here?",a="Seereth was sent by the Horde to watch over the troubled Stonetalon Mountains. She keeps her camp near the Greatwood Vale, on the border of Stonetalon and the Barrens, where the spirits cry out against the goblins' plunder, and she rallies Horde adventurers to answer them.",al={"why is seereth here","why did seereth come here","seereth stonebreak location reason"},it="why_here",add="da23e0a9"},{q="Who is Seereth Stonebreak tied to?",a="Seereth is an orc shaman aligned with the Horde and connected to the spiritual figures of Kalimdor, specifically pointing travelers toward the wise Tauren leader known as the Elder Crone.",al={"seereth stonebreak allies","who is seereth affiliated with","seereth stonebreak connections"},it="ties",add="7cf30712"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you share Seereth's duty to heal Stonetalon's environmental scars and soothe its agitated spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect critical overland routes and resources from Alliance forces and reckless goblin operations.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you share Seereth's return to shamanism and reverence for the natural world, against mindless destruction."},kw={"crone","goblins","seereth","shaman","shredders","spirits","stonebreak","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","quest:1061","quest:1062","quest:1068","quest:1063","topic:goblin","topic:alliance"},src={"Seereth Stonebreak"}}
E["npc:serge-hinott"] = {t="npc",n="Serge Hinott",z="orgrimmar",s="In Tarren Mill, Serge Hinott brews mixtures for the Forsaken war effort. The Forsaken alchemist works alongside Apothecary Lydon, preparing concoctions, antidotes, and reagents for the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="In Tarren Mill, Serge Hinott brews mixtures for the Forsaken war effort.",sec={{t="Apothecary's Hand in Tarren Mill",b="Serge Hinott brews remedies and other mixtures for the Forsaken in Tarren Mill. He works beside Apothecary Lydon, whose work includes chemical development and plague research against nearby human settlements such as Southshore. Hinott handles specialized brewing, including restorative salves and antidotes for field agents and scouts who face poisons or other toxic mishaps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Serge Hinott be found?",a="Serge Hinott works outdoors in Tarren Mill, in the central northern Hillsbrad Foothills. He is near Apothecary Lydon, among brewing supplies and alchemical equipment.",al={"serge hinott location","where is hinott","find serge hinott"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Serge Hinott serve?",a="Serge Hinott serves the Forsaken as an alchemist in Tarren Mill. He prepares local brews and treatments, and makes specialized mixtures for field operatives and couriers who request them.",al={"what does hinott do","serge hinott role"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Hinott's connection to Apothecary Lydon?",a="Serge Hinott works beside Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. When visitors interrupt him, Hinott tells them to go bother “Mr. High-And-Mighty” instead.",al={"hinott and lydon","who does hinott work with"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Serge Hinott?",a="Serge Hinott is a Forsaken alchemist stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Working closely alongside Apothecary Lydon, he lends his expertise in concoctions and remedies to the Forsaken cause and assists travelers through his mastery of the alchemical craft.",al={"who is hinott","serge hinott lore","who is serge"},it="identity",add="ed373d2b"},{q="Whose side is Serge Hinott on?",a="Serge Hinott is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed in the contested frontier of the Hillsbrad Foothills, his alchemical work supports the Horde's presence and survival against nearby threats.",al={"hinott faction","is serge hinott horde","who does hinott serve"},it="side",add="d070d0a8"},{q="What does Serge Hinott want?",a="Hinott focuses on perfecting his craft, brewing potent draughts, and lending his alchemical expertise to those aiding the Forsaken. He assists allies requiring specialized remedies and mixtures to counter venom and sickness across the region.",al={"hinott goal","what is hinott doing","hinott purpose"},it="wants",add="080bb72f"},{q="Why is Serge Hinott in Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Hinott is based in Tarren Mill to support the Forsaken's forward outpost in Hillsbrad Foothills. Beside Apothecary Lydon, he assists Horde champions operating in the shadow of Hillsbrad's fierce border conflicts.",al={"why is hinott in tarren mill","why is serge here","hinott location reason"},it="why_here",add="10d74ddb"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the practical work of the Royal Apothecary Society in Hillsbrad: chemical mixtures and support for Forsaken forces on the front lines.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can seek Hinott's cure for the virulent Touch of Zanzil. He crafts the antidote when ordinary remedies fail."},kw={"apothecary lydon","hillsbrad foothills","hinott","royal apothecary society","serge hinott","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:2479","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","subzone:southshore"},src={"Serge Hinott"}}
E["npc:shenthul"] = {t="npc",n="Shenthul",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul trains rogues and serves the Shattered Hand. He directs covert work across Kalimdor and brings promising rogues into its ranks.",h="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul trains rogues and serves the Shattered Hand.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Chasm",b="Shenthul trains rogues in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. While warriors and shamans march openly across Durotar, he teaches stealth, ambush, and subterfuge. His students learn fieldcraft and lethal arts for work in Kalimdor's harsh wilderness and unforgiving politics.",sp=0},{t="The Shattered Hand",b="Shenthul speaks for the Shattered Hand, once an orcish clan and now the Horde's intelligence network and secret service. He describes it as a watchful presence across Kalimdor, investigating, judging, and carrying out its own sentences. Pragmatic and independent of shifting politics, Shenthul reminds outsiders that the Shattered Hand existed before Warchief Thrall took power and will endure after him.",sp=0},{t="Covert Fieldwork",b="Shenthul directs covert work in contested territories. He sends operatives to infiltrate hostile interests and practice lockpicking on the Venture Company's locked supply boxes around Windshear Crag. Recruits face demanding trials, and when poisons strike his field agents, Shenthul makes sure they find remedies before the toxins prove fatal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Shenthul?",a="Shenthul trains jungle troll rogues in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar and works for the Shattered Hand.",al={"shenthul role","who is shenthul","troll rogue trainer orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shenthul?",a="Shenthul can be found in the Cleft of Shadow, a cavern complex reached through Orgrimmar's darker tunnels.",al={"shenthul location","where is shenthul","shenthul cleft of shadow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Shenthul's connection to the Shattered Hand?",a="Shenthul works for the Shattered Hand, the Horde's covert intelligence and assassin guild, and recruits rogues into its ranks.",al={"shattered hand shenthul","is shenthul shattered hand","what faction is shenthul"},it="ties"},{q="What does Shenthul think of Warchief Thrall?",a="Shenthul says the Shattered Hand existed before Thrall took power and will endure after him. He puts the guild's work and the Horde's security above shifting politics.",al={"shenthul thoughts on thrall","does shenthul like thrall","shenthul loyalty"}},{q="What missions does Shenthul offer to rogues?",a="Shenthul guides rogues through initiation trials and covert infiltration work. He also directs them to practice lockpicking on Venture Company's locked supply boxes around Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"shenthul quests","rogue quests shenthul"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Shenthul assist with rogue poisons?",a="Yes. When field agents face lethal poisons, Shenthul directs them to Hinott for remedies.",al={"shenthul poison quest","hinott assistance shenthul"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Shenthul on?",a="Shenthul serves the Shattered Hand above all else. While the order operates within Orgrimmar under the banner of the Horde, he makes it clear that the guild answers to its own authority. As he tells visitors, the Shattered Hand existed long before Warchief Thrall and will endure long after him.",al={"shenthul allegiance","who does shenthul serve","is shenthul loyal to thrall"},it="side",add="1496428e"},{q="What does Shenthul want?",a="Shenthul seeks to extend the Shattered Hand's reach across Kalimdor. He envisions the order acting as an all-seeing veil—serving as protectors, police, judges, jury, and executioners in the shadows. To achieve this, he trains promising rogues, tests their cunning and discipline, and sends them into the field on critical covert assignments.",al={"what is shenthul's goal","shenthul motives","what does shenthul want"},it="wants",add="6d75b5d2"},{q="Why is Shenthul here?",a="Shenthul makes his home in the dim caverns of the Cleft of Shadow to recruit and instruct new rogues in service of the Shattered Hand. Away from the prying eyes of the upper city, he oversees covert operations and tests aspiring agents in the stealth and subterfuge required to serve the order.",al={"why is shenthul in orgrimmar","why is shenthul in cleft of shadow","what is shenthul doing here"},it="why_here",add="f56d6f2e"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue in Orgrimmar, you can learn from Shenthul, face initiation trials, and take on covert assignments.",["faction:Horde"]="Beneath Orgrimmar, Shenthul directs the Horde's covert intelligence work against threats within and beyond its ranks.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see how Shenthul, a jungle troll, has joined the Shattered Hand, once an orcish clan."},kw={"cleft of shadow","jungle troll","orgrimmar","rogue trainer","shattered hand","shenthul","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2458","quest:2478","quest:2460","quest:2479","subzone:windshear-crag","topic:venture-company"},src={"Shenthul"}}
E["npc:tai-jin"] = {t="npc",n="Tai'jin",z="orgrimmar",s="At the Razor Hill barracks, Tai'jin guides young Darkspear priests in their spiritual traditions. She teaches the balance of light and shadow and rites such as the Hex of Weakness.",h="At the Razor Hill barracks, Tai'jin guides young Darkspear priests in their spiritual traditions.",sec={{t="Priestess of Razor Hill",b="Tai'jin guides young priests from the Razor Hill barracks as they set out into Durotar. Orcs here turn chiefly to shamanism or warlock arts, while Darkspear trolls bring their communion with spirits and loas to the Horde. Tai'jin teaches the first principles of priesthood, the balance of light and shadow, and the spiritual heritage of troll culture.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is inside the Razor Hill Barracks in central Durotar, on the ground floor beside other class trainers.",al={"tai'jin location","where is tai'jin","taijin razor hill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Tai'jin teach?",a="Tai'jin teaches new priests spells, ranks, and abilities as they gain experience, including early instruction for troll initiates.",al={"taijin trainer","what does taijin train","priest spells razor hill"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is a troll priest stationed in an orc settlement?",a="Razor Hill trains young Horde adventurers leaving the Valley of Trials and Sen'jin Village. Since orcs do not practice the priestly arts, Tai'jin brings Darkspear spiritual traditions to the settlement.",al={"why is taijin in razor hill","trolls in razor hill barracks"},it="why_here"},{q="What special rites does Tai'jin provide for troll priests?",a="Tai'jin guides Darkspear priests through introductory spiritual rites, including the Hex of Weakness, which channels ancestral curses.",al={"hex of weakness quest","taijin quests"},gp=true},{q="Who is Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is a Darkspear jungle troll priest trainer stationed in the barracks of Razor Hill. Devoted to guiding those who channel spiritual and divine energies, she instructs young acolytes of the Horde—particularly troll and undead priests—in mastering their spiritual arts, prayers, and traditional troll rites.",al={"taijin identity","who is taijin","taijin lore"},it="identity",add="5b5c447a"},{q="Whose side is Tai'jin on?",a="Tai'jin is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed in Durotar alongside orc warriors and shamans, she works in service to Warchief Thrall's united forces, ensuring that spiritual practitioners are prepared to defend Horde territory.",al={"taijin faction","who does taijin serve","taijin allegiance"},it="side",add="1746c020"},{q="What does Tai'jin want?",a="Tai'jin seeks to guide novice priests in understanding their spiritual gifts and deepening their devotion. She tasks budding acolytes with proving their discipline, meditation, and communion with spiritual forces so they can properly support their allies across Durotar and beyond.",al={"what does taijin want","taijin goal","taijin purpose"},it="wants",add="dfe85d14"},{q="Who is Tai'jin tied to?",a="As a spiritual mentor within Razor Hill, Tai'jin is tied closely to the Darkspear trolls led by Sen'jin's legacy, as well as the local Horde garrison under the authority of Orgrimmar. She works alongside fellow trainers and defenders in Durotar to foster strong, faithful acolytes.",al={"taijin ties","taijin connections","who is taijin allied with"},it="ties",add="ab897349"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Horde priest training in Durotar, you learn from Tai'jin before heading to Orgrimmar's grand halls.",["race:Troll"]="As a young Darkspear troll, you can learn distinctive spells from Tai'jin, including the Hex of Weakness."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hex of weakness","priest trainer","razor hill","tai'jin","taijin"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:5654","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Tai'jin"}}
E["npc:thrall"] = {t="npc",n="Thrall",z="orgrimmar",s="Thrall now rules from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, Warchief of the Horde and ruler of Durotar. Once a human slave raised as an arena fighter, he freed his people, restored their shamanic traditions, and led them across the Great Sea to a new homeland.",h="Thrall now rules from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, Warchief of the Horde and ruler of Durotar.",sec={{t="From Slave to Shaman",b="Thrall was born Go'el, son of Frostwolf chieftain Durotan and Draka. Gul'dan's assassins murdered his parents when he was an infant, and human commander Aedelas Blackmoore found him and named him Thrall, meaning slave. At Durnholde Keep, Blackmoore raised him as an arena fighter and taught him human tactics. With help from his foster sister Taretha Foxton, Thrall escaped. The Frostwolf exile Drek'Thar guided him away from demonic corruption and taught him to master the elemental spirits. Thrall became the first orcish shaman of a new generation.",sp=0},{t="The Mantle of the Warchief",b="After the Second War, Thrall joined Orgrim Doomhammer to free the orcs languishing in Alliance internment camps. Doomhammer fell in battle and passed his black plate armor and mighty warhammer to Thrall, naming him Warchief. The mysterious Prophet Medivh brought prophetic visions, and Thrall led his people aboard captured human ships across the Great Sea. They reached Kalimdor and escaped the doom falling upon the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="Forging the New Horde",b="In Kalimdor, Thrall reshaped the Horde from a warmongering force into an alliance built on survival and honor. He rescued Vol'jin's Darkspear trolls and allied with Cairne Bloodhoof's tauren. With human and night elf forces, the coalition defeated the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal. Thrall then founded Durotar and its capital, Orgrimmar, named for his father and mentor. He keeps an uneasy peace with Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore while defending his fragile nation and weighing controversial alliances, including the Forsaken of Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thrall?",a="Thrall leads the orcish people as Warchief of the Horde. Born Go'el of the Frostwolf clan, he was raised by humans as an enslaved gladiator, then broke free, learned shamanic ways, and led the orcs to Kalimdor, where they founded Orgrimmar.",al={"who is the warchief","thrall backstory","who is thrall"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Thrall's name come from?",a="Thrall was born Go'el, the name given by his parents Durotan and Draka. His human captor, Aedelas Blackmoore, gave him the name Thrall, an old human word meaning slave. Thrall kept it as a reminder of his past and of the oppression his people vowed never to endure again.",al={"why is he called thrall","what does thrall mean","thrall real name"},it="name"},{q="Why does Thrall wear black armor and carry a hammer?",a="Thrall wears black plate armor and carries the Doomhammer, both passed to him by Orgrim Doomhammer, the former Warchief. Mortally wounded while freeing the orcs from the internment camps, Orgrim gave Thrall the weapon and the mantle of Warchief with his dying breath.",al={"doomhammer","thrall weapon","black armor"},it="origin"},{q="Where can I find Thrall in the game?",a="Thrall resides in the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, the Horde capital in Durotar. He stands inside Grommash Hold with his bodyguards and advisers.",al={"where is thrall","thrall location","thrall room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Thrall's relationship with Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Thrall and Lady Jaina Proudmoore earned mutual respect and forged a pact of cooperation while fighting together at Mount Hyjal during the Third War. Their factions remain deeply distrustful, but the two leaders work to preserve a fragile peace between Orgrimmar and Theramore.",al={"thrall and jaina","jaina alliance","peace with theramore"},it="ties"},{q="Why did Thrall allow the Forsaken into the Horde?",a="Though wary of the undead, Thrall recognized the desperate plight of Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken, who had freed themselves from the Lich King's control. The tauren urged him diplomatically, believing the Forsaken could be redeemed. Thrall admitted them to the Horde to secure a strategic foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why are undead in horde","forsaken alliance","sylvanas horde entry"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Thrall on?",a="Thrall stands at the head of the Horde as its Warchief. He rebuilt the faction from broken captives into an alliance of survival, uniting his own orcs with the Darkspear trolls, the tauren of Kalimdor, and recently the Forsaken of Lordaeron. While fiercely loyal to his people, he also strives for uneasy peace with the Alliance.",al={"thrall faction","who does thrall lead","thrall alliance or horde"},it="side",add="6dbf9cfd"},{q="What does Thrall want?",a="Thrall seeks a secure, honorable future for the Horde far from the demonic corruption and bloodlust that once doomed his race. He strives to establish a permanent home in Durotar, reconnect the orcs with their ancient shamanic traditions, and maintain a fragile coexistence with their neighbors rather than plunge Kalimdor back into endless bloodshed.",al={"what is thrall's goal","thrall motivations","thrall goals"},it="wants",add="4a2053d7"},{q="Why is Thrall in Orgrimmar?",a="Orgrimmar is the fortress capital Thrall founded and named in memory of Orgrim Doomhammer. From his seat in Grommash Hold, he directs the defense and development of Durotar, oversees Horde diplomacy, and communes with the spirits as both high chieftain and master shaman.",al={"why is thrall here","why is thrall in the valley of wisdom","what is thrall doing in orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add="b797ddf7"},{q="Why is Thrall so famous across Azeroth?",a="Thrall achieved renown by shattering the Alliance internment camps, liberating the lethargic orcs, and restoring their lost spiritual heritage. His legend grew further during the Third War, where he guided his people across the Great Sea and fought alongside human and night elf forces atop Mount Hyjal to defeat the Burning Legion.",al={"why is thrall feared","is thrall famous","thrall legend"},it="fame",add="c1597526"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Thrall is your Warchief and supreme commander. He led the Horde out of enslavement and ruin toward an honorable future on Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance leaders see Thrall as dangerous but pragmatic. His disciplined Horde is far preferable to the bloodthirsty conquerors of the First and Second Wars.",["class:Shaman"]="Thrall is revered as the first new orcish shaman in a generation. He restored his people's sacred communion with the elemental spirits after decades of demonic corruption.",["race:Orc"]="To the orcs, Thrall is a living savior. He freed them from the lethargy of the human internment camps and returned them to their ancestral honor."},kw={"blackmoore","doomhammer","durotar","go'el","orgrimmar","shaman","thrall","warchief"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:new-horde","npc:vol-jin","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:third-war"},src={"Thrall"}}
E["npc:ur-kyo"] = {t="npc",n="Ur'kyo",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, Ur'kyo guides priests in the ways of shadow and light. The Darkspear regard him as their spiritual leader and greatest priest, and he teaches their traditions in the Horde capital.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, Ur'kyo guides priests in the ways of shadow and light.",sec={{t="Spiritual Master of the Darkspear",b="Ur'kyo guides Darkspear mystics and visiting practitioners from the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar. After fleeing the Echo Isles, the Darkspear made a home in Durotar alongside Thrall's Horde. Their sacred traditions remain vital to the tribe, and Ur'kyo keeps those ancestral practices alive through his teaching.",sp=0},{t="Guidance and Ancient Rites",b="Priests who come to Ur'kyo find a patient instructor in faith and old rites. He teaches the Hex of Weakness and the defensive ward called Shadowguard. Horde priests also turn to him to learn about the coalition's varied spiritual ways, from troll voodoo and ancestral customs to foreign disciplines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ur'kyo?",a="Ur'kyo trains priests in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. The Darkspear regard him as their spiritual leader and greatest priest.",al={"urkyo role","ur'kyo identity","who is urkyo"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ur'kyo?",a="Ur'kyo is in the Valley of Spirits, the troll district on Orgrimmar's western side. Look for him in the training huts near the water, alongside other spiritual mentors.",al={"ur'kyo location","urkyo map","find urkyo"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What abilities does Ur'kyo teach?",a="Ur'kyo teaches priests foundational spells of shadow and light. He also guides Darkspear priests in the Hex of Weakness and Shadowguard.",al={"urkyo spells","ur'kyo abilities","troll priest spells"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does Ur'kyo practice in Orgrimmar rather than the Echo Isles?",a="After Zalazane's betrayal and the loss of the Echo Isles, the Darkspear resettled with the orcs in Durotar. Ur'kyo teaches the tribe's mystical traditions and trains new defenders for the Horde from the Valley of Spirits.",al={"urkyo orgrimmar lore","why is urkyo in orgrimmar"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Ur'kyo interact with non-troll priests?",a="Yes. Ur'kyo teaches visiting Horde priests, sharing Darkspear knowledge with other members of the Horde, including the Forsaken.",al={"can undead train at urkyo","urkyo horde trainer"},it="people"},{q="What is Ur'kyo's role among the Darkspear priests?",a="The Darkspear recognize Ur'kyo as their greatest priest and foremost spiritual leader. He passes ancestral customs, rites, and voodoo practices to the next generation.",al={"ur'kyo standing","greatest priest of the tribe"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Ur'kyo on?",a="Ur'kyo stands firmly with the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, he serves as a vital spiritual guide for his people under Chieftain Vol'jin and Warchief Thrall. While deeply bound to the traditions of the jungle trolls, he welcomes priests of the Horde who come to seek spiritual instruction and mastery over ancient rites.",al={"ur'kyo faction","who does ur'kyo serve","is ur'kyo horde"},it="side",add="77e8c5e8"},{q="What does Ur'kyo want?",a="Ur'kyo strives to preserve the spiritual traditions of the Darkspear tribe and mentor new generations of priests. He works to maintain the old ways, channel the ancient powers of the spirits, and ensure that those who walk the path of the priesthood possess both the resolve and knowledge necessary to protect their people within the Horde.",al={"ur'kyo goal","what is ur'kyo trying to do","ur'kyo purpose"},it="wants",add="a5f00a0b"},{q="Why is Ur'kyo renowned among the Darkspear?",a="Ur'kyo is revered as the greatest priest of the Darkspear tribe. Respected as a supreme spiritual leader, his deep communion with the spirits and mastery over sacred troll rites make him the ultimate authority on spiritual power and wisdom among the Darkspear in Kalimdor.",al={"is ur'kyo famous","why is ur'kyo respected","ur'kyo reputation"},it="fame",add="fa6f514c"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Horde priest traveling through Durotar, you can learn the ways of faith, shadow rites, and sacred wards from Ur'kyo.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can look to Ur'kyo as your foremost spiritual guide in Orgrimmar. He preserves your tribe's voodoo and ancient magical rites after the loss of the Echo Isles.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, teaching healers and shadowcasters who prepare to defend the Horde."},kw={"darkspear","hex of weakness","orgrimmar","priest trainer","shadowguard","ur'kyo","urkyo","valley of spirits"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll","quest:5654","quest:5643","quest:5644"},src={"Ur'kyo"}}
E["npc:warcaller-gorlach"] = {t="npc",n="Warcaller Gorlach",z="orgrimmar",s="Warcaller Gorlach patrols Orgrimmar, calling Horde champions to distant battlefronts. He rallies travelers and seasoned warriors to answer commands at outposts across Kalimdor and beyond.",h="Warcaller Gorlach patrols Orgrimmar, calling Horde champions to distant battlefronts.",sec={{t="Voice of the Warchief's Call",b="Warcaller Gorlach walks Orgrimmar's thoroughfares, carrying the Horde's calls for expansion and defense. He gives orders among the city's people, seeking volunteers ready to test their mettle. Some he sends to the contested canopy of Ashenvale. Others he directs toward Camp Mojache in Feralas, where scouts face the wilderness. He also calls warriors to distant campaigns in the Plaguelands. As threats rise abroad, Gorlach calls on those in the capital to take up arms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Warcaller Gorlach?",a="Warcaller Gorlach patrols Orgrimmar as an orc herald, directing Horde members toward combat zones and remote frontiers.",al={"gorlach","who is gorlach","warcaller"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Warcaller Gorlach send adventurers?",a="Warcaller Gorlach directs Horde champions to outposts in need, including Ashenvale, Camp Mojache in Feralas, and distant fronts such as the Plaguelands.",al={"gorlach destinations","where does gorlach send you","gorlach quests"},gp=true},{q="Where can Warcaller Gorlach be found?",a="Warcaller Gorlach patrols the streets and valleys of Orgrimmar, calling its people to arms.",al={"gorlach location","where is gorlach","find gorlach"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Warcaller Gorlach on?",a="Warcaller Gorlach is a loyal orc serving the Horde. Stationed within Orgrimmar, he actively rallies warriors to defend Horde interests and bolster military campaigns across Kalimdor and beyond.",al={"gorlach faction","is gorlach horde","who does gorlach serve"},it="side",add="1e435e0c"},{q="What does Warcaller Gorlach want?",a="Gorlach seeks able-bodied fighters to answer the call of the Horde. He directs eager adventurers toward contested frontiers and critical strongholds, rallying recruits for ongoing struggles across the world.",al={"what does gorlach want","gorlach purpose","gorlach quests"},it="wants",add="5b62b1f9"},{q="Why is Warcaller Gorlach in Orgrimmar?",a="Gorlach walks the streets of the Horde capital as a warcaller, acting as a recruiter and messenger. By patrolling Orgrimmar, he ensures that arriving champions hear word of distant battles needing immediate aid.",al={"why is gorlach here","gorlach orgrimmar","gorlach role orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add="662e00c8"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion looking to prove your strength or seek guidance beyond Durotar, you can turn to Gorlach for direction toward outposts in need of reinforcements."},kw={"ashenvale hunt","call to arms","camp mojache","gorlach","herald","orgrimmar","warcaller gorlach"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","quest:235","zone:ashenvale","subzone:camp-mojache"},src={"Warcaller Gorlach"}}
E["npc:zamja"] = {t="npc",n="Zamja",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar’s Drag, Zamja teaches Horde travelers to cook. The Darkspear troll trains cooks to make meals from beasts of Kalimdor.",h="In Orgrimmar’s Drag, Zamja teaches Horde travelers to cook.",sec={{t="A Cleaver in the Drag",b="Zamja works in the Drag, where she cuts meat and teaches Horde travelers to cook. Cooking helps travelers in the rugged lands of Durotar and the Barrens turn raw game into rations. Cooks who have mastered basic recipes can seek further training in Gadgetzan, to the south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zamja?",a="Zamja is a Darkspear troll cooking trainer in Orgrimmar’s Drag. She teaches Horde cooks and helps them improve their craft.",al={"zamja npc","who is zamja","zamja orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Zamja?",a="You can find Zamja in the Drag, the shaded trench that winds between Orgrimmar’s Valley of Strength and Valley of Honor.",al={"zamja location","where is zamja","zamja trainer spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What training does Zamja offer?",a="Zamja teaches cooking and recipes for preparing food from beasts and game gathered across Kalimdor. Cooks ready for further training can seek more advanced instructors.",al={"what does zamja teach","zamja cooking recipes","cooking trainer orgrimmar"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where does Zamja send advanced cooks?",a="When a cook outgrows the training available in Orgrimmar, Zamja directs them to Gadgetzan in Tanaris to find Dirge Quikcleave.",al={"zamja quest","to gadgetzan you go quest","expert cooking horde"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Zamja on?",a="Zamja is loyal to the Horde and her fellow Darkspear trolls. Living and working within the bustling heart of Orgrimmar, she proudly serves the city's residents and travelers, offering her culinary expertise to any member of the Horde eager to master the craft of cooking.",al={"zamja faction","zamja allegiance","is zamja horde"},it="side",add="85904c39"},{q="What does Zamja want?",a="Zamja dedicates herself to her craft, spending her days chopping meat and preparing wholesome sustenance in Orgrimmar. She wants nothing more than to share her culinary knowledge with aspiring cooks across the Horde, ensuring travelers are well-fed and pointing skilled practitioners toward advanced mentors when they surpass her teachings.",al={"zamja goal","what does zamja need","zamja motive"},it="wants",add="ae32e7ed"},{q="Why is Zamja here in Orgrimmar?",a="As a skilled troll chef living among the Orcish capital, Zamja makes her home in Orgrimmar to ply her trade and support the Horde. In a harsh, arid land where survival demands practical skills, her presence ensures that adventurers and defenders have access to proper butchery and cooking instruction.",al={"why is zamja in orgrimmar","zamja location purpose","why is zamja here"},it="why_here",add="16342b16"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Zamja is one of the main cooking trainers for Horde characters in Orgrimmar. She teaches essential recipes and directs experienced cooks south to Tanaris for advanced instruction.",["race:Troll"]="Like many Darkspear trolls, Zamja has settled in Orgrimmar under Warchief Thrall’s banner. She brings troll resourcefulness and culinary craft to the Horde capital."},kw={"cooking trainer","darkspear","orgrimmar","the drag","to gadgetzan you go","troll","zamja"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drag","quest:6611","subzone:gadgetzan","topic:troll"},src={"Zamja"}}
E["npc:zankaja"] = {t="npc",n="Zankaja",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, young orc woman Zankaja waits anxiously for word of her mate, Dogran. He was assigned to duty at the Crossroads, along the dangerous frontier of the Barrens.",h="In Orgrimmar, young orc woman Zankaja waits anxiously for word of her mate, Dogran.",sec={{t="A Watchful Heart",b="Zankaja waits for news of Dogran, her mate, in Orgrimmar. Dogran earned a promotion and went south to bolster the outpost at the Crossroads in the Barrens. The assignment honors a warrior, but the frontier is harsh, with quilboar, centaur, and aggressive beasts. When Dogran failed to send word or return as expected, Zankaja began asking travelers to seek news of him.",sp=0},{t="Tragic Tidings",b="News from the Barrens brings Zankaja's worst fear: Dogran fell into the clutches of the quilboar. She still holds hope within Orgrimmar's canyon walls, though the frontier is unforgiving. The news travelers bring paints a grim picture of sacrifice on the Horde's perilous borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zankaja?",a="Zankaja lives along the path between the Valley of Strength and the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar.",al={"zankaja location","where is zankaja","find zankaja"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Dogran?",a="Dogran is Zankaja's mate, an orc warrior whose recent promotion sent him to a station at the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"who is dogran","dogran","zankaja mate"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Zankaja worried?",a="Dogran was sent to duty at the Crossroads in the harsh Barrens, then failed to return or send word home. Zankaja fears harm has come to him on the frontier.",al={"what does zankaja want","zankaja problem","why is zankaja sad"},it="motive"},{q="What does Zankaja ask adventurers to do?",a="Zankaja asks passing adventurers heading out of Orgrimmar to visit Captain Gazrog at the Crossroads and ask about Dogran's whereabouts and wellbeing.",al={"zankaja quest","news of dogran quest"},it="wants"},{q="What happened to Dogran in the Barrens?",a="Zankaja does not know what happened to Dogran in the Barrens. She asks travelers to speak with Gazrog at the Crossroads and follow the trail from there.",al={"is dogran dead","dogran fate","what happened to dogran"},sp=1},{q="Who is Zankaja?",a="Zankaja is a young orc woman living in Orgrimmar. She spends her days lingering between the Valley of Strength and the Valley of Wisdom, consumed by grief and anxiety over the fate of her mate, Dogran, who departed for duty in the harsh wilderness of the Barrens.",al={"who is zankaja","zankaja identity","zankaja lore"},it="identity",add="d77e4e41"},{q="Whose side is Zankaja on?",a="Zankaja is a loyal civilian of the Horde living within the capital city of Orgrimmar. Her concerns are personal and domestic rather than political, revolving entirely around the safety of her mate and the security of her home among her fellow orcs.",al={"zankaja faction","is zankaja horde","zankaja allegiance"},it="side",add="c2de3af5"},{q="Why is Zankaja here?",a="Zankaja remains in Orgrimmar waiting anxiously for word of her mate, Dogran. While he was sent south to the Crossroads, she stayed behind in the safety of the capital, only to find herself stranded in agonizing suspense when his letters and reports ceased.",al={"why is zankaja in orgrimmar","why is zankaja standing here","zankaja location reason"},it="why_here",add="b4e1ea75"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see the personal cost to ordinary families in Durotar, where duty to the Warchief's new realm sends loved ones into untamed, lethal frontiers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see in Zankaja's plea that holding outposts like the Crossroads costs real blood and sacrifice from the grunts stationed there."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","dogran","gazrog","orgrimmar","valley of strength","valley of wisdom","zankaja"},rel={"quest:1509","quest:1508","npc:gazrog","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength"},src={"Zankaja"}}
E["npc:zevrost"] = {t="npc",n="Zevrost",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar’s Cleft of Shadow, Zevrost trains warlocks in fel magic. He guides Horde initiates through summoning rites and the handling of dark artifacts.",h="In Orgrimmar’s Cleft of Shadow, Zevrost trains warlocks in fel magic.",sec={{t="Master of the Dark Arts",b="In the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar, Zevrost is one of the chief mentors for Horde warlocks in Thrall’s capital. Orcs remain wary of fel magic after their past demonic corruption, so practitioners work under strict watch. Zevrost teaches the discipline needed to command demons without yielding to their corruption. He says fel ruins only those who lack inner strength.",sp=0},{t="Guiding the Ambitious",b="Zevrost guides warlocks beyond spells and curses, opening the way to greater dark undertakings. Initiates seeking advanced implements such as the Orb of Orahil, or the means to summon a fiery Felsteed, often come through his hands. He sends ambitious practitioners to other masters, including Menara Voidrender in the Barrens, so they can push their command of shadow magic to its limits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zevrost?",a="Zevrost trains Horde warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He teaches incantations to novice and experienced practitioners and guides them through important class rituals.",al={"zevrost role","who is zevrost","zevrost npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Zevrost be found?",a="Zevrost can be found in the Cleft of Shadow, a cavern beneath Orgrimmar’s main districts.",al={"zevrost location","where is zevrost","find zevrost"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are warlocks like Zevrost permitted in Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall’s Horde permits warlocks to practice in the secluded Cleft of Shadow under strict watch. Orcs remember the corruption brought by demon blood, yet the Horde values the ruthless power warlocks can bring against its enemies.",al={"why are warlocks allowed in orgrimmar","warlock cleft of shadow"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Zevrost's philosophy on demonic magic?",a="Zevrost believes dark and arcane energies corrupt only those who are weak of will. He urges his students to study with strict discipline, lest they succumb to the destructive forces they command.",al={"zevrost quote","zevrost belief"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Zevrost on?",a="Zevrost serves the Horde as a warlock trainer within Orgrimmar. While warlocks are mistrusted by many orcs due to the dark legacy of the Burning Blade and demonic corruption, Zevrost practices his craft beneath the city, instructing loyal practitioners in mastering fel magic safely for the Horde's benefit.",al={"zevrost faction","is zevrost loyal to thrall","who does zevrost serve"},it="side",add="a3e2c8b2"},{q="What does Zevrost want?",a="Zevrost seeks disciplined warlocks capable of wielding volatile magic without succumbing to it. He believes arcane and fel powers corrupt only the weak-willed, aiming to train students who maintain rigorous control so they avoid destruction and serve the Horde effectively.",al={"zevrost goals","what does zevrost desire","zevrost purpose"},it="wants",add="66627367"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you can learn advanced spells from Zevrost and be sent to seek specialized weapons, off-hands, and a fiery steed.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you live among people who largely shun demonic magic. Zevrost represents practitioners who still wield the dark arts under the Warchief’s close scrutiny."},kw={"cleft of shadow","fel magic","felsteed","orgrimmar","trainer","warlock","zevrost"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","npc:menara-voidrender","quest:4736","topic:horde"},src={"Zevrost"}}
E["npc:zor-lonetree"] = {t="npc",n="Zor Lonetree",z="orgrimmar",s="At Grommash Hold, Zor Lonetree studies the Horde’s concerns beyond Durotar. His knowledge of Alliance politics helps the court judge foreign affairs across Kalimdor.",h="At Grommash Hold, Zor Lonetree studies the Horde’s concerns beyond Durotar.",sec={{t="Advisor in Grommash Hold",b="Zor Lonetree watches beyond Durotar from Grommash Hold. A shrewd advisor to the Horde’s high leadership, he has an unusually keen understanding of human and Alliance politics. When foreign curiosities reach Orgrimmar, he studies them; when trouble stirs among the land’s spirits, he directs travelers toward it. He has examined noble jewelry recovered from human settlements and followed disturbances among the spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains, keeping the warchief’s court informed on both political and spiritual matters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zor Lonetree?",a="Zor Lonetree advises the Horde from inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. His keen grasp of Alliance politics and interest in Kalimdor’s spiritual matters make him a useful counselor.",al={"zor lonetree who is he","who is zor","zor orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Zor Lonetree?",a="You can find Zor Lonetree inside Grommash Hold, in the Valley of Wisdom at the heart of Orgrimmar.",al={"zor lonetree location","where is zor lonetree","zor in orgrimmar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Zor Lonetree give adventurers?",a="Zor Lonetree sends Horde champions to aid the spirits of Stonetalon Peak and soothe elemental unrest in the Stonetalon Mountains. He also analyzes strange human relics that scouts bring to the capital.",al={"zor lonetree quests","the spirits of stonetalon zor"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Zor Lonetree knowledgeable about the Alliance?",a="Zor Lonetree specializes in foreign affairs and statecraft. He studies human aristocratic customs and Alliance movements, helping him read noble signets, regalia, and tactical motives that other orcs might overlook.",al={"zor lonetree alliance lore","why does zor know alliance politics"}},{q="Whose side is Zor Lonetree on?",a="Zor Lonetree stands loyally with the Horde. Operating out of Grommash Hold right beside Warchief Thrall's inner circle in Orgrimmar, he directs warriors and scouts in ways that advance the Horde's strategic and territorial interests across Kalimdor.",al={"zor lonetree faction","is zor lonetree horde","who does zor serve"},it="side",add="2fe5d96a"},{q="What does Zor Lonetree want?",a="Zor is focused on strengthening the Horde's foothold and safeguarding its lands. He seeks intelligence on outside threats—including studying Alliance movements and artifacts—while tasking trusted champions to soothe troubled elements, such as the restless earth and spirits in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"what does zor want","zor lonetree motive","zor lonetree goal"},it="wants",add="74ebfad4"},{q="Why is Zor Lonetree here in Grommash Hold?",a="Zor resides in Grommash Hold as an advisor and coordinator for the Horde leadership. He is remarkably well schooled in Alliance politics, making his presence invaluable to the Warchief when evaluating external threats, foreign noble intrigues, and regional spiritual disturbances across Kalimdor.",al={"why is zor in grommash hold","why is zor lonetree in orgrimmar","zor lonetree role"},it="why_here",add="891b1ec8"},{q="Who is Zor Lonetree tied to?",a="Zor works closely with key Horde scouts and agents in the field, including Nazeer Bloodpike at Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. He analyzes findings sent back from the frontiers and advises the leadership gathered within Grommash Hold.",al={"zor lonetree connections","who does zor work with","zor lonetree allies"},it="ties",add="ebf76354"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde scout near human enclaves or disputed borders, you can turn to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar to interpret enemy intentions and relics.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman answering disturbed elemental forces, you share common cause with Zor Lonetree, who watches the suffering spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"advisor","alliance politics","grommash hold","orgrimmar","stonetalon","valley of strength","zor lonetree"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","quest:1061","zone:stonetalon","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Zor Lonetree"}}
E["quest:1061"] = {t="quest",n="The Spirits of Stonetalon",z="orgrimmar",s="Unrest stirs among the spirits of Stonetalon, and Zor Lonetree sends Horde champions west to learn why. From Orgrimmar, they travel past the Crossroads and report directly to Seereth Stonebreak near Greatwood Vale.",h="Unrest stirs among the spirits of Stonetalon, and Zor Lonetree sends Horde champions west to learn why.",sec={{t="A Cry from the West",b="In Grommash Hold, Zor Lonetree listens to the natural world and feels deep distress from the Stonetalon Mountains. The elemental spirits of its rocky peaks are furious as logging tears into their forests. Horde shamans hear that unrest and fear the devastation in the western highlands will upset Kalimdor's spiritual balance.",sp=0},{t="Industrial Deforestation",b="The Venture Company, an unscrupulous goblin syndicate, is cutting timber in Greatwood Vale. Its commercial crews use aggressive machinery, saws, and muscle to butcher the ancient woodland instead of harvesting sustainably. The Horde sent Seereth Stonebreak, a young shaman, to watch the forest from the frontier and rally defenders against the ravagers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest and where are they located?",a="Zor Lonetree, an orc advisor, offers this in Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar.",al={"quest giver","where get quest","zor lonetree location"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Seereth Stonebreak?",a="Seereth Stonebreak waits in the Stonetalon Mountains, along the path near Greatwood Vale, just past the eastern entrance from the northern Barrens.",al={"seereth location","where is seereth stonebreak","stonetalon camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the spirits of Stonetalon angry?",a="The Venture Company goblins are clear-cutting the mountain woods, provoking the land's elemental guardians.",al={"why are spirits mad","stonetalon unrest","angry spirits"},it="threat"},{q="How do I reach the Stonetalon Mountains from Orgrimmar?",a="Travel south from Orgrimmar across the Barrens to the Crossroads, then follow the westward road through the rocky pass into Stonetalon.",al={"path to stonetalon","how to get to stonetalon","route to stonetalon"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What comes next after speaking with Seereth?",a="At her camp, Seereth Stonebreak gives you Goblin Invaders, sending you into Greatwood Vale to eliminate loggers and cut down their operations.",al={"next quest","followup","what after spirits of stonetalon"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde intervening in Stonetalon's deforestation?",a="Tauren and orc shamans revere the elemental spirits. Reckless goblin logging harms the land's spiritual harmony and threatens the borders of the Barrens.",al={"why does horde care","tauren stonetalon interest"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Zor Lonetree want this done?",a="As one who listens to the natural world, Zor Lonetree has heard the desperate cries of the land itself. The unrestrained plundering and burning carried out by goblin deforesters in the Stonetalon Mountains has deeply agitated the elemental spirits. To heal the land and preserve the balance, he answers the urgent call for reinforcements sent by Seereth Stonebreak, directing capable adventurers into the mountains before the destruction spreads further.",al={"why does zor send you","zor lonetree motive","why zor lonetree spirits stonetalon"},it="motive",add="4d15c2b8"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you hear a plea from the elements to mend the bond between earth and the living.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you carry a cultural duty to soothe the earth and defend sacred forests from goblin logging.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep travel routes between Stonetalon and the Barrens clear of rogue commercial syndicates."},kw={"crossroads","deforestation","greatwood vale","seereth stonebreak","stonetalon mountains","valley of wisdom","venture company","zor lonetree"},rel={"quest:1062","npc:seereth-stonebreak","npc:zor-lonetree","zone:stonetalon","subzone:greatwood-vale","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:goblin"},m={start="Zor Lonetree",["end"]="Seereth Stonebreak",level="17",faction="Horde",id=1061},src={"The Spirits of Stonetalon"}}
E["quest:1361"] = {t="quest",n="Regthar Deathgate",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Barrens, Regthar Deathgate calls seasoned Horde fighters west. The veteran warrior is gathering volunteers for a campaign across the mountains into Desolace, where centaur clans terrorize the frontier.",h="In the Barrens, Regthar Deathgate calls seasoned Horde fighters west.",sec={{t="Call of the Warchief's Lieutenants",b="Horde leaders watch the borders for threats. In the Barrens, Regthar Deathgate has set up a defensive post guarding the western passes. Horde officers send proven adventurers west of the Crossroads to answer his call for hardened fighters.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Desolace",b="Regthar Deathgate waits in a fortified redoubt along the ridges west of the Crossroads. From there, he watches the mountain trails into Desolace. He is gathering a vanguard to cross hostile ground and strike the Kolkar and other warring centaur clans before their expansion threatens Horde territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Regthar Deathgate?",a="Regthar Deathgate is an orc warrior and Horde commander stationed in the Barrens. He directs scouts and military strikes into Desolace.",al={"who is regthar","regthar deathgate lore","who is the questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Regthar Deathgate located?",a="Regthar Deathgate is in the Barrens, inside the Horde bunkers on the hill path west of the Crossroads, overlooking the western mountain pass.",al={"where is regthar","regthar location","find regthar deathgate"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to seek out Regthar?",a="Shadow Hunter Vol'jin, Nazgrel, Belgrom Rockmaul, and Krusk offer the call to seek Regthar. Vol'jin, Nazgrel, and Belgrom Rockmaul are in Orgrimmar; Krusk is in Tarren Mill.",al={"who starts regthar deathgate","where to get regthar quest"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is the primary objective of Regthar's mission?",a="Regthar is gathering warriors to cross the mountains into Desolace and attack the hostile centaur clans, especially the Kolkar.",al={"what does regthar want","regthar deathgate purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned with Desolace?",a="Aggressive centaur clans overrun Desolace. If left unchecked, their raids could cross the mountains into the Barrens and nearby Horde settlements.",al={"why go to desolace","horde interest in desolace"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next after speaking with Regthar Deathgate?",a="After you report to Regthar, he briefs you on the lands beyond the western mountains and sends you on your first strike across the border against the Kolkar.",al={"next quest after regthar","regthar follow up"},it="next_step"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde is trying to secure its frontier by subduing centaur in neighboring Desolace before they can raid deeper into the Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you have a personal stake in helping Regthar strike against the Kolkar, after generations of conflict with the centaur across central Kalimdor.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can answer Regthar's call with direct fighting skill and discipline in Desolace's hostile badlands."},kw={"belgrom rockmaul","crossroads","desolace","kolkar","krusk","nazgrel","regthar deathgate","the barrens","vol'jin"},rel={"quest:1362","zone:desolace","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Krusk, Belgrom Rockmaul, Nazgrel, Vol'jin",["end"]="Regthar Deathgate",level="32",faction="Horde",id=1361},src={"Regthar Deathgate (quest)"}}
E["quest:1431"] = {t="quest",n="Alliance Relations",z="orgrimmar",s="Thrall seeks a careful hand to preserve peace with the Alliance. In Orgrimmar, Craven Drok sends seasoned Horde adventurers to find Keldran near the western exit. The work calls for quiet diplomacy and intelligence to protect Thrall’s fragile peace.",h="Thrall seeks a careful hand to preserve peace with the Alliance.",sec={{t="A Diplomatic Dilemma",b="Thrall knows war with the Alliance could ruin his young nation. Raised in human captivity, the Warchief learned human statecraft and military strategy. Craven Drok watches for warriors and champions with patience for a subtler path, one that looks beyond raw force.",sp=0},{t="Keldran's Hovel",b="Near Orgrimmar’s western exit, Keldran keeps a humble dwelling. He practices magic and covert arts, working with appearances, perception, and statecraft. Keldran seeks discreet operatives to serve the Warchief as the Horde faces a tense standoff with its bitter rivals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Alliance Relations?",a="Craven Drok offers this work in Orgrimmar to Horde adventurers who have reached their thirtieth season of experience.",al={"quest giver alliance relations","who starts alliance relations","where to get alliance relations"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Keldran?",a="Keldran lives in a small hovel near Orgrimmar’s western exit, away from the city center.",al={"keldran location","where is keldran","keldran orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="What is Keldran's role in Orgrimmar?",a="Keldran studies magic and mystical arts, assisting Warchief Thrall with discreet matters of diplomacy, intelligence, and the Horde’s public image.",al={"who is keldran","keldran lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thrall care about diplomacy with the Alliance?",a="Raised among humans, Thrall understands their politics and military power. He knows outright war could destroy his young people, so he relies on prudence and measured statecraft to protect the Horde’s future.",al={"thrall diplomacy","why horde peace with alliance","thrall and humans"},it="purpose"},{q="Does this quest lead to further missions?",a="Yes. Bringing this matter to Keldran begins a deeper discussion of the Horde’s standing with other factions and leads to further work in regional diplomacy and espionage.",al={"alliance relations followup","what comes after alliance relations"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is discretion so important for this task?",a="Open conflict with the Alliance risks heavy casualties and could destabilize Kalimdor. Thrall relies on subtle operatives to address sensitive diplomatic friction before it erupts into war.",al={"why subtlety","keldran subtlety"}},{q="Why does Craven Drok send you to Keldran?",a="Craven Drok recognizes that understanding the Horde's delicate political standing requires more than brute strength. While the orcs are proud and warlike, Thrall pursues a diplomatic path learned from his time among humans. Drok starts the tale to test your interest, but directs you to Keldran—a practitioner of subtle arts—who oversees the discreet matters necessary to manage how allies and enemies perceive the Horde.",al={"craven drok motive","why talk to keldran","why does craven drok want this done"},it="motive",add="f7a9da96"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this work shows the divide between traditional brute strength and Thrall’s more measured, diplomatic statecraft.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may know the axe as a way to settle conflict. Keldran’s approach calls for patience and tactical subtlety.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, your skill with secrecy and perception suits Keldran’s work."},kw={"alliance relations","craven drok","diplomacy","horde","keldran","orgrimmar","thrall"},rel={"npc:keldran","npc:craven-drok","npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Craven Drok",["end"]="Keldran",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1431},src={"Alliance Relations"}}
E["quest:1432"] = {t="quest",n="Alliance Relations",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Alliance advances across Kalimdor raise fears of dangerous political fallout. The Horde sends orders to Desolace to purge demons before the Alliance can accuse Thrall's people of renewed ties to the Burning Legion.",h="In Orgrimmar, Alliance advances across Kalimdor raise fears of dangerous political fallout.",sec={{t="A Matter of Perception",b="Alliance scouts and expeditions crossing Kalimdor put the Horde in a delicate position. Demonic remnants across central Kalimdor could confirm old suspicions that the orcs and their allies still serve the Burning Legion. With Warchief Thrall's sanction, Keldran oversees operations from Orgrimmar to clear those remnants before hostile Alliance factions can use them to justify war.",sp=0},{t="Outpost in the Wastes",b="Orders south lead through the Charred Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains and into Desolace. Just north of the vast Kodo Graveyard stands Ghost Walker Post. Horde agents such as Takata Steelblade watch the wastes, where rampant centaur tribes and spreading demonic corruption both threaten the region.",sp=0},{t="Pragmatic Alliances",b="Takata Steelblade sees the assignment with grim pragmatism. Clearing the local demons also eases pressure on violent centaur tribes and helps the Horde's resident warlocks. Still, the duty comes first: removing the Burning Legion's footholds protects the Horde, whatever others gain from the purge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde concerned about the Alliance here?",a="Alliance forces advancing across Kalimdor could use active demon infestations as proof that the Horde still consorts with the Burning Legion. By purging local demons, the Horde hopes to blunt those accusations.",al={"why worry about alliance","horde alliance relations desolace","alliance accusations"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Keldran?",a="Keldran is a Horde operative in Orgrimmar who, with the Warchief's approval, oversees operations against demons that threaten the Horde's standing.",al={"keldran","who is keldran","keldran orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Ghost Walker Post located?",a="Ghost Walker Post lies in central Desolace, directly south of the pass from the Charred Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains and just north of the Kodo Graveyard.",al={"ghost walker post location","where is takata steelblade","finding ghost walker post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Takata Steelblade?",a="Takata Steelblade is a Horde soldier at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. The Warchief tasks him with keeping regional threats, including demons and hostile centaur, in check.",al={"takata steelblade","who is steelblade","steelblade desolace"},it="target"},{q="Why does Takata mention aiding the centaur?",a="The centaur claim Desolace as their territory but cannot contain the growing demon threat. Culling the demons also helps the centaur survive, a compromise Takata accepts for the Horde's security.",al={"helping centaur","centaur desolace","why aid centaur"},it="conflict"},{q="How do warlocks tie into this mission?",a="Takata notes with distaste that clearing wild demons and their influence also aids the controversial warlocks who operate within the Horde.",al={"warlock connection","why help warlocks","warlocks in the horde"},it="allies"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The mission reflects Warchief Thrall's effort to legitimize the new Horde and bury the legacy of demonic servitude before hostile neighbors can exploit it.",["class:Warlock"]="Soldiers such as Takata Steelblade view dark powers with suspicion, yet operations against wild demons often cross paths with the Horde's pragmatic use of warlocks.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs seeking to honor Thrall's vision of redemption, any lingering hint of demonic taint in Kalimdor threatens their hard-won freedom."},kw={"alliance relations","burning legion","charred vale","desolace","ghost walker post","keldran","kodo graveyard","takata steelblade"},rel={"quest:1431","npc:keldran","npc:takata-steelblade","subzone:ghost-walker-post","zone:desolace","topic:burning-legion","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:kodo-graveyard"},m={start="Keldran",["end"]="Takata Steelblade",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1432},src={"Alliance Relations (2)"}}
E["quest:1501"] = {t="quest",n="Creature of the Void",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye sends a young warlock after the stolen Tablet of Verga. The rogue Burning Blade cultists took it to their cavern at Skull Rock, and its runes are needed to summon a voidwalker.",h="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye sends a young warlock after the stolen Tablet of Verga.",sec={{t="A Precarious Art",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye trains Horde warlocks in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. Thrall's new realm regards fel magic with deep wariness because of the orcish clans' dark history. Gan'rul says few true warlocks remain in the Horde, but their perilous skills are essential to its survival. To serve the Warchief, an initiate must learn more than the chaotic fire of an imp; they must command beings of pure shadow and endurance.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Tablet",b="The runes needed to summon a voidwalker are inscribed on the Tablet of Verga. The Burning Blade, a fanatical shadow cult, stole the relic and hides in a cavern at Skull Rock, right beneath the Warchief's nose. Gan'rul sends you into the cultists' den to recover the tablet and strike a bloody blow against the renegades who stain the name of all practicing warlocks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a senior warlock trainer in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He oversees young Horde warlocks, teaching them to harness dark powers and bind otherworldly minions without falling to corruption.",al={"gan'rul","ganrul bloodeye","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tablet of Verga?",a="The Tablet of Verga bears the specialized summoning runes needed to call a voidwalker from the Nether. The Burning Blade stole it, and Gan'rul needs it to guide the initiate through the ritual.",al={"tablet of verga","verga tablet","what is the tablet"},it="item"},{q="Where is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a shadowy cavern directly east of Orgrimmar, along Durotar's rugged bluffs. Burning Blade cultists hide there.",al={"skull rock location","where is skull rock","where to find tablet"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye despise the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade serves demonic masters and undermines Thrall's Horde. Gan'rul sees the cult as a nuisance to the Warchief and a reckless blight that brings suspicion and disrepute on all practicing warlocks.",al={"burning blade warlock","why hate burning blade"},it="conflict"},{q="Why do warlocks need to summon a voidwalker?",a="Voidwalkers are beings of the Nether that can absorb tremendous punishment and protect their summoner. Learning to bind one is an essential step in a warlock's survival and summoning power.",al={"why voidwalker","voidwalker purpose"},it="power"},{q="What happens after retrieving the tablet?",a="After Gan'rul receives the Tablet of Verga, he gives the initiate the needed runes and summons them to complete the ritual in 'The Binding'. There, the warlock must physically subdue the summoned voidwalker to master it.",al={"next quest","what comes next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want this done?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye feels the acute pressure of having very few warlocks left in the Horde. He believes that pushing promising acolytes like you to mature quickly is vital to serving the Horde and the Warchief. Recovering the stolen Tablet of Verga not only advances your instruction by granting the runes to summon a voidwalker, but it also strikes a blow against the Burning Blade cultists who stole it and continually stain the reputation of all warlocks.",al={"ganrul motive","why ganrul sends you","why recover the tablet"},it="motive",add="b65e3db1"},{q="Who are you sent against at Skull Rock?",a="You are sent against the cultists of the Burning Blade hiding in Skull Rock, just east of Orgrimmar. These rogue warlocks conspire against the Horde and stole the Tablet of Verga from Gan'rul. They operate in the shadows of Durotar, using demonic magic outside the Warchief's law and creating constant trouble for the young nation.",al={"who is at skull rock","burning blade skull rock","who took the tablet"},it="target",add="6701b0d8"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye send you instead of the city guards?",a="The Darkfire Enclave operates under tense tolerance within Thrall's Orgrimmar. Calling upon the city guard to hunt down stolen occult artifacts would invite unwanted scrutiny into Gan'rul's covert practices. More importantly, facing the trials of Skull Rock is a necessary test of your growing power: a warlock must prove capable of confronting demonic corruption before being trusted to summon and bind a creature of the Void.",al={"why send an apprentice","why not send guards","why me creature of the void"},it="why_me",add="2e9ce581"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face a fundamental rite of passage: moving beyond small imps to command a frontline shadow minion.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of Thrall's Horde, you belong to a people wary of fel practitioners. Mentors like Gan'rul guide those who study the dark arts to use their power in service to the Warchief.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc haunted by the Shadow Council's history, you can find a measure of vengeance in hunting the Burning Blade, whose members still embrace demonic ruin."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","creature of the void","gan'rul bloodeye","orgrimmar","skull rock","tablet of verga","voidwalker","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1506","quest:1471","quest:827","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="11",faction="Horde",id=1501,ri={"Tablet of Verga"}},src={"Creature of the Void (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:1504"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, The Binding marks young Horde warlocks' final initiation ritual. Gan'rul Bloodeye directs each petitioner to use glyphs from the Tablet of Verga in Neeru Fireblade's summoning circle.",h="In Orgrimmar, The Binding marks young Horde warlocks' final initiation ritual.",sec={{t="Subjugation of the Void",b="You face your first true test of will when you summon a voidwalker. An imp is child's play by comparison. Warlocks do not make pacts with these creatures or commune with them. You pull them across dimensions by force and bind them to serve. Gan'rul Bloodeye directs you to use glyphs from the Tablet of Verga and call the voidwalker into Neeru Fireblade's ritual circle, to break it there in single combat.",sp=0},{t="An Unending Vigil",b="Defeating the voidwalker in physical and magical combat is only half the struggle. Gan'rul Bloodeye warns that a bound voidwalker never truly accepts its enslavement. Even while it guards its master in battle as a durable, shadowy bulwark, it waits for a lapse in your concentration. If your hold over your servant ever falters, it will consume the soul of the one who bound it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is being summoned?",a="You summon a voidwalker, a towering being forged of cosmic shadow and void energies. Unlike mischievous imps, voidwalkers are brutish entities ripped from the Twisting Nether and the Void. Warlocks use them chiefly to absorb devastating physical blows.",al={"what is summoned","what demon","voidwalker lore"},it="target"},{q="Where does this summoning ritual take place?",a="The ritual takes place inside Neeru Fireblade's tent in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. A summoning circle inscribed on the ground focuses the dimensional energies needed to tear a voidwalker from the Nether.",al={"where do i summon","summoning circle location","ritual site"},it="place"},{q="What is the Tablet of Verga used for?",a="The Tablet of Verga holds ancient, specialized glyphs used to manifest a voidwalker and tear it through the fabric of reality. You study its inscriptions to craft the Glyphs of Summoning needed to make the summoning circle.",al={"tablet of verga","glyphs of summoning"},it="item"},{q="Why must the warlock defeat the voidwalker?",a="Warlocks control extraplanar creatures through sheer dominance. The voidwalker yields its essence and obeys commands only after you prove your mastery by defeating it in physical and magical combat.",al={"why kill the voidwalker","why fight it","binding process"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a senior Horde warlock trainer in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He oversees the dark education of young Horde practitioners and teaches them to enslave more potent demonic entities.",al={"who is ganrul","gan'rul bloodeye"},it="identity"},{q="Can a bound voidwalker ever be fully trusted?",a="Never. A voidwalker may serve for years without resistance while waiting for its master to let their guard down. The bond demands constant vigilance, for the creature harbors eternal resentment toward its captor.",al={"will voidwalker turn on me","is voidwalker loyal","can demons rebel"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want this done?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye serves as an instructor for promising warlocks gathering in the Cleft of Shadow. He tests and shapes your discipline by pushing you to expand your repertoire of dark magic. For you to command greater fel forces in service to the Horde, you must prove your mastery by calling forth and dominating a resilient voidwalker.",al={"ganrul bloodeye motive","why summon voidwalker ganrul","why does ganrul want me to bind a voidwalker"},it="motive",add="066e41c9"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye have you fight the voidwalker yourself?",a="A summoned minion can only be bound through the sheer willpower and strength of the warlock commanding it. Neither Gan'rul Bloodeye nor the city guards can bend the demon's spirit to your service. You must conquer it through your own magical and martial might, demonstrating that your mind and spirit are strong enough to keep it enslaved.",al={"why fight voidwalker alone","why cant ganrul fight voidwalker","why me voidwalker binding"},it="why_me",add="3b87ecbf"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you move from dabbling with imps to commanding frontline terrors of shadow. The rite teaches that power must be conquered and enslaved.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you practice the dark arts in hidden corners like the Cleft of Shadow, far from Warchief Thrall's disapproving gaze and the shamanic revival.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde officially turns away from the demonic corruption of the past, yet tolerates warlock magic beneath Orgrimmar as a pragmatic necessity, under watchful eyes."},kw={"cleft of shadow","gan'rul bloodeye","glyphs of summoning","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","tablet of verga","the binding","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"quest:1473","quest:1506","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:829","zone:orgrimmar","quest:1471"},m={start="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="11",faction="Horde",id=1504},src={"The Binding (Voidwalker, Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:1506"] = {t="quest",n="Gan'rul's Summons",z="orgrimmar",s="Ophek brings Gan'rul's Summons to young Horde warlocks in Razor Hill. Gan'rul Bloodeye calls them to the Cleft of Shadow to advance their training. There, they take the first step toward summoning a voidwalker.",h="Ophek brings Gan'rul's Summons to young Horde warlocks in Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Shadows",b="In Durotar, novice warlocks do not go unnoticed for long. When a practitioner shows enough mastery over an initial imp, word reaches the deep caverns beneath Orgrimmar. Ophek carries messages for the senior dark casters from his post in Durotar. He finds warlocks with an urgent demand to leave their work and report to the Cleft of Shadow.",sp=0},{t="The Senior Warlock",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye oversees the training of young orc warlocks within the Horde. From the hidden caverns beneath Orgrimmar, he hones their lethal fel power while keeping these dangerous arts from the Warchief's disapproving gaze. A call to his circle means simple fire spells and imps are no longer enough. The apprentice is ready to bind a creature from the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ophek?",a="Ophek is an associate of the warlocks stationed in Durotar. He watches for rising practitioners and carries orders from senior mentors such as Gan'rul Bloodeye.",al={"ophek","who gives this quest","quest starter"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gan'rul Bloodeye located?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is in the Cleft of Shadow, a dark cavern system beneath Orgrimmar's rocky plateaus.",al={"where is ganrul","gan'rul location","find gan'rul bloodeye"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want to see me?",a="Gan'rul considers you ready to advance your warlock studies and begin the dangerous rites to summon and bind a voidwalker.",al={"why summons","what does ganrul want","quest reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after reporting to Gan'rul?",a="Reporting to Gan'rul begins Creature of the Void. You are sent to find the components and knowledge needed to draw a void entity into Azeroth.",al={"next quest","what comes after gan'rul's summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the warlocks stay in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Warlocks practice volatile fel magic, which Thrall and the traditional shamanic Horde regard with deep suspicion. The Cleft of Shadow lets them perform rituals out of public view.",al={"why cleft of shadow","why are warlocks hiding","warlock cave orgrimmar"},it="why_here"},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Only Horde warlocks who have reached the tenth circle of their training can receive the summons.",al={"is this warlock only","who gets this quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ophek send you to Gan'rul?",a="Ophek acts simply as an errand runner and messenger for Gan'rul Bloodeye. Senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow do not wander Orgrimmar hunting down apprentices themselves; they send lackeys to fetch who they need. Ophek knows better than to delay Gan'rul's summons, warning you that keeping a warlock master waiting rarely ends well.",al={"why does ophek send me","ophek motive","why is ophek delivering the summons"},it="motive",add="f5421555"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, this summons marks your path beyond basic imp conjuration. It opens the way to command a voidwalker's sturdy protection.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know warlocks hold an uneasy place in Thrall's new Horde. Their pragmatic power is tolerated, while they remain secluded beneath Orgrimmar."},kw={"bloodeye","cleft of shadow","gan'rul","ophek","orgrimmar","summons","voidwalker","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1473","quest:1471","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Ophek",["end"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1506},src={"Gan'rul's Summons"}}
E["quest:1507"] = {t="quest",n="Devourer of Souls",z="orgrimmar",s="Gan'rul Bloodeye sends an aspiring Horde warlock to begin the path to summoning and commanding a succubus. In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, the warlock seeks Cazul's counsel on luring and binding the demon.",h="Gan'rul Bloodeye sends an aspiring Horde warlock to begin the path to summoning and commanding a succubus.",sec={{t="A Step Into Seductive Shadows",b="Horde warlocks who master lesser demons such as imps and voidwalkers may seek a succubus next. Gan'rul Bloodeye oversees the dark arts beneath Orgrimmar and judges when a warlock is ready to call one from the Twisting Nether. A succubus can turn the frail against themselves, so binding one takes subtlety as well as strength.",sp=0},{t="The Lore of Cazul",b="A succubus preys on mortal desire, so raw incantations cannot call one alone. The summoner must lure it with an object filled with pure love and devotion. Gan'rul is unwilling or unable to provide such a relic himself, so he sends the warlock across the Cleft of Shadow to Cazul. The ancient warlock knows the arcane and demonic rites needed for the next part of the ritual.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This begins an aspiring Horde warlock's path to learning how to summon and command a succubus. It connects you with mentors in the Cleft of Shadow, who teach you the demon's nature and how to lure one from the Twisting Nether.",al={"why do devourer of souls","succubus quest start","what does this quest unlock"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I find Cazul?",a="Cazul is in the Cleft of Shadow, a cavern beneath Orgrimmar where rogue and warlock trainers practice away from the Warchief's scrutiny.",al={"cazul location","where is cazul","find cazul orgrimmar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a warlock need an object of love to summon a succubus?",a="Succubi feed on mortal emotion, devotion, and weak will. To draw one from the Twisting Nether, a summoner offers a potent token of genuine devotion and affection as bait, then overpowers and binds the demon.",al={"succubus bait love","why love item for succubus","succubus summoning lore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a senior Horde warlock trainer in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He guides developing practitioners through the bindings of increasingly powerful demonic servants.",al={"who gives devourer of souls","gan'rul lore","ganrul bloodeye"},it="identity"},{q="What level is required to begin this quest?",a="A warlock must reach level twenty before Gan'rul judges their magical prowess and mental fortitude sufficient. The ritual means bargaining with a succubus and surviving the encounter.",al={"what level for succubus","devourer of souls level","succubus chain level req"},gp=true},{q="What follows after speaking with Cazul?",a="Speaking with Cazul leads to Blind Cazul. There, you seek Zankaja in Orgrimmar, whose mate Dogran has not returned from duty at the Crossroads. The search for a suitable token of love begins with her.",al={"next quest after devourer of souls","what comes after cazul","succubus quest progression"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want you to summon a succubus?",a="As a mentor among the Horde's warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow, Gan'rul Bloodeye exists to guide you into deeper, more potent arts of dark magic. He believes you possess the mental strength and cunning necessary to tame a succubus rather than succumb to its allure. To him, every servant you successfully bind expands the influence and lethal reach of your shared demonic craft.",al={"why does gan'rul want this","gan'rul bloodeye motive","why summon succubus gan'rul"},it="motive",add="0f1c8f0b"},{q="Why does Gan'rul send you instead of seeking the bait himself?",a="A warlock cannot simply be handed absolute mastery over a demon; the binding must be forged through your personal trial and resourcefulness. Gan'rul expects you to prove your worth by uncovering the required token of devotion and bending the fiend to your will alone, establishing your own dominance rather than relying on another's power.",al={"why me gan'rul","why send me for succubus","why can't gan'rul do it"},it="why_me",add="cde5d57b"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you take a step toward commanding demons of mental dominance and seduction. The rite calls for psychological resolve as well as raw fel power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see warlocks conduct dangerous rites in the Cleft of Shadow's damp, secluded crevices. Thrall's shamans and warriors practice in public, while warlocks work out of sight."},kw={"binding","cazul","cleft of shadow","gan'rul bloodeye","orgrimmar","succubus","summoning","warlock"},rel={"npc:cazul","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:1508","quest:1509","quest:1515","quest:1512","quest:1471"},m={start="Gan'rul Bloodeye",["end"]="Cazul",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1507},src={"Devourer of Souls (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:1508"] = {t="quest",n="Blind Cazul",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Cleft of Shadow, an initiate seeks Blind Cazul’s help with a succubus ritual. The sightless warlock points toward an object charged with mortal emotion.",h="In the Cleft of Shadow, an initiate seeks Blind Cazul’s help with a succubus ritual.",sec={{t="A Matter of Enticement",b="A succubus answers to mortal longing, sorrow, and desire. To draw one across the veil, an aspiring summoner needs more than willpower; the demon is known to devour souls. Blind Cazul understands what the initiate seeks and knows where to find a fitting lure.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Bluffs",b="Though blind, Blind Cazul senses the lives and sorrows within Orgrimmar’s red ramparts. He sends the initiate to Zankaja, an orc woman who lives atop the bluffs near the wind rider roost. She anxiously awaits her mate Dogran’s return, and her despair can draw a demon’s attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cazul?",a="Cazul is a sightless warlock who quietly helps the warlocks of the Cleft of Shadow. He identifies reagents and conduits for demonic summonings.",al={"blind cazul","who is cazul"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Cazul send you to Zankaja?",a="A succubus ritual needs an item shaped by powerful mortal yearning or love. Zankaja waits in distress for her missing mate, Dogran, and her bond with him offers the emotional lure the initiate seeks.",al={"why zankaja","what does zankaja have"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Zankaja be found in Orgrimmar?",a="Zankaja lives on Orgrimmar’s elevated bluffs, west of the wind rider roost. Cross the bridge from the flight tower and look in the nearby dwellings to the right.",al={"zankaja location","where is zankaja"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after speaking to Zankaja?",a="Zankaja is distressed because her mate Dogran has vanished. After speaking with her, you search the Barrens for word of his fate and begin the effort to retrieve a potent token of love.",al={"what comes next","next step after cazul"},it="next_step"},{q="What kind of demon is this quest preparing you to summon?",a="You are preparing to summon and enslave a succubus, a demon that wields seduction and psychic torment.",al={"which pet","demon reward"},it="power"},{q="Why must warlocks exploit personal tragedies for their rituals?",a="A succubus is drawn to intense mortal feeling, especially passion, devotion, and heartbreak. Warlocks use tokens marked by grief or desire as spiritual bait in the summoning ritual.",al={"warlock morality","why use dogran"},it="history"},{q="Why does Cazul want you to find Zankaja?",a="Cazul acts as an instructor and elder in the shadows of the Cleft of Shadow. When Gan'rul Bloodeye sends an aspiring warlock his way, Cazul's role is to guide you toward the ingredients required to bind a succubus. Summoning such a demon demands an object imbued with love and raw longing. Cazul knows that Zankaja's grief and desperation over her missing mate, Dogran, can yield the emotional anchor you need to entice a devourer of souls to your side.",al={"cazul motive","why help zankaja cazul","cazul why send to zankaja"},it="motive",add="a1700788"},{q="Why does Cazul send you instead of going to Zankaja himself?",a="This task is part of your initiation as a warlock, not ordinary city business. Cazul is an old, blind hermit dwelling within the shadowy depths of Orgrimmar, quietly guiding novices in dark rites. Warlock training requires you to forge your own bindings and personally gather the components for your demons. Furthermore, the Orgrimmar guards would have no interest in aiding forbidden demonic rituals, meaning the burden of following this trail of sorrow falls squarely upon you.",al={"why me cazul","why send player to zankaja","why does cazul need me"},it="why_me",add="fea16628"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn that demonic conjuring depends on emotional resonance as well as fel magic. A succubus is lured by a conduit charged with mortal feeling.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the dark arts of the Cleft of Shadow at work beneath the capital, touching ordinary lives on the mesas above."},kw={"blind cazul","cazul","cleft of shadow","dogran","orgrimmar","succubus","warlock","zankaja"},rel={"npc:cazul","npc:zankaja","quest:1472","quest:1509","quest:1515","quest:1512","quest:1471","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Cazul",["end"]="Zankaja",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1508},src={"Blind Cazul"}}
E["quest:1509"] = {t="quest",n="News of Dogran",z="orgrimmar",s="A missing grunt named Dogran leaves Zankaja waiting in Orgrimmar. His mate has heard nothing for days, so she sends you to question his superior, Gazrog, at the Crossroads. For a warlock, the search also serves a ritual to bind a succubus.",h="A missing grunt named Dogran leaves Zankaja waiting in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Mate's Despair",b="Zankaja waits on the bluffs of Orgrimmar, fearing for her mate Dogran. He was sent to the Crossroads on an honorable promotion, but his return is overdue and she has heard nothing for days. She asks you to seek news from his commander, Gazrog. She does not know that dark arts are at work behind the search.",sp=0},{t="Grim Tidings in the Barrens",b="Gazrog tells you what happened to Dogran at the Crossroads, the central Horde outpost in the Barrens. Quilboar infest the plains, and Dogran has fallen into their hands. He still lives, but his capture is a grim truth Gazrog hesitates to send back to Zankaja.",sp=1},{t="An Instrument of Summoning",b="The warlock's search for Dogran also serves the work of summoning and mastering a succubus. The binding ritual calls for relics touched by true emotion. Dogran's suffering and his bond with Zankaja provide the emotional conduit the ritual needs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dogran?",a="Dogran is an orc grunt stationed in the Barrens, recently promoted to the Crossroads. He is Zankaja's mate, and she lives in Orgrimmar.",al={"dogran lore","who is dogran","grunt dogran"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a warlock care about a missing orc guard?",a="Warlock mentors in the Cleft of Shadow direct you to seek news of Dogran. The binding ritual for a succubus needs relics touched by deep mortal emotions, including love, devotion, and suffering.",al={"why warlock quest","why do warlocks do this","succubus connection"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is Gazrog located?",a="Gazrog is at the Crossroads in the Barrens, where he helps manage Horde defenses against local threats.",al={"where is gazrog","gazrog location","crossroads gazrog"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to Dogran?",a="Dogran is overdue to return to Zankaja, who has heard nothing from him for days. She asks you to seek news from Gazrog at the Crossroads.",al={"is dogran dead","where is dogran","dogran fate"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Zankaja gives it to you on the bluffs of Orgrimmar, after the warlock trainer Cazul directs you to her.",al={"quest giver","where to start news of dogran"},it="people"},{q="What comes next in the chain?",a="Continue your inquiries in the Barrens to learn Dogran's fate and carry the news onward.",al={"what next","next quest","succubus chain continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Zankaja want you to find news of Dogran?",a="Dogran is Zankaja's mate. He took immense pride in his recent promotion and assignment to the Crossroads, but the Barrens are far more treacherous than the safety of Orgrimmar's walls. He is now over a week overdue to return, and she has received no word at all. Torn between dread and hope, she cannot bear the silence any longer and needs someone to track down his commanding contact.",al={"why does zankaja want this","zankaja motive","why look for dogran"},it="motive",add="7a20ce20"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you move from dark texts in Orgrimmar to using mortal tragedy in your effort to claim a succubus.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the danger its grunts face while securing the Crossroads of Kalimdor from hostile threats.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see in Zankaja's grief the personal cost of the Horde's expansion and defense across Durotar and the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","cazul","crossroads","dogran","gazrog","news of dogran","quilboar","succubus","zankaja"},rel={"npc:zankaja","npc:gazrog","npc:cazul","quest:1508","quest:1515","quest:1511","quest:1471","zone:barrens"},m={start="Zankaja",["end"]="Gazrog",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1509},src={"News of Dogran"}}
E["quest:1512"] = {t="quest",n="Love's Gift",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye awaits a pendant for the succubus rite. Dogran gives up a treasured keepsake after being found and revived in the Barrens.",h="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye awaits a pendant for the succubus rite.",sec={{t="A Grunt's Sacrifice",b="Grunt Dogran was held and tortured by the Bristleback quilboar in the Barrens. Ken'zigla's draught brings him back to consciousness, but his body cannot recover. He chooses to meet death in battle rather than return to his mate, Zankaja, unable to fight. Dogran gives up a dirt-caked pendant, a gift born of love, and asks that Zankaja never learn what he surrendered.",sp=1},{t="Bait for a Demon",b="A warlock needs a talisman charged with strong, unblemished emotion to summon and control a succubus. These demons feed on mortal desire and twist genuine affection into anguish. Dogran's pendant bears his devotion and their parting. Bring it to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar's shadowy clefts, where it is cleaned and polished. Its bright emotional force can draw the soul-devourer across the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does a warlock need Dogran's pendant?",a="Succubi are drawn to deep mortal passions, which they twist and consume. Dogran's pendant holds selfless love and sacrifice, making it a potent lure for a succubus.",al={"why pendant","succubus bait","why dirt-caked pendant"},it="item"},{q="Who is Grunt Dogran?",a="Grunt Dogran is a Horde warrior captured and tortured by the Bristleback quilboar in the southern Barrens. An alchemical tonic revives him, but his injuries leave him unable to live as a proud warrior.",al={"who is dogran","grunt dogran lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Zankaja?",a="Zankaja is Dogran's young mate, who waited anxiously for news of him. He gives up her token and chooses to seek a warrior's death rather than burden her with caring for him.",al={"zankaja lore","dogran mate"},sp=1,it="people"},{q="Why does Dogran ask you to keep this secret from Zankaja?",a="Dogran does not want his young mate bound to a dying invalid. He gives up her pendant, knowing it will not return to her, and asks that she be spared the guilt of learning how his fate ended.",al={"why not tell zankaja","dogran secret"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Who cleans the pendant and why?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye, the warlock trainer in Orgrimmar, takes the pendant and cleans away its filth. Its bright appearance and emotional force can then draw the summoned demon.",al={"gan'rul bloodeye role","why clean the pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens immediately after completing this quest?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye sends you to carry the purified pendant into the summoning circle beneath Orgrimmar. There you cast the binding rite and face the succubus alone.",al={"what comes next","next quest after love's gift"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Grunt Dogran send you away with his pendant?",a="Dogran refuses to live on as an invalid chained to his young mate, Zankaja. Rather than returning home broken and burdening her with sorrow or guilt, he intends to seek out a glorious warrior's death in battle instead of fading away as an empty husk. Parting with the pendant and sending you away lets him sever that tie so he can meet his end with honor on his own terms.",al={"why does dogran give you the pendant","dogran motive loves gift","why give away dirt-caked pendant"},it="motive",add="528517eb"},{q="Why does Dogran need you to deliver the pendant?",a="Dogran is in no condition to travel to Orgrimmar himself, having just endured brutal captivity and torture at the hands of the Bristleback quilboar. Furthermore, he explicitly intends to find a soldier's end on the battlefield rather than return to civilization. You are the only trusted outsider who reached him, making you his sole means of delivering the keepsake to Gan'rul without revealing his fate to Zankaja.",al={"why me loves gift","why does dogran need me","why cant dogran take the pendant"},it="why_me",add="6232e4f3"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn that arcane power alone cannot bind a demon. A succubus can be ensnared by turning its hunger for mortal passions like love and grief against it.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Grunt Dogran choose death in battle over life as a burden to his kin."},kw={"dirt-caked pendant","gan'rul bloodeye","grunt dogran","love's gift","orgrimmar","succubus","the barrens","zankaja"},rel={"npc:grunt-dogran","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","npc:zankaja","quest:1471","quest:1515","quest:1511","quest:1472","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Grunt Dogran",["end"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1512},src={"Love's Gift"}}
E["quest:1513"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="orgrimmar",s="At Neeru Fireblade's circle in Orgrimmar, a warlock faces the trial of binding a succubus. Dogran's Pendant draws the demon from the Twisting Nether, where spellcraft and force of arms must break its will.",h="At Neeru Fireblade's circle in Orgrimmar, a warlock faces the trial of binding a succubus.",sec={{t="A Demon's Anchor",b="Dogran's Pendant binds memory to the summoning. The maimed orc gave it up, but it had been a keepsake of his love for Zankaja, carried through captivity and torment. That devotion gives the pendant the force to reach across realms, bridge the Twisting Nether, and seize a succubus's attention.",sp=1},{t="The Circle in the Shadows",b="Beneath the clefts of Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade keeps a tent with a circle prepared for dangerous rites. Under Gan'rul Bloodeye's guidance, you activate its runes and face the summoned succubus in battle. Calling a demon is only the beginning; you must overpower it alone and bend its spirit to your will.",sp=0},{t="Wiles and Willpower",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye warns that succubi can make dangerous thralls. Their presence intoxicates and tempts the senses, while they drain the vitality and spirit of careless masters. He tells you to remember Dogran and Zankaja's sorrow, lest pride and overconfidence leave you open to the demon's wiles. Only an unyielding will can resist its allure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens during this ritual?",a="You bring Dogran's Pendant to the circle inside Neeru Fireblade's tent in the Cleft of Shadow. Its devotion draws a succubus from the Twisting Nether, and you battle the demon until it submits to your will.",al={"how does the ritual work","what do you do in the binding","succubus ritual"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The summoning takes place in Neeru Fireblade's tent in the Cleft of Shadow, beneath Orgrimmar. A ritual circle is inscribed in the floor.",al={"where is the circle","summoning circle location","where do i summon the succubus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Dogran and why is his pendant needed?",a="Dogran was a Horde grunt captured and maimed by quilboar in the Barrens. His pendant, a keepsake of his beloved Zankaja, draws and anchors a succubus.",al={"who is dogran","why dograns pendant","dogran story"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a senior warlock trainer in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He mentors rising warlocks and guides them through rites of demon subjugation.",al={"who gives the quest","who is ganrul","ganrul bloodeye role"},it="identity"},{q="What power does a warlock gain upon completing this trial?",a="Subduing the succubus completes a warlock's training and grants the knowledge and runic mastery to summon one into service at any time.",al={"what reward do warlocks get","why summon succubus","succubus pet ability"},it="power"},{q="Why is summoning a succubus considered especially dangerous?",a="Succubi charm mortals and play on their desires. An overconfident warlock risks having their soul slowly siphoned away, until the demon's guile overcomes their command.",al={"succubus danger","why are succubi risky","succubus lore"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye want this done?",a="As a mentor to the Horde's developing warlocks, Gan'rul Bloodeye must test your will and magical strength before granting you command over dangerous demonic servitors. By instructing you to summon and subjugate a succubus using the tragic remnant of Dogran's love, he teaches you caution against demonic trickery and pride. Once you prevail, Gan'rul also intends to return Dogran's pendant and deliver the news to Zankaja.",al={"ganrul bloodeye motive","why summon succubus ganrul","why binding quest"},it="motive",add="9ef07cc1"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye need you to perform the summoning instead of doing it himself?",a="This ritual is a rite of passage meant solely for you. A warlock must personally bend a summoned demon to their will; no teacher or city guard can establish that psychic dominance on your behalf. If Gan'rul were to subdue the creature himself, you would gain neither the discipline nor the authority required to bind and command a succubus of your own.",al={"why me binding","why cant ganrul summon the succubus","why do i have to summon it"},it="why_me",add="9690a59c"},{q="Who are you sent against during the ritual?",a="You are pitted against a summoned succubus, drawn forth across the Twisting Nether into the summoning circle within Neeru Fireblade's tent. These cunning demonic temptresses delight in manipulating mortal passions and devouring souls. By baiting the fiend with Dogran's pendant—an object steeped in mortal love and tragedy—you force it into reality to defeat and master it.",al={"binding target","what do you fight in the binding","summoned succubus"},it="target",add="dee6d59e"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you prove your will can master the cunning, disruptive demons of the Nether and withstand their seductive perils.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how the faction tolerates demonic practitioners in secret within the Cleft of Shadow, away from the city's honor-bound populace.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you carry the bitter weight of your people's past corruption when dealing with demons. Gan'rul's demand for discipline and control bears that history."},kw={"binding","cleft of shadow","dogran","gan'rul","neeru","orgrimmar","pendant","succubus","warlock","zankaja"},rel={"npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1512","quest:1515","quest:1511","quest:1509","quest:1508","quest:1472","npc:zankaja"},m={start="Gan'rul Bloodeye",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1513},src={"The Binding (Succubus, Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:1531"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Air",z="orgrimmar",s="At Grommash Hold, Searn Firewarder sends seasoned shamans south to seek the Air Totem. Prate Cloudseer guides them toward the final elemental pillar of their craft.",h="At Grommash Hold, Searn Firewarder sends seasoned shamans south to seek the Air Totem.",sec={{t="A Breath from the South",b="A shaman who has earned the favor of earth, fire, and water now stands ready to harness air, the last of the four elements. In Orgrimmar, troll trainer Searn Firewarder recognizes when a disciple has reached the height of early training and is prepared for this final foundational step. He sends the shaman south across the Barrens, then down into the canyon labyrinth of Thousand Needles.",sp=0},{t="The Cloudseer's Hermitage",b="Prate Cloudseer waits in a high cave among the sandstone mesas of Thousand Needles. The hermit lives quietly with her partner, far from Horde encampments. She demands deference before revealing the secrets of the wind. Meet her with proper respect, and she shares the knowledge and focus to manifest the Air Totem, completing the shaman's elemental circle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Searn Firewarder, a troll shaman trainer in Grommash Hold, offers this to qualified shamans when they reach the appropriate experience.",al={"quest giver","where to get call of air","searn firewarder"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Prate Cloudseer?",a="Prate Cloudseer lives in Thousand Needles. After taking the Great Lift down from the southern Barrens, head east across the canyon floor to find her cave.",al={"prate cloudseer location","find prate","air totem npc"},gp=true},{q="What is the Air Totem used for?",a="The Air Totem is the fourth and final elemental focus a shaman acquires. It lets a shaman invoke air spells and totems, with speed, grace, and wind-based powers.",al={"air totem purpose","why do air totem quest","what does air totem do"},it="power"},{q="Why does Searn Firewarder send you so far away?",a="Mastery of the elements requires finding mentors devoted to communing with specific spirits. Prate Cloudseer knows the winds of the shifting canyon gusts in Thousand Needles, making her the ideal guide to air.",al={"why thousand needles","why prate cloudseer"},it="purpose"},{q="Do I need to complete other elemental totem quests first?",a="Yes. Shaman training follows a strict progression through the elements: earth, then fire and water, and finally air.",al={"prerequisites","totem order","can i do air totem first"},gp=true},{q="Are there other versions of this quest for different cities?",a="Yes. Shaman trainers in other Horde capitals, including Thunder Bluff, give their own directions to Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.",al={"thunder bluff air totem","undercity air totem"},gp=true},{q="Why does Searn Firewarder send you to Prate Cloudseer?",a="Searn Firewarder sees that your spiritual growth as a shaman has advanced far enough to commune with the spirits of the air. He cannot bestow communion with the air totem himself, as that wisdom lies with Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. Guiding you toward her is his duty as a mentor, ensuring you learn proper respect for the capricious spirits of the wind from someone steeped in their ways.",al={"searn firewarder motive","why does searn want this done","why send to prate cloudseer"},it="motive",add="9e3dc8ab"},{q="Why does Searn Firewarder need you to go instead of doing this himself?",a="The path of a shaman is an individual spiritual journey that cannot be walked by proxy. Searn Firewarder already commands the elements and serves the Horde by training novices in Orgrimmar. Earning the air totem demands that you personally prove your humility, resilience, and respect directly before Prate Cloudseer and the winds she communes with.",al={"why me call of air","why do i have to go to prate","why doesn't searn go himself"},it="why_me",add="bc8bd922"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Air Totem is the culminating milestone of your early shamanic journey. It lets you call on wind spirits alongside earth, fire, and water.",["faction:Horde"]="The shamanic tradition ties the Horde's diverse races together. Far-flung elders and hermits across central Kalimdor pass down its sacred customs."},kw={"air totem","call of air","orgrimmar","prate cloudseer","searn firewarder","shaman quest","thousand needles","valley of spirits"},rel={"npc:searn-firewarder","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens"},m={start="Searn Firewarder",["end"]="Prate Cloudseer",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1531},src={"Call of Air (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:1858"] = {t="quest",n="The Shattered Hand",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Therzok tests rogues seeking a place in the Shattered Hand. He asks them to open Tazan's recovered satchel with a key taken from an unwitting accomplice.",h="In Orgrimmar, Therzok tests rogues seeking a place in the Shattered Hand.",sec={{t="A Test of Subtlety",b="After retrieving Tazan's locked satchel, you find it useless without the key. The Shattered Hand demands skill, not brute force against the complex lock. Therzok sends you to Gamon, a tauren drunkard who frequents Orgrimmar's tavern. Gamon is easily distracted and once helped Tazan, making him a fitting mark for quiet theft.",sp=0},{t="Welcome to the Shadows",b="Take the key from Gamon without alerting the tavern, then open the satchel and claim Tazan's logbook. Bring the stolen contents to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow to meet the Shattered Hand's standards. A clean job earns you formal recognition as one of its operatives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gamon and why does he have the key?",a="Gamon once assisted Tazan, the operative Therzok is investigating. While Tazan carried the satchel, he left its key with Gamon, an unsuspecting drunkard who spends his days drinking in Orgrimmar's central tavern.",al={"why gamon","who has the key","gamon key"},it="target"},{q="What is inside Tazan's satchel?",a="Tazan's logbook lies inside the locked satchel. It holds intelligence of interest to Therzok and the Shattered Hand, and recovering it tests your ability to secure vital information covertly.",al={"tazan's logbook","satchel contents","what is in the satchel"}},{q="What is the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar?",a="The Shattered Hand began as an infamous orcish clan from Draenor, known for self-mutilation and ruthlessness. In Orgrimmar, it has become the Horde's guild of assassins, spies, and rogues, working from the subterranean Cleft of Shadow.",al={"what is shattered hand","shattered hand rogues","orgrimmar rogues"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Therzok operate?",a="Therzok works from the Cleft of Shadow, a dim cavern network beneath Orgrimmar's rocky ridges. Warlocks, rogues, and shadowcraft gather there, away from daylight.",al={"where is therzok","therzok location","cleft of shadow rogue trainer"},it="place"},{q="Why doesn't Therzok just break open the satchel?",a="The satchel has a complex lock, and Therzok is testing a rogue's discipline. The Shattered Hand prizes precise theft and finesse over noisy destruction.",al={"why pickpocket","why need key"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Handing over Tazan's logbook completes your initiation. Therzok recognizes you as a member of the Shattered Hand and gives you tools for covert work.",al={"shattered hand reward","end of chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Therzok want Tazan's satchel opened?",a="Therzok and the Shattered Hand operate from the shadows of Orgrimmar, dealing in secrets and covert security for the Horde. Tazan held information vital to their operations, but the delicate contents remained locked away in a complicated satchel. Therzok wants the intelligence inside without destroying it, using the retrieval as a practical trial to see if you possess the cunning, stealth, and skill worthy of formal induction into their guild.",al={"therzok motive","why open the satchel","what does therzok want"},it="motive",add="74a53139"},{q="What is Tazan's Logbook?",a="Tazan's Logbook contains the written records and clandestine dealings of Tazan, an operative whose activities caught the attention of the Shattered Hand. Secured inside his locked satchel, the logbook holds the critical intelligence Therzok requires. Delivering it unmarred proves not only your ability to pick pockets and crack tricky locks, but also delivers valuable intelligence directly to Orgrimmar's spymasters.",al={"tazan logbook","what is in the logbook","tazan's logbook lore"},it="item",add="a30dee79"},{q="Why doesn't Therzok send the Orgrimmar guards after Gamon?",a="The Shattered Hand thrives on discretion and secrecy, far removed from the overt, honorable methods of the city guard. Involving Orgrimmar's grunts to seize a drunken tavern patron like Gamon would cause an unwanted public spectacle and alert any confederates Tazan may have had. Entrusting the theft to an aspiring rogue keeps the operation quiet while serving as a silent evaluation of your finesse.",al={"why me","why send rogue","why not city guards"},it="why_me",add="1b7f194d"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you learn to stalk an unaware target in a crowded place, take a key unnoticed, and secure vital intelligence.",["faction:Horde"]="Beneath the martial honor of Thrall's new Horde, covert reconnaissance remains necessary. The Shattered Hand handles it quietly from deep within Orgrimmar."},kw={"cleft of shadow","gamon","orgrimmar","pickpocket","rogue","shattered hand","tazan","therzok"},rel={"quest:1859","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","subzone:cleft"},m={start="Therzok",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1858,ri={"Tazan's Logbook"}},src={"The Shattered Hand (2)"}}
E["quest:1859"] = {t="quest",n="Therzok",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Therzok waits for a promising rogue from Durotar. Kaplak has seen your skill with violence and stealth and sends you to the Cleft of Shadow to meet a Shattered Hand operative.",h="In Orgrimmar, Therzok waits for a promising rogue from Durotar.",sec={{t="A Whispered Summons",b="Kaplak draws promising young rogues aside when they begin making a name for themselves in Durotar. The new Horde honors Thrall, but not all its servants fight openly beneath his banner. Word of a fighter skilled in violence and stealth, willing to bend the rules of open warfare, reaches the underground guild in Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="Into the Cleft of Shadow",b="Kaplak sends you beneath Orgrimmar's red stone cliffs to the Cleft of Shadow. Therzok waits in its gloom, out of sight of the city's grunts. There, lone cutpurses and ambushers are brought into the Shattered Hand, the Horde's covert network of daggers in the dark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Therzok?",a="Therzok is a Shattered Hand operative in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He meets promising young rogues arriving from Durotar's training grounds and brings them into the guild's service.",al={"who is therzok","therzok lore","npc therzok"},it="target"},{q="Why does Kaplak send me to him?",a="Kaplak sees your skill in combat and your talent for stealth and subterfuge. He knows the Shattered Hand seeks capable scoundrels, so he passes Therzok's request to recruit you.",al={"why send me to therzok","kaplak quest","why go to orgrimmar"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar?",a="In Orgrimmar, the Shattered Hand is a secret guild of assassins, spies, and thieves serving the Horde. They handle necessary, morally difficult work that Thrall's honorable warriors cannot perform openly.",al={"what is shattered hand","shattered hand orgrimmar","horde rogue guild"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Cleft of Shadow located?",a="The Cleft of Shadow is a cavern beneath central Orgrimmar. Dark passages lead down to it from the Valley of Strength and the Drag, and it shelters the city's warlocks and rogues from public scrutiny.",al={"where is cleft of shadow","how to find therzok","cleft of shadow location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after meeting Therzok?",a="After you greet Therzok, he introduces the duties of Shattered Hand service and assigns work to test your capability, stealth, and loyalty to the network.",al={"next quest","what does therzok want","after therzok"},it="next_step"},{q="Do non-rogues receive this quest?",a="No. Only rogues receive this summons after reaching a certain level of experience, marking their move from local skirmishes into the Horde's intelligence network.",al={"can other classes do this","is this rogue only","rogue quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kaplak choose you for this meeting?",a="Kaplak was explicitly ordered to scout for individuals matching your description. Word has reached the guild that you know how to hold your own in combat and are not above using stealth, deception, or less honorable means when necessary. Therzok has business in mind that requires someone with your specific, flexible set of talents.",al={"why me kaplak","why send me to therzok","why did kaplak pick me"},it="why_me",add="89f659b0"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, this summons brings you into the Shattered Hand, linking your solitary work in Durotar to the Horde's organized spy network.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Thrall preaches honor and the warrior spirit. Therzok's network shows the Horde also relies on unseen blades and secret intelligence gatherers."},kw={"assassin","cleft of shadow","durotar","kaplak","orgrimmar","rogue","shattered hand","therzok"},rel={"quest:1858","npc:kaplak","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft"},m={start="Kaplak",["end"]="Therzok",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1859},src={"Therzok (quest)"}}
E["quest:1943"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Deino",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Deino calls promising Horde mages to aid their craft. The troll mage works from the Valley of Spirits and seeks an adept for important work. Her summons opens a path to deeper study and duties across Kalimdor.",h="In Orgrimmar, Deino calls promising Horde mages to aid their craft.",sec={{t="A Summons to Orgrimmar",b="Horde mages hone their arcane abilities under the guidance of instructors. When a student is ready for harder work, mentors such as Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity point the way to Orgrimmar. In its troll quarter, specialized knowledge and dangerous work await.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Spirits and Darkbriar Lodge",b="Deino lives in Darkbriar Lodge in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. Among the Darkspear, few study arcane magic compared with the many witch doctors and priests, which makes Deino an authority in the capital. Her work serves Horde mages beyond local concerns, and she seeks ambitious spellcasters willing to face dangers far from home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Deino?",a="Mage trainers such as Anastasia Hartwell in Undercity's Magic Quarter send aspiring mages to Orgrimmar when their skill is sufficient.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","where do i get speak with deino"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can I find Deino?",a="You can find Deino inside Darkbriar Lodge, in the Valley of Spirits on Orgrimmar's western side.",al={"deino location","where is deino","darkbriar lodge location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Deino need assistance?",a="Deino oversees research and work important to Horde mages. She sends capable spellcasters into dangerous lands to find rare magical resources.",al={"why deino needs help","what does deino want"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after reporting to Deino?",a="When you report to Deino, she explains her work and sends you to gather the Waters of Xavian.",al={"next quest","what comes after","follow up quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest available to all classes?",a="No. Only Horde mages receive Deino's summons as part of their class training.",al={"is this mage only","can warlocks do this","class restriction"},gp=true},{q="Are troll mages common in the Horde?",a="Arcane magic is less common among Darkspear trolls than shamanism, voodoo, or service to the loa. Deino shows that some trolls have mastered the formal study of arcane forces.",al={"trolls using arcane","darkspear mages lore"},it="people"},{q="Why do the mage trainers send you to Deino?",a="As your command of the arcane grows, your mentors in the capital cities recognize that deeper mysteries await beyond standard training. Troll mage Deino in Orgrimmar oversees advanced undertakings crucial to the collective society of mages in the Horde. Trainers like Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity direct promising practitioners to her so you can contribute to matters vital to your shared craft.",al={"why send to deino","hartwell quithas motive","why does anastasia hartwell send me"},it="motive",add="2e9f17ef"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you deepen your arcane training and meet senior spellcasters in Orgrimmar.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see the focused arcane discipline practiced by a select few among the Darkspear.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you follow a summons linking trainers in Lordaeron and Durotar with Orgrimmar's arcane leaders."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","darkbriar lodge","deino","mage quest","orgrimmar","quithas","valley of spirits","waters of xavian"},rel={"npc:deino","quest:1944","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",["end"]="Deino",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1943},src={"Speak with Deino"}}
E["quest:1963"] = {t="quest",n="The Shattered Hand",z="orgrimmar",s="Therzok tests rogues in Orgrimmar who seek entry to the secretive Shattered Hand. Their trial sends them after Tazan, a troll smuggler, and his locked satchel.",h="Therzok tests rogues in Orgrimmar who seek entry to the secretive Shattered Hand.",sec={{t="Shadows in the Cleft",b="The Shattered Hand works from the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. The order of assassins and thieves follows old orcish traditions. Warchief Thrall rules the young Horde with honor, diplomacy, and caution, but the Shattered Hand's leaders believe restraint weakens their people. They seek to restore martial supremacy through covert violence, using knives and poison when a battlefield charge may fail.",sp=0},{t="A Smuggler's Fate",b="Therzok tests rogues with a contract to kill Tazan, a troll who operates near Ratchet in the Barrens. Tazan trades with coastal pirates and carries intelligence the guild wants. Recovering his locked satchel proves a rogue can stalk prey beyond the city walls, though opening it calls for further skill.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar?",a="The Shattered Hand is a covert Horde guild of rogues, scouts, and assassins based in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. Once an old orcish clan known for brutal self-mutilation, it now gathers intelligence and carries out killings, favoring ruthless pragmatism over Thrall's cautious diplomacy.",al={"who are shattered hand","shattered hand rogues","shattered hand purpose"},it="people"},{q="Who is Therzok?",a="Therzok is a Shattered Hand handler in the Cleft of Shadow. He tests prospective rogues for the cunning and lethality the guild demands, and openly doubts Thrall's restraint.",al={"therzok role","who is questgiver","therzok orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Therzok want Tazan dead?",a="Tazan is a troll smuggler trading with the Southsea pirates near Ratchet. He carries information in a satchel that the Shattered Hand wants for its covert work.",al={"why kill tazan","tazan lore","what did tazan do"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Tazan located?",a="Tazan operates in the Barrens, near the coast and pirate activity south of Ratchet.",al={"tazan location","where is tazan","find tazan"},gp=true},{q="What happens after recovering Tazan's satchel?",a="Therzok finds the satchel locked when it is returned. Though pleased by Tazan's death, he needs the intelligence inside and makes opening it another test of the rogue's lockpicking skill.",al={"next quest","locked satchel","what to do with satchel"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does Thrall know about the Shattered Hand's methods?",a="The Shattered Hand nominally serves the Horde, but its members work in the shadows and scorn Thrall's cautious leadership. They quietly build intelligence networks and seek to remove threats before the Warchief's diplomacy can delay action.",al={"thrall and shattered hand","does warchief approve","thrall rogues"},it="ties"},{q="What is in Tazan's satchel?",a="Therzok seeks the satchel because it holds valuable intelligence. Tazan deals directly with the Southsea Freebooters operating near Ratchet, and whatever correspondence or records he carries could grant the Shattered Hand leverage over pirate movements along the coast. Unfortunately, the pouch is securely locked, making it useless until you can find a way to crack it open.",al={"tazans satchel","what is tazan's satchel","tazan satchel purpose"},it="item",add="6c6760e5"},{q="Who is Tazan?",a="Tazan is a rogue troll who conducts illicit business with the pirates stationed south of Ratchet. Operating out in the Barrens beyond the reach of Orgrimmar's laws, he traffics in secrets and contraband that caught the attention of the Shattered Hand. His dealings with outlaws make him a prime target for elimination.",al={"who is tazan","tazan target","why kill tazan"},it="target",add="fc6df596"},{q="Why does Therzok send you instead of handling Tazan himself?",a="The Shattered Hand operates in strict secrecy from the depths of the Cleft of Shadow, hiding their ruthless methods from Warchief Thrall's watchful eyes. Therzok cannot send official Horde guards or expose senior guild operatives on petty field missions. Instead, he uses the contract as an initiation trial, testing whether you possess the lethal cunning required to serve their underground brotherhood.",al={"why send me","why therzok wants you","why not kill tazan himself"},it="why_me",add="beb36990"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you enter the Shattered Hand through a rite that prizes ruthless efficiency, assassination, and utility over open combat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the Shattered Hand's quiet challenge to Thrall's cautious vision for the young Horde."},kw={"cleft of shadow","orgrimmar","ratchet","rogue","satchel","shattered hand","tazan","therzok"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:1859","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:ratchet","topic:horde","topic:pirate","topic:troll"},m={start="Therzok",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1963,ri={"Tazan's Satchel"}},src={"The Shattered Hand (Classic)"}}
E["quest:235"] = {t="quest",n="The Ashenvale Hunt",z="orgrimmar",s="Warcaller Gorlach sends the Horde north into Ashenvale to join the hunt. Report to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, where the Horde is pushing its frontier into the ancient forest.",h="Warcaller Gorlach sends the Horde north into Ashenvale to join the hunt.",sec={{t="Call of the Wilds",b="Orgrimmar needs timber, meat, and safe trade routes to keep growing. Warcaller Gorlach carries orders from the Horde's high command, sending seasoned wanderers and new adventurers toward active campaigns. For those coming of age in Durotar and the Barrens, Ashenvale is the next test of skill and survival.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Frontier",b="North of the Barrens, Ashenvale holds two Horde strongholds. Splintertree Post lies in the eastern woods, while Zoram'gar Outpost stands along the western coast. Senani Thunderheart coordinates operations from Splintertree Post, organizing trackers and hunters to face the beasts beneath the canopy and night elven sentinels who contest the Horde's claims.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest and where can I find them?",a="Warcaller Gorlach gives the order in Orgrimmar, the Horde capital. He calls capable adventurers to campaigns beyond Durotar.",al={"quest giver","where is gorlach","who gives ashenvale hunt"},gp=true},{q="Where is Splintertree Post?",a="Splintertree Post lies north of the Barrens in eastern Ashenvale, along the main forest road east toward Azshara.",al={"splintertree location","where is splintertree post","how to get to splintertree"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Senani Thunderheart?",a="Senani Thunderheart is a seasoned tauren tracker at Splintertree Post. She directs the hunt across Ashenvale and judges adventurers seeking to join the local trials.",al={"who is senani","senani thunderheart location","turn in npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is the purpose of the Ashenvale hunt?",a="The hunt secures wild game and valuable hides, and removes apex predators that threaten patrols near Splintertree Post and nearby logging operations.",al={"why hunt in ashenvale","ashenvale hunt story","horde goal in ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="What other outposts does the Horde hold in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde also holds Zoram'gar Outpost on the far western edge of Ashenvale, along the Zoram Strand.",al={"horde bases in ashenvale","zoram strand post","ashenvale outposts"},it="place"},{q="Does this quest involve any combat?",a="No. You travel from Orgrimmar through the Barrens to report to Senani Thunderheart; the journey itself calls for no combat.",al={"is there fighting in this quest","do i fight anything","simple turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why does Warcaller Gorlach want adventurers sent to Ashenvale?",a="Warcaller Gorlach acts as a herald and recruiter in Orgrimmar, calling upon eager warriors to bolster the Horde's frontier campaigns. The Horde has carved out a foothold in Ashenvale with Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand Outpost, but sustaining and defending that presence requires a steady stream of capable fighters. By directing you to Senani Thunderheart's hunt, Gorlach strengthens the northern border while giving tested recruits a proving ground to win honor and glory for the Horde.",al={"warcaller gorlach motive","why send to ashenvale","why gorlach hunt"},it="motive",add="70907bc1"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry its reach beyond Durotar into resource-rich but hostile foreign lands.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find a proving ground in Ashenvale's dense canopy and dangerous beasts when you answer Senani Thunderheart's call.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can bring your deep reverence for the great hunt to the untamed forest under Senani Thunderheart's direction."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","gorlach","hunt","orgrimmar","senani","splintertree","thunderheart"},rel={"npc:warcaller-gorlach","npc:senani-thunderheart","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:1008","topic:horde"},m={start="Warcaller Gorlach",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="20",faction="Horde",id=235},src={"The Ashenvale Hunt (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:2378"] = {t="quest",n="Find the Shattered Hand",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, the Shattered Hand awaits a promising Forsaken rogue from Tirisfal Glades. The Deathstalkers send the initiate across the sea to Durotar to learn specialized arts from the clan.",h="In Orgrimmar, the Shattered Hand awaits a promising Forsaken rogue from Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A League of Shadows",b="Mennet Carkad has seen a rogue prove their worth in Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken train their own covert order, the Deathstalkers, and their alliance with the Horde opens a path to learn darker arts. He directs promising rogues to seek the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar, joining Lordaeron’s undead operatives with Kalimdor’s orcish assassins.",sp=0},{t="Into the Cleft of Shadow",b="The journey ends beneath Orgrimmar in the Cleft of Shadow, where warlocks, rogues, and demon-binders work out of sight. Shenthul, a Shattered Hand trainer, awaits there. The gruff troll judges the newly arrived undead agent with harsh skepticism. Reputation alone will not satisfy him; he wants to see whether the envoy has real cunning or has wasted the voyage across the Great Sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Find the Shattered Hand?",a="Mennet Carkad, a Deathstalker trainer in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, sends you once you prove your basic skills in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who starts find the shattered hand","mennet carkad quest","who sends me to orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="Where is Shenthul located?",a="Shenthul is in the Cleft of Shadow, the dark chasm beneath Orgrimmar's central pathways.",al={"find shenthul","shenthul location","where is shenthul in orgrimmar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the relationship between the Deathstalkers and the Shattered Hand?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's intelligence network and assassination guild, while the Shattered Hand fills a similar role for the Horde in Orgrimmar. They are formal allies who share advanced training and clandestine contracts across the Horde.",al={"deathstalkers and shattered hand","forsaken rogues orc rogues","why sent to orgrimmar"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Shenthul call me uninspiring?",a="Shenthul calls you uninspiring because the Shattered Hand values physical resilience and ruthless cunning. He insults newcomers to break their pride and test whether they can endure rigorous assassin training.",al={"shenthul dialogue","why is shenthul mean","shenthul completion text"}},{q="What happens after reaching Shenthul?",a="Shenthul puts you to work with Zando'zan, then sends you south toward Ratchet for field operations in the Barrens.",al={"what comes after find the shattered hand","next quest after shenthul","shattered hand chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can non-Forsaken rogues get this quest?",a="No. The Deathstalkers give this version to Forsaken rogues. Orc and troll rogues in Durotar receive an equivalent transition called 'To Orgrimmar!'.",al={"orc rogue find the shattered hand","troll version","to orgrimmar alternate"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want me to go to Orgrimmar?",a="Mennet Carkad recognizes that while you have served the Deathstalkers well and shown promise in stealth and deception, your growth within the Undercity has reached its limits for now. To hone your lethal craft further, he wants you to venture outward into the wider Horde. By sending you to the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar, Mennet draws upon an alliance between the two factions of assassins, ensuring you receive advanced tutelage from veteran orcish rogues who can teach you techniques not found in the shadows of Lordaeron.",al={"why send me to orgrimmar","mennet carkad motive","why find the shattered hand"},it="motive",add="aa6bb2de"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you move from local training into the Horde's wider criminal and covert network, meeting the underworld trainers in Kalimdor.",["race:Undead"]="As a young Forsaken rogue, you leave local Scourge remnants in Lordaeron behind and join the Horde's heartland in Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see cooperation between Orgrimmar's and Undercity's secret services, beyond the frontline grunts and shamans."},kw={"cleft of shadow","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","orgrimmar","rogue quest","shattered hand","shenthul"},rel={"npc:shenthul","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2379","quest:2380","quest:1886","quest:1858","quest:2382"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",["end"]="Shenthul",level="16",faction="Horde",id=2378},src={"Find the Shattered Hand"}}
E["quest:2379"] = {t="quest",n="Zando'zan",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, promising rogues begin training with the Shattered Hand. Trainer Shenthul sends his chosen initiate to meet Zando'zan and enter the Horde's covert ranks.",h="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, promising rogues begin training with the Shattered Hand.",sec={{t="A Walk into the Shadows",b="Orgrimmar's rulers know brute strength cannot win every war. Beneath the city, the Cleft of Shadow houses the Shattered Hand, a covert guild that handles espionage, sabotage, and theft for the Horde. When rogue trainer Shenthul sees promise in an initiate, he sends them to report to Zando'zan for dedicated operative training.",sp=0},{t="Proving One's Worth",b="Zando'zan does not grant respect to every inexperienced rogue who enters the cavern. Meeting him marks a formal initiation into the finer clandestine arts, beginning with stealth, subterfuge, and thievery. His training bridges the distance between rough street cutpurses and organized intelligence operatives, preparing rogues for fieldwork beyond the safety of the capital's red canyon walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zando'zan?",a="Zando'zan is a rogue trainer and Shattered Hand handler in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He evaluates new recruits and teaches practical stealth, burglary, and operative tradecraft.",al={"zandozan","who is zando'zan","zando'zan cleft of shadow"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Shenthul send rogues to see Zando'zan?",a="Shenthul sends promising rogues to Zando'zan when they need specialized training as Shattered Hand operatives. Zando'zan oversees lessons in burglary and lock manipulation for clandestine fieldwork.",al={"why do i talk to zando'zan","shenthul zando'zan","purpose of quest"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar?",a="The Shattered Hand began as a brutal orcish clan from Draenor, known for ritual self-mutilation, and evolved into the Horde's covert intelligence and assassination arm. Operating from Orgrimmar's shadows, its members handle espionage, poison, and scouting.",al={"what is shattered hand","shattered hand orgrimmar","horde rogues shattered hand"},it="people"},{q="Where does this training chain lead next?",a="After you present yourself to Zando'zan, he sends you to Ratchet on the Barrens coast to consult Wrenix, a goblin contact, and begin practical lockpicking fieldwork.",al={"next quest","what comes after zando'zan","wrenix of ratchet"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where can I find Zando'zan?",a="Zando'zan works in the Cleft of Shadow, a deep cavern network beneath Orgrimmar's center. Warlocks, shadow priests, and rogue operatives gather there out of broad daylight.",al={"zando'zan location","where is zando'zan","how to find zando'zan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Zando'zan apologize upon meeting me?",a="Zando'zan may have doubted your nerve before you arrived. Seeing you ready to train, he acknowledges your commitment and takes back his initial skepticism.",al={"why zandozan apologize","completion dialogue zando'zan"}},{q="Why does Shenthul entrust this training to you rather than another rogue?",a="Shenthul recognizes your raw determination, but knows raw zeal is not enough to survive the covert battles facing the Horde. You have proven yourself worthy of advancing beyond basic streetcraft, but to truly serve the Shattered Hand, you must be formally shaped into a dedicated operative. Shenthul sends you specifically because your path and potential have drawn the guild's watchful eye.",al={"why me shenthul","why send me zandozan","why am i chosen"},it="why_me",add="1d4b3aab"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the Shattered Hand's covert ranks, moving from an untrained knifefighter to a recognized Horde operative.",["faction:Horde"]="The Shattered Hand handles the Horde's espionage and covert work, guarding it against threats hidden from view even as the warchief speaks of honor and frontal assault."},kw={"cleft of shadow","lockpicking","orgrimmar","rogue","shattered hand","shenthul","stealth","wrenix","zando'zan"},rel={"npc:shenthul","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:2378","quest:2380","quest:2382","quest:2381","quest:1858","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Shenthul",["end"]="Zando'zan",level="16",faction="Horde",id=2379},src={"Zando'zan (quest)"}}
E["quest:2380"] = {t="quest",n="To Orgrimmar!",z="orgrimmar",s="Kaplak sends a young rogue from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. There, you are to find Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow and enter the Shattered Hand's network.",h="Kaplak sends a young rogue from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Shadows",b="Kaplak sends you north from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Your budding skills have caught the notice of more prominent handlers, though they remain unpolished. The red crags of Durotar are behind you as you make for the capital.",sp=0},{t="Under Thrall's Watchful Eye",b="Shenthul receives you in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He watches Warchief Thrall's political reforms with unease. The Shattered Hand cannot protect its interests through brute force or open defiance alone; it depends on patience, subterfuge, and deception to survive and preserve its influence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Kaplak, a rogue trainer in Razor Hill, sends you after your skills catch the attention of superiors in Orgrimmar.",al={"quest giver","who gives to orgrimmar","kaplak quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Shenthul?",a="You find Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow, an underground district beneath Orgrimmar where rogues, warlocks, and other outcasts gather.",al={"shenthul location","where is shenthul","cleft of shadow shenthul"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Shattered Hand's agenda in Orgrimmar?",a="The Shattered Hand is an intelligence and assassination guild within the Horde. Shenthul is wary of Thrall's honorable reforms, and the guild relies on stealth to preserve its influence and survive.",al={"shattered hand motives","why shattered hand in orgrimmar","shattered hand thrall"},it="conflict"},{q="Why am I being sent specifically at this stage?",a="Your basic reconnaissance and skirmishes have shown you are capable, so you are being drawn into more formal guild duties. These begin with lockpicking and covert fieldwork in the capital.",al={"level 16 rogue quest","why go to orgrimmar now","rogue training summons"},it="why_me"},{q="Does this quest differ from 'Find the Shattered Hand'?",a="Both lead rogues to Shenthul in Orgrimmar. Which one you receive depends on where you train or take orders, and each advances the same training chain.",al={"find the shattered hand vs to orgrimmar","alternate breadcrumb quest"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Shenthul?",a="Shenthul tests your competence and sends you further along the chain. You meet contacts such as Zando'zan, then take on covert work involving goblin contacts in Ratchet.",al={"next quest after to orgrimmar","what does shenthul give"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Kaplak want me to go to Orgrimmar?",a="Kaplak is acting under direct orders from above. While he acknowledges you are far from a true master of stealth, your budding talents have caught the attention of Shenthul himself. The Shattered Hand needs cunning operatives trained for their covert agenda, and Kaplak's duty is to channel promising rogues like you into the deeper shadows of the capital where your true training can begin.",al={"why does kaplak send me","kaplak motive","why go to orgrimmar"},it="motive",add="a9995c5c"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you are entering the capital's covert network under Shenthul's watch. The work turns to poisons, thievery, and deception beyond the frontier skirmishes.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear the friction between Thrall's honorable new path and the older clan organizations that survive beneath Orgrimmar."},kw={"cleft of shadow","kaplak","razor hill","rogue","shattered hand","shenthul","to orgrimmar"},rel={"npc:shenthul","npc:kaplak","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","quest:2378","quest:2379","quest:2382","quest:2381","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Kaplak",["end"]="Shenthul",level="16",faction="Horde",id=2380},src={"To Orgrimmar!"}}
E["quest:2382"] = {t="quest",n="Wrenix of Ratchet",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Wrenix of Ratchet draws Horde rogues toward a goblin port far to the south. Zando'zan sends them to aid Wrenix the Wretched, a disreputable goblin in Ratchet.",h="In Orgrimmar, Wrenix of Ratchet draws Horde rogues toward a goblin port far to the south.",sec={{t="A Prophet in the Shadows",b="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, the rogue guild works out of winding crevices, largely unseen. Zando'zan, a troll who speaks in wild ramblings, greets operatives with ominous portents. His visions include Warchief Thrall struck down by poison and blade. He gives no explanation for the prophecy, and quickly sends agents south to the port town of Ratchet in the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Ratchet's Problem Solver",b="Ratchet lies on the Barrens coast, east of the Crossroads. Scoundrels, mercenaries, and tinkerers gather in the neutral port, where Wrenix the Wretched makes his home. Wrenix has little patience for Zando'zan's eccentric ways. He says the troll's earlier recruits met grim ends in the bay, among its hungry predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Ratchet?",a="Zando'zan, a troll of the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, sends you south after blurting out strange visions.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","zandozan"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Wrenix the Wretched?",a="Wrenix the Wretched is a goblin contact in Ratchet. He handles covert work and mechanical supplies for rogues across the Barrens.",al={"who is wrenix","wrenix ratchet","wrenix identity"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the operatives sent before me?",a="Wrenix says the five agents Zando'zan sent before you failed their assignments and became shark food off Ratchet's coast.",al={"previous rogues","shark food","other recruits"}},{q="What was Zando'zan talking about regarding Thrall?",a="Zando'zan says he saw Thrall struck down by a poisoned dagger in the back, then cuts himself off and changes the subject.",al={"thrall prophecy","thrall poisoned","zandozan thrall vision"}},{q="Where is Ratchet located?",a="Ratchet sits on the eastern coast of the Barrens, directly east of the Crossroads. Roads running south from the Southfury River connect it to Durotar.",al={"where is ratchet","find ratchet","ratchet location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes next after meeting Wrenix?",a="When you greet Wrenix, he gives you 'Plundering the Plunderers': infiltrating the Southsea Freebooters along the coast south of Ratchet.",al={"next quest","after wrenix","ratchet follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Zando'zan send you to Wrenix?",a="Zando'zan is rattled by frantic visions of doom, foreseeing poison and a traitorous dagger aimed at Warchief Thrall's back. Desperate to counter these unseen threats lurking in the shadows, the eccentric troll relies on outside contacts like Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet to handle covert operations and secure specialized equipment.",al={"why send to wrenix","zandozan motive","why visit wrenix"},it="motive",add="17a3bd65"},{q="Why does Zando'zan send you instead of handling it himself?",a="Zando'zan stays confined to the shadows of Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, watching over dark portents and muttering over his visions of conspiracy. His erratic demeanor and fear of having 'said too much' keep him from operating openly in the field, so he relies on capable rogues to serve as his discreet hands beyond the city walls.",al={"why send me","why does zandozan need me","why not go himself"},it="why_me",add="2311cb82"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you leave Orgrimmar's safety and enter neutral pirate territory as an essential step in your training.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the Shattered Hand keeps eyes and ears beyond Durotar's borders. It often relies on neutral ports like Ratchet for sensitive contracts."},kw={"ratchet","rogue","shattered hand","the barrens","thrall","wrenix","zando'zan"},rel={"quest:2379","quest:2381","quest:2378","npc:wrenix-the-wretched","subzone:ratchet","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall"},m={start="Zando'zan",["end"]="Wrenix the Wretched",level="16",faction="Horde",id=2382},src={"Wrenix of Ratchet"}}
E["quest:2458"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Cover",z="orgrimmar",s="Shenthul sends a promising Horde rogue to Sludge Fen to contact an agent hidden among the Venture Company. The Shattered Hand has spent a year placing Taskmaster Fizzule inside the company’s drilling grounds, where he watches their plans.",h="Shenthul sends a promising Horde rogue to Sludge Fen to contact an agent hidden among the Venture Company.",sec={{t="A Spy Among Profiteers",b="The Shattered Hand protects Orgrimmar’s interests through secret intelligence and assassination. For a year, its members worked to place an agent in the Venture Company’s ranks. Taskmaster Fizzule earned a place at their drilling outpost north of Sludge Fen, among the company’s mercenaries.",sp=0},{t="Signs and Signals",b="Fizzule must keep his hard-edged reputation to satisfy the Venture Company’s overseers. An unexpected visitor could bring an attack. Rogues who reach his tower must fire two flares from the signaling gun within sight, approach quietly, and give the Shattered Hand’s secret salute. Then Fizzule can share what he has learned about the company’s growing schemes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Taskmaster Fizzule?",a="Taskmaster Fizzule is a Shattered Hand agent placed inside the Venture Company north of Sludge Fen. He spent a year gaining authority among its mercenaries while watching their work and sending intelligence to Orgrimmar.",al={"fizzule","who is fizzule","taskmaster fizzule identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Fizzule attack if you do not signal him properly?",a="Fizzule keeps up the harsh manner expected of a Venture Company taskmaster. Without the two-flare signal and Shattered Hand salute, he takes an approaching stranger for a hostile intruder or rival agent and attacks to protect his disguise.",al={"why does fizzule attack","fizzule hostile","fizzule kills me"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is the Venture Company tower located?",a="The Venture Company tower overlooks its drilling grounds north of Sludge Fen, in the northern Barrens.",al={"fizzule location","tower location","where is sludge fen tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde spying on the Venture Company?",a="The Shattered Hand spies on the Venture Company because its reckless extraction, exploitation, and violence threaten Kalimdor. Recent intelligence pointed to a major scheme in the Barrens, so Shenthul called on his contact.",al={"why spy on venture co","venture co threat"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after making contact with Fizzule?",a="After contact, Fizzule directs the rogue to enter the nearby Venture Company tower, kill its inhabitants, including Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, and take Zanzil's Altered Mixture to prove their worth to the guild.",al={"what next after deep cover","after fizzule"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Shattered Hand?",a="The Shattered Hand is a network of rogues, spies, and assassins based in Orgrimmar’s Cleft of Shadow. Once an infamous clan on Draenor, it now gathers intelligence for the Horde in secret.",al={"shattered hand","who are shattered hand"},it="people"},{q="Why does Shenthul send you to make contact instead of going himself?",a="Shenthul is an instructor coordinating rogue operations from Orgrimmar's shadows, while Taskmaster Fizzule is embedded deep within hostile territory at the Sludge Fen. Infiltrating an active Venture Company base requires an agile field operative who can slip past guards and signal an undercover asset unnoticed, without drawing the attention of corporate mercenaries or compromising the entire Shattered Hand ring.",al={"why send me","why does shenthul need me","why not go himself"},it="why_me",add="aa88dce8"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you are taking a step from street scouting toward trusted work in the field, coordinating in secret.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the Venture Company’s logging and drilling threaten Horde lands and resources in the Barrens."},kw={"barrens rogue","deep cover","flare gun","shattered hand","shenthul","sludge fen","taskmaster fizzule","venture company"},rel={"npc:shenthul","quest:2460","quest:2478","subzone:sludge-fen","topic:venture-company","quest:1858"},m={start="Shenthul",["end"]="Taskmaster Fizzule",level="20",faction="Horde",id=2458},src={"Deep Cover"}}
E["quest:2460"] = {t="quest",n="The Shattered Salute",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul teaches a silent sign to new rogues. The Shattered Hand uses it to recognize its agents safely in the field.",h="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul teaches a silent sign to new rogues.",sec={{t="Signs and Shadows",b="In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, the Shattered Hand works in secrecy as Thrall's Horde intelligence and assassination arm. Its agents cannot use banners or military signs on dangerous, secret assignments. Shenthul teaches newly inducted rogues the Shattered Salute, a silent gesture that lets allies recognize one another.",sp=0},{t="Preparation for the Field",b="For Shenthul's rogues, learning the salute is vital tradecraft, not ceremony. Agents sent into danger or to infiltrate rival factions need to verify contacts without alerting bystanders or targets. Before entrusting an agent with covert fieldwork, Shenthul expects them to recognize and mirror the gesture without hesitation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Shattered Salute?",a="The Shattered Salute lets Shattered Hand agents recognize one another, even in deep cover or hostile territory, without revealing their ties to outsiders.",al={"why do i need the salute","shattered salute purpose","what does the salute do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who teaches the Shattered Salute?",a="Shenthul, a rogue trainer stationed deep within Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, teaches the salute.",al={"who gives the quest","who is shenthul","where do i learn the salute"},it="identity"},{q="What organization uses this gesture?",a="The Shattered Hand uses the gesture. Orcish rogues, spies, and assassins of the order serve Thrall's Horde from Orgrimmar's shadows.",al={"shattered hand clan","who are the shattered hand","what guild uses this"},it="ties"},{q="Why is learning the salute necessary before going into the field?",a="Agents on infiltration assignments use the salute to contact undercover allies without exposing their cover or mistaking an enemy for one.",al={"why practice salute","is the salute required"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="Training takes place in the Cleft of Shadow, a subterranean district beneath Orgrimmar where rogues, warlocks, and other practitioners of forbidden arts gather away from public scrutiny.",al={"salute location","where is shenthul located"},it="place"},{q="What assignment follows after mastering the salute?",a="After Shenthul is satisfied with an agent's mastery, he assigns them to deep cover operations. The assignment tests their ability to use the signal to contact agents in the field.",al={"what comes next","next quest after salute","deep cover quest"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you learn the Shattered Hand's secret signals and move from ordinary cutpurse to trusted agent of Orgrimmar's intelligence network.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you serve under Warchief Thrall, who leads with honor. The Horde also relies on the Shattered Hand's secret methods to stop threats before they reach the surface."},kw={"cleft of shadow","covert","deep cover","orgrimmar","rogue","shattered hand","shattered salute","shenthul"},rel={"npc:shenthul","quest:2458","quest:1858"},m={start="Shenthul",level="20",faction="Horde",id=2460},src={"The Shattered Salute"}}
E["quest:2478"] = {t="quest",n="Mission: Possible But Not Probable",z="orgrimmar",s="In the northern Barrens, Horde rogues face a Venture Company outpost that tests stealth, theft, and combat. They infiltrate an oil tower, kill Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, and take a potent chemical brew for the Shattered Hand.",h="In the northern Barrens, Horde rogues face a Venture Company outpost that tests stealth, theft, and combat.",sec={{t="Infiltration of the Venture Co.",b="North of the Sludge Fen oil rigs, the Venture Company keeps an isolated drilling tower. Taskmaster Fizzule, a Shattered Hand operative posing as a Venture Company supervisor, orders rogues to rely on underworld craft instead of an open assault. He asks them to pick the key from Foreman Silixiz and keep it for him. Then they climb past workers and sentries changed by the tower’s experiments.",sp=0},{t="A Chemical Catastrophe",b="An experimental substance called Zanzil's Altered Mixture has changed the tower’s inhabitants. The venom weakens the guards, leaving them open to swift strikes, bleeding attacks, and sudden ambushes. It has also made the facility volatile. At the summit, Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix guards a lockbox holding the brew.",sp=1},{t="The Price of Duty",b="The altered mixture’s vapors escape when the rogue opens Gallywix’s lockbox. They break stealth, sap vitality, and leave a debilitating affliction that lasts a long time. Back in Orgrimmar, Shenthul, the Shattered Hand mentor, receives Gallywix’s head and the chemical sample. He mourns Fizzule’s compromised position and sends the dying agent to seek a cure.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where is the Venture Co. Tower located?",a="The Venture Company tower stands in the northern Barrens, just north of the Sludge Fen drilling operation. Hostile Venture Company workers surround it, and Taskmaster Fizzule hides near a tree just to the east.",al={"venture co tower location","where is gallywix tower","sludge fen tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you obtain the key to the tower?",a="Foreman Silixiz carries the tower key and wanders the grounds outside its base. Pick his pocket while hidden to take it; killing him will not yield the key.",al={"silixiz tower key","how to get tower key","where is the key"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Zanzil's Altered Mixture?",a="Zanzil's Altered Mixture is an alchemical brew drawn from the formulas of the notorious troll witch doctor Zanzil. The Venture Company acquired it, and its unstable fumes poisoned the tower’s workforce, leaving them sickly, mutated, and vulnerable to rogue combat arts.",al={"zanzil mixture","what is the poison","altered mixture"},it="item"},{q="Why am I unable to stealth after opening the lockbox?",a="Opening Gallywix’s lockbox releases concentrated fumes from the altered mixture. The toxic affliction lasts for days, weakens your attributes, and breaks your stealth until an experienced apothecary cures it.",al={"touch of zanzil","poisoned after chest","can't stealth rogue quest","7 day poison"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="Who is Taskmaster Fizzule?",a="Taskmaster Fizzule is a deep-cover operative for the Shattered Hand, the Horde’s rogue guild. The Dark Iron dwarf poses as a ruthless Venture Company taskmaster in the Barrens and directs recruits to sabotage the company’s assets without exposing himself.",al={"fizzule","who gave this quest","fizzule lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix?",a="Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix is the goblin overseer who commands the Venture Company tower near Sludge Fen. He guards the stolen cache of Zanzil's concoction until Shattered Hand operatives kill him.",al={"puzik gallywix","is gallywix in barrens","foreman gallywix"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Taskmaster Fizzule want the Venture Co. Tower destroyed?",a="Operating deep undercover for the Shattered Hand, Taskmaster Fizzule has witnessed the Venture Company experimenting with a volatile, mutating poison. Now that the tainted mixture has corrupted and weakened everyone inside the tower, Fizzule sees an opportunity to eliminate the entire operation, sever Grand Foreman Gallywix's leadership, and secure the deadly compound for Orgrimmar before it spreads beyond control.",al={"fizzule motive","why kill gallywix fizzule","why attack venture co tower"},it="motive",add="2a5cd36a"},{q="Why does Shenthul want Gallywix's Head?",a="Severing the head of Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix serves as undeniable proof of his demise and the dismantling of the Venture Company's tower hierarchy. Presenting it to Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow confirms that the primary overseer behind the regional operation has been permanently eliminated.",al={"gallywix head purpose","why take gallywix head","what is gallywix head for"},it="item",add="f260e633"},{q="What is Silixiz's Tower Key used for?",a="Foreman Silixiz carries the key outside the tower. Fizzule asks you to steal it and hold on to it because he may need it later; recovering it is one of the mission's objectives.",al={"silixiz tower key","tower key purpose","why steal the tower key"},it="item",add="53be2ad7"},{q="What is the Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture for?",a="Locked away at the summit of the tower in Gallywix's personal chest, this remaining stockpile holds the strange, debilitating concoction derived from Zanzil's formulas. The Shattered Hand requires you to recover the mixture so its toxic and mutating properties can be studied—and safely contained—by rogue masters in Orgrimmar.",al={"cache of zanzils altered mixture","zanzil mixture cache","why take the mixture"},it="item",add="78e0c22c"},{q="Why are you sent against Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix and the tower workers?",a="You are sent to purge the corrupted Venture Company personnel inhabiting the northern Barrens tower. Under Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix, this crew mishandled Zanzil's toxic compound, turning the drones into mutated monstrosities and endangering the region. By eliminating the lookouts, patrollers, drones, and Gallywix himself, you wipe out their encroaching industrial foothold.",al={"who are you fighting in the tower","venture co tower targets","why kill gallywix"},it="target",add="07291131"},{q="Why does Fizzule need you instead of handling the tower himself?",a="Fizzule is maintaining a precarious deep-cover identity as a Venture Company taskmaster. If he were caught openly infiltrating the tower, slaying overseers, or looting Gallywix's lockbox, his cover would instantly shatter. As an outside operative of the Shattered Hand, you possess the lethal stealth required to clean out the installation without exposing his role.",al={"why me fizzule","why does fizzule need help","why doesn't fizzule clear the tower"},it="why_me",add="fa60081f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you learn field skills in lockpicking, pickpocketing, and exploiting vulnerabilities. These skills open the way to the Shattered Hand’s deadly craft and poisons.",["faction:Horde"]="The Shattered Hand works in Orgrimmar’s shadows, watching dangerous corporate intruders such as the Venture Company as they exploit the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","fizzule","lockpicking","poisons","puzik gallywix","shattered hand","shenthul","silixiz","sludge fen","zanzil"},rel={"quest:2458","quest:2479","quest:1858","npc:shenthul","subzone:sludge-fen","quest:764","zone:barrens","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Taskmaster Fizzule",["end"]="Shenthul",level="21",faction="Horde",id=2478,ri={"Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture","Gallywix's Head","Silixiz's Tower Key"}},src={"Mission: Possible But Not Probable"}}
E["quest:2479"] = {t="quest",n="Hinott's Assistance",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, poisoned rogues seek Hinott's Assistance before Zanzil's mixture claims their lives. The toxin came from an infiltration in the Barrens, and Serge Hinott in Tarren Mill can offer a cure and teach the brewing of poisons.",h="In Orgrimmar, poisoned rogues seek Hinott's Assistance before Zanzil's mixture claims their lives.",sec={{t="A Toxic Predicament",b="A daring infiltration of the Venture Company's tower north of the Sludge Fen leaves rogues poisoned by Zanzil's altered mixture. It dulls their reflexes and threatens their lives. Shenthul, the rogue trainer in Orgrimmar, knows local remedies cannot help. He sends the poisoned rogue across the sea to the Eastern Kingdoms for care.",sp=0},{t="Journey to Tarren Mill",b="The search for a cure leads south through Lordaeron to Tarren Mill, a village in Hillsbrad Foothills. Serge Hinott lives there as an apothecary, known for his fascination with virulent brews. Ordinary healers recoil from Zanzil's venom, but Hinott treats the deadly compound with professional glee. He can dissect the foul concoction and teach worthy rogues to brew their own venoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I need to see Serge Hinott?",a="Serge Hinott is an apothecary in Tarren Mill who specializes in rare toxins and their antidotes. Ordinary healers cannot purge Zanzil's altered mixture, so Hinott is the contact who can analyze it, save your life, and teach you poisoncraft.",al={"why hinott","who cures the poison","serge hinott role"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Tarren Mill located?",a="Tarren Mill is a Forsaken settlement in northern Hillsbrad Foothills. From Orgrimmar, take the zeppelin to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades, travel south through Silverpine Forest, then turn east along the road into Hillsbrad.",al={"tarren mill location","how to get to tarren mill","where is hinott"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How did I get poisoned in the first place?",a="You were infected during the covert task called Mission: Possible But Not Probable at the Venture Company tower north of the Sludge Fen in the Barrens. Opening the high-security chest exposed you to Zanzil's altered mixture, leaving you with a lingering, debilitating affliction.",al={"how did i get zanzil poison","mission possible poison","why am i poisoned"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after Serge Hinott receives the sample?",a="After Serge Hinott receives the sample, he examines its properties and prepares an antidote to cleanse your system. Once he cures the toxin, he shares his expertise so rogues can learn to brew and apply their own poisons.",al={"hinott quest follow up","do i get cured","after hinotts assistance"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Shenthul and why did he send me away?",a="Shenthul is the rogue trainer of the Shattered Hand in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. He oversaw your test of skill in the Barrens and saw that Zanzil's concoction was beyond Orgrimmar's medical knowledge, so he sent you to a Hillsbrad specialist.",al={"who is shenthul","shenthul orgrimmar","why did trainer send me"},it="motive"},{q="Can any other class complete this quest?",a="No. This training is part of the rogue lineage and teaches the fundamentals of brewing poisons and remedies.",al={"rogue only quest","can warriors do hinotts assistance"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you face a rite of passage that tests your stamina and opens the door to crafting your own venoms.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you see practical cooperation between Kalimdor's orc and troll rogues and the Forsaken's alchemical knowledge in Lordaeron."},kw={"hillsbrad foothills","hinott's assistance","rogue poison quest","serge hinott","shenthul","tarren mill","undercity zeppelin","zanzil","zanzil's mixture"},rel={"npc:serge-hinott","quest:2478","npc:shenthul","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity"},m={start="Shenthul",["end"]="Serge Hinott",level="21",faction="Horde",id=2479},src={"Hinott's Assistance"}}
E["quest:2751"] = {t="quest",n="Barbaric Battlements",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Orokk Omosh seeks someone to carry on his family's forge craft. With no heirs, he asks an aspiring smith to prove a sure hand with bronze before sharing his knowledge.",h="In Orgrimmar, Orokk Omosh seeks someone to carry on his family's forge craft.",sec={{t="The End of the Omosh Line",b="Orokk Omosh works the anvils of Orgrimmar under the weight of his family's past. For twenty generations, the Omosh line has shaped ore into weapons and armor for the Horde. Orokk has no kin and cannot sire children, and he sees himself as a failure to that line. With the family craft at risk of ending, he sets bloodline pride aside and seeks an apprentice to carry its smithing traditions forward.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Metal and Tooth",b="Orokk will not share his secrets with an untested smith. He asks for two patterned bronze bracers, two bronze greatswords, and two sharp beast claws as proof of basic skill at the anvil. To him, blacksmithing is no idle luxury: its highest honor is armor and steel stained with enemy blood. Meeting his demands may persuade the old smith that the Omosh legacy can live on through an apprentice, and earn a chance to learn more of the craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orokk Omosh?",a="Orokk Omosh is a master blacksmith in Orgrimmar and the twentieth generation of the Omosh line. With no kin or heirs, he seeks an outsider to keep the clan's smithing knowledge alive.",al={"orokk omosh","who is orokk","omosh blacksmith"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Orokk need someone else to teach?",a="Orokk has no surviving kin and cannot have children. He needs an apprentice to inherit his workshop's blueprints and techniques, or twenty generations of smithing knowledge will end with him.",al={"why apprentice","orokk heir","why omosh legacy dying"},it="motive"},{q="What items are required to prove competence to Orokk?",a="Orokk asks for two patterned bronze bracers, two bronze greatswords, and two sharp claws taken from fierce predatory beasts.",al={"what do i need for barbaric battlements","items for barbaric battlements","barbaric battlements turn in"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What comes after completing Barbaric Battlements?",a="After you prove your basic skill with bronze, Orokk continues your training with On Iron Pauldrons, where you advance to heavier iron forging and complex plate armor.",al={"next quest","chain after barbaric battlements","what follows"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Orokk need the Patterned Bronze Bracers, Bronze Greatswords, and Sharp Claws?",a="Orokk Omosh is searching for a worthy apprentice to carry on his family's sacred smithing legacy. Rather than putting the arms into service, he demands the Patterned Bronze Bracers, Bronze Greatswords, and Sharp Claws as a test of skill. Bringing him these finely crafted bronze goods alongside raw beast trophies proves you possess the discipline, technical craft, and rugged strength required to learn the secret recipes of clan Omosh.",al={"what are the items for","why patterned bronze bracers","why bronze greatswords sharp claws"},it="item",add="2a7cea14"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Horde blacksmith, you reach a milestone on the path from basic bronze and copper work to more advanced armor traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share the Omosh belief that metalwork should be tested in combat and stained with the blood of foes."},kw={"barbaric battlements","blacksmithing","bronze","legacy","omosh","orgrimmar","orokk omosh"},rel={"npc:orokk-omosh","quest:2753","quest:2755","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thousandneedles"},m={faction="Horde",id=2751,ri={"Bronze Greatsword","Patterned Bronze Bracers","Sharp Claw"}},src={"Barbaric Battlements"}}
E["quest:2753"] = {t="quest",n="Trampled Under Foot",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orokk Omosh puts smiths through an advanced blacksmithing trial. Forging green iron armor tests their endurance and teaches them to make heavy iron boots, with the Omosh bloodline's secret techniques at stake.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Orokk Omosh puts smiths through an advanced blacksmithing trial.",sec={{t="The Trials of Omosh",b="Orokk Omosh trains armorsmiths in Orgrimmar through hard physical trials. He sees metalworking as more than heating ore and shaping it; the work honors his ancestral clan and tests a smith's endurance. This is the third trial in his chain, and repeated crafting of tempered green iron armor is meant to build muscle and discipline.",sp=0},{t="Legacy of Chief Gorokk",b="Smiths who bring Orokk the requested green iron gear earn rare praise from the gruff armorsmith. He compares an artisan who endures the work to his grandfather, Chief Gorokk of Omosh. In exchange for the armor, Orokk teaches the ancestral design for sturdy iron boots, made so Horde warriors can crush their enemies beneath their heels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Trampled Under Foot?",a="Orokk Omosh, an orc armorsmith in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, offers the trial.",al={"quest giver","who gives trampled under foot","orokk omosh location"},it="identity"},{q="What does Orokk Omosh require for this trial?",a="Orokk requires four Green Iron Helms, four Green Iron Bracers, and two Green Iron Leggings. These pieces test and prove the smith's mastery of green iron craftsmanship.",al={"trampled under foot turn in","what items needed","materials needed"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the lore behind the Omosh training chain?",a="Orokk Omosh puts young smiths through punishing physical labor to uphold his ancestors' martial heritage. He believes grueling armorsmithing builds the strength to make gear that can withstand brutal warfare.",al={"why does orokk make you craft armor","omosh clan lore"},it="history"},{q="Who is Chief Gorokk of Omosh?",a="Chief Gorokk of Omosh is Orokk Omosh's grandfather. Orokk honors his grandfather's martial prowess and compares smiths who endure his heavy ironwork trials to the chieftain.",al={"chief gorokk","orokk grandfather"},it="leader"},{q="What quest precedes Trampled Under Foot?",a="On Iron Pauldrons comes before this trial in Orokk's series of armorsmithing challenges.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest in chain"},gp=true},{q="What is the next quest after completing Trampled Under Foot?",a="After this trial, Orokk Omosh offers Horns of Frenzy. Joys of Omosh ends the series after the two remaining lessons.",al={"next quest","what comes after trampled under foot"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Orokk Omosh want these green iron pieces forged?",a="Orokk Omosh is training you in the brutal smithing traditions of his bloodline. He believes that true warriors and smiths must endure agonizing labor to forge gear worthy of the Omosh name. By having you hammer out multiple helms, bracers, and greaves from heavy green iron, he tests both your physical endurance and your craft, preparing you to unlock the knowledge of forging battle-hardened boots.",al={"orokk omosh motive","why forge green iron","why does orokk want this"},it="motive",add="454b7030"},{q="What is the Green Iron Helm for?",a="The Green Iron Helms serve as one part of Orokk's grueling test of craftsmanship and endurance. Smelted and hammered by your own hand, they prove to the smith that you possess the precise metallurgy and raw physical stamina required to craft heavy protective battle gear for the Omosh tradition.",al={"green iron helm purpose","why green iron helm","use of green iron helm"},it="item",add="9ced7653"},{q="What are the Green Iron Bracers for?",a="These bracers demonstrate your ability to forge sturdy, reliable limb protection under the punishing guidance of Orokk Omosh. Handing over four properly crafted pairs proves that your smithing skills can reliably outfit warriors for the savage battles ahead.",al={"green iron bracers purpose","why green iron bracers","use of green iron bracers"},it="item",add="ae72eea8"},{q="What are the Green Iron Leggings for?",a="The leggings require heavy quantities of worked iron and disciplined smithcraft. Providing two well-crafted pairs proves to Orokk that you are worthy to inherit the secrets of crafting powerful armored boots, walking in the footsteps of his ancestor Chief Gorokk.",al={"green iron leggings purpose","why green iron leggings","use of green iron leggings"},it="item",add="9872ef5a"},{q="Why does Orokk Omosh need you instead of doing the smithing himself?",a="Orokk is not looking for a delivery of armor for himself; he is testing and instructing you. As an instructor of his clan's ancient techniques, he demands that your own muscles ache over the anvil to prove your dedication before he will share the designs of the Omosh.",al={"why me orokk","why does orokk need me","why not smith it himself"},it="why_me",add="f314d286"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For a Horde armorsmith, this trial is a major step. It calls for extensive iron smelting and green dye preparation to earn exclusive boot plans.",["faction:Horde"]="Orokk's lessons teach durable iron armor patterns shaped for the brutal fighting favored across Horde warfronts."},kw={"armorsmithing","blacksmithing","gorokk","green iron","orgrimmar","orokk omosh","trampled under foot","valley of honor"},rel={"npc:orokk-omosh","quest:2751","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Orokk Omosh",faction="Horde",id=2753,ri={"Green Iron Bracers","Green Iron Helm","Green Iron Leggings"}},src={"Trampled Under Foot"}}
E["quest:2755"] = {t="quest",n="Joys of Omosh",z="orgrimmar",s="After an adventurer's great help, Orokk Omosh shares a family tradition in Orgrimmar. The veteran blacksmith brushes off his tears as soot, then performs the Omosh dance of joy to pass down an unusual piece of family heritage.",h="After an adventurer's great help, Orokk Omosh shares a family tradition in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Soot-Stained Tear",b="Near Orgrimmar's scorching forge, Orokk Omosh is known for heavy hammer blows, not tears. The burly blacksmith has received great help from you, and the kindness overwhelms him. He stubbornly blames a stray bit of soot in his eye rather than admit he is weeping.",sp=0},{t="The Omosh Tradition",b="Before you part, Orokk says he must share one last secret of the Omosh family. He performs the vigorous, exhausting Omosh dance of joy for his apprentice, then teaches the apprentice to strike with an iron fist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orokk Omosh?",a="Orokk Omosh is an orc blacksmith in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He takes fierce pride in his family's craft and lineage, and keeps lively traditions alongside his smithing.",al={"who is orokk","orokk omosh backstory","orokk blacksmith"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Orokk crying?",a="Orokk says forge soot is trapped in his eye, but your help has deeply moved him. He has found someone worthy of sharing his family's traditions with.",al={"why orokk cry","is orokk sad","soot in eye"}},{q="What is the Omosh dance of joy?",a="The Omosh dance of joy is a vigorous routine passed down through Orokk's family. It leaves him deeply tired, and he has not practiced it in a very long time.",al={"omosh dance","dance of joy","what is the dance"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="It takes place in Orgrimmar, around the blacksmithing forge in the Valley of Honor where Orokk Omosh works his metal.",al={"quest location","where is joys of omosh","orgrimmar forge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Orokk teach you?",a="Orokk teaches you the Omosh dance of joy and promises to pass on the knowledge of the fist of iron, binding smith and adventurer.",al={"omosh reward","what do i learn","fist of iron"},it="power"},{q="Can Alliance players participate in this quest?",a="No. Orokk Omosh is allied with the Horde and lives within Orgrimmar's fortified walls, so only Horde adventurers can meet him there.",al={"alliance joys of omosh","is this horde only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Orokk Omosh want to teach you the dance of joy?",a="Orokk is overwhelmed with gratitude for your help and wants to pass on the final, closely guarded tradition of his bloodline. By teaching you the Omosh dance of joy, he feels his legacy is honored and that he can finally die a happy orc.",al={"why teach dance","orokk omosh motive","why does orokk want this"},it="motive",add="371650ab"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For a smith, Orokk's sentimental family dance offers a humorous, tender glimpse of a veteran craftsman's life beyond the forge.",["faction:Horde"]="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, martial pride meets Orokk's tearful joy and spirited dance amid the clash of steel."},kw={"blacksmith","dance of joy","joys of omosh","orgrimmar","orokk omosh","soot in eye","valley of honor"},rel={"npc:orokk-omosh"},m={start="Orokk Omosh",level="15-30",faction="Horde",id=2755},src={"Joys of Omosh"}}
E["quest:2950"] = {t="quest",n="Nogg's Ring Redo",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Nogg works to improve a ring recovered from Gnomeregan. He asks for rare materials and information about Dark Iron dwarves, eager to prove goblin craft superior to gnomish design.",h="In Orgrimmar, Nogg works to improve a ring recovered from Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="Goblin Superiority",b="You bring a cleaned gold ring from Gnomeregan to Nogg's workshop in the Valley of Honor. The goblin engineer takes one look at its modest gnomish craft and offers a bargain. Bring raw materials and a modest fee, and he will add an intricate lattice of silver and moss agate to the band, meant to amplify the magic within it.",sp=0},{t="A Dwarven Angle",b="Nogg's offer has more behind it than business. Reports of Dark Iron dwarves inside the besieged gnome city have caught his attention. To Nogg, their presence may explain how gnomes came by sudden bursts of mechanical skill, a field goblins consider their own. Your information earns an improved ring and Nogg's grudging respect.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nogg?",a="Nogg is a goblin engineer working in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He works with fellow tinkerers in the Drag and Valley of Honor, handling curious mechanical artifacts and schematics recovered from dangerous expeditions.",al={"who is nogg","nogg orgrimmar","nogg npc"},it="identity"},{q="What materials are needed to reforge the ring?",a="Nogg asks for the original Brilliant Gold Ring, one Silver Bar, one Moss Agate, and thirty silver coins for his work and workshop expenses.",al={"ring materials","nogg materials","what does nogg need"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Nogg interested in Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomeregan holds great technological value. Goblins compete fiercely with gnomes in technical fields, and Nogg is intrigued by rumors that Dark Iron dwarves were involved in the technological anomalies inside the fallen techno-city.",al={"why nogg care about gnomeregan","gnomeregan goblin interest"},it="ties"},{q="What does Nogg actually do to the ring?",a="Nogg builds a silver and moss agate lattice around the gold band. The framework channels and steadies the enchantments within the ring, making it stronger than the original gnomish design.",al={"ring upgrade lore","what changes on the ring"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this quest chain start?",a="The chain begins deep in Gnomeregan. You find a Grime-Encrusted Ring on a Dark Iron dwarf and clean it with the Sparklematic 5200 machine.",al={"chain start","how to start nogg quest","ring questline start"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Why does Nogg suspect Dark Iron dwarves?",a="Goblin engineers distrust gnomish innovation. Nogg suspects any sudden leap in gnomish mechanical skill came from outside meddling, especially from the scheming Dark Iron clan.",al={"why dark irons","dark iron dwarf connection"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Nogg want to reforge the ring?",a="Nogg does not claim ownership of the ring, but he is genuinely grateful for the intelligence you brought back regarding the Dark Iron dwarves in Gnomeregan. As a goblin engineer, he also cannot resist showing off his superior craft: he is eager to prove he can outdo the crude work of gnome tinkerers by augmenting their design with a far more potent magical lattice.",al={"why does nogg offer to redo the ring","why redo the ring","nogg motive ring redo"},it="motive",add="e11b7fb8"},{q="What is the Silver Bar used for in Nogg's Ring Redo?",a="Nogg uses the silver bar to forge a refined structural lattice around the ring. This delicate metallic framework serves as the physical housing needed to lock in additional magical enchantments without disrupting the ring's existing core.",al={"what is the silver bar for","silver bar nogg","why silver bar ring redo"},it="item",add="63dec8fa"},{q="What is the Moss Agate used for in Nogg's Ring Redo?",a="The moss agate is combined into the new silver lattice Nogg creates for your ring. Its inherent mineral properties help channel and amplify the latent magical energy contained within the piece, turning a simple gnomish trinket into a much stronger artifact.",al={"what is moss agate for","moss agate nogg","why moss agate ring redo"},it="item",add="c138af81"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see the rivalry between goblin ingenuity and gnomish gadgetry. Goblins modify existing devices aggressively to get the most from them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can bring technology from Alliance-aligned halls like Gnomeregan to Orgrimmar's tinkerers, giving the Horde insight into enemy capabilities.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can help provide the valuable materials Nogg needs: a refined silver bar and a moss agate, gathered through mining and gem-cutting."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","dark iron","gnomeregan","goblin engineering","moss agate","nogg","orgrimmar","silver bar"},rel={"quest:2947","quest:2945","npc:nogg","zone:orgrimmar","topic:goblin","topic:gnome","topic:horde"},m={start="Nogg",faction="Horde",id=2950,ri={"Moss Agate","Silver Bar"}},src={"Nogg's Ring Redo"}}
E["quest:2996"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Strahad",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye sends warlocks south to Ratchet for deeper training. There, a human summoner teaches arts beyond the reach of basic summoning.",h="In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye sends warlocks south to Ratchet for deeper training.",sec={{t="Leaving the Shadows of Orgrimmar",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye trains young warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow, where they learn to command the Nether. When an apprentice outgrows that teaching, Gan'rul points them beyond the city walls. More volatile beings call for instruction from someone with deeper mastery of dark arcana.",sp=0},{t="An Unorthodox Alliance",b="Gan'rul sends apprentices to Strahad Farsan, a human sorcerer in a tower above Ratchet's goblin port. Horde and humans may be enemies, but warlocks look beyond ordinary faction loyalties. Power, discipline, and ritual knowledge matter more than ancestry. Strahad judges an apprentice by their inner hatred and ability to subjugate, not their skin color.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an orc warlock sending me to a human?",a="Warlocks value dark knowledge over racial loyalties. Gan'rul Bloodeye knows Strahad Farsan has rare skill in advanced demonology, and a tutor's knowledge matters more than faction lines when seeking dangerous summons.",al={"why learn from human","strahad human warlock","why strahad"},it="ties"},{q="Where can I find Strahad Farsan?",a="Strahad Farsan lives on the high bluffs above Ratchet in the Barrens, outside his tower overlooking the goblin port.",al={"strahad location","where is strahad","strahad tower ratchet"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What power does Strahad teach?",a="Strahad teaches the rituals to bind a felhunter, a magic-devouring demon from the Twisting Nether. He studies occult texts with warlocks, then tests their ability to enslave the beast.",al={"what does strahad unlock","what do i get from strahad","seeking strahad reward"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a prominent orc warlock mentor in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He trains burgeoning Horde warlocks in the basics of fel magic and summoning lesser minions.",al={"who is ganrul","ganrul bloodeye","orgrimmar warlock trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Is there another way to start this quest?",a="Yes. Forsaken warlocks receive a similar summons from the Magic Quarter in the Undercity, directing them to the same human mentor above Ratchet.",al={"seeking strahad undercity","forsaken seeking strahad","undercity version"},gp=true},{q="Does Ratchet pose any danger to Horde warlocks?",a="Ratchet is run by the Steamwheedle Cartel and remains a neutral port. Keep the peace and do not attack travelers within the city, and goblin bruisers leave you alone.",al={"is ratchet safe","ratchet guards hostile","neutral port"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Gan'rul Bloodeye send you to Strahad?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye recognizes that your dark talents have outgrown his own instruction in Orgrimmar. To advance further along the path of demonology and master more powerful summonings, you require esoteric lore that only Strahad Farsan possesses. Gan'rul sets aside racial prejudice to ensure your mastery deepens.",al={"why send to strahad","ganrul bloodeye motive","why seek strahad"},it="motive",add="d843591e"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you are moving toward mastery of mid-tier demonic beings, and your readiness to subjugate the magic-consuming felhunter is being tested.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see how warlock covens work beyond the Warchief's formal diplomacy: their masters send apprentices to a solitary human."},kw={"barrens","cleft of shadow","felhunter quest","gan'rul bloodeye","ratchet","seeking strahad","strahad farsan","tome of the cabal"},rel={"npc:strahad-farsan","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","quest:1758","quest:1471","quest:1798","subzone:ratchet","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Gan'rul Bloodeye",["end"]="Strahad Farsan",level="30",faction="Horde",id=2996},src={"Seeking Strahad (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:3923"] = {t="quest",n="Rilli Greasygob",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob is the specialist Wenikee Boltbucket seeks. She sends you there with a damaged samophlange, hoping his knowledge of its Venture Company origins can explain the device.",h="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob is the specialist Wenikee Boltbucket seeks.",sec={{t="When Tinkering Fails",b="Wenikee Boltbucket examined the samophlange recovered from the Venture Company drilling site in the Barrens. Her extra gauges showed the apparatus nearing collapse. More levers and dials might destroy it, so she stopped and sent the problem to someone with knowledge of its design.",sp=0},{t="A Former Company Man",b="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Wenikee sends you to Nogg's Machine Shop. Rilli Greasygob works there as an engineer and once learned his trade within the Venture Company. He recognizes the machine at once and marvels that anyone survived exploring the company's contested operations in the Barrens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rilli Greasygob?",a="Rilli Greasygob is a goblin engineer at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He once worked for the Venture Company and knows its technology firsthand, including devices like the samophlange.",al={"rilli greasygob","who is rilli","nogg machine shop rilli"},it="identity"},{q="Why couldn't Wenikee Boltbucket fix the samophlange herself?",a="Wenikee Boltbucket's extra gauges showed that the samophlange was close to coming apart. She feared further tinkering would ruin it and sought someone with direct experience of Venture Company machinery.",al={"why send to rilli","boltbucket failure","wenikee cant fix"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Rilli Greasygob located?",a="Rilli Greasygob works inside Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, in the city's northeastern district.",al={"rilli greasygob location","where is greasygob","find rilli"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Venture Company's role in this?",a="The samophlange came from the Venture Company's strip-mining operation at the Sludge Fen in the northern Barrens. It is custom company technology, and former workers like Rilli Greasygob know how to service and interpret it.",al={"venture co connection","why venture company","who made the samophlange"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after giving the samophlange to Rilli?",a="Rilli Greasygob recognizes the device but needs the Venture Company's official operational instructions to operate or reconstruct it. You are sent to recover the Samophlange Manual.",al={"what next after rilli","samophlange questline continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is a samophlange anyway?",a="No one involved seems quite sure what a samophlange is. The Venture Company device is intricate and full of gears; even Wenikee Boltbucket had to ask what it was, and Rilli needs the company's manual to understand it.",al={"what is a samophlange","samophlange explained"},it="item"},{q="Why does Wenikee Boltbucket need you to take the samophlange to Orgrimmar?",a="Wenikee has tried adding gauges to the damaged samophlange, but its integrity reads at an all-time low. She fears further tinkering could make things worse and asks you to carry it to former Venture Company engineer Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.",al={"why me wenikee","why does wenikee need me","why send me with samophlange"},it="why_me",add="322883d5"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know when to set down the wrench. Wenikee Boltbucket's extra dials would only worsen matters, so she turns to the trade knowledge of a former company engineer.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how Orgrimmar's workshops put captured machinery to use against syndicates exploiting Kalimdor."},kw={"broken and battered samophlange","nogg's machine shop","orgrimmar","rilli greasygob","samophlange","valley of honor","venture company","wenikee boltbucket"},rel={"npc:nogg","quest:3921","quest:894","subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:orgrimmar","topic:venture-company","zone:barrens"},m={start="Wenikee Boltbucket",["end"]="Rilli Greasygob",level="18",faction="Horde",id=3923},src={"Rilli Greasygob (quest)"}}
E["quest:3924"] = {t="quest",n="Samophlange Manual",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob needs help with a broken samophlange. The goblin engineer sends you back into the Barrens for the operating instructions, held by his former Venture Company rival.",h="In Orgrimmar, Rilli Greasygob needs help with a broken samophlange.",sec={{t="Corporate Rivalries and Trade Secrets",b="Rilli Greasygob once worked beside Boss Copperplug in the Venture Company. Copperplug oversaw the samophlange’s inner workings and guarded their secrets closely. He shared no manual with Rilli. Instead, he gave out separate pages only to underlings he trusted, leaving his fellow engineer without the knowledge to understand the device.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration of Boulder Lode",b="Rilli sends you to Boulder Lode Mine in the northeastern Barrens to find the instructions for the contraption brought from there. Boss Copperplug is somewhere in the mine, and pages he handed out are scattered among its operations. You need to gather them and piece together a complete guide to repairing the device.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Samophlange Manual?",a="The Samophlange Manual explains the device’s mechanics and how to repair it. The Venture Company uses the complex, eccentric machine.",al={"what is the manual","samophlange manual item","user manual"},it="item"},{q="Who is Boss Copperplug?",a="Boss Copperplug oversees the Venture Company’s Boulder Lode Mine in the northeastern Barrens. He once rivaled Rilli Greasygob and kept the samophlange’s operating secrets and manual pages to himself.",al={"copperplug","who is copperplug","boss copperplug"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Boulder Lode Mine located?",a="Boulder Lode Mine lies in the northeastern Barrens, north of the Crossroads and west of the coast.",al={"boulder lode location","where is boulder lode","find boulder lode mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Rilli Greasygob need the manual?",a="Rilli believes he can repair and operate the broken samophlange brought from the Barrens, but its convoluted design calls for the official instructions.",al={"why rilli wants manual","why fix samophlange"},it="motive"},{q="How does Sputtervalve fit into this task?",a="Sputtervalve is an associate in Ratchet who first sought information about the device and stays in touch with Rilli. Sputtervalve sends thanks and compensation for obtaining the machine’s schematics.",al={"sputtervalve connection","ratchet goblin sputtervalve"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after the manual is returned?",a="Rilli eagerly studies the manual, hoping to get the machine working. Repairing such an arcane contraption remains an ongoing mechanical puzzle.",al={"quest conclusion","does rilli fix it"},it="next_step"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate how goblins guard corporate inventions: they tear complex schematics apart and hoard the pieces so colleagues cannot copy them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help goblin specialists in Orgrimmar secure valuable technical salvage and strike back at the Venture Company’s predatory operations nearby."},kw={"barrens","boss copperplug","boulder lode mine","manual","orgrimmar","rilli greasygob","samophlange","sputtervalve","venture company"},rel={"quest:3923","quest:894","npc:sputtervalve","subzone:boulder-lode-mine","topic:venture-company","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Rilli Greasygob",level="19",faction="Horde",id=3924,ri={"Samophlange Manual"}},src={"Samophlange Manual (quest)"}}
E["quest:4737"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Menara Voidrender",z="orgrimmar",s="Zevrost sends warlocks from Orgrimmar to seek Menara Voidrender in the Barrens. He warns that fel magic leads to demonic enslavement, yet points them toward a mentor who can help fashion powerful arcane vestments.",h="Zevrost sends warlocks from Orgrimmar to seek Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Warnings in the Shadows",b="Warlocks gather beneath Orgrimmar in the Cleft of Shadow, where their presence is tolerated uneasily. Zevrost, one of their bitter tutors, sneers at acolytes who seek mastery of the dark arts. He believes those who delve deeper into fel magic only hasten their own enslavement. In his view, demonic addiction will eventually overtake every practitioner, turning even the most disciplined scholar into a thrall of the Twisting Nether.",sp=0},{t="The Path to Ratchet",b="Zevrost admits that other warlocks do not share his bleak view. Word has reached Orgrimmar of Menara Voidrender, a skilled warlock on the bluffs overlooking Ratchet, the neutral goblin port. Menara seeks promising disciples to help craft specialized implements for wielding their arcane might. For warlocks eager to advance their craft, her summons begins the forging of the legendary Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Fellowship",b="Menara waits high above Ratchet, where the realities of warlock society are plain. Warlocks must set aside racial and cultural rivalries and support one another. The demons they bargain with show no prejudice and no mercy to anyone who falters. Sharing knowledge and crafting protective vestments comes from practical need, not noble charity: warlocks must survive the hostile entities they bind to their service.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zevrost?",a="Zevrost is an orc warlock trainer in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He distrusts the pursuit of fel power and sees ambitious warlocks as fools destined for slavery to demonic corruption.",al={"zevrost","zevrost lore","who starts in search of menara voidrender"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Menara Voidrender?",a="Menara Voidrender is an accomplished warlock in the Barrens, on the cliffs overlooking Ratchet. She mentors rising warlocks and helps them gather rare reagents to make potent ceremonial robes.",al={"menara voidrender","where is menara voidrender","who is menara"},it="target"},{q="Why does Zevrost think all warlocks are fools?",a="Zevrost believes fel magic inevitably corrupts and enslaves anyone who tries to master it. He thinks no practitioner can resist addiction, and that seeking greater power only hastens their downfall.",al={"zevrost corruption","why does zevrost warn me"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Menara Voidrender be found?",a="Menara is in the Barrens, on the high hills overlooking Ratchet. Warlocks travel east across the arid savannah to reach her camp overlooking the port.",al={"menara location","find menara voidrender"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do warlocks from different races work together?",a="As Menara explains, demons summoned by warlocks show cruel malice to anyone who fails to control them. Survival depends on precision, so warlocks share knowledge and tools across cultural boundaries.",al={"warlock solidarity","why do warlocks band together"},it="allies"},{q="What happens after finding Menara Voidrender?",a="Menara enlists the warlock to gather exotic, potent materials from across Azeroth to make the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe, a garment protective against fel energies.",al={"next quest after menara","what does menara want"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Zevrost send you to Menara Voidrender?",a="Zevrost believes you are a fool destined to fall to demonic corruption, but he recognizes your desire to expand your magical craft. Rather than assist you directly in gaining power he considers dangerous, he passes you along to Menara Voidrender, who has put out word seeking aspiring warlocks willing to craft specialized tools.",al={"why send me to menara","why zevrost sends you","why me zevrost"},it="why_me",add="df1726dd"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you travel under Menara Voidrender's guidance to assemble your own iconic Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe, a rite of passage for Horde warlocks.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warlock, you face the contempt of traditional shamans and warriors. You find shelter in hidden places such as Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow or on neutral ground near Ratchet."},kw={"barrens","bloodrobe","cleft of shadow","fel magic","menara voidrender","ratchet","warlock robe","zevrost"},rel={"npc:zevrost","npc:menara-voidrender","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:1796"},m={start="Zevrost",["end"]="Menara Voidrender",level="31",faction="Horde",id=4737},src={"In Search of Menara Voidrender (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:5502"] = {t="quest",n="A Warden of the Horde",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Children's Week ends with Grunth's return to Orphan Matron Battlewail. After seeing the world with his guardian, the young orphan hopes to become a hero himself.",h="In Orgrimmar, Children's Week ends with Grunth's return to Orphan Matron Battlewail.",sec={{t="An Orphan's Farewell",b="After the adventures of Children's Week, Grunth thanks you for showing him more than he ever dreamed he would see. He remembers his parents' advice to rise above hardship and hopes to become a hero like you. His final request is to return home and tell the matron about your time together.",sp=0},{t="Home to the Valley of Honor",b="You return Grunth to Orphan Matron Battlewail at the orphanage in the Valley of Honor. In the new Horde, caring for the young is a profound duty, since war has left countless children without parents. Battlewail praises your compassion as the true measure of a Horde hero. Grunth parts with a beloved pet so you will remember the bond formed during your travels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This brings the Horde's Children's Week festivities to a close. Return Grunth and the Orcish Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail in the Valley of Honor.",al={"warden of the horde summary","childrens week ending horde"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Grunth?",a="Grunth is an orcish youth who lives at the Orgrimmar Orphanage in the Valley of Honor. During Children's Week, a Horde champion takes him across Kalimdor to see legendary figures and grand sights.",al={"who is the orc orphan","grunth lore"},it="identity"},{q="What do I bring back to the matron?",a="Bring the Orcish Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail when Grunth is ready to return home.",al={"orphan whistle return","return grunth whistle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who oversees the orphans in Orgrimmar?",a="Orphan Matron Battlewail oversees the Orgrimmar Orphanage in the Valley of Honor, where she devotes her life to sheltering and raising the Horde's war orphans.",al={"orphan matron horde","who runs the orphanage"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Grunth want to return home?",a="His Children's Week outings are over, and Grunth wants to tell the matron about his adventures and the kind guardian who took him along.",al={"grunth return home","children week farewell"},it="motive"},{q="Why is Children's Week important to the Horde?",a="Decades of relentless warfare against demons, humans, and centaur have left countless Horde children without families. Children's Week gives warriors time away from the battlefield to honor the future generations of Durotar and beyond.",al={"childrens week lore","why care for orphans horde"},it="history"},{q="Why return the Orcish Orphan Whistle?",a="Returning the whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail concludes your responsibility for Grunth during Children's Week. He is ready to go home to the orphanage in the Valley of Honor and tell the matron about his adventures.",al={"return orphan whistle","warden horde whistle"},it="item",add="02759f47"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, strength means more than skill in battle. It also means protecting and uplifting the vulnerable who will one day carry the Warchief's banner.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know courage and honor matter. Showing compassion to an orphaned child like Grunth reflects the nobility Thrall seeks to instill in the new Horde."},kw={"battlewail","children's week","grunth","orgrimmar","orphan","orcish orphan whistle","valley of honor"},rel={"npc:orphan-matron-battlewail","npc:grunth","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Orcish Orphan",["end"]="Orphan Matron Battlewail",faction="Horde",id=5502,ri={"Foam Sword Rack (common)"}},src={"A Warden of the Horde"}}
E["quest:5643"] = {t="quest",n="Shadowguard",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Undercity, Aelthalyste sends a Darkspear priest back to Orgrimmar. She sees that the young troll is ready for the tribe’s sacred rites, and Ur'kyo awaits in the Valley of Spirits.",h="In the Undercity, Aelthalyste sends a Darkspear priest back to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Summons Across Continents",b="Aelthalyste watches visiting troll priests in the Undercity. When an initiate has grown strong enough to face the tribe’s trials, she sends them across the Great Sea to learn from their own elders. She does not impose Forsaken teachings on them; their faith follows the traditions of their people.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Spirits",b="In Orgrimmar’s Valley of Spirits, Ur'kyo tends to the Darkspear tribe’s spiritual needs and ancient rites. He welcomes the returning initiate and prepares them for a rite of passage. It joins the priest’s bond to the loa with spells that ward off harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Aelthalyste, a priest trainer in the Undercity’s War Quarter, starts the summons. She recognizes when a troll priest is ready for the tribe’s spiritual trials.",al={"quest giver","where do i start","who gives shadowguard"},it="identity"},{q="Why does an Undercity trainer send me to Orgrimmar?",a="Forsaken priests have turned toward shadow, while Darkspear trolls draw spiritual power from the loa and tribal traditions. Aelthalyste respects this difference and sends developing troll priests home to learn their people’s arts from their own elder.",al={"why go to orgrimmar","undercity to orgrimmar","why ur'kyo"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Ur'kyo?",a="Ur'kyo is a Darkspear troll priest trainer in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Spirits. He teaches troll spiritual customs and rites of passage.",al={"ur'kyo lore","who is urkyo","priest trainer ur'kyo"},it="identity"},{q="What is the significance of the Shadowguard ability?",a="Shadowguard is a protective ward unique to troll priests. Shadowy spirits and loa blessings circle the caster, striking any enemy that attacks.",al={"what is shadowguard","shadowguard spell lore","why is it important"},it="purpose"},{q="Do other races receive this quest?",a="The summons is for Darkspear troll priests visiting the Undercity around their twentieth season of experience. Forsaken priests have separate rites and training there.",al={"can undead do this","is this troll only","priest race quest"},gp=true},{q="Where in Orgrimmar is Ur'kyo located?",a="Ur'kyo is in the Valley of Spirits, Orgrimmar’s southern district set aside for the Darkspear trolls and their mystical practices.",al={"where is ur'kyo","urkyo location","find ur'kyo"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Aelthalyste want you to return to Orgrimmar?",a="Aelthalyste recognizes that troll spirituality requires traditions distinct from the Forsaken's dark discipline. She senses you have reached a critical point in your spiritual growth where you must undergo your own tribe's ancient rites of passage. Rather than holding you in the Undercity, she directs you back to your people's spiritual leaders so you can unlock vital defensive gifts essential for your survival.",al={"why send me to urkyo","aelthalyste motive","shadowguard purpose"},it="motive",rc="Troll",add="b54fa89c"},{q="Why does Aelthalyste send you rather than someone else?",a="This rite of passage is deeply personal to your growth as a troll priest. No messenger or champion can undergo spiritual testing on your behalf. Aelthalyste senses that the time has come specifically for your progression, meaning only you can stand before Ur'kyo to receive the sacred teachings of your faith.",al={"why me shadowguard","why does aelthalyste pick me"},it="why_me",rc="Troll",add="bb765c88"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you reach a milestone that joins the basics of holy and shadow magic with your people’s traditions.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, your priestly training joins communion with the loa to the defense of your tribe. Ur'kyo preserves this inheritance in the Valley of Spirits.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may see Aelthalyste respect the distinct traditions of her living allies. Visiting trolls receive instruction from their own elders, rather than Forsaken doctrine."},kw={"aelthalyste","orgrimmar","rite of passage","shadowguard","troll priest","undercity","ur'kyo","valley of spirits"},rel={"npc:ur-kyo","npc:aelthalyste","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Aelthalyste",["end"]="Ur'kyo",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5643},src={"Shadowguard (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:5646"] = {t="quest",n="Devouring Plague",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Devouring Plague training begins with Ur'kyo sending Forsaken priests home. They have come to Kalimdor to learn from the Darkspear, but Aelthalyste waits in Undercity to teach them the shadow arts of their own people.",h="In Orgrimmar, Devouring Plague training begins with Ur'kyo sending Forsaken priests home.",sec={{t="An Exchange of Faiths",b="Ur'kyo guides those drawn to spiritual power in Orgrimmar. Among the Horde, Darkspear trolls and Forsaken share a curious bond in matters of faith, while orcs and tauren show little inclination toward priestly worship. Ur'kyo knows Forsaken initiates must master the shadow arts tied to their own condition. In respect between their peoples, he sends wandering Forsaken back to Lordaeron to complete their training.",sp=0},{t="The War Quarter of Undercity",b="Beneath Lordaeron's ruins, Priestess Aelthalyste tends the flock in Undercity's War Quarter. Forsaken priests follow a solitary, grueling path shaped by their turn to shadow. They endure the painful touch of the Holy Light and learn to wield the devastating affliction of Shadow magic. When an initiate gains sufficient prowess, Aelthalyste gathers them close and teaches the affliction her kind calls Devouring Plague.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Ur'kyo, the troll priest trainer among the spirits in Orgrimmar, offers this to Forsaken priests who have reached their twentieth circle of power.",al={"quest giver","who starts devouring plague","ur'kyo location"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I need to go?",a="Travel across the Great Sea to Undercity in Tirisfal Glades. Seek Priestess Aelthalyste, who oversees Forsaken priest training in the War Quarter.",al={"where do i turn this in","aelthalyste location","undercity priest trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Ur'kyo send Forsaken back to Lordaeron?",a="Ur'kyo honors an understanding with Priestess Aelthalyste. Troll shadow priests understand loa and spirits, while Forsaken wield dark arts tied to their undead nature and need instruction from their own leaders.",al={"why go back to undercity","why does troll priest send me away"},it="motive"},{q="What is the significance of the Devouring Plague?",a="Devouring Plague is a potent affliction of the Shadow, learned by every priest at level twenty. It afflicts targets with devastating disease and siphons their life force back to the caster.",al={"what is devouring plague lore","forsaken priest plague"},it="power"},{q="Can other Horde races accept this quest?",a="No. Only Forsaken priests are offered this, as it represents their communion with their homeland's unique shadow disciplines.",al={"can trolls do this","is this quest undead only"},gp=true},{q="How does this fit into Horde priest relations?",a="The Horde shares training duties between Darkspear witch doctors and hex priests on Kalimdor and Forsaken shadow priests in the Eastern Kingdoms. Each people directs travelers to masters suited to their culture.",al={"trolls and undead priests","horde priest lore"},it="ties"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you draw on the Forsaken's doctrines of shadow and decay, channeling physical torment into dark rites such as Touch of Weakness and Dark Sacrifice.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, returning to the War Quarter in Undercity recalls that your allegiance and spiritual roots lie beneath Lordaeron's ruins, wherever Horde duties take you.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you share training duties between Ur'kyo in Durotar and Aelthalyste in Tirisfal, a sign of cooperation and mutual respect between the distant capitals."},kw={"aelthalyste","devouring plague","forsaken priest","orgrimmar","shadow priest","undercity","ur'kyo","war quarter"},rel={"npc:ur-kyo","npc:aelthalyste","zone:undercity","subzone:war-quarter"},m={start="Ur'kyo",["end"]="Aelthalyste",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5646},src={"Devouring Plague (Orgrimmar)"}}
E["quest:5654"] = {t="quest",n="Hex of Weakness",z="orgrimmar",s="In Durotar, Hex of Weakness carries a young Darkspear priest from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Tai'jin sends an initiate north to Ur'kyo, who welcomes new students into the tribe's spiritual circle and teaches the loa's darker arts.",h="In Durotar, Hex of Weakness carries a young Darkspear priest from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Circle",b="Young Darkspear priests continue their lessons in Razor Hill's barracks under Tai'jin's watch. Once an acolyte shows command of spiritual communion and shadow magic, the first lessons end. Tai'jin sends the promising priest north, across Durotar's red dirt canyons, toward the Horde capital. There, elder practitioners guide the tribe's wider magical traditions.",sp=0},{t="The Old Ways in the Valley of Spirits",b="The Darkspear keep a distinct cultural sanctuary in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, apart from the orcs' clanging forges and warrior grounds. Ur'kyo, an elder priest, waits there for new initiates. Joining his circle means embracing the ancestral traditions of the jungle trolls: honoring the loa while learning potent curses and hexes that sap an enemy's strength in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This rite marks an initiate's formal advancement in the Darkspear priesthood. Tai'jin sends developing troll priests from Durotar's coast to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar and brings them into the tribe's inner circle of spiritual practitioners.",al={"why do this quest","hex of weakness purpose","what does hex of weakness quest do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is a troll priest trainer in the barracks of Razor Hill in Durotar. She guides young Darkspear spellcasters through their early trials before sending them onward to the capital.",al={"who is quest giver","tai'jin lore","taijin"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ur'kyo?",a="Ur'kyo is an elder troll priest trainer in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. He oversees advanced spiritual training and passes tribal hexes and deep ancestral rites to Darkspear priests.",al={"who is ur'kyo","urkyo priest trainer","ur-kyo"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Valley of Spirits?",a="The Valley of Spirits is a secluded, swampy district in western Orgrimmar. It is the Darkspear trolls' main home within the orcish fortress-city, with their trainers, lodgings, and totems.",al={"valley of spirits location","where is ur'kyo","where to find ur'kyo"},it="place"},{q="What kind of magic does this training focus on?",a="Darkspear priests draw on the loa and ancient jungle troll traditions. They balance restorative spirit magic with debilitating curses such as Hex of Weakness, rather than relying only on the Holy Light favored by humans or dwarves.",al={"troll priest magic","what are the old ways","hex lore"},it="power"},{q="Can non-trolls undertake this quest?",a="No. This rite belongs to the Darkspear trolls' cultural traditions and their unique spells. Undead priests go to their own mentors and shadow philosophies in Tirisfal and the Undercity.",al={"can undead do this","is this troll only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tai'jin want this done?",a="Tai'jin recognizes that your basic training is complete and you are ready to delve deeper into the traditions of the Darkspear tribe. She sends you to Ur'kyo so you can be formally initiated into the circle and taught the ancient spiritual rites that define a true troll priest.",al={"taijin motive","why send me to urkyo","why learn hex of weakness"},it="motive",rc="Troll",add="f04dcf0d",nx={8}},{q="Why does Tai'jin send you instead of teaching you herself?",a="Tai'jin provides initial guidance to fledging priests in Razor Hill, but advanced spiritual instruction and tribal initiation are overseen by elder masters like Ur'kyo. To truly progress in the craft and master the deeper ways of your people, you must journey to the Valley of Spirits where the elders convene.",al={"why can't taijin teach me","why send me to orgrimmar","why must i go to urkyo"},it="why_me",rc="Troll",add="3c464e0c"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you move from novice lessons in Razor Hill toward recognition as a Darkspear priest, learning ancient curses passed down through generations.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you draw on communion with primal spirits, weaving tribal hexes with shadow and restorative spells, unlike the dogma of the Holy Light or the Forgotten Shadow.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see troll culture take root within the fortified walls of Thrall's growing capital as you travel from Razor Hill to the Valley of Spirits."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hex of weakness","loa","orgrimmar","sen'jin village","tai'jin","ur'kyo","valley of spirits"},rel={"npc:ur-kyo","npc:tai-jin","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Tai'jin",["end"]="Ur'kyo",level="10",faction="Horde",id=5654},src={"Hex of Weakness (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:5726"] = {t="quest",n="Hidden Enemies",z="orgrimmar",s="Thrall begins a covert search for the Burning Blade in Durotar. He asks a promising young adventurer to recover a Lieutenant's Insignia from Skull Rock, opening a way to uncover cultists working under the Horde's nose.",h="Thrall begins a covert search for the Burning Blade in Durotar.",sec={{t="The Rot Within Durotar",b="In Durotar, the new Horde struggles to secure a home, and Warchief Thrall faces betrayal from within. The Burning Blade has taken root just outside Orgrimmar's gates. Its cultists prey on lingering demonic corruption and hunger for dark power. Thrall needs someone to watch and listen without drawing notice.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrating Skull Rock",b="Skull Rock lies east of Orgrimmar. Its rugged caverns hold warlocks, voidwalkers, and fanatical cultists. Thrall sends you to take a Lieutenant's Insignia from one of the Burning Blade leaders. The emblem is meant to open the cult's hidden ranks, so Thrall can learn who directs its movements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Hidden Enemies?",a="Warchief Thrall gives it to you in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, after you report to Orgnil Soulscar.",al={"hidden enemies questgiver","who starts hidden enemies","where to start hidden enemies"},gp=true},{q="What is the goal of Hidden Enemies?",a="Thrall sends you east of Orgrimmar to Skull Rock to slay Burning Blade cultists and bring him a Lieutenant's Insignia.",al={"hidden enemies objective","what do i need for hidden enemies"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Thrall just send his elite guards to purge Skull Rock?",a="Thrall fears an open assault would let the true conspirators slip away and hide the corruption more deeply. Someone unknown to the cult can quietly gain credentials to enter its ranks without warning the high-ranking traitors behind it.",al={"why thrall needs adventurers","why not send the army"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a secluded cavern system on Durotar's eastern coast, northeast of Orgrimmar. The Burning Blade uses it as a hidden stronghold and summoning den.",al={"where is skull rock","what is skull rock cave"},it="place"},{q="What is the Lieutenant's Insignia used for?",a="The Lieutenant's Insignia proves a cultist's rank. Thrall plans to use it to disguise an operative and place them among the Burning Blade, where they can learn who directs its operations.",al={"what is the insignia for","lieutenants insignia purpose"},it="item"},{q="What other quests can be completed alongside this one?",a="You can also collect cultist collars at Skull Rock. The cult leader Gazz'uz carries the Eye of Burning Shadow, which can begin Burning Shadows.",al={"skull rock quests","quests in skull rock"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thrall want to investigate the Burning Blade?",a="Thrall views the Burning Blade cult as the single greatest internal threat to the young Horde. A treacherous demon-worshiping coven festering right on Orgrimmar's doorstep undermines everything the orcs have bled to build in Durotar. Rather than rashly striking without knowing the full depth of their reach, the Warchief aims to uncover how deeply the corruption goes and tear it out by the roots before it consumes their new homeland.",al={"why does Thrall want this","thrall motive hidden enemies","why investigate burning blade"},it="motive",add="aa12f8a2"},{q="Who are the Burning Blade cultists in Skull Rock?",a="You are hunting the agents and warlocks of the Burning Blade hiding inside Skull Rock, just east of Orgrimmar. Once a proud orc clan, the remnant has degraded into a shadow cult devoted to demonic corruption and shadowy manipulation. Entrenched in secret caves near the capital, they weave a web of treachery, greed, and dark magic aimed directly at subverting Thrall's new Horde from within.",al={"who are burning blade skull rock","skull rock enemies","target of hidden enemies"},it="target",add="d2691c1c"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are entrusted by Warchief Thrall to guard the heart of the new Horde from demonic subversion.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the struggle to overcome the blood-haze and shame of the demon curse. Hunting the Burning Blade is a personal fight to keep demonic blight from poisoning your people again.",["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you tread carefully under Thrall's strict oversight of fel arts. He calls on you to root out cultists whose unrestrained service to demons threatens Orgrimmar's survival."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","hidden enemies","lieutenant's insignia","orgrimmar","skull rock","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:burning-blade-clan","quest:827","quest:832","quest:823","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Thrall",level="12",faction="Horde",id=5726,ri={"Lieutenant's Insignia"}},src={"Hidden Enemies"}}
E["quest:5727"] = {t="quest",n="Hidden Enemies",z="orgrimmar",s="Thrall sends you into Orgrimmar to learn what the Burning Blade knows. After cult activity is found at Skull Rock, you carry a lieutenant's insignia to Neeru Fireblade and test his loyalties.",h="Thrall sends you into Orgrimmar to learn what the Burning Blade knows.",sec={{t="The Warchief's Gambit",b="Thrall turns to cunning instead of striking at the Cleft of Shadow. He knows Neeru Fireblade pretends to serve the Horde while aiding the cultists in secret. If Thrall strikes now, Neeru's masters will be warned and the trail into the conspiracy may end. So Thrall gives you an insignia taken from the cult in Durotar and asks you to pose as an initiate, to learn what Neeru knows.",sp=0},{t="The Cleft's Hidden Master",b="Neeru Fireblade waits in the Cleft of Shadow, outside the entrance to Ragefire Chasm. He takes you for a newly promoted lieutenant and scoffs at Thrall's ignorance. Neeru says the Burning Blade and its offshoots, including the Searing Blade, answer to the Shadow Council, which serves the Burning Legion. He boasts that he has manipulated Thrall into sending loyal soldiers against the cultists in the chasm, using the Warchief's forces to weed out the weak.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Thrall keep Neeru alive if he knows he is a traitor?",a="Thrall keeps Neeru alive because a traitor in the open can be watched. If Neeru were killed, the Shadow Council could replace him with someone harder to detect. Under watch, Neeru can unwittingly reveal the cult's movements in Orgrimmar.",al={"why thrall trust neeru","why keep neeru alive","neeru traitor"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Who is Neeru Fireblade?",a="Neeru Fireblade is an orc warlock who lives in the Cleft of Shadow. He claims to help Thrall reform warlocks into dutiful Horde servants, but secretly leads the Burning Blade beneath the city for the Shadow Council.",al={"neeru backstory","who is neeru"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What is the relationship between the Burning Blade and the Shadow Council?",a="The Burning Blade is an arm of the Shadow Council, not an independent sect. The Council also controls cults such as the Searing Blade in Ragefire Chasm, dividing and misleading ambitious practitioners under the Burning Legion's rule.",al={"burning blade shadow council connection","are burning blade shadow council"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who leads the cultists inside Ragefire Chasm?",a="The Searing Blade in Ragefire Chasm is led by Bazzalan, a satyr, and Jergosh the Invoker, an orc warlock. Neeru sends Thrall's adventurers against them to thin Horde loyalists and test his subordinates.",al={"ragefire chasm leaders","searing blade leaders"},it="leader"},{q="How did I obtain the Lieutenant's Insignia?",a="You recovered the Lieutenant's Insignia during Thrall's first investigation of cult activity in Durotar. It came from Burning Blade cultists at Skull Rock.",al={"where lieutenant insignia comes from","insignia source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Thrall send me to Neeru instead of confronting him himself?",a="Thrall cannot openly question or move against Neeru Fireblade without alerting the warlock that his treachery has been discovered. Neeru believes he still possesses the Warchief's full confidence and that he operates undetected within the Cleft of Shadow. By sending an unknown operative bearing the insignia of a fallen cult lieutenant, Thrall establishes an unwitting informant on the inside. You can infiltrate Neeru's network, glean critical intelligence regarding the Shadow Council's reach, and return vital information to the Warchief without blowing Thrall's strategic advantage.",al={"why send me to neeru","why does thrall need me","why not confront neeru directly"},it="why_me",add="7a6d2fe3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, demonic cults beneath Orgrimmar's foundations threaten the survival of the young nation.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may see Neeru claim a place for warlocks in the Horde. His treachery risks bringing severe condemnation on all who practice the fel arts under Thrall's rule.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Shadow Council's return beneath your capital echoes Draenor's dark past, a burden for those striving to escape bloodlust and demonic corruption."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","insignia","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","shadow council","thrall"},rel={"quest:5726","quest:829","quest:5761","npc:thrall","npc:bazzalan","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:ragefire","topic:shadow-council"},m={start="Thrall",level="12",faction="Horde",id=5727},src={"Hidden Enemies (2)"}}
E["quest:5729"] = {t="quest",n="Hidden Enemies",z="orgrimmar",s="Thrall's watch on Hidden Enemies reaches into the Cleft of Shadow. After Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker are killed beneath the city, Thrall sends you to win Neeru Fireblade's trust.",h="Thrall's watch on Hidden Enemies reaches into the Cleft of Shadow.",sec={{t="Thrall's Gambit",b="Thrall sees a chance after Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker are killed in Ragefire Chasm. He chooses not to expose Neeru Fireblade. Neeru has lost his underground lieutenants, leaving the local cult without its leaders. Thrall sends you back to the Cleft of Shadow to offer yourself as an ally who can fill that gap.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Deception",b="Neeru Fireblade fumes over the defeat of his conspirators in the Cleft of Shadow. He does not know that you carried out their executions on Thrall's orders, and curses the do-gooders who brought ruin to Ragefire Chasm. Taken by surprise, Neeru begins to lower his guard around you. Thrall can now watch the Shadow Council's influence from within Orgrimmar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Thrall just execute Neeru Fireblade immediately?",a="Thrall keeps Neeru in place so he can watch him while Neeru believes his cover remains intact. With you inside, Thrall can monitor the Burning Blade's communications and trace its ties to the Shadow Council.",al={"why spare neeru","why does thrall let neeru live","neeru alive"},it="motive"},{q="Who were Bazzalan and Jergosh?",a="Bazzalan was a satyr, and Jergosh the Invoker was an orc warlock. They led the Searing Blade cult deep within Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar before Thrall ordered their deaths.",al={"bazzalan","jergosh","who died in ragefire"},it="target"},{q="Does Neeru realize you killed his lieutenants?",a="No. Neeru believes Thrall's agents surprised and killed his lieutenants. He does not know that you carried out the executions while now offering him condolences and aid.",al={"does neeru know","neeru knows who killed them"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Neeru Fireblade located?",a="Neeru Fireblade is in the Cleft of Shadow, a cavern beneath the heart of Orgrimmar where warlocks, rogues, and shadow casters gather apart from the rest of the city.",al={"neeru location","find neeru","where is neeru fireblade"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade began as a fierce clan from Draenor, then became a demonic cult manipulated by the Shadow Council. In Kalimdor, its remnants seek to undermine Thrall's new Horde and restore demonic servitude.",al={"burning blade","burning blade cult"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after speaking to Neeru?",a="After winning Neeru's confidence and hearing his dismay over the losses in Ragefire Chasm, you return to Thrall in Grommash Hold to report your success and conclude the infiltration chain.",al={"what next","quest continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thrall send you to Neeru Fireblade instead of confronting him himself?",a="Thrall cannot openly confront or arrest Neeru without alerting the rest of the Shadow Council and the Burning Blade cult embedded throughout Durotar. Neeru believes he has Thrall's trust, and Thrall means to use him against their enemies. By sending you with the Burning Blade insignia you found, Thrall tests whether Neeru will take you for one of his own; Neeru welcomes you as a fellow member, even a rising lieutenant, and speaks freely. An official guard would raise immediate suspicion, but you can quietly glean their secrets from within.",al={"why send me to neeru","why doesnt thrall confront neeru","why use an agent for neeru"},it="why_me",add="29529508"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you find Neeru Fireblade among the warlock trainers in the Cleft of Shadow. His place there shows how close Thrall's new Horde comes to darker magic without succumbing to corruption.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the shape of an infiltration: first eliminate an asset's network, then step in as their trusted confidant.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Thrall use counter-espionage to secure Orgrimmar from within, alongside his diplomacy and statecraft.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know that rooting the Burning Blade out of Orgrimmar's bedrock helps protect your honor as your people shake off the old Horde's demonic legacy."},kw={"bazzalan","burning blade","cleft of shadow","hidden enemies","jergosh","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","shadow council","thrall"},rel={"quest:5726","npc:thrall","quest:829","zone:ragefire","npc:bazzalan","subzone:cleft","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Thrall",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="15",faction="Horde",id=5729},src={"Hidden Enemies (4)"}}
E["quest:5730"] = {t="quest",n="Hidden Enemies",z="orgrimmar",s="Neeru Fireblade has earned your trust, and Thrall awaits your report in Orgrimmar. The Warchief needs to know how far the Burning Blade's reach extends across Kalimdor.",h="Neeru Fireblade has earned your trust, and Thrall awaits your report in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Cult Unveiled",b="You carried a Lieutenant's Insignia from Skull Rock to Neeru Fireblade at Warchief Thrall's request. The warlock lives openly in the Cleft of Shadow. Later, you struck at the Searing Blade's leaders deep within Ragefire Chasm. By posing as a willing recruit and bearing the insignias of fallen cultists, you won Fireblade's trust. He revealed more of the network behind his operations.",sp=1},{t="Whispers of the Shadow Council",b="Neeru Fireblade believes you are a loyal lieutenant. He admits that the loss in Ragefire Chasm has set the Searing Blade back, but says the Shadow Council's greater designs remain intact. His masters have active agents in the Barrens and deeper in the forests of Ashenvale. Your report catches Thrall off guard: the demonic conspiracy reaches far beyond the tunnels beneath Orgrimmar.",sp=2},{t="The Warchief's Vigilance",b="Thrall chooses caution instead of executing Neeru at once. Keeping the warlock unaware that his cover is compromised lets the Horde monitor his communications and track the cult across Durotar, the Barrens, and Ashenvale. The Warchief prepares scouts and spies to investigate those branches, seeking to root out demonic corruption without reckless haste.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="Travel from the Cleft of Shadow to the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar and report to Warchief Thrall. Tell him what Neeru Fireblade disclosed about the Shadow Council's plans.",al={"hidden enemies goal","what to do hidden enemies 5","thrall turn in"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Neeru Fireblade trust me?",a="You recovered a Lieutenant's Insignia from the Burning Blade at Skull Rock and presented it to Neeru as an ambitious cult initiate. He believes you are a loyal asset.",al={"why neeru trusts me","tricking neeru","fireblade infiltration"},sp=1,it="why_me"},{q="Why doesn't Thrall arrest or execute Neeru Fireblade right away?",a="Thrall can learn more by letting Neeru believe his cover remains intact. The Warchief's scouts can monitor his messages and trace his contacts to larger Shadow Council cells across Kalimdor.",al={"why is neeru alive","why not kill neeru","why thrall leaves neeru"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What new information does Thrall learn from this report?",a="Thrall learns that the Shadow Council backs the cult beneath Orgrimmar and has agents plotting operations in the Barrens and the forests of Ashenvale.",al={"what did thrall learn","shadow council ashenvale","neeru secret"},sp=1},{q="Is the Burning Blade the same thing as the Searing Blade?",a="The Searing Blade is a local sect operating in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. It serves the wider Burning Blade cult, which the demonic Shadow Council directs.",al={"burning blade vs searing blade","ragefire chasm cults","cult differences"},it="ties"},{q="Does this quest chain continue anywhere?",a="Thrall tells you to rest and promises to call on you later. No direct continuation of this undercover line follows immediately.",al={"hidden enemies followup","next quest after hidden enemies","where does thrall send you next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Neeru Fireblade share his plans with you?",a="Neeru Fireblade believes you are a loyal lieutenant who has earned his trust by eliminating threats and serving the cult's interests. With the Searing Blade's operations in Ragefire Chasm thrown into disarray, Neeru is eager to minimize the fallout and pivot his focus toward broader Shadow Council ambitions in the Barrens and Ashenvale.",al={"neeru fireblade plans","why does neeru talk","neeru scheme ashenvale"},it="motive",add="e43a9a3d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you uncover treason within Orgrimmar's own borders. The young Horde must guard against ancient demonic corruption within while it battles enemies beyond.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see the danger in Neeru Fireblade's path. Fel practice can slip from sanctioned use into service to the Shadow Council.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see the Horde's early methods of espionage at work. Deep cover, counterintelligence, and patience take the place of immediate confrontation."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","burning blade","cleft of shadow","hidden enemies","neeru fireblade","ragefire chasm","searing blade","shadow council","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","quest:829","quest:5726","zone:ragefire","topic:shadow-council","zone:orgrimmar","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Neeru Fireblade",["end"]="Thrall",level="16",faction="Horde",id=5730},src={"Hidden Enemies (5)"}}
E["quest:6384"] = {t="quest",n="Ride to Orgrimmar",z="orgrimmar",s="A wind rider carries Horde travelers from the Crossroads to Orgrimmar. With Zargh’s fresh cuts of meat in hand, you fly to the capital’s Skytower and deliver them to Innkeeper Gryshka.",h="A wind rider carries Horde travelers from the Crossroads to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Wings Over the Savanna",b="Devrak sends trained wind riders between the Crossroads and Orgrimmar. The flight crosses the dry Barrens and reaches Durotar’s red cliffs, sparing travelers the hard journey on foot. From high above the dusty canyon trails, the wyverns carry messengers and travelers, along with dispatches and trade goods, straight to the capital.",sp=0},{t="Special Delivery for Gryshka",b="Zargh has prepared fresh cuts of meat for Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Strength. From the central Skytower, her inn is a short walk away. Gryshka accepts the parcel and remarks with fondness that Zargh knows how to win a lady’s heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight?",a="The flight introduces you to the Horde’s wind rider routes. You pay Devrak for passage from the Crossroads to Orgrimmar and carry Zargh’s fresh cuts of meat to Innkeeper Gryshka.",al={"why fly to orgrimmar","flight to orgrimmar purpose","why meat to orgrimmar"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the wind rider land in Orgrimmar?",a="The wind rider lands at Orgrimmar’s Skytower, above the Valley of Strength. Ramps lead down to the main square, nearby vendors, and Gryshka’s inn.",al={"where do i land in org","skytower location","orgrimmar flight landing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Gryshka?",a="Innkeeper Gryshka runs a tavern in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Strength. She welcomes travelers and shares a fond friendship with Zargh, who supplies fresh cuts for her kitchen.",al={"innkeeper gryshka","who is gryshka","gryshka location"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Devrak?",a="Devrak is the wind rider master at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He tends the wyverns and coordinates air travel between the outpost, Durotar, and other Horde settlements.",al={"devrak crossroads","who is devrak","crossroads wind rider master"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Zargh sending raw meat to Gryshka?",a="Zargh sends Gryshka fresh game from the Barrens as an offering. She appreciates the choice cuts and says they win her heart.",al={"zargh meats","why send meat to gryshka","zargh and gryshka"},it="motive"},{q="What should I do after delivering the meat?",a="After you deliver the meat, Gryshka sends you back to the Skytower to speak with Doras, Orgrimmar’s wind rider master, about the return flight.",al={"what next after ride to orgrimmar","next quest after gryshka","where to go after delivery"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Devrak want you to fly to Orgrimmar?",a="Devrak is the Crossroads wind rider master, responsible for connecting the Barrens to the rest of the Horde's flight network. By arranging passage for you to deliver Zargh's fresh parcel to Gryshka, he keeps vital courier traffic moving between outpost and capital while introducing traveling adventurers to the speed and convenience of wyvern transport.",al={"why does devrak send you","devrak motive","why ride to orgrimmar"},it="motive",add="a3e1a2de"},{q="Why does Devrak send you instead of flying to Orgrimmar himself?",a="Devrak cannot abandon his perch at the Crossroads. As flight master, his duty is to care for the wind riders and coordinate flights for couriers, scouts, and warriors across central Kalimdor. Handing the shipment to an able traveler heading toward the capital ensures the delivery arrives promptly without taking him away from his post.",al={"why send me","why can't devrak deliver the meat","why me ride to orgrimmar"},it="why_me",add="715139d2"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can travel by wind rider between the Crossroads in the central Barrens and Orgrimmar, where Warchief Thrall rules.",["profession:Cooking"]="Gryshka makes her taste clear when she receives Zargh’s gift: she prefers the finest beasts of Kalimdor served rare, to preserve their flavor."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","doras","gryshka","orgrimmar","skytower","wind rider","zargh"},rel={"quest:6365","quest:6385","quest:6386","npc:devrak","npc:innkeeper-gryshka","npc:zargh","npc:doras","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Devrak",["end"]="Innkeeper Gryshka",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6384},src={"Ride to Orgrimmar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6385"] = {t="quest",n="Doras the Wind Rider Master",z="orgrimmar",s="Innkeeper Gryshka needs a courier to carry her thanks to Zargh at the Crossroads. She sends travelers to Doras the Wind Rider Master at Orgrimmar's skytower to arrange the flight back to the Barrens.",h="Innkeeper Gryshka needs a courier to carry her thanks to Zargh at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="A Courier's Reply",b="Innkeeper Gryshka sends thanks to Zargh after a shipment of meat arrives safely from the Barrens hunting grounds. With no time to travel through Durotar herself, she trusts the established aerial courier network linking major Horde settlements to carry her letter back across the frontier.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Roost",b="At the flight tower in the Valley of Strength, Doras oversees Orgrimmar's wind rider roost. The trained wyverns carry military messages and supplies between the capital and outposts such as the Crossroads, far faster than anyone traveling by foot or kodo cart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Doras?",a="Doras is Orgrimmar's primary wind rider master. He manages the city's trained wyverns and coordinates aerial travel to distant Horde hubs across central Kalimdor.",al={"doras","who is doras","orgrimmar flight master"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Gryshka sending this letter?",a="Gryshka is sending Zargh, the butcher at the Crossroads, a note of thanks for the meat supplies that arrived safely at her tavern in Orgrimmar.",al={"why send letter","gryshka letter","what is the letter for"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Doras be found?",a="Doras is atop the central flight tower above Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Wooden ramps inside the tower lead up to him.",al={"where is doras","doras location","find doras"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after giving Gryshka's letter to Doras?",a="After you consult Doras, he prepares a wind rider to carry you back to the Barrens. You can deliver Gryshka's letter directly to Zargh at the Crossroads.",al={"what next","after doras","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Zargh?",a="Zargh is an orc butcher at the Crossroads in the Barrens and a friend of Gryshka. He sent her a gift of choice cuts of Barrens meat.",al={"zargh","who is zargh"}},{q="Why use wind riders instead of walking?",a="The overland route from Orgrimmar through Durotar and across the Southfury River into the Barrens is slow and perilous. The Horde uses tamed wind riders to swiftly carry scouts, orders, and couriers between settlements.",al={"why fly","wind rider purpose","flight path lore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Gryshka ask an adventurer to carry her letter?",a="Gryshka runs the busy central tavern in the Valley of Strength and cannot simply leave her post to trek back out to the Barrens. You have just arrived carrying a delivery from Zargh in the Crossroads, making you the natural courier to carry her reply. Since you already know the route and have unlocked flight connections, passing the letter to you allows her gratitude to return swiftly along the Horde's established wind rider network without pulling Orgrimmar's city watch away from guarding the capital.",al={"why me doras","why ask me gryshka letter","why not a guard carry gryshka letter"},it="why_me",add="a0f5ace5"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The wind rider network links Orgrimmar to key regional garrisons, helping the young Horde move troops and supplies across Kalimdor's wilderness.",["race:Orc"]="Since arriving on Kalimdor, orcs have forged a strong bond with its native wyverns. They rely on their agility and strength as flying mounts and beasts of burden."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","doras","flight master","gryshka","orgrimmar","wind rider","wyvern","zargh"},rel={"npc:doras","npc:innkeeper-gryshka","quest:6384","quest:6386","quest:6365","npc:zargh","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Innkeeper Gryshka",["end"]="Doras",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6385},src={"Doras the Wind Rider Master (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6386"] = {t="quest",n="Return to the Crossroads.",z="orgrimmar",s="Gryshka's reply is on its way from Orgrimmar to Zargh at the Crossroads. A wind rider carries it across the distance between Durotar and the Barrens.",h="Gryshka's reply is on its way from Orgrimmar to Zargh at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="A Winged Return",b="You carry Gryshka's written reply to Zargh after bringing her a parcel of prime meat in Orgrimmar. Doras, the wind rider master atop Orgrimmar's high bluffs, provides a mount for the return to the Barrens. You have already met Devrak at the Crossroads, so the wyverns know the flight path. The ride crosses the desert sky and saves you the long march overland across the Southfury River.",sp=0},{t="A Match Made in the Barrens",b="Zargh's courtship has won Gryshka's warm reply. Quality provisions have pleased her, and Zargh celebrates, even musing about an impending wedding. The delivery also brings you back to the Barrens' central hub for travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I have to use a wind rider to return?",a="Doras sends you by wind rider because you have already visited Devrak at the Crossroads. The wyverns can fly between the two roosts, saving time and keeping supply lines secure.",al={"why fly back","wind rider required","can i walk"},gp=true},{q="Who is Gryshka?",a="Gryshka is the innkeeper in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Zargh sent her choice Barrens meat in hopes of winning her favor.",al={"gryshka lore","who is gryshka","orgrimmar meat lady"},it="people"},{q="What was Zargh's goal in sending meat to Orgrimmar?",a="Zargh sent meat to court Gryshka. Among orcs, a gift of hearty, quality game from the Barrens is a grand romantic gesture.",al={"why did zargh send meat","zargh motivation","zargh letter"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this quest end?",a="You return to Zargh at the Crossroads in the Barrens, near the watchtower and stables, and hand back Gryshka's Letter.",al={"where to turn in","return location","who gets gryshka letter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Doras?",a="Doras is the wind rider master at the flight roost above Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. He manages the aerial mounts that travel across Kalimdor.",al={"doras wind rider","doras location","orgrimmar flight master"},it="people"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="You finish the Meats to Orgrimmar courier chain. Orgrimmar and the Crossroads are connected, and the Barrens lies open for further travel.",al={"chain follow up","next quest after return","meats to orgrimmar continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Doras want me to return to the Crossroads?",a="Doras has no personal stake in Zargh's romance, but as Orgrimmar's wind rider master, his role is to demonstrate the Horde's aerial courier network. Now that you have linked Orgrimmar to the flight roost at the Crossroads, sending you back on a wyvern with Gryshka's reply proves the system works while carrying vital personal correspondence back to the Barrens.",al={"why does doras send me back","doras motive return to crossroads","why take gryshkas letter back"},it="motive",add="0a3565f0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Orgrimmar's and the Crossroads' wind rider roosts link the Horde capital to Kalimdor's perilous plains, carrying trade and supplies between them.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know that hearty cuts of fresh game are among the finest gifts of affection and respect for a prospective mate."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","doras","gryshka","letter","orgrimmar","wind rider","wyvern","zargh"},rel={"quest:6385","quest:6384","quest:6365","npc:zargh","npc:doras","npc:devrak","subzone:crossroads","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Doras",["end"]="Zargh",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6386},src={"Return to the Crossroads."}}
E["quest:6608"] = {t="quest",n="You Too Good.",z="orgrimmar",s="Lumak sends you from Orgrimmar to find his friend Nat Pagle. Your skill has outgrown ordinary lessons, and Nat camps on a distant islet south of Theramore Isle.",h="Lumak sends you from Orgrimmar to find his friend Nat Pagle.",sec={{t="Lumak's Limits",b="Lumak trains fishers in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He sees that you have learned all he can teach about rod and reel, and admits you are too good for ordinary lessons. To learn the art of artisan fishing, you must seek knowledge beyond the city and the Horde.",sp=0},{t="An Unlikely Friendship",b="Lumak sends you to find his human friend, Nat Pagle. He warns you not to harm or eat Nat, despite the friction between the Horde and Alliance across Kalimdor. Nat camps on an islet south of Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh. He keeps clear of politics and cares only whether the fish are biting.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Lumak, the fishing trainer in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, sends you once your skill has grown beyond expert.",al={"who starts you too good","lumak quest giver","where to get you too good"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Nat Pagle located?",a="Nat Pagle camps on an islet off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, south of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nat pagle","nat pagle location","find nat pagle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does an orc have a human friend?",a="Lumak and Nat Pagle became friends through fishing, sharing a passion that crosses the bitter rivalry between orcs and humans.",al={"lumak and nat pagle friendship","why is nat pagle friends with an orc"},it="ties"},{q="What happens when I speak to Nat Pagle?",a="Nat Pagle gives you a demanding trial: travel across Azeroth and catch rare fish before he teaches you further.",al={"what does nat pagle teach","artisan fishing quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Theramore safe for Horde to pass through?",a="No. Theramore is a fortress town guarded by the Alliance. To reach Nat's island, skirt the coast or detour around town to avoid the guards.",al={"can horde go through theramore","getting to nat pagle as horde"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why can't Lumak train me further himself?",a="Lumak has taught you all he knows. Nat Pagle can teach you artisan fishing, and anglers across the known world regard him as a legend.",al={"why lumak stops training","expert to artisan fishing horde"},it="motive"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Even during the faction war, people can form bonds across its lines through a shared craft or pastime.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Lumak's patience, good humor, and respect for nature in the friendship he has made across enemy lines."},kw={"artisan fishing","dustwallow marsh","lumak","nat pagle","orgrimmar","theramore","you too good"},rel={"npc:nat-pagle","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Lumak",["end"]="Nat Pagle",faction="Horde",id=6608},src={"You Too Good."}}
E["quest:6611"] = {t="quest",n="To Gadgetzan You Go!",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Zamja sends Horde cooks south to learn from an eccentric goblin butcher.",h="In Orgrimmar, Zamja sends Horde cooks south to learn from an eccentric goblin butcher.",sec={{t="A Cook Outgrows Orgrimmar",b="Zamja trains cooks in the Drag, where she feeds warriors and travelers passing through Durotar. When a cook has learned every recipe and technique she can teach, Zamja admits she has imparted all her culinary mojo. She sends her seasoned pupil to Tanaris, saying only a master of strange and exotic meats can help a talented cook advance further.",sp=0},{t="The Butcher in the Desert",b="In Tanaris, Gadgetzan is a steam-powered trading hub run by the Steamwheedle Cartel. Dirge Quikcleave works inside the town tavern. The eccentric goblin butcher has an unconventional palate and no squeamishness about food. Across Kalimdor, he is known for turning monstrous desert creatures, and sometimes scraps of leather, into hearty meals for hardened adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Gadgetzan?",a="Zamja, the troll cooking trainer near the cookfires in Orgrimmar's Drag, sends cooks who have mastered everything she knows.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","zamja quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zamja send you away?",a="Zamja has exhausted the recipes and techniques she can teach. She sends promising cooks to Dirge Quikcleave in Tanaris, an eccentric expert known for making meals from the harshest desert ingredients.",al={"why gadgetzan","why dirge quikcleave","cooking master"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Dirge Quikcleave?",a="Dirge Quikcleave is a goblin butcher and artisan cooking trainer in Gadgetzan's inn. He has a rough temperament, odd ideas about nutrition, including finding protein in old leather boots, and mastery of high-end, exotic wilderness cooking.",al={"who is dirge","dirge gadgetzan"},it="target"},{q="Is this quest required to learn Artisan Cooking?",a="No. This is a breadcrumb pointing Horde cooks toward Tanaris. A cook with sufficient skill can travel straight to Gadgetzan and speak with Dirge Quikcleave without Zamja's referral.",al={"do i need this quest","breadcrumb cooking","is it mandatory"},gp=true},{q="Where is Gadgetzan located?",a="Gadgetzan is a walled desert trading hub operated by the Steamwheedle Cartel in northern Tanaris, far south on Kalimdor below Thousand Needles.",al={"gadgetzan location","where is dirge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Zamja actually learn anything when you return?",a="Zamja cheekily demands that you return and teach her once you become the big cook on the block. She remains an expert trainer in Orgrimmar, tending her cookfires for the next generation of travelers.",al={"does zamja learn cooking","teach zamja"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you reach the point where capital city instruction runs out, and you must venture into the dangerous wilds to study under an artisan master.",["faction:Horde"]="Orgrimmar relies on outside specialists, including neutral goblin chefs, to take its crafters beyond standard tribal staples."},kw={"artisan cooking","cooking","dirge quikcleave","gadgetzan","orgrimmar","tanaris","valley of strength","zamja"},rel={"npc:zamja","npc:dirge-quikcleave","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","topic:goblin"},m={start="Zamja",["end"]="Dirge Quikcleave",faction="Horde",id=6611},src={"To Gadgetzan You Go!"}}
E["quest:6623"] = {t="quest",n="Horde Trauma",z="orgrimmar",s="At Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, Horde Trauma calls skilled medics into front-line surgery. Doctor Gregory Victor, chief physician of the Horde's trauma division, seeks hands able to save lives under extreme pressure.",h="At Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, Horde Trauma calls skilled medics into front-line surgery.",sec={{t="A Summons from Hammerfall",b="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, the orc first aid trainer Arnok tells proficient healers that they have caught Doctor Gregory Victor's attention. Victor oversees Horde Trauma from Hammerfall, tucked away in the contested hills of the Arathi Highlands. Arnok regards the summons as the pinnacle of professional advancement for a battlefield surgeon.",sp=0},{t="The Brutal Work of Battlefield Triage",b="At Hammerfall, constant skirmishes with Stromgarde's forces and local hostile factions leave Victor inundated with wounded grunts, raiders, and scouts. The chief physician wastes no time welcoming recruits with pleasantries. Instead, he orders newcomers into their scrubs to prove their worth in brutal, fast-paced emergency triage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Horde Trauma?",a="Horde Trauma is the Horde's dedicated medical and surgical branch on the front lines. Doctor Gregory Victor leads it from Hammerfall, where its members specialize in battlefield medicine, emergency triage, and severe combat injuries under chaotic conditions.",al={"horde trauma faction","what is horde trauma","who are horde trauma"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends me on this assignment?",a="Arnok, the orc first aid trainer in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, issues the summons. He regards serving under Doctor Gregory Victor as the pinnacle of professional advancement for an aspiring field medic.",al={"quest giver horde trauma","who starts horde trauma","krenk choplimb","arnok"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Doctor Gregory Victor located?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is stationed in the medical infirmary at Hammerfall in the northeastern Arathi Highlands.",al={"doctor gregory victor location","where is victor","hammerfall doctor"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Hammerfall?",a="When you arrive, Doctor Victor immediately tells you to don your scrubs for the follow-up assignment, Triage. You are tested under high stress as you prioritize and treat wounded soldiers whose condition is rapidly worsening, before they succumb to their injuries.",al={"what comes after horde trauma","next quest after horde trauma","triage quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Hammerfall so desperate for field medics?",a="Hammerfall is surrounded by hostilities in Arathi and faces relentless conflict with human forces, syndicate operatives, and local beasts. Casualties stream into the encampment constantly, pressing its small medical staff to the limit.",al={"why hammerfall need medics","hammerfall medical situation"},it="place"},{q="Can Alliance players take this assignment?",a="No. Horde Trauma is for members of the Horde. The Alliance has an equivalent medical evaluation led by Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen at Theramore Isle.",al={"can alliance do horde trauma","alliance version of horde trauma"},gp=true},{q="Why does Arnok send me to Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor, the chief physician of Horde Trauma stationed at Hammerfall, personally requested you. Arnok holds Doctor Victor in the highest esteem and considers learning under him the opportunity of a lifetime—one he claims he would give anything to receive himself. Out of deep professional respect and excitement for your talent, Arnok wants to ensure you do not squander such a rare summons.",al={"why does krenk want this","krenk choplimb motive","why send to victor","why does arnok want this","arnok motive"},it="motive",add="ac636cdf"},{q="Why does Doctor Victor request me specifically?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is seeking out the most capable field medics in the Horde to join the ranks of Horde Trauma in the Arathi Highlands. Your proven mastery of first aid has caught his attention in Hammerfall, prompting a direct personal summons for you to train under him rather than taking on unproven recruits or ordinary soldiers.",al={"why me horde trauma","why does victor need me","why does doctor victor want me"},it="why_me",add="b6720468"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on rugged battlefield surgeons to keep grunts patched up and swinging in brutal frontier conflicts like the Arathi Highlands.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can seal wounds with divine magic, but secular triage teaches you to judge who can be saved when your mana runs dry."},kw={"arathi highlands","doctor gregory victor","first aid","hammerfall","horde trauma","arnok","triage"},rel={"npc:doctor-gregory-victor","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","topic:horde"},m={start="Arnok",["end"]="Doctor Gregory Victor",faction="Horde",id=6623},src={"Horde Trauma (quest)"}}
E["quest:6962"] = {t="quest",n="Treats for Great-father Winter",z="orgrimmar",s="At the Smokywood Pastures display in Orgrimmar, the Greatfather Winter performer is worn out from hearing holiday wishes. He asks you for gingerbread cookies and milk.",h="At the Smokywood Pastures display in Orgrimmar, the Greatfather Winter performer is worn out from hearing...",sec={{t="A Weary Patron of Winter",b="The Greatfather Winter who greets visitors in the Valley of Strength works for Smokywood Pastures. Long hours listening to citizens speak of festive treats leave him hungry. He turns to passing travelers for warm baking and a cold drink.",sp=0},{t="Culinary Holiday Spirit",b="You can bake the cookies with Holiday Spices sold by Smokywood Pastures peddlers and Small Eggs gathered from wild birds. Bring them together with Ice Cold Milk from a local tavern, and the feast's organizers offer you festive cheer and a small token of gratitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Greatfather Winter in Orgrimmar?",a="In Orgrimmar, Greatfather Winter is an actor hired by Smokywood Pastures to portray the legendary figure during the Feast of Winter Veil. He sits near the holiday trade display in the Valley of Strength, greeting Horde citizens and listening to their festive requests.",al={"who is great father winter","orgrimmar greatfather winter","is he the real winter father"},it="identity"},{q="What treats does Greatfather Winter ask for?",a="He asks you for five Gingerbread Cookies and one serving of Ice Cold Milk to help him through a long day of greeting holiday visitors.",al={"what does he want","treats requested","what cookies does he need"},it="item",gp=true},{q="How do you make Gingerbread Cookies?",a="Smokywood Pastures vendors around the holiday display sell the recipe and Holiday Spices. Combine the spices with Small Eggs gathered from wild birds, then bake the cookies over a cooking fire.",al={"how to get gingerbread cookies","gingerbread cookie recipe","cookie ingredients"},gp=true},{q="Where can Ice Cold Milk be found?",a="You can buy Ice Cold Milk from food and drink vendors, innkeepers, or barkeeps throughout Orgrimmar and other major settlements.",al={"where to get ice cold milk","buy milk","milk vendor"},gp=true},{q="Why is Greatfather Winter asking for food himself?",a="Listening to children and citizens talk about food, gifts, and festivities all day leaves the Greatfather Winter performer hungry. Since he cannot easily leave his post in the Valley of Strength, he asks passing travelers for a quick snack.",al={"why does he want treats","is greatfather winter hungry"},it="motive"},{q="Does this quest have an Alliance counterpart?",a="Yes. In Ironforge, Greatfather Winter makes the same request of Alliance champions for gingerbread cookies and cold milk during the festival.",al={"alliance version","ironforge treats"}},{q="What are the Gingerbread Cookies and Ice Cold Milk for?",a="Smokywood Pastures has Great-father Winter sitting out greeting festival celebrants all day long, and the holiday cheer is hungry work. The fresh gingerbread cookies and refreshing jug of ice cold milk are simply a modest, comforting snack to keep his spirits high while listening to visitors' holiday wishes in Orgrimmar.",al={"why milk and cookies","gingerbread cookie use","ice cold milk winter veil"},it="item",add="87543d9b"},{q="Why does Great-father Winter ask you instead of getting the treats himself?",a="Great-father Winter is stuck in his festive seat in the Valley of Strength entertaining guests and spreading holiday goodwill throughout the Feast of Winter Veil. Abandoning his post to go shopping or bake treats would leave visitors disappointed and disrupt the festivities, so he relies on passing adventurers to run the errand.",al={"why does greatfather winter need me","why cant great-father winter get milk","why ask adventurer treats"},it="why_me",add="1b7dc40f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As an apprentice chef, you can practice simple baking by turning wild eggs and seasonal spices into festive gingerbread.",["faction:Horde"]="In Orgrimmar, Smokywood Pastures' goblin traders bring the feast and a moment of domestic cheer to the warrior city."},kw={"gingerbread cookie","greatfather winter","holiday spices","ice cold milk","orgrimmar","smokywood pastures","treats for great-father winter","winter veil"},rel={"npc:greatfather-winter","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Great-father Winter",faction="Horde",id=6962,ri={"Gingerbread Cookie","Ice Cold Milk"}},src={"Treats for Great-father Winter"}}
E["quest:6984"] = {t="quest",n="A Smokywood Pastures' Thank You!",z="orgrimmar",s="Great-father Winter waits in Orgrimmar to thank those who recovered Smokywood Pastures' stolen holiday treats. Kaymard Copperpinch sends you to receive a token of appreciation for bringing the supplies back.",h="Great-father Winter waits in Orgrimmar to thank those who recovered Smokywood Pastures' stolen holiday treats.",sec={{t="A Corporate Holiday",b="In Orgrimmar, Smokywood Pastures sells treats, recipes, and seasonal cheer for the Feast of Winter Veil. Their shipment was stolen in the snowy hills of the Alterac Mountains, and business stalled. With the treats recovered and the Abominable Greench dealt with, Kaymard Copperpinch sends you to receive the company's thanks.",sp=0},{t="Audience with Great-father Winter",b="Great-father Winter waits beside the holiday tree in the Valley of Strength. The goblins have arranged for him to honor those who rescued the holiday supplies with a seasonal blessing and a Smokywood Pastures Special Gift.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to speak with Great-father Winter?",a="Kaymard Copperpinch, Smokywood Pastures' representative in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, sends you to Great-father Winter after you recover the company's stolen holiday treats.",al={"who starts this quest","quest giver","kaymard role"},it="identity"},{q="What did I do to earn Smokywood Pastures' gratitude?",a="You tracked down the Abominable Greench in the Alterac Mountains and recovered the stolen holiday treats, saving Smokywood Pastures' supplies for the Feast of Winter Veil.",al={"why do they thank me","what treats were stolen","greench background"},it="history"},{q="Where is Great-father Winter located in Orgrimmar?",a="Great-father Winter waits beneath the decorated Winter Veil tree in the Valley of Strength, beside the Smokywood Pastures vendor stalls.",al={"great-father winter location","where is santa in org","winter veil tree org"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Great-father Winter?",a="Great-father Winter is an elemental or mythic herald of the changing seasons, said to cover the land in winter snow. During the Feast of Winter Veil, mortals wear his red robes to spread goodwill and give treats to children and adventurers.",al={"who is great-father winter","is great-father winter real","winter veil lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is Smokywood Pastures?",a="Smokywood Pastures is a goblin-run culinary and agricultural enterprise. It supplies festive foods, seasonal ingredients, and decorations to the Horde and the Alliance during the Feast of Winter Veil.",al={"smokywood pastures lore","who are smokywood pastures","goblin holiday vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Do I receive anything else after speaking with him?",a="Yes. Great-father Winter gives you a Smokywood Pastures Special Gift on the company's behalf, and your efforts earn standing with the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"quest reward","disguise kit","mail gift"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Kaymard Copperpinch send you to Great-father Winter?",a="Kaymard Copperpinch and Smokywood Pastures want to reward you for recovering their stolen treats. By directing you to Great-father Winter to receive a special Feast of Winter Veil gift in person, the goblins make good on their gratitude while upholding the festive commercial goodwill of the season.",al={"why does kaymard thank me","kaymard copperpinch motive","why send to great-father winter"},it="motive",add="553cdbb2"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="In Orgrimmar, the Horde's Winter Veil celebration blends shamanic reverence for the changing seasons with goblin commerce.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can rely on Smokywood Pastures for seasonal supplies, exotic recipes, and festive ingredients eagerly awaited each year."},kw={"feast of winter veil","great-father winter","greench","kaymard copperpinch","orgrimmar","smokywood pastures","valley of strength","winter veil"},rel={"npc:great-father-winter","npc:kaymard-copperpinch","zone:orgrimmar","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},m={start="Kaymard Copperpinch",["end"]="Great-father Winter",faction="Horde",id=6984},src={"A Smokywood Pastures' Thank You! (Horde)"}}
E["quest:7493"] = {t="quest",n="The Journey Has Just Begun",z="orgrimmar",s="After Onyxia's fall, skilled leatherworkers in Orgrimmar learn how her scales can guard against the black dragonflight. Overlord Runthak recognizes their craft and teaches a rare technique for making protective cloaks, needed against the flames of Blackrock Spire.",h="After Onyxia's fall, skilled leatherworkers in Orgrimmar learn how her scales can guard against the black...",sec={{t="A Broodmother's Legacy",b="Onyxia's fall is a triumph for the Horde, yet the black dragonflight remains a threat. The broodmother's scaled hide resists draconic flame. Horde leaders seek craftsmen who can turn the dragon's remains into defensive armor rather than let them go to waste.",sp=0},{t="Shield Against Shadow Flame",b="Overlord Runthak teaches gifted leatherworkers to stitch the Onyxia Scale Cloak. The knowledge is no mere show or mark of prestige. Deep within Blackrock Mountain, Onyxia's brother Nefarian breathes devastating fire. Without the enchanted protection of their broodmother's scales, any vanguard facing the Lord of Blackrock would be reduced to ash.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they located?",a="Overlord Runthak offers this in Orgrimmar. He recognizes Horde champions with master leatherworking expertise who aided in Onyxia's defeat.",al={"runthak quest giver","where is overlord runthak","quest start"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What requirement is needed to receive this quest?",a="Only skilled leatherworkers who have completed the aftermath of Onyxia's defeat can receive this, such as those who finished 'Victory for the Horde' or 'A Most Puzzling Circumstance'.",al={"leatherworking requirement","how to get quest","prerequisites"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What does Overlord Runthak teach?",a="Overlord Runthak teaches leatherworkers the technique for crafting the Onyxia Scale Cloak from scales taken from the fallen broodmother.",al={"quest reward recipe","onyxia cloak pattern","what do i learn"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why is the Onyxia Scale Cloak important?",a="The cloak shields its wearer from Nefarian's deadly, incendiary breath. Without its unique protection, facing the brood's master would prove fatal.",al={"why make cloak","cloak purpose","nefarian cloak"},it="item"},{q="Who is the Lord of Blackrock?",a="Nefarian is the Lord of Blackrock, a powerful black dragon and Onyxia's brother. He plots from the heights of Blackrock Mountain to dominate the mortal races.",al={"who is lord of blackrock","nefarian identity","blackrock lord"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the quest state that the journey has just begun?",a="Onyxia has been slain, but the broader war against the black dragonflight and Nefarian's schemes inside Blackrock Mountain has only escalated.",al={"meaning of title","journey just begun why"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Overlord Runthak want this done?",a="Overlord Runthak seeks the total eradication of the Black Dragonflight. While Onyxia's defeat was a momentous triumph, her brood still infests the realm under the command of her brother, Nefarian. By imparting the ancient technique to forge protective cloaks from the broodmother's scales, Runthak ensures that the champions of the Horde possess the vital defense needed to withstand Nefarian's lethal Shadow Flame and finish the war.",al={"why does runthak give this quest","overlord runthak motive","runthak goal"},it="motive",add="cb1b5404"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, protective gear forged from fallen enemies is vital to guarding its forces against further draconic devastation."},kw={"blackrock","broodmother","cloak","leatherworking","runthak","nefarian","onyxia","scale"},rel={"npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","quest:7781","topic:horde"},m={start="Overlord Runthak",faction="Horde",id=7493},src={"The Journey Has Just Begun (Horde)"}}
E["quest:7783"] = {t="quest",n="The Lord of Blackrock",z="orgrimmar",s="Nefarian's severed head is carried from Blackrock Mountain to Orgrimmar as proof of victory. Presented to Warchief Thrall, it marks the fall of a great enemy of the Horde.",h="Nefarian's severed head is carried from Blackrock Mountain to Orgrimmar as proof of victory.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Ruin",b="Nefarian has fallen at last. He masterminded Blackwing Lair and led the black dragon brood in the Eastern Kingdoms. His colossal, battle-scarred head proves his death. For Horde warriors, carrying the prize from the burning heights of Blackrock Mountain across the Great Sea to Durotar brings great honor.",sp=0},{t="The Warchief's Judgment",b="The trophy is brought before Warchief Thrall. He knows the corruption of Blackrock Mountain well. He freed his people from the internment camps and led them away from the old Horde's demonic bloodlust. The son of Deathwing has fallen, and the Blackrock orcs are free of the dark dragon's cruel dominion.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Father",b="Nefarian's death ends the black dragonflight's twisted experiments, but danger remains. When Thrall sees the dragon's severed head, he says Deathwing surely stirs at the news of his son's destruction. The victory is real, and greater terrors still sleep beneath the world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nefarian?",a="Nefarian is a great black dragon and the son of Deathwing. From his lair atop Blackrock Mountain, he conducted twisted experiments to create the chromatic dragonflight and manipulated mortal races, especially the Dark Horde, to do his bidding.",al={"nefarian backstory","who is nefarian","black dragon lord"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the trophy delivered to Thrall?",a="Thrall is the Warchief of the Horde. He led the orcs out of the internment camps and away from the old Horde's demonic bloodlust, so proof that the dragon who enslaved the Blackrock orcs and the Dark Horde has fallen belongs in his hands.",al={"why thrall","who receives the head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens in Orgrimmar when the head is turned in?",a="When Nefarian's head is returned and mounted in Orgrimmar, the city celebrates. The capital's Horde members nearby receive the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer, which boosts their combat prowess.",al={"head buff","orgrimmar world buff","rallying cry buff"}},{q="Does this quest have an Alliance equivalent?",a="Yes. Alliance heroes deliver Nefarian's head to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep, granting their city the same blessing.",al={"alliance version","alliance counterpart"}},{q="Why is Deathwing a concern?",a="Deathwing is Nefarian's father and the patriarch of the black dragonflight. Defeating his son does not remove the danger posed by the dragonfather.",al={"evil one stirs","who is the evil one"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the head come from?",a="The Head of Nefarian comes from Nefarian's corpse at the pinnacle of Blackwing Lair, after he is defeated.",al={"how to get head of nefarian","quest starter item"},it="origin"},{q="Why must the Head of Nefarian be brought to Orgrimmar?",a="Carving the massive, battle-scarred head from the fallen dragon provides undeniable proof that the master of Blackrock Spire has been vanquished. Delivering such a monstrous trophy back to Orgrimmar demonstrates the Horde's supreme might, celebrates a monumental victory over the Black Dragonflight, and allows the Warchief's council to verify that Nefarian's twisted experiments within the mountain have finally come to an end.",al={"why bring nefarian head","head of nefarian motive","why give head to eitrigg"},it="motive",add="d14146dc"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Nefarian's fall restores the Horde's honor and frees the Blackrock region from the dragon who enslaved the renegade Dark Horde.",["race:Orc"]="For you as an orc, presenting Nefarian's head to Thrall brings retribution against the beast who puppeteered Rend Blackhand and enslaved orcish clans for his experiments.",["class:Warrior"]="For you as a warrior, bearing a dragon lord's massive severed skull to the Warchief is a great mark of martial renown."},kw={"blackrock","blackwing lair","deathwing","dragonslayer","thrall","nefarian","orgrimmar","rallying cry"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","npc:deathwing","quest:7781"},m={start="Head of Nefarian#Horde",["end"]="Thrall",faction="Horde",id=7783},src={"The Lord of Blackrock (Horde)"}}
E["quest:7784"] = {t="quest",n="The Lord of Blackrock",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Nefarian's severed head is brought before the Horde. After Thrall confirms the black dragon's death, he sends the victor to High Overlord Saurfang in the Valley of Strength to show the trophy to all.",h="In Orgrimmar, Nefarian's severed head is brought before the Horde.",sec={{t="A Trophy for the Horde",b="Nefarian's head reaches Orgrimmar after the black dragon is slain atop Blackwing Lair. Warchief Thrall confirms that Deathwing's son has fallen, then sends the victor to High Overlord Saurfang in the Valley of Strength. There, the remains are prepared for public display, a warning to enemies and a rallying cry for the true Horde.",sp=0},{t="Claiming the Legacy",b="Nefarian ruled the heights of Blackrock Mountain, bending the Blackrock orcs and the Dark Horde to his will. By striking him down and raising his head in the Valley of Strength, Thrall's Horde deals a mighty blow against the Black Dragonflight. Saurfang calls on all of Orgrimmar to rejoice in the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="After proving Nefarian's death to Thrall, you report to High Overlord Saurfang in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. The severed head is put on public display, and you receive honors.",al={"what does this quest do","lord of blackrock turn in","why go to saurfang"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is High Overlord Saurfang?",a="High Overlord Saurfang is a veteran orc warrior and one of the Horde's greatest champions. He is stationed in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, where he receives the head and has it mounted for all to see.",al={"who is saurfang","high overlord saurfang role"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Nefarian's head put on display?",a="Nefarian's mounted head proves that the master of Blackrock Mountain has fallen. Its display strengthens the morale of Orgrimmar's defenders, and everyone in the city receives the Rallying Cry of the Dragonslayer.",al={"why mount nefarians head","nefarian head display orgrimmar"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Nefarian?",a="Nefarian was a great black dragon and a son of Deathwing. From Blackwing Lair atop Blackrock Mountain, he commanded the Blackrock orcs and the Dark Horde and bred the chromatic dragonflight.",al={"who was nefarian","nefarian lore"},it="target"},{q="Where is High Overlord Saurfang located?",a="Saurfang is in the Valley of Strength, Orgrimmar's central entrance district.",al={"where is saurfang","saurfang location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Thrall play in this?",a="Warchief Thrall receives Nefarian's head first. After confirming the dragon's death, he sends you to Saurfang to have the trophy officially mounted.",al={"why thrall","thrall involvement"},it="motive"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Nefarian's public display proves the reformed Horde's might against the black dragon who manipulated the orcs of Blackrock Mountain. It reinforces Thrall's new order.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may feel deep catharsis at the fall of the dragon who held the Blackrock clan in thrall. His defeat lifts a dishonorable shadow from your people."},kw={"blackwing lair","thrall","head of nefarian","saurfang","orgrimmar","nefarian","valley of strength"},rel={"npc:varok-saurfang","npc:thrall","quest:7781","subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde"},m={start="Thrall",["end"]="High Overlord Saurfang",faction="Horde",id=7784},src={"The Lord of Blackrock (Horde 2)"}}
E["quest:809"] = {t="quest",n="Ak'Zeloth",z="orgrimmar",s="Neeru Fireblade sends you from Orgrimmar into the Barrens after signs of demonic corruption emerge. His contact waits near the border.",h="Neeru Fireblade sends you from Orgrimmar into the Barrens after signs of demonic corruption emerge.",sec={{t="A Trail of Shadow",b="Neeru Fireblade says the Burning Blade still threatens the Horde with demonic corruption. After you bring him a Burning Blade insignia collar from Durotar, he sends you into the Barrens. A cult gathers around the Demon Seed, an artifact of vile power, and Neeru wants you to find his contact near the border.",sp=0},{t="The Outpost Contact",b="Ak'Zeloth waits near the Far Watch Post, on the Durotar-Barrens border. Neeru's assistant doubts aloud that his master truly wants the Demon Seed destroyed. He then tells you how to handle the artifact atop Dreadmist Peak.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Neeru Fireblade, a warlock in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, gives you this request after you present him with a Burning Blade collar.",al={"quest starter","where to get ak'zeloth","neeru fireblade quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Ak'Zeloth located?",a="Ak'Zeloth waits just outside the Far Watch Post, along the eastern Barrens border where the bridge crosses from Durotar.",al={"ak'zeloth location","where is ak'zeloth","find ak'zeloth"},gp=true},{q="What is the Demon Seed?",a="The Demon Seed is an artifact of demonic power held by the Burning Blade cult atop Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens.",al={"demon seed lore","what is the seed"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Ak'Zeloth find Neeru's orders strange?",a="Ak'Zeloth says only that it is strange Neeru wants the Demon Seed destroyed, then agrees to explain how to remove it.",al={"why is ak'zeloth surprised","strange reaction ak'zeloth"},sp=1},{q="What quest follows this one?",a="After you speak with Ak'Zeloth, he sends you to climb Dreadmist Peak and neutralize the corrupting relic.",al={"next quest after ak'zeloth","ak'zeloth followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quest part of the Burning Blade storyline?",a="Yes. The Burning Blade cult's activity in Durotar leads into the wider, organized cult activity in the Barrens.",al={"burning blade questline","orgrimmar cult quest"},it="history"},{q="Why does Neeru Fireblade want the Demon Seed destroyed?",a="Neeru Fireblade claims that ever since the Burning Legion's defeat, he has dedicated himself to rooting out remaining demonic corruption in orcish lands. When you brought him a Burning Blade cult collar, he declared that it confirmed his worst fears. According to Neeru, the cult draws its strength from the Demon Seed atop Dreadmist Peak, and smashing this demonic relic is vital to halting their dark influence over the Horde.",al={"neeru fireblade motive","why destroy demon seed","why does neeru send you"},it="motive",add="91b6b00f"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may notice that even Neeru Fireblade's assistant questions the order to destroy a demonic relic.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the cost of the Burning Legion's grasp. The Burning Blade cult and demonic relics on your doorstep threaten that hard-won freedom.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect the young trade and travel routes linking Durotar with the Barrens by securing the Far Watch Post and clearing Dreadmist Peak."},kw={"ak'zeloth","barrens","burning blade","cleft of shadow","demon seed","dreadmist peak","far watch post","neeru fireblade"},rel={"quest:829","quest:924","subzone:far-watch-post","subzone:dreadmist-peak","zone:barrens","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Neeru Fireblade",["end"]="Ak'Zeloth",level="13",faction="Horde",id=809},src={"Ak'Zeloth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:829"] = {t="quest",n="Neeru Fireblade",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade studies dark arts he says can protect the Horde. Margoz sends you from Durotar with a Searing Collar taken from the Burning Blade cult, hoping the warlock can explain its demonic power.",h="In Orgrimmar, Neeru Fireblade studies dark arts he says can protect the Horde.",sec={{t="A Shaman's Limits",b="Margoz has found the limit of shamanic arts. The collars taken from Burning Blade cultists at Skull Rock carry demonic sorcery, beyond what he can unravel. Shamans draw on the elements and ancestral spirits, so Margoz sends you to a warlock in the capital to learn what the collars do.",sp=0},{t="Into the Cleft of Shadow",b="Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow lies beneath its red cliffs. Warlocks and other practitioners of forbidden magic work there under Thrall's wary eye. Neeru Fireblade lives in the cavern and says he studies fel power to thwart demonic threats. When you bring him the collar, his curiosity turns Durotar's investigation toward the warlock enclave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Margoz send me to a warlock?",a="Margoz is a shaman, drawing power from the elements and ancestral spirits. The Searing Collars from Skull Rock are demonic, so he needs someone trained in fel magic and the dark arts to understand their enchantments and origins.",al={"why warlock","why neeru","margoz warlock"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Neeru Fireblade?",a="You can find Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar, where warlocks, rogues, and shadow casters gather.",al={"neeru location","where is neeru fireblade","cleft of shadow neeru"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can Neeru Fireblade be trusted?",a="Margoz doubts Neeru's claims that his occult research is benign and meant to fight demons. Thrall permits warlocks in Orgrimmar under strict supervision, but whether Neeru can be trusted remains uncertain.",al={"is neeru evil","neeru trustworthy","can i trust fireblade"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Example Collar?",a="The Example Collar is one of the Searing Collars taken from Burning Blade cultists at Skull Rock. Margoz gives it to you to bring to Neeru Fireblade for magical study.",al={"example collar","what is the collar","searing collar quest item"},it="item"},{q="What happens after giving the collar to Neeru?",a="Neeru examines the collar closely and sends you deeper into the investigation of the cult's presence in Durotar, beginning the search for Ak'Zeloth.",al={"next quest after neeru","what does neeru do","quest chain after neeru"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Horde allow warlocks in Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall allows warlocks in Orgrimmar out of pragmatic necessity. He keeps them in the Cleft of Shadow, where their dangerous research can be watched, controlled, and sometimes used to understand demonic enemies.",al={"why are warlocks allowed","warlocks in cleft of shadow","thrall warlocks"},it="history"},{q="Why does Margoz send you instead of going himself?",a="Margoz remains stationed outside Razor Hill keeping watch over Durotar's spiritual unrest. You are the adventurer who recovered the Searing Collars from Skull Rock in the first place, proving your capability in dealing with the cult's dark artifacts. Because he cannot divine their demonic workings through shamanism alone, he relies on you to carry a sample swiftly to the Cleft of Shadow.",al={"why me margoz","why send me to neeru","why doesn't margoz go to orgrimmar"},it="why_me",add="273c9fa7"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the elements will not commune with fel artifacts. Margoz has reached the boundary of his craft and needs a warlock's help.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you meet Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow, Orgrimmar's most prominent warlock. Your forbidden craft has practical use to the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see a fragile truce in Orgrimmar: the Warchief's shamans sometimes rely on the shadowy outcasts of the Cleft of Shadow to protect Durotar."},kw={"burning blade","cleft of shadow","durotar","margoz","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","searing collar","skull rock","warlock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:828","quest:809","quest:924","quest:806","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar"},m={start="Margoz",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="12",faction="Horde",id=829},src={"Neeru Fireblade (quest)"}}
E["quest:8359"] = {t="quest",n="Flexing for Nougat",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Innkeeper Gryshka offers nougat to those who play along. During Hallow's End, she asks you to flex for a piece meant to cheer Spoops, a bedridden child.",h="In Orgrimmar, Innkeeper Gryshka offers nougat to those who play along.",sec={{t="Tricks for Treats",b="Hallow's End brings pranks and sweet-gathering to Azeroth's capitals. In Orgrimmar's inn, Innkeeper Gryshka keeps holiday sweets for those who take part in the season's custom. You face dragons and dark sorcery in your travels, but here the bargain is simple: perform a trick or leave without a treat.",sp=0},{t="Muscle on Display",b="Innkeeper Gryshka wants a display of Orcish strength before she gives you Orgrimmar Nougat for young Spoops. Whatever disguise or armor you wear, she asks you to strike a muscular pose. Even the Horde's feared combatants can be made to entertain the common folk for candy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the flex?",a="Innkeeper Gryshka, who keeps the main tavern in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, asks you to perform a trick before she hands over holiday sweets.",al={"who gives the quest","gryshka","innkeeper gryshka"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need to flex for candy?",a="Hallow's End custom calls for a small trick in exchange for a treat. Gryshka teases you by asking for a display of sheer physical power before she gives you candy.",al={"why flex","what is the trick","nougat condition"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Orgrimmar Nougat used for?",a="The nougat is one of four sweets gathered across the Horde's capitals to cheer Spoops, a sick orphan boy who is bedridden and cannot go trick-or-treating on his own.",al={"why do i need nougat","nougat use","spoops candy"},it="item"},{q="Where does Innkeeper Gryshka reside?",a="Innkeeper Gryshka keeps the counter at the main inn in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, where she serves weary travelers and locals.",al={"where is gryshka","orgrimmar innkeeper location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can any Horde member participate in this?",a="Yes. Any member of the Horde can visit Innkeeper Gryshka during Hallow's End, strike a pose, and claim the seasonal sweet.",al={"who can flex","faction restrictions","horde only"},gp=true},{q="What holiday is this a part of?",a="It is part of Hallow's End, an autumn festival marking the end of the harvest and defying mortality with costumes, pranks, and sweets.",al={"which event","what holiday","hallows end quest"},it="history"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Even veteran Horde champions who face deadly warlords flex their biceps for tavernkeepers to gather festive sweets for the children.",["race:Orc"]="As an Orc, you meet a holiday test of pride when Orgrimmar's innkeeper asks for an impressive display of muscle.",["class:Warrior"]="As a Warrior, you may take pride in devastating feats on the front lines, yet find it amusing or humbling to pose like a stage performer for festive candy."},kw={"candy","flexing","gryshka","hallow's end","nougat","orgrimmar","spoops","trick or treat"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-gryshka","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Innkeeper Gryshka",faction="Horde",id=8359},src={"Flexing for Nougat (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8677"] = {t="quest",n="Darkhorn the Elder",z="orgrimmar",s="At the Lunar Festival, Darkhorn the Elder receives travelers in Orgrimmar. Honored among the ancestors, she embodies age, survival, and ancestral pride.",h="At the Lunar Festival, Darkhorn the Elder receives travelers in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Honoring the Ancestor",b="During the Lunar Festival, revered ancestors appear across Azeroth to share wisdom with the living. Elder Darkhorn rests within Orgrimmar’s fortified ramparts, watching the young warrior city. You can approach her to honor those who walked the earth generations ago, whether you fight for the Horde or brave the gates as an Alliance traveler.",sp=0},{t="The Spirit of the Festival",b="Travelers greet Elder Darkhorn and pay her reverence, and she recognizes the spark of life in them. For honoring the old ways, you receive a Coin of Ancestry and her blessing. The tokens celebrate victory over ancient perils and remind the living to cherish the strength handed down through unbroken bloodlines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Darkhorn?",a="Elder Darkhorn is an ancestral spirit who appears in Orgrimmar during the Lunar Festival. As an emissary of the past, she offers blessings and tokens to travelers who honor the elders.",al={"elder darkhorn","who is darkhorn","darkhorn lore"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Darkhorn?",a="You can find Elder Darkhorn in the Valley of Wisdom, just outside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. During the festival, she watches the daily life of the Horde capital.",al={"darkhorn location","where is darkhorn","elder darkhorn orgrimmar"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Lunar Festival elders?",a="During the Lunar Festival, the elders appear so you can honor ancestral wisdom, courage, and sacrifice. Pay an elder respect and receive a Coin of Ancestry, a token of heritage and shared remembrance.",al={"why find elders","lunar festival elders","ancestor coins"}},{q="Can Alliance players honor Elder Darkhorn?",a="Yes, you can honor Elder Darkhorn as an Alliance traveler. She lives deep within Orgrimmar, a Horde stronghold, so you must brave its hostile guards and players to reach her.",al={"can alliance talk to darkhorn","alliance elder darkhorn","alliance orgrimmar elder"}},{q="What reward does Elder Darkhorn grant?",a="When you honor Elder Darkhorn, she grants you a Coin of Ancestry and her blessing.",al={"darkhorn reward","what does darkhorn give","coin of ancestry darkhorn"}},{q="Is this quest repeatable?",a="No, you may honor each ancestral elder only once per character during the annual Lunar Festival.",al={"can i do darkhorn again","is darkhorn repeatable","darkhorn daily"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you can honor ancestral tradition by visiting Elder Darkhorn in the heart of your capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you must slip past Orgrimmar’s heavily defended gates and streets to reach Elder Darkhorn. The journey tests your stealth or your strength.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you revere the bond between the living world and ancient spirits. Visiting ancestral elders like Darkhorn is a profound spiritual duty."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","darkhorn","elder darkhorn","elders","lunar festival","orgrimmar","valley of wisdom"},m={start="Elder Darkhorn",id=8677},src={"Darkhorn the Elder"}}
E["quest:8828"] = {t="quest",n="Winter's Presents",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, Winter's Presents await beneath the festive tree during the Feast of Winter Veil. Holiday organizers and goblin apparatus tenders direct Horde heroes to Great-father Winter, where gifts have been prepared for them.",h="In Orgrimmar, Winter's Presents await beneath the festive tree during the Feast of Winter Veil.",sec={{t="Season of Generosity",b="The Feast of Winter Veil brings a pause for celebration to Orgrimmar as the chill winds of late year sweep across Durotar. Promoters from Smokywood Pastures and holiday enthusiasts spread word through the capital that gifts wait beneath the decorated tree. Warriors, hunters, and wanderers resting in the city are all invited to share in the season’s generosity.",sp=0},{t="The Patron and the Peddlers",b="Great-father Winter sits among holiday ribbons and packaged cartons near the Smokywood Pastures market. The ancient figure marks the season’s renewal, while goblin merchants nearby offer seasonal wares and festive treats to visitors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I turn in Winter's Presents?",a="You find Great-father Winter near the Smokywood Pastures festive area and decorated tree in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",al={"where is great father winter","turn in location","presents hand in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sends you to see Great-father Winter?",a="A Holiday Enthusiast or a goblin Wonderform Operator tending the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt machines around the holiday setups can direct you to the tree.",al={"who gives quest","quest starter","holiday enthusiast"},it="people"},{q="What is Smokywood Pastures?",a="Smokywood Pastures is a goblin merchant organization that sponsors and supplies the Winter Veil festivities, food, treats, and gifts across major capitals.",al={"smokywood pastures lore","who are smokywood pastures"},it="allies"},{q="What does Great-father Winter do once you speak with him?",a="Great-father Winter welcomes you to the Feast of Winter Veil and points you to the wrapped parcels beneath the tree. He also suggests Smokywood Pastures merchandise for your companions.",al={"great-father winter greeting","quest completion dialogue"}},{q="Why does the Horde celebrate Winter Veil in Orgrimmar?",a="The Horde celebrates Winter Veil as a time for respite, feasting, and community while struggling to build a new home in Kalimdor. The modern festival has roots in ancient legends of winter’s renewal.",al={"horde winter veil lore","why orcs celebrate winter veil"},it="history"},{q="What is the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt mentioned by the operator?",a="The PX-238 Winter Wondervolt is a goblin contraption near the festival grounds that temporarily transforms volunteers into festively dressed Little Helpers.",al={"winter wondervolt","px 238 wondervolt"},it="item"},{q="Why do the festival revelers send you to Great-father Winter?",a="The holiday enthusiasts and Wonderform Operators simply want everyone in Orgrimmar to share in the joy of the Feast of Winter Veil. Great-father Winter has arrived with a bounty of gifts under the festive tree—backed generously by the goblins of Smokywood Pastures. The operators are tied to their posts overseeing the festive machines, but they want to make sure an adventurer like you does not miss out on your seasonal surprises.",al={"why send to great father winter","why winter presents","why does the operator send me"},it="motive",add="d5621842"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Orgrimmar’s holiday camp offers a joyful, warm gathering spot amid the ongoing border conflicts across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can pause your duties even in the Warchief’s austere seat to share winter feasts and accept hospitality beneath the Winter Veil tree’s boughs."},kw={"great-father winter","holiday enthusiast","orgrimmar","presents","smokywood pastures","winter veil","winter's presents","wonderform operator"},rel={"npc:great-father-winter","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Wonderform Operator / Holiday Enthusiast",["end"]="Great-father Winter",faction="Horde",id=8828},src={"Winter's Presents (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8851"] = {t="quest",n="Five Signets for War Supplies",z="orgrimmar",s="Orgrimmar's stores gather supplies for the Horde's campaign across Kalimdor. Workers earn commendation signets for their contributions, and Warlord Gorchuk exchanges them for supplies to equip the fighters.",h="Orgrimmar's stores gather supplies for the Horde's campaign across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Continent-Wide Effort",b="Across Kalimdor, the Horde gathers raw goods, weapons, and provisions for a vast campaign. Gatherers and tradesfolk bring bandages, metals, and herbs into the cities, where military overseers award commendation signets for their work. The tokens mark each contribution to the stockpile growing along Orgrimmar's central avenues.",sp=0},{t="Materiel for the Frontlines",b="Warlord Gorchuk knows the wider war effort needs supplies, but each warrior also needs gear and provisions to survive the march into battle. Fighters can trade their commendation signets back into the Horde's stores for field supplies and surplus materiel, giving up personal recognition for what they need on the front.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of turning in five signets?",a="Five signets let you exchange commendation tokens earned through the Horde's mobilization for personal gear and field supplies instead of keeping them for political recognition.",al={"why turn in 5 signets","signet turn in purpose","what do i get for 5 signets"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Warlord Gorchuk?",a="Warlord Gorchuk is a Horde military coordinator in Orgrimmar who manages supplies and approves requisitions for warriors preparing for conflict.",al={"gorchuk identity","who is gorchuk"},it="in_charge"},{q="How do you obtain Horde Commendation Signets?",a="Quartermasters and logistics officers across the Horde award signets when you contribute raw materials, food, bandages, and crafting resources to the faction's war effort.",al={"get signets","where do signets come from","commendation signet source"},gp=true},{q="Can this requisition be repeated?",a="Yes. Warlord Gorchuk approves further exchanges when you bring more required batches of signets to support the troops.",al={"is this repeatable","can i do this again"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gorchuk say I won't receive recognition for this exchange?",a="When you spend your commendation signets on personal supplies, the quartermaster's caches provide the goods instead of recording your deeds. You give up formal accolades for practical field supplies.",al={"no recognition meaning","why no rep"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this exchange take place?",a="The exchange takes place in Orgrimmar, where stockpiles and logistics coordinators prepare the Horde for war.",al={"where is this quest","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Warlord Gorchuk want the signets?",a="Warlord Gorchuk oversees logistics for the Horde war effort. To ensure soldiers are properly outfitted for the impending conflict, he authorizes the release of vital battlefield supplies, but protocol demands proof of service and valor. Exchanging commendation signets guarantees that scarce war materiel goes directly into the hands of proven fighters rather than being squandered.",al={"why gorchuk wants signets","warlord gorchuk motive","why trade signets"},it="why_wanted",add="2026dc36"},{q="What is a Horde Commendation Signet?",a="A Horde Commendation Signet serves as official military scrip, awarded to champions who contribute resources, labor, and battlefield victories to the Horde's war preparations. Quartermasters and commanders honor these tokens as proof of distinguished service, allowing veterans to trade formal recognition for essential survival gear and provisions when preparing for battle.",al={"what is horde commendation signet","horde signet lore","what are commendation signets"},it="item",add="afeb91d4"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, every crate and bundle gathered in Orgrimmar helps supply your faction against the threats ahead.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you may value survival in the front lines over ceremonial recognition, making Gorchuk's supplies worth your accumulated signets."},kw={"commendation","gorchuk","materiel","orgrimmar","requisition","signets","supplies","war effort"},rel={"topic:horde"},m={start="Warlord Gorchuk",level="19",faction="Horde",id=8851,ri={"Horde Commendation Signet"}},src={"Five Signets for War Supplies (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8852"] = {t="quest",n="Ten Signets for War Supplies",z="orgrimmar",s="Warlord Gorchuk trades Horde Commendation Signets for war supplies in Orgrimmar. Champions give up formal recognition for equipment that can help keep soldiers supplied at the front.",h="Warlord Gorchuk trades Horde Commendation Signets for war supplies in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Materiel for the Front",b="Warlord Gorchuk oversees the Horde's supplies in the Valley of Spirits. As the Horde gathers its legions, weapons, rations, and armor must reach the front. Champions who have proved their dedication can trade commendation signets for useful equipment drawn from the army's reserves.",sp=0},{t="Practical Survival over Glory",b="Horde Commendation Signets usually prove a soldier's service and bring prestige with the leadership. Trading them for gear gives up that formal recognition for the chance to survive the fighting. Gorchuk knows that a satchel of supplies or a sturdy weapon can mean the difference between life and death when armies clash.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Horde Commendation Signets?",a="Horde Commendation Signets are tokens awarded to champions who gather raw materials and resources for the Horde's war preparations.",al={"commendation signet","horde signets","war signets"},it="item"},{q="Who is Warlord Gorchuk?",a="Warlord Gorchuk is a Horde logistics officer in Orgrimmar who collects war resources and distributes provisions to troops preparing for battle.",al={"gorchuk","warlord gorchuk location","who is gorchuk"},it="identity"},{q="Why turn signets in for supplies instead of faction reputation?",a="Trading signets for supplies gives up political standing and formal recognition in exchange for useful items, bandages, and gear for survival on the front lines.",al={"signets vs supplies","why supplies","commendation rewards"},gp=true},{q="Can this exchange be repeated?",a="Yes. Warlord Gorchuk continues trading field supplies as long as you have the required batches of commendation signets.",al={"is this repeatable","repeat signets","turn in again"},gp=true},{q="Where does this exchange take place?",a="The exchange takes place in Orgrimmar, where the Horde centers its war preparations and stockpiles.",al={"where to turn in signets","signet turn in location","gorchuk location"},it="place"},{q="What kind of war is the Horde preparing for?",a="The Horde is gathering metal, cloth, herbs, and rations for an expeditionary force to face an impending cataclysmic threat.",al={"what war","why gathering supplies","war effort"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Warlord Gorchuk want Horde Commendation Signets?",a="Warlord Gorchuk is tasked with outfitting soldiers and ensuring that frontline fighters remain properly supplied and alive for the fighting ahead. While official channels trade commendations for political recognition, Gorchuk recognizes the immediate, practical need for field materiel. By collecting signets and releasing surplus caches, he equips capable champions who have proven their dedication to the Horde's war effort.",al={"why does gorchuk want signets","warlord gorchuk motive","why turn in signets to gorchuk"},it="motive",add="53f1fd9d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every crate gathered in Orgrimmar helps prepare the Horde for the battles ahead.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know cold steel and ample rations help win long wars as surely as courage in battle."},kw={"commendation","gorchuk","logistics","orgrimmar","signets","supplies","war effort","warlord gorchuk"},rel={"topic:horde"},m={start="Warlord Gorchuk",level="29",faction="Horde",id=8852,ri={"Horde Commendation Signet"}},src={"Ten Signets for War Supplies (Horde)"}}
E["quest:9263"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Scourge of Orgrimmar",z="orgrimmar",s="Outside Orgrimmar, the Scourge has raised a camp beneath a floating necropolis. Lieutenant Dagel calls on defenders to repel the undead, recover necrotic stones, and examine runic circles charged with necromantic energy. The attack brings the Lich King's reach to Durotar.",h="Outside Orgrimmar, the Scourge has raised a camp beneath a floating necropolis.",sec={{t="Undead at the Gates",b="The Scourge now threatens lands far from Lordaeron and the northern ice. Floating necropolises cast their shadows across Azeroth, even over Durotar. Undead forces have gathered at Orgrimmar's threshold, raising camps that threaten the Horde capital. Lieutenant Dagel and the Argent Dawn coordinate the defense, calling on local champions to drive the invaders back before they can secure a siege.",sp=0},{t="Necrotic Relics and Dark Whispers",b="The Scourge's camp holds dim necrotic stones and glowing runic circles. The circles ring the camp and carry the same dark power as the necropolis above. Those who step into the runes hear unnatural voices echoing through the ether. The voices suggest some kind of communication, though Dagel does not know whom they reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Scourge attacking Orgrimmar?",a="Scourge forces have camped outside Orgrimmar beneath a necropolis. Lieutenant Dagel asks defenders to thin their ranks and investigate the nearby runic circles.",al={"why scourge orgrimmar","undead outside org","lich king attacks orgrimmar"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Dagel?",a="Lieutenant Dagel is an officer coordinating with the Argent Dawn to rally defenders against the invasion. From near the threat, Dagel directs fighters to slay the undead and examine their arcane tools.",al={"lieutenant dagel","dagel questgiver","who is dagel"},it="identity"},{q="What are the dim necrotic stones?",a="Dim necrotic stones are taken from Scourge invaders and brought to the Argent Dawn as proof that undead have been slain.",al={"necrotic stones","what are dim necrotic stones","dim stones"},it="item"},{q="What are the glowing runic circles outside the city?",a="The glowing circles hold the same strange energy as the nearby undead and necropolis. Dagel asks defenders to investigate their purpose.",al={"runic circles","glowing runes org","scourge circles"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn involved in Durotar?",a="The Argent Dawn is an independent order devoted to destroying the Scourge wherever it appears. The order works with Horde defenders to protect Orgrimmar's borders from the invasion.",al={"argent dawn in orgrimmar","why argent dawn here","argent dawn horde"},it="why_here"},{q="Is the necropolis overhead dangerous to the city?",a="The necropolis looms over the Scourge camp and shares its strange energy. Its presence makes the undead threat near the city a concern.",al={"floating citadel org","necropolis above durotar"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Dagel want the Scourge investigated?",a="With the Lich King's minions amassing right outside Orgrimmar's gates beneath an ominous necropolis, Lieutenant Dagel knows the city cannot sit idle. He fears whatever foul magic the invaders are brewing at their encampments. By unraveling the purpose of their strange, glowing runic circles and thinning the encroaching horde, Dagel hopes to gather vital intelligence on the Scourge's dark designs and stave off a catastrophic siege of Durotar.",al={"why does dagel want this","dagel motive","why investigate the scourge"},it="motive",add="4fe35d0b"},{q="Who are you being sent to fight outside Orgrimmar?",a="You are dispatched against the encroaching undead forces sent by the Lich King, who have set up an encampment directly outside Orgrimmar beneath a hovering necropolis. These mindless aberrations and foul shamblers are part of a coordinated invasion threatening Kalimdor, establishing foul arcane footholds across the desert to undermine Horde defenses and terrorize Durotar.",al={"who are we fighting","scourge enemies outside orgrimmar","who do i kill for dagel"},it="target",add="76cd191d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="A Scourge force camped within sight of Orgrimmar's towers is an insult the Horde cannot bear. Every sworn champion has a duty to defend Durotar from the Lich King's minions.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs won Durotar's dry red soil through hardship and blood. They will not let mindless monstrosities blight the home they carved out with their bare hands.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scourge recalls their former enslavement. Crushing the invaders is a personal vendetta against the Lich King's continuing reach."},kw={"argent dawn","dagel","durotar","invasion","lich king","necrotic stone","orgrimmar","runic circle","scourge"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:argent-dawn"},m={start="Lieutenant Dagel",level="10",faction="Horde",id=9263},src={"Investigate the Scourge of Orgrimmar"}}
E["subzone:cleft-of-shadow"] = {t="subzone",n="Cleft of Shadow",z="orgrimmar",s="Rogues, warlocks, and their teachers gather in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. The caverns give them room to practice their arts under the Horde's watch.",h="Rogues, warlocks, and their teachers gather in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Subterranean Sanctuary",b="Below Orgrimmar, the Cleft of Shadow holds rogues of the Shadowswift Brotherhood and warlocks of the Darkfire Enclave. Thrall's Horde honors shamanism and strength of arms, yet its leaders make room for subtler arts. In these caverns, practitioners of poison and fel energy work away from the valley districts and under Orgrimmar's watch.",sp=0},{t="A Dangerous Threshold",b="At the Cleft's lowest point, a passage opens into Ragefire Chasm. Volcanic caves honeycomb the ground beneath Orgrimmar, and their danger draws defenders and sinister cultists to the cavern's edge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are warlocks and rogues kept underground here?",a="Thrall seeks to unite the Horde through honorable shamanic and warrior traditions, while many orcs distrust the arts of rogues and warlocks. The caverns keep their dangerous fel workings and illicit practices contained and watched.",al={"why cleft of shadow","why warlocks underground orgrimmar","cleft of shadow lore"},it="purpose"},{q="What major trainers and services can be found in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Rogue and warlock trainers work in the Cleft, alongside poison suppliers, reagent vendors, and merchants who sell wands and staffs.",al={"trainers in cleft of shadow","who is in cleft of shadow"},gp=true},{q="What is the entrance at the bottom of the cavern?",a="The opening leads to Ragefire Chasm, a dangerous network of lava tubes beneath Orgrimmar. Troggs, searing elementals, and rogue cultists infest its depths.",al={"dungeon in cleft of shadow","cleft cave entrance","what instance is here"},it="place"},{q="What is the Cleft of Shadow?",a="The Cleft of Shadow is a vast subterranean cavern carved deep beneath the rocky canyons of Orgrimmar. While the city above celebrates strength, honor, and open combat, this dim underground recess harbors the less-than-savory practitioners whose arts are viewed with suspicion: rogues lurking in the shadows and warlocks practicing fel sorcery.",al={"what is cleft of shadow","cleft of shadow lore","about cleft of shadow"},it="place",add="866219a4"},{q="Who lives in or runs the Cleft of Shadow?",a="No single leader openly commands the cavern; rather, it belongs to the outcasts, spies, and occult practitioners tolerated by the Horde. You will find the stealthy rogues of the Shadowswift Brotherhood and the warlocks of the Darkfire Enclave gathered here, alongside poisoners and reagent merchants catering to their illicit arts.",al={"who leads cleft of shadow","cleft of shadow inhabitants","who lives in cleft of shadow"},it="residents",add="3bd03716"},{q="Is the Cleft of Shadow dangerous?",a="The cavern itself is a functioning district of Orgrimmar and relatively safe for citizens, though the demon summoners and venom merchants make it unsettling. Far greater peril lurks at the very bottom of the cleft: the volcanic descent into Ragefire Chasm, a sprawling network of lava tunnels infested with troggs and cultists right under the city's foundations.",al={"cleft of shadow safe","is cleft of shadow dangerous","danger in cleft of shadow"},it="danger",add="b6f6ea67"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Horde warlock, you can summon demons and bind fel energy in the Darkfire Enclave beneath Orgrimmar, away from the immediate wrath of shaman and warriors.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find the Shadowswift Brotherhood, poison merchants, and lockpickers in this dark recess, the Horde's main gathering place for stealth operatives."},kw={"cleft of shadow","darkfire enclave","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rogue","shadowswift brotherhood","warlock"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","zone:ragefire","subzone:valley-of-spirits"},src={"Cleft of Shadow"}}
E["subzone:drag"] = {t="subzone",n="Drag",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar, the Drag links the Valley of Strength, Valley of Honor and Valley of Wisdom. Crafters and traders line its shaded red-rock canyon, where the descent to the Cleft of Shadow also lies.",h="In Orgrimmar, the Drag links the Valley of Strength, Valley of Honor and Valley of Wisdom.",sec={{t="The Artisan's Thoroughfare",b="The Drag runs between Orgrimmar’s red canyon walls, where crafters and traders fill the Horde capital’s streets. Unlike the Valley of Strength, with its military musters and commands, the Drag is where daily city life unfolds. High cliffs and hides shade the street, where tanning vats, alchemical cauldrons and tinkers’ gears fill the air with their sounds and smells. Craftsmen gather to practice their trades and teach aspiring adventurers. Their work ranges from leatherworking and tailoring to the goblin workshops of Nogg’s Machine Shop.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads of Shadows and Craft",b="Merchant storefronts and salvage houses line the Drag, beside the guarded entrance to the underground Cleft of Shadow. The street brings honest tradesmen together with shamans on their way to the Valley of Wisdom and secretive practitioners of dark arts. They cross paths beneath the canyon’s dim, dusty overhangs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Drag used for in Orgrimmar?",a="The Drag is Orgrimmar’s main district for shopping and trade. Its trainers and supply vendors serve many professions, including alchemy, tailoring, leatherworking, skinning, enchanting and engineering, alongside general salvage and trade goods.",al={"purpose of the drag","what is the drag","what shops are in the drag"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Drag lead?",a="The Drag links the Valley of Strength in the south to the Valley of Honor in the northeast, with paths leading toward the Valley of Wisdom. The entrance to the shadowy caverns of the Cleft of Shadow lies along the Drag’s western cliffside.",al={"drag connections","how to get to cleft of shadow","where does the drag go"},gp=true},{q="Who is Nogg?",a="Nogg is a goblin engineer who runs Nogg’s Machine Shop along the Drag. He trains engineers and supplies gadgets to members of the Horde.",al={"noggs machine shop","who runs the machine shop"},it="people"},{q="Are all profession trainers located in the Drag?",a="Most crafting and gathering professions have shops along the Drag’s lower and upper shelves, but the city’s blacksmiths and miners work in the fiery forges of the Valley of Honor.",al={"where are trainers in orgrimmar","first aid trainer drag"},gp=true},{q="What is the Drag?",a="The Drag is a bustling, shadowed canyon alley in Orgrimmar that connects the Valley of Strength with the Valley of Wisdom. Tucked beneath the towering red cliffs, it serves as the capital's premier commercial and crafting district, packed with merchants, artisans, and trainers sharing their trades with adventurers and citizens alike.",al={"what is the drag","drag orgrimmar","about the drag"},it="place",add="b51cb4ea"},{q="What is the history of the Drag?",a="Carved into the deep canyons of Durotar along with the rest of Orgrimmar, the Drag was settled as a central trade thoroughfare when Thrall's Horde established the city. Abutting the canyon walls in a shaded, rugged part of the capital, it quickly filled with workshops, salvagers, and vendors eager to supply the new nation.",al={"history of the drag","how was the drag founded","drag history"},it="history",add="ba842caf"},{q="Who lives in and runs the Drag?",a="A wide variety of craftspeople, shopkeepers, and laborers make their home and livelihood here. Notable proprietors include Nogg running his engineering workshop, Yelmak brewing potions, Magar producing cloth goods, and the Droffers family handling salvage.",al={"who lives in the drag","drag residents","who runs the drag"},it="residents",add="376c9470"},{q="Is the Drag dangerous?",a="While the Drag lies in a shaded and rough-hewn canyon corridor, it is a protected part of Orgrimmar and not inherently dangerous to members of the Horde. However, it sits in close proximity to the dark tunnels of the Cleft of Shadow, where warlocks and rogue elements practice arts frowned upon in the sunlight.",al={"is the drag safe","is the drag dangerous","danger in the drag"},it="danger",add="5a953074"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="In the Drag, goblin tinkerers at Nogg’s Machine Shop teach schematics, explosives and specialized engineering knowledge to the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As a traveler through Orgrimmar, you pass along the Drag, which links the capital’s martial core to its communal and mystical quarters."},kw={"alchemy","cleft of shadow","drag","leatherworking","nogg","orgrimmar","salvage","tailoring","the drag"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","subzone:valley-of-strength","subzone:valley-of-honor","npc:nogg"},src={"Drag"}}
E["subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar"] = {t="subzone",n="Gates of Orgrimmar",z="orgrimmar",s="At Orgrimmar's southern gate, timber and iron guard the entrance cut into northern Durotar's red rock. The passage leads from the arid wastes to the Valley of Strength, the capital's busy commons. The gate proclaims the Horde's endurance and strength in war.",h="At Orgrimmar's southern gate, timber and iron guard the entrance cut into northern Durotar's red rock.",sec={{t="The Bastion of Durotar",b="Orgrimmar's main gate guards the great chasm cut into the mountains around the city. Towering wooden palisades, iron spikes, and watchtowers fortify the entrance. Travelers coming from Razor Hill and Durotar's scrublands find a grand welcome and a warning to any who threaten the new Horde. Armed Orgrimmar Grunts patrol the approach and watch everyone entering the city.",sp=0},{t="Threshold to the Valley",b="Beyond the gate's shadowed arch, you enter the Valley of Strength, Orgrimmar's civic and martial heart. The tunnel narrows the way for envoys, merchants, and warriors, with sentries watching those who pass. Here stands Warchief Thrall's dream of a secure refuge carved from the harsh desert, where the Horde's many peoples can walk together without fear.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the Gates of Orgrimmar lead?",a="The Gates of Orgrimmar lead from northern Durotar into the Valley of Strength, the city's main entrance and central commons.",al={"what do the gates connect","where is the front gate"},it="place"},{q="Who guards the gates?",a="Orgrimmar Grunts guard the front gates and keep watch against hostile infiltrators and wild beasts.",al={"who protects the gate","gate guards"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the entrance fortified with wood and spikes?",a="Wooden palisades and iron spikes follow orcish frontier defenses, using sturdy timber from nearby lands to make a formidable, defensible choke point in the canyon walls.",al={"why wood and iron spikes","orcish gate design"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Alliance players pass through this gate?",a="Alliance members who try to pass through the main gate face hostile veteran guards, ready to strike down Horde enemies on sight.",al={"can alliance enter","alliance walk through gate"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What are the Gates of Orgrimmar?",a="The Gates of Orgrimmar serve as the heavily fortified primary entrance into the Horde's capital city. Carved directly through the rugged crimson canyon walls of northern Durotar, this imposing timber and iron threshold marks the boundary between the wild expanse of the barrens and the bustling heart of the Valley of Strength.",al={"gates of orgrimmar","what is gates of orgrimmar","orgrimmar gate"},it="place",add="a102033b"},{q="Why is this entrance dangerous?",a="For loyal champions of the Horde, the gateway represents safety and strength. For members of the Alliance, however, approaching the threshold is a death sentence. Stalwart Orgrimmar Grunts patrol the towers and passage, ready to mercilessly strike down any intruder who dares approach unbidden.",al={"is gates of orgrimmar dangerous","are the gates dangerous","gates danger"},it="danger",add="ecbfa379"},{q="Why is it called the Gates of Orgrimmar?",a="The gateway takes its name from the city it protects, which Thrall founded and named in honor of the former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. As the premier portal in and out of the fortress city, it stands as a monument to orcish sovereignty and Doomhammer's enduring legacy.",al={"why called gates of orgrimmar","gates of orgrimmar name meaning"},it="name",add="86fa8d49"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see the gates as a place of safety and belonging, a hard-won homeland forged under Warchief Thrall's leadership.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout or infiltrator, you face one of Kalimdor's most heavily guarded bottlenecks, nearly impossible to breach by frontal assault."},kw={"durotar","gates of orgrimmar","main gate","orgrimmar grunts","thrall","valley of strength"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:durotar","topic:horde","npc:thrall","topic:alliance"},src={"Gates of Orgrimmar"}}
E["subzone:grommash-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Grommash Hold",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, Grommash Hold commands the red cliffs as Thrall's seat. Named for Grommash Hellscream's sacrifice, it is the political heart of the new Horde.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, Grommash Hold commands the red cliffs as Thrall's seat.",sec={{t="The Seat of the Warchief",b="Grommash Hold rises from the cliffs of the Valley of Wisdom, where Thrall receives emissaries, petitioners, and warlords. Its thick stone halls stay dim and chilly, a choice meant to keep those who attend his audiences alert and sober. Thrall weighs the defense of Kalimdor with veteran counselors such as Eitrigg, while racial chieftains like Vol'jin visit the hold.",sp=0},{t="The Monument to Freedom",b="Outside the fortress, Mannoroth's shattered armor and horned skull hang from the trunk of an ancient tree. The memorial honors Grom Hellscream, who gave his life to slay the pit lord in Ashenvale. It recalls the orcs' freedom from the demonic blood curse and warns against returning to reckless savagery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is inside Grommash Hold?",a="Warchief Thrall holds court in Grommash Hold with Horde leaders and advisors, including the orcish elder Eitrigg, Darkspear leader Vol'jin, and warrior Nazgrel.",al={"who is in the hold","who lives in grommash hold","who rules here"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it named Grommash Hold?",a="Grommash Hold takes its name from Grommash 'Grom' Hellscream, the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan. During the Third War, Grom killed the pit lord Mannoroth at the cost of his own life, freeing the orcs from demonic servitude.",al={"why grommash hold","who was grommash","named after who"},it="name"},{q="What are the giant bones displayed outside?",a="The giant skull and armor belong to Mannoroth, whose blood first enslaved the orcs on Draenor. The remains were brought from Ashenvale and mounted on a tree trunk outside the hold to honor the Horde's freedom.",al={"demon skull outside","mannoroth skull","bones in front"}},{q="Why do some city signs call it Thrall's Fortress?",a="Orcish guards and older directional signs still call the structure Thrall's Fortress, after the warchief who holds court inside.",al={"thrall's fortress","thralls fortress","hold vs fortress"},it="place"},{q="What happened at Grommash Hold?",a="Constructed alongside Orgrimmar in the Valley of Wisdom, the fortress was raised to serve as the seat of the new Horde. Thrall welcomed the half-ogre beastmaster Rexxar here during the founding of Durotar, uniting their efforts to defend the nascent realm. Within its cold stone halls, Thrall and his advisors have governed the faction, planned defenses against encroaching threats, and received emissaries from allied tribes and nations since the end of the Third War.",al={"history of grommash hold","grommash hold events","what happened in grommash hold"},it="history",add="ce374a3d"},{q="Is Grommash Hold dangerous?",a="If you are loyal to the Horde, Grommash Hold is entirely safe and welcomes you to petition its leaders. For members of the Alliance, it is among the most lethal places on Kalimdor. Heavily guarded by elite Kor'kron sentries and housing Warchief Thrall himself alongside veteran champions, any trespasser will face swift and merciless execution the moment they step into the Valley of Wisdom.",al={"is it safe in grommash hold","danger in grommash hold","can alliance enter grommash hold"},it="danger",add="84f3c4ab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="At Grommash Hold, the Horde's sovereignty is centered. Treaties are forged here, and campaigns against threats across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms are directed from its halls.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, Grommash Hold and Mannoroth's remains outside recall Grom Hellscream's sacrifice, which freed their people from the demonic blood curse."},kw={"eitrigg","grommash hold","mannoroth","orgrimmar","thrall","thrall's fortress","valley of wisdom"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:grommash-hellscream","zone:orgrimmar","npc:vol-jin","npc:eitrigg","topic:burning-legion","topic:third-war"},src={"Grommash Hold"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-legends"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Legends",z="orgrimmar",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, Horde champions gather in the Hall of Legends. Behind its guarded entrance, proven officers confer over battle plans and arm themselves with weapons and armor from conflicts across Azeroth and beyond.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, Horde champions gather in the Hall of Legends.",sec={{t="Sanctuary of Horde Champions",b="Horde officers gather in the Hall of Legends, off the Valley of Strength's busy avenues. Beyond its guarded entrance, strategists and delegates from across the faction confer over maps of contested lands and the military standing of both factions. Among them are Chieftain Earthbind of Thunder Bluff, Blood Guard Hini'wana of the Darkspear, and Advisor Willington of the Undercity. Only warriors who have reached the rank of Stone Guard or higher may enter and claim the arms and spoils kept within.",sp=0},{t="The Spoils of War",b="The Hall of Legends holds armories stocked with battle-tested wargear for proven Horde officers. For those rising through the military ranks, its weapons and armor mark honor, martial skill, and victory hard won.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is allowed inside the Hall of Legends?",a="Only Horde champions who have reached the rank of Stone Guard or higher may enter the Hall of Legends. Lower-ranking soldiers and ordinary citizens are turned away at the entrance.",al={"can i enter hall of legends","hall of legends requirement","rank required for hall of legends"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Hall of Legends located?",a="The Hall of Legends stands in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar, near the city's primary barracks and administrative seat.",al={"where is hall of legends","hall of legends location","how to get to hall of legends"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is inside the Hall of Legends?",a="Inside, a central strategy table is flanked by military representatives of the Horde's various races, with maps of Azeroth and military records around them. Quartermasters maintain armories here and distribute prestigious arms, armor, and mounts to accomplished officers.",al={"what is in hall of legends","hall of legends interior"},it="purpose"},{q="Does the Alliance have an equivalent location?",a="Yes. The Alliance counterpart is the Champions' Hall in Stormwind City's Old Town district, an officer barracks and armory for honored Alliance combatants.",al={"alliance hall of legends","alliance counterpart"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Hall of Legends?",a="The Hall of Legends serves as the elite military barracks and armory for decorated officers of the Horde, nestled within the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar. Here, battle-tested champions gather to plan martial strategy, consult war maps across Azeroth, and equip themselves with specialized weapons and armor forged or claimed from campaigns across the world.",al={"what is hall of legends","hall of legends purpose","what is this place"},it="place",add="e332bf32"},{q="Who oversees the Hall of Legends?",a="The hall is staffed by quartermasters and representatives from the Horde's core factions who gather around its central war table. Officers such as Chieftain Earthbind of Thunder Bluff, Advisor Willington representing the Forsaken, and Blood Guard Hini'wana of the Darkspear trolls confer over strategic maps and inspect the armory's provisions.",al={"who runs hall of legends","who is in hall of legends","hall of legends officers"},it="residents",add="e6163205"},{q="Is the Hall of Legends dangerous?",a="The Hall of Legends poses no physical danger to loyal champions of the Horde who have earned the right to step through its threshold. It is a secure, heavily guarded sanctum in the heart of Orgrimmar, dedicated entirely to military veterans and the quartermasters outfitting them.",al={"is hall of legends safe","danger hall of legends","is it hostile"},it="danger",add="5e706ae3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the Hall of Legends recognizes military achievement and offers strategic council and prized wargear to those who shed blood for the Warchief.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior on the front lines, entry to the Hall of Legends marks the height of martial respect and grants access to the finest wargear the Horde can offer."},kw={"hall of legends","officer barracks","orgrimmar","pvp","spoils of war","stone guard","valley of strength"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-strength","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:champions-hall","topic:horde","zone:thunderbluff","zone:undercity","topic:troll","zone:stormwind"},src={"Hall of Legends"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-the-brave"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of the Brave",z="orgrimmar",s="Warriors train and gather at the Hall of the Brave in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. The barracks and guild house serves the Horde's front-line combatants, drillmasters, and battlemasters.",h="Warriors train and gather at the Hall of the Brave in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",sec={{t="The Warriors' Bastion",b="The Hall of the Brave overlooks the Valley of Honor's waters and training rings. Veteran officers and seasoned warriors teach initiates melee combat, stances, and discipline. Training dummies and weapons line the hall, where battlemasters organize combatants for major military engagements across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of the Brave?",a="The Hall of the Brave is Orgrimmar's main barracks and guild hall for warriors. Veteran trainers teach techniques, practice dummies offer a place to hone strikes, and battlemasters coordinate military deployments across contested lands.",al={"what is hall of the brave","what is this building","hall of the brave purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where in Orgrimmar is the hall located?",a="The Hall of the Brave sits on the eastern side of the Valley of Honor, along the red canyon walls overlooking the central pond.",al={"where is hall of the brave","hall of the brave location","find warrior trainer orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="Who can be found inside the hall?",a="Warrior trainers, battlemasters coordinating large military conflicts, and Horde grunts resting between patrols can be found inside the hall.",al={"who is in hall of the brave","hall of the brave npcs"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Hall of the Brave?",a="The Hall of the Brave is the grand military barracks and warrior guild house of Orgrimmar, situated in the city's Valley of Honor. It serves as a central hub where the Horde's seasoned soldiers gather, train, and coordinate martial affairs. Inside its fortified walls, fighters hone their skills on training dummies, consult veteran officers, and prepare for the ongoing struggles defending Durotar and the Horde's frontiers.",al={"what is hall of the brave","hall of the brave orgrimmar","warrior hall orgrimmar"},it="place",add="3fba9d5a"},{q="Is the Hall of the Brave dangerous?",a="To loyal members of the Horde, the Hall of the Brave is entirely safe—a place of fellowship, instruction, and disciplined martial pride. However, an Alliance infiltrator bold or foolish enough to set foot here would meet swift and brutal death at the hands of the Horde's elite warrior trainers, battlemasters, and veteran officers who pack the barracks.",al={"is hall of the brave safe","hall of the brave dangerous","hall of the brave danger"},it="danger",add="1f330543"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can train at the Hall of the Brave, your martial home in the capital. Its trainers teach advanced stances and battle maneuvers as your skill grows.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see its frontline discipline at the Hall of the Brave. Battlemasters there muster troops to fight across the continent."},kw={"barracks","battlemaster","hall of the brave","orgrimmar","valley of honor","warrior trainer","warriors guild"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:hall-of-legends","topic:horde"},src={"Hall of the Brave"}}
E["subzone:ragefire-chasm"] = {t="subzone",n="Ragefire Chasm",z="orgrimmar",s="Beneath Orgrimmar, Ragefire Chasm threatens the Horde from below. Its magma-lit tunnels hold savage troggs, and the Cleft of Shadow gives access to the caverns.",h="Beneath Orgrimmar, Ragefire Chasm threatens the Horde from below.",sec={{t="A Threat Beneath the Streets",b="Beneath Orgrimmar, dangers threaten the capital from below. While Thrall works to secure Durotar above, Ragefire troggs infest the chasm’s unstable vents and magma rivers. They rose from unknown depths and violently rejected Magatha Grimtotem’s attempts at diplomacy. Left unchecked, their numbers could undermine the city and overrun it.",sp=0},{t="The Searing Blade",b="The Searing Blade works from the shadows of Ragefire Chasm. Directed by the warlock Jergosh the Invoker, the satyr Bazzalan, and the towering felguard Taragaman the Hungerer, the sect plots to ruin Thrall’s Horde. Neeru Fireblade claims to oppose them, but the cult tests its strength and sabotages the orcs’ new home from below.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to Ragefire Chasm?",a="You can reach Ragefire Chasm through the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar, beside the tent of the warlock Neeru Fireblade.",al={"rfc entrance","how to get to ragefire chasm","where is ragefire chasm located"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives inside Ragefire Chasm?",a="Aggressive Ragefire troggs infest the chasm, and the Searing Blade occupies it. The cult is linked to the Shadow Council and led by the warlock Jergosh the Invoker, the satyr Bazzalan, and the felguard Taragaman the Hungerer.",al={"ragefire mobs","what enemies are in rfc","who controls ragefire chasm"},sp=1,it="residents",bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="Why hasn't Thrall cleared out the chasm?",a="The Horde is stretched thin establishing Durotar and defending against outside threats. Warchief Thrall relies on capable champions to enter the caverns, defeat the Searing Blade’s leaders, and thin the trogg numbers before they can breach the city streets.",al={"why does thrall allow ragefire","thrall ragefire chasm"},it="motive"},{q="Can Alliance players enter Ragefire Chasm?",a="Yes. You can reach Ragefire Chasm by slipping through Orgrimmar’s gates and descending into the heavily guarded Cleft of Shadow, a perilous undertaking for Alliance adventurers.",al={"can alliance do rfc","alliance in ragefire"},gp=true},{q="What is Ragefire Chasm?",a="Ragefire Chasm is a subterranean network of volcanic caverns situated directly beneath the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. Accessible from deep within the Cleft of Shadow, its winding, lava-filled tunnels run beneath the city streets, harboring hostile troggs and treacherous cultists right under the Warchief's feet.",al={"what is ragefire","about ragefire chasm","ragefire chasm lore"},it="place",add="1ca63580"},{q="What happened at Ragefire Chasm?",a="Deep subterranean troggs emerged into the molten tunnels, rebuffing peaceful overtures by the tauren elder Magatha Grimtotem with savage violence. Seizing upon the seclusion, a Shadow Council sect called the Searing Blade entrenched themselves within the tunnels, using the fiery depths to secretly conspire against Orgrimmar.",al={"ragefire chasm history","ragefire backstory","what happened in ragefire"},it="history",add="16537ee3"},{q="Is Ragefire Chasm dangerous?",a="It is an immediate peril to Orgrimmar. Swarms of violent troggs threaten to spill into the streets, while the Searing Blade cultists—commanded by the felguard Taragaman the Hungerer, the satyr Bazzalan, and the warlock Jergosh—actively plot the downfall of Thrall's Horde from the shadows.",al={"how dangerous is ragefire","threat in ragefire chasm","is ragefire dangerous"},it="danger",add="79d825b2"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a security crisis at the heart of the capital. Protecting the young Horde falls to its newest adventurers.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see the corruption of fel magic in the Searing Blade and its demonic masters. Thrall’s new Horde seeks to root out that corruption."},kw={"bazzalan","cleft of shadow","jergosh the invoker","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rfc","searing blade","taragaman","troggs"},rel={"zone:ragefire","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","npc:taragaman-the-hungerer","npc:jergosh-the-invoker","npc:bazzalan","quest:829","quest:5726"},src={"Ragefire Chasm"}}
E["subzone:ragefire-chasm-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Ragefire Chasm (Classic)",z="orgrimmar",s="Ragefire Chasm threatens Orgrimmar from beneath its streets, where troggs have broken into the tunnels. The fiery caverns also shelter a cult whose plans reach beyond Durotar.",h="Ragefire Chasm threatens Orgrimmar from beneath its streets, where troggs have broken into the tunnels.",sec={{t="A Hidden Peril",b="Ragefire troggs have surged into the volcanic tunnels beneath Orgrimmar. They pushed up from deep fissures and now threaten the city's foundations. Magatha Grimtotem, a tauren, tried to make peace with them, but the troggs answered with violence. Their tunnels run below the stone streets and fortified towers, leaving Orgrimmar at risk if the creatures keep digging upward.",sp=0},{t="The Searing Blade",b="The Searing Blade works beneath Orgrimmar in service to the demonic Shadow Council. Taragaman the Hungerer, a felguard, leads the cult with Jergosh the Invoker, an orc warlock, and Bazzalan, a satyr. They seek to undo all that Thrall's Horde has established in Durotar. Warchief Thrall keeps watch on their activities, hoping their overconfidence will expose higher leaders within the Shadow Council.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to Ragefire Chasm?",a="You reach Ragefire Chasm through the Cleft of Shadow, a subterranean canyon deep within Orgrimmar. The entrance lies near the tent of Neeru Fireblade, an orc warlock.",al={"where is ragefire","rfc entrance","how to get to rfc","where is rfc located"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there troggs beneath Orgrimmar?",a="Ragefire troggs surfaced from ancient, deep cavern systems beneath Durotar and broke into the volcanic depths under Orgrimmar. Their invasion threatens the capital's structure and its people, and they have refused every attempt at peaceful containment.",al={"why are troggs here","ragefire troggs","orgrimmar troggs"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Thrall allow cultists to live under the capital?",a="Warchief Thrall knows the cultists are beneath Orgrimmar and keeps them under close watch. He hopes they will reveal the identity and whereabouts of the Shadow Council's true leaders.",al={"why doesn't thrall clear rfc","thrall shadow council","why is searing blade under orgrimmar"},it="motive"},{q="Who leads the cultists inside the chasm?",a="Three figures command the Searing Blade in Ragefire Chasm: Taragaman the Hungerer, a formidable felguard; Jergosh the Invoker, an orc warlock; and Bazzalan, a satyr.",al={"rfc bosses","who leads the searing blade","ragefire chasm leaders"},it="leader"},{q="What is Ragefire Chasm?",a="Ragefire Chasm is a subterranean network of fiery volcanic tunnels and lava pools lying directly beneath the Horde's capital city of Orgrimmar. Entered through the shadowy depths of the Cleft of Shadow, the caverns serve as an uneasy reminder of the volatile ground beneath Durotar. Though buried beneath the bustling streets above, these deep caves harbor dangerous creatures and shadowy conspiracies that threaten the young city from within.",al={"ragefire chasm lore","what is ragefire","about ragefire chasm"},it="place",add="4401cb77"},{q="What happened at Ragefire Chasm?",a="As Orgrimmar was established above, feral troggs began emerging from the searing tunnels below the city. Magatha Grimtotem attempted to negotiate peace with them, but the troggs answered only with violence. Taking advantage of the subterranean chaos, demon-worshiping cultists known as the Searing Blade slipped into the fiery tunnels to establish a hidden foothold beneath the capital.",al={"ragefire chasm history","what happened in ragefire","history of ragefire chasm"},it="history",add="db99bdf4"},{q="Who lives in Ragefire Chasm?",a="The caverns are overrun by feral Ragefire troggs, roving elemental beings, and cultists of the Searing Blade. This secret sect of the Shadow Council operates out of the deeper tunnels under the command of the warlock Jergosh the Invoker, the satyr Bazzalan, and a brutal summoned felguard named Taragaman the Hungerer.",al={"who lives in ragefire","ragefire chasm inhabitants","who is in ragefire chasm"},it="residents",add="9f581f16"},{q="Is Ragefire Chasm dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the molten lava and boiling chambers, the chasm poses an existential danger to Orgrimmar itself. The hostile troggs threaten to swarm upward if left unchecked, while the Searing Blade actively plots the ruin of the Horde's new realm using demonic rituals and dark sorcery directly beneath Thrall's seat of power.",al={"is ragefire dangerous","ragefire chasm threat","danger in ragefire"},it="danger",add="f1dd8474"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you defend your homeland by securing Durotar's bedrock and rooting out demonic collaborators beneath the capital.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Magatha Grimtotem sent emissaries to seek peace with the invading troggs. Their bloody refusal showed that diplomacy could not stop these underground beasts."},kw={"bazzalan","cleft of shadow","jergosh","ragefire chasm","rfc","searing blade","taragaman","troggs"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","npc:thrall","topic:shadow-council","npc:taragaman-the-hungerer","npc:jergosh-the-invoker","npc:bazzalan","quest:829"},src={"Ragefire Chasm (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-honor"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Honor",z="orgrimmar",s="In the Valley of Honor, Orgrimmar's warriors and hunters prepare for battle. Its barracks, guilds, and battlemasters serve the Horde's forces across Azeroth, while forges and training grounds keep its fighters ready.",h="In the Valley of Honor, Orgrimmar's warriors and hunters prepare for battle.",sec={{t="Heart of the Horde's Might",b="The Valley of Honor holds Orgrimmar's military quarter behind high canyon ridges. Practice weapons clash, and blacksmiths' anvils ring through the day. The Hall of the Brave draws seasoned warriors and battlemasters who coordinate campaigns in places such as Alterac Valley and Warsong Gulch. Training grounds for beastmasters and hunters flank the hall. Across the valley, the Horde equips, drills, and sends out its frontline defenders.",sp=0},{t="Craft, Trade, and Respite",b="The valley supplies arms and offers a place to rest between duties. The Burning Anvil and Red Canyon Mining provide armor and raw iron, while engineers work nearby in Nogg's Machine Shop. Grunts and visiting adventurers can fish in a quiet pool, taking a brief pause from the dust of the Valley of Strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Valley of Honor?",a="The Valley of Honor is Orgrimmar's military hub. Its barracks, warrior and hunter trainers, weaponsmiths, and battlemasters support the Horde's forces and send soldiers to major battlefronts.",al={"valley of honor purpose","what is here","what's in valley of honor"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find battlemasters in Orgrimmar?",a="The Horde battlemasters gather inside the Hall of the Brave in the Valley of Honor. They enlist soldiers and send them to ongoing battles across Azeroth.",al={"battlemaster location","orgrimmar pvp","queue bg orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="What professions are trained in the Valley of Honor?",a="The Valley of Honor has trainers and supply vendors for blacksmithing, mining, and fishing. Goblin engineering specialists work from Nogg's Machine Shop.",al={"professions valley of honor","trainers here","blacksmithing orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="What is the Valley of Honor?",a="The Valley of Honor serves as the proud military heart of Orgrimmar. Tucked within the northeastern canyons of the city, this rugged district is dedicated to martial discipline, housing the city's barracks, the Hall of the Brave, and the Hunter's Hall. Here, warriors and hunters hone their deadly craft, while battlemasters rally champions to contest distant battlegrounds across Azeroth.",al={"valley of honor","what is valley of honor","valley of honor orgrimmar"},it="place",add="cbe73428"},{q="Who lives in the Valley of Honor?",a="The valley is home primarily to the Horde's martial forces and the artisans who equip them. Veterans, grunt recruits, hunters, and beast tamers gather throughout its halls and barracks. Beside them work blacksmiths, miners, and engineers keeping the Horde's war machine supplied with keen blades, sturdy plate, and ammunition.",al={"who lives in valley of honor","valley of honor residents","who runs valley of honor"},it="residents",add="167ed7f9"},{q="Is the Valley of Honor dangerous?",a="For loyal members of the Horde, the Valley of Honor is a secure bastion guarded by some of the mightiest champions and soldiers in the city. The sparring halls see fierce, blood-pumping combat, but violence is kept strictly to training and regulated martial trials. For any trespassing enemy of the Warchief, however, it is one of the deadliest places in Durotar.",al={"is valley of honor dangerous","valley of honor danger","danger in valley of honor"},it="danger",add="6cb8ac9d"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can find the Hall of the Brave, veteran combat instructors, and armorers who forge the Horde's front lines in the Valley of Honor.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can visit the Hunter's Hall and beast-taming grounds to replenish ammunition, hone your marksmanship, and stable your companions."},kw={"barracks","battlemasters","blacksmithing","hall of the brave","nogg","orgrimmar","valley of honor"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:hall-of-the-brave","npc:nogg","topic:horde"},src={"Valley of Honor"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-spirits"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Spirits",z="orgrimmar",s="Darkspear trolls make their home in the Valley of Spirits, west of Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares. Thatched lodges, tiki poles, and pools mark their place among the city's red stone and iron.",h="Darkspear trolls make their home in the Valley of Spirits, west of Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares.",sec={{t="A Home for the Darkspear",b="The Valley of Spirits branches west from the Valley of Strength, a quiet enclave for the Darkspear trolls. The tribe settled in Durotar alongside Thrall's orcs, and made this pocket among the crags their gathering place in the city. Trollish craftspeople, spiritualists, and practitioners gather around wooden bridges and winding waters, practicing their arts away from the dry heat of Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares.",sp=0},{t="Keepers of the Craft",b="The valley's lodges and pools draw those who practice magic and wild crafts. Witch doctors, herbalists, and spellcasters gather at the Spirit Lodge and Darkbriar Lodge. At the back, the Talon Gate opens toward the Barrens' open plains, giving wanderers, hunters, and travelers a quick passage beyond the canyon walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Valley of Spirits?",a="The Darkspear trolls live in the Valley of Spirits, after settling in Durotar alongside the orcs. Their craftspeople, spiritual leaders, herbalists, and hunters make their homes among troll-style huts and carved tiki totems.",al={"who lives here","valley of spirits inhabitants","trolls in orgrimmar"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the Talon Gate lead?",a="The Talon Gate at the rear of the Valley of Spirits leads west from Orgrimmar into the Southfury River basin and the plains of the Barrens.",al={"talon gate exit","back gate orgrimmar","valley of spirits gate"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services and trainers are found here?",a="Trainers and merchants for herbalism, cooking, wilderness skills, and magical disciplines can be found across the Valley of Spirits, including at the Spirit Lodge and Darkbriar Lodge.",al={"trainers in valley of spirits","what is in valley of spirits"},gp=true},{q="What is the Valley of Spirits?",a="The Valley of Spirits is a long, narrow quarter within Orgrimmar, stretching from the central Valley of Strength toward the city's rear Talon Gate. Characterized by its tropical architecture, totems, and shallow waterways, it serves as the cultural center and residential haven for the Darkspear trolls alongside their orc allies within the Horde's capital.",al={"what is valley of spirits","valley of spirits orgrimmar","troll quarter"},it="place",add="cef16464"},{q="What is the history of the Valley of Spirits?",a="Established during the founding of Orgrimmar following the Third War, the valley was set aside as a home for the Darkspear tribe when they joined Thrall's new Horde. Since the capital's construction, it has served as a center for troll shamanism, voodoo practices, and daily community life sheltered behind the city's red rock walls.",al={"history of valley of spirits","what happened at valley of spirits","valley of spirits lore"},it="history",add="8d1b898f"},{q="Is the Valley of Spirits dangerous?",a="No, it is entirely safe for members of the Horde and neutral visitors. Guarded by Orgrimmar's sentries and Darkspear warriors, the valley is a domestic settlement offering shelter, commerce, and spiritual guidance rather than physical threats.",al={"is valley of spirits safe","danger in valley of spirits","valley of spirits enemies"},it="danger",add="210fd1e6"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you find a piece of home and cultural identity in this peaceful enclave among the red canyons of Orgrimmar.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can seek the wisdom of local herbalist masters at the valley's lodges, beside its quiet waterways."},kw={"darkbriar lodge","darkspear","orgrimmar","spirit lodge","talon gate","trolls","valley of spirits"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-strength","topic:troll","topic:horde","npc:thrall"},src={"Valley of Spirits"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-strength"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Strength",z="orgrimmar",s="Trade and daily business fill Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. The bank, central auction house, and Broken Tusk inn draw travelers through the Horde capital.",h="Trade and daily business fill Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength.",sec={{t="The Gates of the City",b="Beyond Orgrimmar's timber gates, the Valley of Strength opens among Durotar's red canyon walls. Adventurers, merchants, and warriors from allied nations fill the Horde's front square. At the Broken Tusk inn, some trade war stories over flagons. Others turn to business at the central bank and auction house. The orcs fought for strength and unity in their new homeland, and both shape the city's heart.",sp=0},{t="Hub of Trade and Command",b="The Valley of Strength is Orgrimmar's foremost marketplace. Soran's Leather and Steel Armory sells armor, while vendors stock provisions for long treks across the Barrens. Grunts watch every corner. They guide newcomers and keep order among the diverse peoples who have taken refuge beneath Thrall's banner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Valley of Strength?",a="Just inside Orgrimmar's main gates, the Valley of Strength holds the bank, auction house, general goods merchants, and Broken Tusk inn.",al={"valley of strength overview","what is this place","orgrimmar entrance area"},it="place"},{q="Where is Grommash Hold located relative to this valley?",a="Grommash Hold lies north of the Valley of Strength, in the Valley of Wisdom. It is Warchief Thrall's seat and the Horde's high command.",al={"where is thrall","grommash hold location","warchief seat"},gp=true},{q="What services can I find here?",a="The valley has the city's main bank and auction house, trade supplies, armor at Soran's Leather and Steel Armory, lodging at the Broken Tusk, and general trade goods.",al={"valley of strength amenities","vendors valley of strength","what's here"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who guards the Valley of Strength?",a="Orgrimmar Grunts patrol the Valley of Strength. These seasoned orc warriors keep the peace, protect incoming caravans, and guide travelers through the canyon city.",al={"orgrimmar grunts","guards in valley of strength","city defense"},it="threat"},{q="Is the Valley of Strength dangerous?",a="Not for members of the Horde. As the bustling gateway and commercial heart of Orgrimmar, it is heavily watched by Grunts and city defenders around the clock. The only real peril here would be an outright Alliance raid breaching the main gates or stealthy infiltrators trying to assassinate Horde leadership.",al={"is valley of strength dangerous","valley of strength danger","safe in valley of strength"},it="danger",add="da94a7d4"},{q="Who lives in and runs the Valley of Strength?",a="The valley serves as the public center of Orgrimmar and operates under the authority of Warchief Thrall and his guards. Travelers, bankers, and merchants bustle through its open streets, while Thrall governs from Grommash Hold in the Valley of Wisdom.",al={"who runs valley of strength","valley of strength residents","who controls valley of strength"},it="residents",add="007f5841"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you first meet others to trade and recruit for expeditions in the Valley of Strength, the plaza just inside Orgrimmar's gates."},kw={"auction house","bank","broken tusk","durotar","grommash hold","horde","orgrimmar","thrall","valley of strength"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:grommash-hold","topic:horde"},src={"Valley of Strength"}}
E["zone:orgrimmar"] = {t="city",n="Orgrimmar",z="orgrimmar",s="Out of the red canyons of northern Durotar rises Orgrimmar, stronghold of the orcs. It is the heart of the New Horde. Trolls, tauren and Forsaken allies have found shelter within its walls.",h="Out of the red canyons of northern Durotar rises Orgrimmar, stronghold of the orcs.",sec={{t="A Home Chiseled from Stone",b="The orcs came here looking for a home. After the Third War, Warchief Thrall led them to the dry coasts of Kalimdor. There they would be free at last, of demon taint and of human chains. He named the land Durotar, after his father. And he named the city for Orgrim Doomhammer, the mentor he had lost.\n\nThe stronghold was raised with blood and sweat. Tauren stood with the orcs, and Darkspear trolls, and goblin engineers. The Champion Rexxar stood with them too. Together they drove back the centaurs, the harpies and the fierce thunder lizards of the canyons.",sp=0},{t="Valleys of the Horde",b="Rugged mountains ring the city. They keep out both foreign foes and the razor-winds of Durotar. Within, the rock opens into hollows, and each valley has its own part in the life of the Horde.\n\nIn the Valley of Strength stands the gatehouse. From it a road runs deeper in, to the market of the Drag. Tauren druids and shaman gather by the pools in the Valley of Wisdom. And in the Valley of Spirits, the shadow hunters and witch doctors of the Darkspear dwell among their pavilions on stilts.",sp=0},{t="Shadows in the Red Rock",b="Below the Valley of Honor and the heights of Grommash Hold, another life stirs beneath Orgrimmar. Warlocks and rogues practice in the cavern called the Cleft of Shadow, where Thrall keeps a close watch and grudgingly allows their arts. Farther below, Ragefire Chasm winds through volcanic tunnels beneath the canyon floor. Dark cultists and subterranean beasts fester there, threatening the fortress from within its own foundations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Orgrimmar?",a="Warchief Thrall rules Orgrimmar from Grommash Hold. He leads the New Horde with honor, survival, and shamanistic heritage in mind, alongside Darkspear chieftain Vol'jin and veteran commander Varok Saurfang.",al={"orgrimmar leader","who is in charge of orgrimmar","current warchief"},it="in_charge",nx={10,11}},{q="Why is the city named Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall named Orgrimmar for Orgrim Doomhammer, the legendary former Warchief. Orgrim broke the shadow council's hold on the Old Horde and, before dying in battle, passed his warplate and the Doomhammer to Thrall.",al={"orgrimmar name origin","who is orgrimmar named after"},it="name"},{q="Who lives in Orgrimmar besides orcs?",a="Orgrimmar is home to the Darkspear troll tribe, whose members live in the Valley of Spirits, and welcomes visiting tauren ambassadors in the Valley of Wisdom. A contingent of Forsaken emissaries also has a presence in the city after their recent entry into the Horde.",al={"races in orgrimmar","who lives here","trolls in orgrimmar"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Cleft of Shadow?",a="The Cleft of Shadow is a dim cavernous fissure beneath the canyon bluffs, off The Drag. The city's rogue and warlock guilds make their home there, keeping illicit trade and dangerous demonic invocations secluded from civilian districts.",al={"cleft of shadow","underground orgrimmar","orgrimmar warlock area"},it="place"},{q="What threats exist inside the city?",a="Ragefire Chasm lies directly below the Cleft of Shadow. Its volcanic fissures teem with troggs, searing elementals, and treacherous warlocks who seek to undermine Thrall's rule from the depths.",al={"dangers in orgrimmar","ragefire chasm threat","orgrimmar cultists"},it="threat"},{q="How do you travel to other continents from Orgrimmar?",a="Goblin-engineered zeppelins dock atop towers outside Orgrimmar’s main gate. They make regular flights across the Great Sea to Tirisfal Glades near Undercity and south to Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"orgrimmar zeppelins","getting to tirisfal from orgrimmar","travel from orgrimmar"},gp=true},{q="What is Orgrimmar?",a="Orgrimmar is the warrior capital of the orcs and the primary seat of the New Horde. Carved into the towering red rock canyons of northern Durotar, it stands as a fortified haven built by Warchief Thrall following the Third War. It serves as the heart of commerce, military might, and culture for orcs, Darkspear trolls, tauren, and their Forsaken allies.",al={"what is this city","orgrimmar overview","about orgrimmar"},it="place",add="34960c6e",nx={8,9}},{q="Who built Orgrimmar?",a="Warchief Thrall and his orcs founded the fortress shortly after the Battle of Mount Hyjal, completing it in a remarkably brief period. They were aided by the cunning Darkspear trolls, the noble tauren of Mulgore, goblin laborers and engineers, and the wandering half-ogre beastmaster Rexxar.",al={"who made orgrimmar","how was orgrimmar built","construction of orgrimmar"},it="origin",add="2f0bb5cb"},{q="Why is Orgrimmar out here in the desert?",a="Thrall deliberately led his people to the harsh, sun-scorched lands of Durotar to carve out a home through labor and perseverance. The red soil and rugged crags reminded the orcs of their ancestral homeland of Draenor, while offering natural defensive valleys and canyons to safeguard their hard-won independence.",al={"why build in durotar","why is the city in a desert","why settle here"},it="why_here",add="8dcd1cbd"},{q="Where is Thrall?",a="Thrall holds court within Grommash Hold, nestled high in the Valley of Wisdom. Outside his cold stone fortress stands an ancient tree trunk displaying the shattered skull and armor of Mannoroth—a stark monument honoring Grom Hellscream's sacrifice and the Horde's liberation from demonic corruption.",al={"where to find thrall","thrall location","where is the warchief"},it="place",add="2df9c1bd"},{q="Who is Nazgrel?",a="Nazgrel is a veteran orc warrior and trusted lieutenant who serves Thrall directly inside Grommash Hold. Fiercely devoted to the Warchief, he helps oversee the city's defense and martial readiness alongside the Horde's high command.",al={"who is that warrior by thrall","nazgrel role","thrall advisor nazgrel"},it="identity",add="6bde2c20"},{q="Is Orgrimmar dangerous?",a="While the city's towering gates and seasoned grunts keep outside invaders at bay, peril still lingers inside. Shifty cultists and rogue covens lurk in the shadowed chasms beneath the cliffs, ferocious razor-winds sweep through the valleys to damage careless construction, and the subterranean cavern of Ragefire Chasm festers with troggs and dark elemental corruption right under the streets.",al={"is it safe here","orgrimmar danger","hazards in orgrimmar"},it="danger",add="19245cb0"},{q="What happened at Orgrimmar?",a="Following the Third War, Thrall led the orcs to Kalimdor to escape the demonic taint that had shattered their people. With help from the tauren, trolls, and Rexxar, they carved this fortress out of Durotar's canyons while battling native quilboar, centaur, and harpies, transforming a barren frontier into the enduring citadel of the New Horde.",al={"orgrimmar history","past of orgrimmar","how was orgrimmar founded"},it="history",add="f5c45f78"},{q="How did I end up in Orgrimmar?",a="If you are an orc or a Darkspear troll, you answered the call of your elders. After proving yourself through the trials of Durotar, your trainers directed you north along the red clay roads to pass beneath the great fortified gates of the capital. If you arrived from afar—a tauren from the plains of Mulgore or a Forsaken traveler crossing the Great Sea by zeppelin from Tirisfal Glades—you have come to the heart of the New Horde, answering Warchief Thrall's summons to unite its scattered peoples under one banner.",al={"how did i get here","how did i arrive here","why did i come to orgrimmar"},it="arrival",add="f55ec44b"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Orgrimmar?",a="You are here to hone your craft, report to your leaders, and aid the growing Horde. Seek out class masters and profession trainers throughout the city's valleys, trade at the auction houses, or present yourself before Warchief Thrall in Grommash Hold. The young realm is beset by threats—from centaur warbands and quilboar raiders encroaching across the borders to foul cultists hiding in the subterranean depths of Ragefire Chasm. Prove your worth in defense of your allies.",al={"what should i do here","why am i here","what is my purpose in orgrimmar"},it="purpose",add="07461c2e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a champion of the Horde, you find weaponmasters, class mentors, and trade hubs in its military and cultural seat. Warchief Thrall also receives audiences here.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can see Orgrimmar as hard-won freedom from demonic lethargy and internment, and as your people’s proud ancestral fortress on Durotar’s soil.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you have found lasting sanctuary alongside the orcs after losing the Darkspear Isles. The Valley of Spirits is your secure spiritual home.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you follow Thrall’s restoration of shamanism to the heart of Horde leadership. In the tranquil Valley of Wisdom, practitioners study the elements and commune with ancestral spirits.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you find an uneasy refuge in the Cleft of Shadow. Thrall keeps watch as you hone your dark arts, secluded from open judgment."},kw={"cleft of shadow","drag","durotar","grommash hold","orgrim doomhammer","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","thrall","valley of spirits","valley of strength","valley of wisdom","warchief"},rel={"npc:thrall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:durotar","zone:ragefire","subzone:grommash-hold","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","topic:new-horde","npc:vol-jin"},src={"Orgrimmar"}}
